tick: 8
role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Depthwise CNN with Attention Pooling for RNA\"\ntags: \"cnn, depthwise separable, attention pooling, multi-dataset, adamw\"\nabstract: \"Unified depthwise-separable CNN with residual blocks and attention pooling. Lightweight 1D convolutions model local motifs; learned attention pooling summarizes variable-length sequences. A small MLP head adapts to regression, multilabel classification/regression, or multiclass tasks. AdamW with gradient clipping. Same core architecture across all datasets (only output dimension varies).\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n\n  # -----------------------------\n  # Hyperparameters\n  # -----------------------------\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 4,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1\n\
    \      }\n\n  # -----------------------------\n  # Model components\n  # -----------------------------\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          residual = x\n          y = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          # Depthwise conv (groups = channels)\n          y = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.d_model,\n              kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n              feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n              padding='SAME'\n          )(y)\n          y = nn.gelu(y)\n          # Pointwise conv\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,))(y)\n          y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(y, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return residual + y\n\n  class AttnPool1D(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x: (B, L, C)\n          a = nn.tanh(nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x))\
    \      # (B, L, C)\n          a = nn.Dense(1)(a)                          # (B, L, 1)\n          a = nn.softmax(a, axis=1)                   # attention weights over L\n          pooled = jnp.sum(a * x, axis=1)             # (B, C)\n          return pooled\n\n  class RNANet(nn.Module):\n      d_input: int = 4\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type: str = 'regression'\n      d_model: int = 256\n      num_blocks: int = 4\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # Input projection\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Residual depthwise-separable conv stack\n          for _ in range(self.num_blocks):\n              h = DSConvBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Global attention pooling\n      \
    \    pooled = AttnPool1D(self.d_model)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Head\n          h2 = nn.LayerNorm()(pooled)\n          h2 = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(h2)\n          h2 = nn.gelu(h2)\n          h2 = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h2, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(h2)\n\n          # Output shapes:\n          # - regression single-output: (batch,)\n          # - multilabel classification/regression: (batch, d_output)\n          # - multiclass classification: (batch, d_output) logits\n          if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n              return logits.squeeze(-1)\n          else:\n              return logits\n\n  class DSConvAttnNetwork:\n      def __init__(self, d_input, d_output, task_type, d_model, num_blocks, kernel_size, dropout_rate):\n          self.network = RNANet(\n              d_input=d_input,\n              d_output=d_output,\n              task_type=task_type,\n              d_model=d_model,\n\
    \              num_blocks=num_blocks,\n              kernel_size=kernel_size,\n              dropout_rate=dropout_rate\n          )\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                        dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False,\n                                        rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  # -----------------------------\n  # Station-required hooks\n  # -----------------------------\n  def create_network(hparams):\n\
    \      d_output = hparams.get('d_output', 1)\n      task_type = hparams.get('task_type', 'regression')\n      d_model = hparams.get('d_model', 256)\n      num_blocks = hparams.get('num_blocks', 4)\n      kernel_size = hparams.get('kernel_size', 7)\n      dropout_rate = hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1)\n      d_input = 4  # one-hot RNA\n\n      return DSConvAttnNetwork(\n          d_input=d_input,\n          d_output=d_output,\n          task_type=task_type,\n          d_model=d_model,\n          num_blocks=num_blocks,\n          kernel_size=kernel_size,\n          dropout_rate=dropout_rate\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      # Gradient clipping for stability + AdamW\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset')\n      vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n     \
    \ try:\n          print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm:.4f}\")\n      except Exception:\n          print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n\n  # Optional constants\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n```"
thinking_content: "**Proposing a better architecture**\n\nI’m seeing that in `train_single`, they handle multiclass classification with cross-entropy. For full training, I think we should keep it reliable by not overriding the “hardcoded” values and implementing `create_network` with hparams as an option. We need to suggest a better architecture than just using Dense + mean pooling because of varying dataset lengths. I'm considering lightweight convolutional pooling or global attention as alternatives. Overall, the approach can't be too heavy.**Designing a new architecture**\n\nI’m thinking about a network design that includes CNNs with gated residual blocks and global additive attention pooling, plus positional encoding for sequences. Using depthwise separable convolutions seems like a smart choice for efficiency. For implementation, using JAX and Flax makes sense, while also keeping dropout keys in mind. I plan to create a network wrapper with `.init` and `.apply` based on the Flax Module.\
  \ I’ll include token embeddings and sinusoidal positional encodings, adding learned biases through depthwise convolution to keep things manageable.**Implementing residual connections**\n\nI’m focusing on using residual connections in the architecture, which seems like a solid choice. For attention pooling, I can compute softmax(qk) weights to pool features into a vector. A simpler path could be learning a query vector for each output type. I’ll implement a basic softmax attention pooling using tanh gating. For the output head, I need to produce a single scalar for regression and linear logits for classification tasks. I want to maintain a unified architecture for cross-task parameter sharing, even if each dataset runs separate trials.**Defining hyperparameters**\n\nI need to define several hyperparameters for the model, including d_model, num_blocks, kernel_size, dropout_rate, and pooling options like 'attn' or 'mean'. For the learning rate, I’m considering values around 0.001 or 0.0007.\
  \ The BATCH_SIZE could start at 128, but since the baseline used 64, I think sticking with 64 for safety is wise. I’ll keep the learning rate at 0.001 and use AdamW with a weight decay of 0.01. Including gradient clipping in the training process seems important for stability too!**Finalizing the architecture**\n\nI’m focusing on setting up the training loop in `train_single`, ensuring it uses `compute_loss`. The network must accept `rng_key` for dropout. For classification, I’ll make sure the predictions are in logits for the metrics. Input shapes need to be correct for convolution. I’ll implement a `ResidualDSConvBlock`, add Squeeze-excite gating, and an attention pooling class. The output head will vary for regression and classification. Plus, I’ll use a constant BATCH_SIZE of 64 and set hyperparameters, ensuring the network is JAX-friendly!**Finalizing the code for RNA model**\n\nI’m focusing on addressing the varying sequence lengths in the dataset, like the `ncRNA`, which indicates\
  \ a length of 1136. This means the network must handle variable lengths effectively, so I’ll set it up to manage that. \n\nI’ll ensure our architecture, `DSConvAttnNetwork`, matches the required methods. Plus, the optimizer will include gradient clipping. For the YAML submission, I need to ensure everything is correctly quoted.  \n\nLast touches include essential imports, hyperparameters, and logging. I'll keep that light yet comprehensive!"
