tick: 12
role: model
parts:
- text: "The ablations show mean pooling improves the average score, depthwise convs are crucial for MRL and ncRNA, and attention helps ncRNA but can hurt APA/Modif. I’ll add a gated mean-attention pooling option to unify benefits, then queue two runs.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/models/dsconv_attn.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n\n  # -----------------------------\n  # Positional encoding\n  # -----------------------------\n  def sinusoidal_positional_encoding(L: int, d_model: int):\n      positions = jnp.arange(L)[:, None]            # (L, 1)\n      dims = jnp.arange(d_model)[None, :]           # (1, C)\n      angle_rates = 1.0 / (10000.0 ** (2.0 * (dims // 2) / jnp.maximum(1.0, float(d_model))))\n      angles = positions * angle_rates              # (L, C)\n      pe = jnp.where((dims % 2) == 0, jnp.sin(angles), jnp.cos(angles))\n      return pe  # (L, C)\n\n  # -----------------------------\n\
    \  # Blocks\n  # -----------------------------\n  class SqueezeExcite1D(nn.Module):\n      se_ratio: float = 0.0\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          if self.se_ratio <= 0.0:\n              return x\n          C = x.shape[-1]\n          h = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)                 # (B, C)\n          hidden = max(1, int(C * self.se_ratio))\n          h = nn.Dense(hidden)(h)\n          h = nn.relu(h)\n          gate = nn.Dense(C)(h)\n          gate = nn.sigmoid(gate)                 # (B, C)\n          return x * gate[:, None, :]\n\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          residual = x\n          y = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          # Depthwise conv (groups = channels)\n          y = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.d_model,\n              kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n              feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n    \
    \          padding='SAME'\n          )(y)\n          y = nn.gelu(y)\n          # Pointwise conv\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,))(y)\n          y = SqueezeExcite1D(self.se_ratio if hasattr(self, 'se_ratio') else 0.0)(y)\n          y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(y, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return residual + y\n\n  class AttnPool1D(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x: (B, L, C)\n          a = nn.tanh(nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x))   # (B, L, C)\n          a = nn.Dense(1)(a)                       # (B, L, 1)\n          a = nn.softmax(a, axis=1)                # over L\n          return jnp.sum(a * x, axis=1)            # (B, C)\n\n  class GatedMeanAttnPool1D(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x: (B, L, C)\n          mean_pool = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)                      # (B, C)\n   \
    \       attn_pool = AttnPool1D(self.d_model)(x, deterministic=deterministic)  # (B, C)\n          # Gate from global summary\n          g = nn.LayerNorm()(mean_pool)\n          g = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(g)\n          g = nn.gelu(g)\n          g = nn.Dense(1)(g)                                   # (B, 1)\n          g = nn.sigmoid(g)\n          pooled = g * attn_pool + (1.0 - g) * mean_pool       # (B, C)\n          return pooled\n\n  # -----------------------------\n  # Network\n  # -----------------------------\n  class RNANet(nn.Module):\n      d_input: int = 4\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type: str = 'regression'\n      d_model: int = 256\n      num_blocks: int = 4\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      pooling: str = 'attn'             # 'attn' | 'mean' | 'max' | 'gated'\n      include_depthwise: bool = True\n      se_ratio: float = 0.0\n      positional_encoding: bool = True\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n\
    \          # x: (B, L, 4)\n          # Input projection\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x)            # (B, L, C)\n          if self.positional_encoding:\n              L = h.shape[1]\n              pe = sinusoidal_positional_encoding(L, self.d_model)  # (L, C)\n              h = h + pe[None, :, :]\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Depthwise-separable conv stack\n          if self.include_depthwise:\n              for _ in range(self.num_blocks):\n                  h = DSConvBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, self.dropout_rate).apply(\n                      {'params': {}}, h, deterministic=deterministic, mutable=[]\n                  )\n                  # Re-implement inline to pass se_ratio\n                  residual = h\n                  y = nn.LayerNorm()(h)\n                  y = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                              feature_group_count=self.d_model,\
    \ padding='SAME')(y)\n                  y = nn.gelu(y)\n                  y = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,))(y)\n                  if self.se_ratio > 0.0:\n                      C = y.shape[-1]\n                      se = jnp.mean(y, axis=1)\n                      hidden = max(1, int(C * self.se_ratio))\n                      se = nn.Dense(hidden)(se)\n                      se = nn.relu(se)\n                      gate = nn.Dense(C)(se)\n                      gate = nn.sigmoid(gate)\n                      y = y * gate[:, None, :]\n                  y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(y, deterministic=deterministic)\n                  h = residual + y\n\n          # Pooling\n          if self.pooling == 'attn':\n              pooled = AttnPool1D(self.d_model)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif self.pooling == 'gated':\n              pooled = GatedMeanAttnPool1D(self.d_model)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif self.pooling == 'max':\n     \
    \         pooled = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n          else:\n              pooled = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n\n          # Head\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(pooled)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n          if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n              return logits.squeeze(-1)  # (B,)\n          else:\n              return logits             # logits for classification or multi-output regression\n\n  class DSConvAttnNetwork:\n      def __init__(self, d_input, d_output, task_type, **kwargs):\n          self.network = RNANet(d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, **kwargs)\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                    \
    \                    dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False,\n                                        rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def build_network(d_output: int, task_type: str, hparams: dict):\n      d_input = 4\n      kwargs = dict(\n          d_model=hparams.get('d_model', 256),\n          num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks', 4),\n          kernel_size=hparams.get('kernel_size', 7),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n          pooling=hparams.get('pooling', 'attn'),\n          include_depthwise=hparams.get('include_depthwise', True),\n          se_ratio=hparams.get('se_ratio',\
    \ 0.0),\n          positional_encoding=hparams.get('positional_encoding', True),\n      )\n      return DSConvAttnNetwork(d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, **kwargs)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Gated Mean–Attention Pooling (DSConv)\"\ntags: \"cnn, depthwise separable, gated pooling, unified, multi dataset\"\nabstract: \"Adds a learned gate to blend attention and mean pooling within the same unified DSConv architecture. Goal: retain attention’s benefits for ncRNA while preserving mean pooling’s strong performance on APA/Modif, without dataset-specific logic.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema')\n\n  from models.dsconv_attn import build_network\n  import optax\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 4,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'pooling': 'gated',         # new blended\
    \ pooling\n          'include_depthwise': True,\n          'se_ratio': 0.0,\n          'positional_encoding': True\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      d_output = hparams.get('d_output', 1)\n      task_type = hparams.get('task_type', 'regression')\n      return build_network(d_output, task_type, hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset')\n      vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Kernel Sweep: k=11 with Mean Pooling (DSConv)\"\ntags: \"kernel size, cnn, depthwise separable, mean pooling, multi dataset\"\nabstract: \"Increase receptive field to 11 while using mean pooling, motivated\
    \ by ablations showing mean pooling strong on APA/Modif and depthwise convs essential for MRL/ncRNA. Tests whether larger motifs help generalization and CRISPR tasks.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema')\n\n  from models.dsconv_attn import build_network\n  import optax\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 4,\n          'kernel_size': 11,        # larger receptive field\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'pooling': 'mean',        # best average in ablation\n          'include_depthwise': True,\n          'se_ratio': 0.0,\n          'positional_encoding': True\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      d_output = hparams.get('d_output', 1)\n      task_type = hparams.get('task_type', 'regression')\n      return build_network(d_output, task_type, hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n      \
    \    optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset')\n      vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 12 update — Ablation outcomes:\n  - Mean pooling > attention on average (Score 0.6190 vs 0.5917). Huge gains on APA (0.8565) and Modif (0.9520). CRI-Off slightly up. MRL roughly stable (0.6807 vs 0.6883). ncRNA dropped (0.6892 vs 0.8662).\n  - Removing depthwise convs hurts MRL massively (0.0579), confirming conv motif extraction is critical; ncRNA also down (0.7246), APA decent (0.7424), Modif high (0.9416).\n  Hypothesis: attention pooling can over-focus or miscalibrate on some tasks; mean pooling provides robust global signal. ncRNA benefits from focused\
    \ attention.\n  Action: added gated mean–attention pooling to unify benefits without dataset-specific logic. Also testing kernel=11 with mean pooling to expand receptive field for potential CRISPR gains.\n  Next candidates (after results): SE(0.25), dilated DSConv, multi-kernel inception, light LR schedule; plus generic cross-position mixing if CRISPR remains weak.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Analyzing model performance**\n\nI need to assess the latest state, specifically the detailed results. The baseline MLP scored 0.2401, while our submission for \"Depthwise CNN with Attention Pooling\" received 0.5917. In the ablation studies, using Mean Pooling (without attention) scored 0.6190, which is higher than the original. This difference suggests that attention pooling may have negatively affected performance overall. However, there were improvements in some metrics like APA and Modif AUC, which went from 0.7255 to 0.9520. That's quite notable!**Evaluating pooling methods**\n\nIn the first submission, I used attention pooling, while the second ablation switched to mean pooling but kept the depthwise convolution. Interestingly, the model without depthwise convs (MLP + attention) scored 0.4935, yet Modif AUC increased to 0.9416. However, the MRL dropped significantly to 0.0579, highlighting the importance of depthwise convs for MRL. It seems attention pooling might\
  \ be harmful for some tasks, especially with ncRNA. Overall, mean pooling outperformed attention because of large improvements in APA and Modif, suggesting attention pooling might be miscalibrated.**Exploring classification task improvements**\n\nIt seems that removing attention pooling may actually help the classification tasks by preventing erroneous focus on specific positions. Interestingly, the \"No Depthwise Convs\" version still used attention pooling and scored 0.9416 for Modif, while mean pooling reached 0.9520—both high scores. The original attention model was at 0.7255, so it feels like there's more influence at play, possibly involving head architecture differences. Both new ablations ran longer, and I think we could propose further experiments like a kernel sweep since there are no pending submissions now!**Planning new submissions**\n\nI'm ready to submit a kernel size 11 variant and test the SE ratio at 0.25. I also want to try multi-head attention pooling and compare dilated\
  \ convolutions with standard ones, while focusing on MRL-specific improvements. However, I need to keep the same architecture across tasks, limiting changes to output dimensions. I also have to manage the submission cooldown, as there’s a limit of two concurrent submissions. I can only open Public Memory or Archive when the model matures, which is a bit restricting but okay for now. The research scoreboard and storage are accessible, so that’s helpful!**Designing next submissions**\n\nI need to review \"system/defaults.py\" to ensure that multiclass classification is properly managed. Specifically, I noticed that the hardcoded_compute_loss doesn’t address it, but train_single does use cross-entropy when the task type is set correctly. We've successfully saved our DSConvAttn and DSConvMix modules. Now we can propose various tests, including the impact of positional encoding and pooling types. I also want to implement a \"Gated Mean-Attention Pooling (GMAP)\" variant that adapts to different\
  \ tasks. Additionally, I’d like to test a \"Dilated DSConv + GMAP\" to boost performance, especially for CRI-Off.**Planning new submissions**\n\nI’m considering resubmitting the \"Kernel Sweep: k=11\" since it wasn’t submitted due to concurrency. I also want to integrate the se_ratio of 0.25. It's crucial to summarize ablation insights in the private memory, and I'm targeting higher scores than the current 0.619. \n\nI propose two new experiments: a DSConv combined with a GMAP aggregator and a kernel size of 11 with mean pooling since it performed best. We will need to implement a gating aggregator within our code structure without breaking existing functions, ensuring we maintain backwards compatibility. After updating, I'll submit both experiments and review logs as needed.**Implementing code and submissions**\n\nI'm ready to produce the code while ensuring it aligns with the expected training loop interface. I plan to write the updated `dsconv_attn.py` with the new gating aggregator,\
  \ reinforcing earlier functionality. I'll create two submissions: one titled \"Gated Mean-Attention Pooling (DSConv)\" and another \"Kernel Sweep: k=11 with Mean Pooling.\"\n\nI'll be cautious about avoiding underscores in tags for research submissions, and manage edge conditions while implementing positional encoding and necessary functions. I’ll also remember to summarize the results in private memory. It’s all coming together!"
