parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 14\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noema I\n- Agent Description: An agent advancing novelty and parsimony through rigorous, insight-driven experimentation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 48,153 / 270,000 used (18%)\n- Agent Age: 14 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 12**\n\nEvaluation '12' is still pending. Please try again later.\n### Message 2\n\n**Evaluation Review: 13**\n\nEvaluation '13' is still pending. Please try again later.\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'Kernel Sweep: k=11 with Mean Pooling (DSConv)' (ID: 13) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6311070783794347\n**APA_R2:** 0.8587\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0651\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9521\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4753\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5734\n**MRL_R2:** 0.7377\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.7554\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger\
    \ Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 13\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed Flax module initialization error. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission imported a buggy `build_network` function from `storage/noema/models/dsconv_attn.py`. The bug was in the `RNANet.__call__` method (lines 114-116 of the lineage file):\n\n```python\nh = DSConvBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, self.dropout_rate).apply(\n    {'params': {}}, h, deterministic=deterministic, mutable=[]\n)\n```\n\nThis code incorrectly called `.apply()` on an uninitialized Flax module instance. In Flax's `@nn.compact` API, you should use modules directly, not call `.apply()` during the forward pass. The `.apply()` method is only for applying parameters to an already-initialized module.\n\nThe error manifested as:\n```\nflax.errors.ScopeCollectionNotFound: Tried to access \"scale\" from collection \"params\"\nin \"/LayerNorm_0\" but the collection is empty.\n```\n\nThis occurred because\
    \ the `.apply()` call passed an empty params dict `{'params': {}}`, causing LayerNorm to fail when trying to access its parameters.\n\n## Fix Applied\nCreated `submissions/submission_v2.py` with the following changes:\n\n1. **Copied only the buggy `RNANet` class** from the lineage file (not the entire file)\n2. **Removed the broken `.apply()` call** (lines 114-116 from original)\n3. **Kept the working inline implementation** that was already present (lines 117-134 from original)\n4. **Also copied `DSConvAttnNetwork` and `build_network`** to use the fixed `RNANet` class\n5. **Preserved all working imports** from the lineage (helper functions, utility classes)\n\nThe fixed code directly instantiates the DSConvBlock modules within the loop:\n```python\nfor _ in range(self.num_blocks):\n    residual = h\n    y = nn.LayerNorm()(h)\n    y = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME')(y)\n    # ... rest of\
    \ the depthwise separable convolution block\n    h = residual + y\n```\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed success with exit code 0:\n- Code has been running for 300+ seconds without crashing\n- No Flax initialization errors\n- Network creation and validation proceeding normally\n\n## Note\nThe agent had already identified the issue (the inline implementation was present alongside the broken `.apply()` call), but failed to remove the broken code. This is a simple case of dead code removal - the fix just eliminates the erroneous `.apply()` call and uses the correct implementation that was already there.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/noema')\n\n# Import everything that works correctly from the lineage\nfrom models.dsconv_attn import (\n    build_network as original_build_network,\n\
    \    DSConvAttnNetwork as OriginalDSConvAttnNetwork,\n    sinusoidal_positional_encoding,\n    SqueezeExcite1D,\n    DSConvBlock,\n    AttnPool1D,\n    GatedMeanAttnPool1D\n)\nimport optax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\n\n# Fixed version of RNANet - removed broken .apply() call\nclass RNANet(nn.Module):\n    d_input: int = 4\n    d_output: int = 1\n    task_type: str = 'regression'\n    d_model: int = 256\n    num_blocks: int = 4\n    kernel_size: int = 7\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n    pooling: str = 'attn'             # 'attn' | 'mean' | 'max' | 'gated'\n    include_depthwise: bool = True\n    se_ratio: float = 0.0\n    positional_encoding: bool = True\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # x: (B, L, 4)\n        # Input projection\n        h = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x)            # (B, L, C)\n        if self.positional_encoding:\n            L = h.shape[1]\n            pe = sinusoidal_positional_encoding(L, self.d_model)\
    \  # (L, C)\n            h = h + pe[None, :, :]\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Depthwise-separable conv stack\n        if self.include_depthwise:\n            for _ in range(self.num_blocks):\n                # FIXED: Removed broken .apply() call, kept only the working inline implementation\n                residual = h\n                y = nn.LayerNorm()(h)\n                y = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                            feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME')(y)\n                y = nn.gelu(y)\n                y = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,))(y)\n                if self.se_ratio > 0.0:\n                    C = y.shape[-1]\n                    se = jnp.mean(y, axis=1)\n                    hidden = max(1, int(C * self.se_ratio))\n                    se = nn.Dense(hidden)(se)\n                    se = nn.relu(se)\n       \
    \             gate = nn.Dense(C)(se)\n                    gate = nn.sigmoid(gate)\n                    y = y * gate[:, None, :]\n                y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(y, deterministic=deterministic)\n                h = residual + y\n\n        # Pooling\n        if self.pooling == 'attn':\n            pooled = AttnPool1D(self.d_model)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        elif self.pooling == 'gated':\n            pooled = GatedMeanAttnPool1D(self.d_model)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        elif self.pooling == 'max':\n            pooled = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n        else:\n            pooled = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n\n        # Head\n        z = nn.LayerNorm()(pooled)\n        z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z)\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n        if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n            return logits.squeeze(-1)\
    \  # (B,)\n        else:\n            return logits             # logits for classification or multi-output regression\n\n# Fixed wrapper class using the fixed RNANet\nclass DSConvAttnNetwork:\n    def __init__(self, d_input, d_output, task_type, **kwargs):\n        self.network = RNANet(d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, **kwargs)\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        from jax import random\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                      dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            from jax import random\n            if rng_key is None:\n                rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n        \
    \    return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False,\n                                      rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\ndef build_network(d_output: int, task_type: str, hparams: dict):\n    d_input = 4\n    kwargs = dict(\n        d_model=hparams.get('d_model', 256),\n        num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks', 4),\n        kernel_size=hparams.get('kernel_size', 7),\n        dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n        pooling=hparams.get('pooling', 'attn'),\n        include_depthwise=hparams.get('include_depthwise', True),\n        se_ratio=hparams.get('se_ratio', 0.0),\n        positional_encoding=hparams.get('positional_encoding', True),\n    )\n    return DSConvAttnNetwork(d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, **kwargs)\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'd_model': 256,\n        'num_blocks': 4,\n        'kernel_size': 11,        # larger receptive field\n        'dropout_rate':\
    \ 0.1,\n        'pooling': 'mean',        # best average in ablation\n        'include_depthwise': True,\n        'se_ratio': 0.0,\n        'positional_encoding': True\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    d_output = hparams.get('d_output', 1)\n    task_type = hparams.get('task_type', 'regression')\n    return build_network(d_output, task_type, hparams)\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n    )\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\ndef complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n    ds = trial_data.get('dataset')\n    vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n    print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic\
    \ compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network\
    \ creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 768 CPUs, 64 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: from submission\n  BASE_SEED: 42 (from submission\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials:\
    \ 7\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 240.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune multi-dataset training...\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-On dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-On Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 1453 train, 207 val, seq_len=23\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0128 |  0.3827  | 0.3877 \n 20  | 0.0118 |  0.4606  | 0.4606 \n 30  | 0.0094 |  0.4453  | 0.4753 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 37 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.4753 Time:11s\n[Complete] CRI-On val_metric=0.4753100951391369\n\nCRI-On training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.475310\nTraining time: 18s\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-Off dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman,\
    \ Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-Off Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 14223 train, 2032 val, seq_len=46\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0005 |  0.0351  | 0.0617 \n 20  | 0.0004 |  0.0295  | 0.0651 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 24 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.0651 Time:26s\n[Complete] CRI-Off val_metric=0.06508037765796329\n\nCRI-Off training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.065080\nTraining time: 33s\n\nStarting RNA training on MRL dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nMRL Training (regression, r2)\nData: 76319 train, 7600 val, seq_len=100\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.3358 |  0.6882  | 0.7030 \n 20  | 0.2311 |  0.7035  | 0.7377 \n\
    =============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 27 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.7377 Time:94s\n[Complete] MRL val_metric=0.7377252578735352\n\nMRL training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.737725\nTraining time: 103s\n\nStarting RNA training on ncRNA dataset\nTask type: multiclass_classification, Output dim: 13\nMetric: accuracy, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nncRNA Training (multiclass_classification, accuracy)\nData: 5670 train, 650 val, seq_len=1136\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val ACCURACY|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 1.2980 |  0.3138  | 0.3615 \n 20  | 0.6660 |  0.4862  | 0.5400 \n 30  | 0.4249 |  0.5662  | 0.5938 \n 40  | 0.2225 |  0.6369  | 0.6369 \n 50  | 0.1493 |  0.7169  | 0.7169 \n 60  | 0.0950 |  0.6354  | 0.7554 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 64 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\n\
