    \ dim: 3\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nPRS Training (multilabel_regression, r2)\nData: 73227 train, 9153 val, seq_len=148\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0379 |  0.5366  | 0.5545 \n 20  | 0.0338 |  0.5646  | 0.5734 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 28 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.5734 Time:385s\n[Complete] PRS val_metric=0.573367178440094\n\nPRS training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.573367\nTraining time: 394s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: d66be0fe-da9f-4804-b9af-bb8b6a7b647d\nTotal time: 784s\n============================================================\nFull training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-10-21 03:48:17,923\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1760989697923975564\n2025-10-21 03:48:17,938\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected\
    \ to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1760989697938538960\n\n```\n### Message 4\n\nYour research submission 'Gated Mean–Attention Pooling (DSConv)' (ID: 12) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.601751758243711\n**APA_R2:** 0.8584\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0618\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9518\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4625\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5726\n**MRL_R2:** 0.6698\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.6354\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 12\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the Flax module initialization error. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code in `storage/noema/models/dsconv_attn.py` had a critical bug in the `RNANet.__call__` method (lines 114-116). It attempted to use `.apply()` on a `DSConvBlock` module with an empty params dictionary:\n\n```python\nh = DSConvBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, self.dropout_rate).apply(\n    {'params': {}}, h, deterministic=deterministic, mutable=[]\n\
    )\n```\n\nThis caused a `flax.errors.ScopeCollectionNotFound` error because:\n1. When using `@nn.compact` modules inside another `@nn.compact` module, you should call them directly, not use `.apply()`\n2. The `.apply()` method requires properly initialized parameters, but an empty dictionary `{'params': {}}` was passed\n3. This caused LayerNorm inside DSConvBlock to fail when trying to access its scale parameters\n\nAdditionally, the code had duplicate logic (lines 118-134) that re-implemented the DSConvBlock inline, suggesting the author was aware of the issue but didn't remove the problematic `.apply()` call.\n\n## Fix Applied\nCreated `submission_v2.py` with the following changes:\n\n1. **Removed the problematic `.apply()` call** - Deleted lines 114-116 that incorrectly used `.apply()` on DSConvBlock\n\n2. **Kept the inline implementation** - The duplicate inline implementation (lines 118-134 in original) was actually the correct approach, so I kept this logic and removed the broken\
    \ `.apply()` attempt\n\n3. **Created complete fixed module** - Since the bug was in the imported `RNANet` class from `storage/noema/models/dsconv_attn.py`:\n   - Imported working helper classes: `sinusoidal_positional_encoding`, `SqueezeExcite1D`, `AttnPool1D`, `GatedMeanAttnPool1D`\n   - Copied and fixed the `RNANet` class directly in the submission\n   - Created `FixedDSConvAttnNetwork` wrapper to replace the buggy `DSConvAttnNetwork`\n   - Updated `create_network()` to use `FixedDSConvAttnNetwork` instead of `build_network()`\n\nThe fixed version properly implements the depthwise-separable convolution blocks inline within the `@nn.compact` module, which is the correct Flax pattern.\n\n## Verification\nRan `monitor_evaluation.py 2` which confirmed:\n- Exit code: 0 (SUCCESS)\n- Code ran for 300+ seconds without crashing\n- The submission is now executing the training pipeline successfully\n\nThe fix allows the network to initialize properly and begin training on the RNA datasets as\
    \ intended.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/noema')\n\n# Import everything except the buggy RNANet module\nfrom models.dsconv_attn import (\n    sinusoidal_positional_encoding,\n    SqueezeExcite1D,\n    AttnPool1D,\n    GatedMeanAttnPool1D,\n    DSConvAttnNetwork,\n    build_network\n)\nimport optax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\n\n# Fixed version of RNANet with corrected DSConvBlock usage\nclass RNANet(nn.Module):\n    d_input: int = 4\n    d_output: int = 1\n    task_type: str = 'regression'\n    d_model: int = 256\n    num_blocks: int = 4\n    kernel_size: int = 7\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n    pooling: str = 'attn'             # 'attn' | 'mean' | 'max' | 'gated'\n    include_depthwise: bool = True\n    se_ratio: float = 0.0\n    positional_encoding:\
    \ bool = True\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # x: (B, L, 4)\n        # Input projection\n        h = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x)            # (B, L, C)\n        if self.positional_encoding:\n            L = h.shape[1]\n            pe = sinusoidal_positional_encoding(L, self.d_model)  # (L, C)\n            h = h + pe[None, :, :]\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Depthwise-separable conv stack\n        if self.include_depthwise:\n            for _ in range(self.num_blocks):\n                # Fixed: Implement DSConv block inline to pass se_ratio properly\n                residual = h\n                y = nn.LayerNorm()(h)\n                # Depthwise conv (groups = channels)\n                y = nn.Conv(\n                    features=self.d_model,\n                    kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                    feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n     \
    \               padding='SAME'\n                )(y)\n                y = nn.gelu(y)\n                # Pointwise conv\n                y = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,))(y)\n\n                # Squeeze-Excite if enabled\n                if self.se_ratio > 0.0:\n                    C = y.shape[-1]\n                    se = jnp.mean(y, axis=1)\n                    hidden = max(1, int(C * self.se_ratio))\n                    se = nn.Dense(hidden)(se)\n                    se = nn.relu(se)\n                    gate = nn.Dense(C)(se)\n                    gate = nn.sigmoid(gate)\n                    y = y * gate[:, None, :]\n\n                y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(y, deterministic=deterministic)\n                h = residual + y\n\n        # Pooling\n        if self.pooling == 'attn':\n            pooled = AttnPool1D(self.d_model)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        elif self.pooling == 'gated':\n            pooled = GatedMeanAttnPool1D(self.d_model)(h,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic)\n        elif self.pooling == 'max':\n            pooled = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n        else:\n            pooled = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n\n        # Head\n        z = nn.LayerNorm()(pooled)\n        z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z)\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n        if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n            return logits.squeeze(-1)  # (B,)\n        else:\n            return logits             # logits for classification or multi-output regression\n\n# Fixed DSConvAttnNetwork wrapper\nclass FixedDSConvAttnNetwork:\n    def __init__(self, d_input, d_output, task_type, **kwargs):\n        self.network = RNANet(d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, **kwargs)\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        from jax import random\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n\
    \        variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                      dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        from jax import random\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None:\n                rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False,\n                                      rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'd_model': 256,\n        'num_blocks': 4,\n        'kernel_size': 7,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n        'pooling': 'gated',         # new blended pooling\n        'include_depthwise': True,\n        'se_ratio': 0.0,\n        'positional_encoding': True\n    }\n\
    \ndef create_network(hparams):\n    d_output = hparams.get('d_output', 1)\n    task_type = hparams.get('task_type', 'regression')\n    d_input = 4\n    kwargs = dict(\n        d_model=hparams.get('d_model', 256),\n        num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks', 4),\n        kernel_size=hparams.get('kernel_size', 7),\n        dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n        pooling=hparams.get('pooling', 'attn'),\n        include_depthwise=hparams.get('include_depthwise', True),\n        se_ratio=hparams.get('se_ratio', 0.0),\n        positional_encoding=hparams.get('positional_encoding', True),\n    )\n    return FixedDSConvAttnNetwork(d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, **kwargs)\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n    )\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\ndef complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n \
    \   ds = trial_data.get('dataset')\n    vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n    print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation\
    \ works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 768 CPUs, 64 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: from submission\n  BASE_SEED: 42 (from submission\n\
