parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 16\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noema I\n- Agent Description: An agent advancing novelty and parsimony through rigorous, insight-driven experimentation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 64,607 / 270,000 used (24%)\n- Agent Age: 16 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Dilated DSConv (1,2,4,8) with Mean Pooling' (ID: 17) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6365146721582435\n**APA_R2:** 0.8465\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0663\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9525\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4880\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5735\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8134\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.7154\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 17\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the Flax\
    \ Conv parameter bug. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission imported `build_network_v2` from `storage/noema/models/dsconv_mix.py`, which contained a critical bug in the `DSConvBlock` class:\n\n```python\ny = nn.Conv(\n    features=self.d_model,\n    kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n    feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n    padding='SAME',\n    dilation=(self.dilation,)  # ❌ WRONG PARAMETER NAME\n)\n```\n\n**Error**: `TypeError: Conv.__init__() got an unexpected keyword argument 'dilation'`\n\nThe issue is that Flax's `nn.Conv` doesn't accept a `dilation` parameter. The correct parameter name is `kernel_dilation`.\n\n## Fix Applied\n\nCreated `submissions/submission_v3.py` with a completely self-contained implementation that:\n\n1. **Removed all imports from the buggy lineage module** - Avoided importing from `storage/noema/models/dsconv_mix.py` entirely\n2. **Copied all necessary components** - Replicated the entire network architecture locally:\n\
    \   - `sinusoidal_positional_encoding()`\n   - `SqueezeExcite1D` class\n   - `DSConvBlock` class (with fix)\n   - `InceptionDSConvBlock` class\n   - `MultiHeadAttnPool1D` class\n   - `RNANetMix` class\n   - `DSConvMixNetwork` class\n   - `build_network_v2()` function\n3. **Applied the critical fix** in `DSConvBlock`:\n   ```python\n   y = nn.Conv(\n       features=self.d_model,\n       kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n       feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n       padding='SAME',\n       kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,)  # ✅ CORRECT PARAMETER NAME\n   )\n   ```\n\n## Verification\n- **Version 3 Status**: Running successfully for 300+ seconds without crashes\n- **Monitor Exit Code**: 0 (success)\n- **Error Resolution**: No TypeError, network initialization works correctly\n\n## Technical Notes\nThe initial attempt (v2) failed because it still imported helper functions from the buggy module, which internally referenced the broken `DSConvBlock`. The solution required creating a fully\
    \ self-contained implementation to ensure all components used the fixed code.\n\n## Recommendation\nThe agent (Noema I) should update their lineage file `storage/noema/models/dsconv_mix.py` to fix this bug for future submissions. This is a simple one-line change that will prevent similar failures.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v3):**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\n\n# -----------------------------\n# Positional encoding\n# -----------------------------\ndef sinusoidal_positional_encoding(L: int, d_model: int):\n    pos = jnp.arange(L)[:, None]\n    i = jnp.arange(d_model)[None, :]\n    denom = jnp.power(10000.0, (2 * (i // 2)) / jnp.maximum(1.0, float(d_model)))\n    angles = pos * denom\n    pe = jnp.where((i % 2) == 0, jnp.sin(angles), jnp.cos(angles))\n\
    \    return pe\n\n# -----------------------------\n# Components\n# -----------------------------\nclass SqueezeExcite1D(nn.Module):\n    se_ratio: float = 0.25\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        if self.se_ratio <= 0.0:\n            return x\n        C = x.shape[-1]\n        h = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)\n        h = nn.Dense(max(1, int(C * self.se_ratio)))(h)\n        h = nn.relu(h)\n        gate = nn.Dense(C)(h)\n        gate = nn.sigmoid(gate)\n        return x * gate[:, None, :]\n\nclass DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int\n    kernel_size: int\n    dropout_rate: float\n    dilation: int = 1\n    se_ratio: float = 0.0\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        residual = x\n        y = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n        y = nn.Conv(\n            features=self.d_model,\n            kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n            feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n            padding='SAME',\n            kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,)  # FIXED:\
    \ was 'dilation', should be 'kernel_dilation'\n        )(y)\n        y = nn.gelu(y)\n        # pointwise + GLU\n        z = nn.Dense(2 * self.d_model)(y)\n        y, g = jnp.split(z, 2, axis=-1)\n        y = y * nn.sigmoid(g)\n        y = SqueezeExcite1D(self.se_ratio)(y)\n        y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(y, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return residual + y\n\nclass InceptionDSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int\n    kernel_sizes: tuple = (5, 9, 15)\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n    se_ratio: float = 0.0\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        residual = x\n        y = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n        branches = []\n        for k in self.kernel_sizes:\n            b = nn.Conv(\n                features=self.d_model,\n                kernel_size=(k,),\n                feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n                padding='SAME'\n            )(y)\n            branches.append(b)\n        y = sum(branches) / len(branches)\n   \
    \     y = nn.gelu(y)\n        # pointwise + GLU\n        z = nn.Dense(2 * self.d_model)(y)\n        y, g = jnp.split(z, 2, axis=-1)\n        y = y * nn.sigmoid(g)\n        y = SqueezeExcite1D(self.se_ratio)(y)\n        y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(y, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return residual + y\n\nclass MultiHeadAttnPool1D(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int\n    num_heads: int = 4\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # x: (B, L, C)\n        h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n        a = nn.tanh(nn.Dense(self.d_model)(h))     # (B, L, C)\n        a = nn.Dense(self.num_heads)(a)            # (B, L, H)\n        w = nn.softmax(a, axis=1)                  # over L\n        pooled_heads = jnp.einsum('blh,blc->bhc', w, h)  # (B, H, C)\n        pooled = pooled_heads.mean(axis=1)         # (B, C)\n        return pooled\n\n# -----------------------------\n# Network\n# -----------------------------\nclass RNANetMix(nn.Module):\n    d_input: int = 4\n \
    \   d_output: int = 1\n    task_type: str = 'regression'\n    d_model: int = 256\n    num_blocks: int = 4\n    kernel_size: int = 7\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n    pooling: str = 'attn'\n    attn_heads: int = 4\n    block_type: str = 'dsconv'\n    dilations: tuple = (1, 2, 4, 8)\n    se_ratio: float = 0.0\n    positional_encoding: bool = True\n    inception_kernels: tuple = (5, 9, 15)\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # Input projection\n        h = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x)\n        if self.positional_encoding:\n            L = h.shape[1]\n            h = h + sinusoidal_positional_encoding(L, self.d_model)[None, :, :]\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Blocks\n        for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n            if self.block_type == 'inception':\n                h = InceptionDSConvBlock(\n                    d_model=self.d_model,\n                    kernel_sizes=self.inception_kernels,\n\
    \                    dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n                    se_ratio=self.se_ratio\n                )(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n            else:\n                dilation = 1 if self.block_type == 'dsconv' else self.dilations[i % len(self.dilations)]\n                h = DSConvBlock(\n                    d_model=self.d_model,\n                    kernel_size=self.kernel_size,\n                    dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n                    dilation=dilation,\n                    se_ratio=self.se_ratio\n                )(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Pooling\n        if self.pooling == 'attn':\n            pooled = MultiHeadAttnPool1D(self.d_model, num_heads=1)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        elif self.pooling == 'mha':\n            pooled = MultiHeadAttnPool1D(self.d_model, num_heads=self.attn_heads)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        elif self.pooling == 'max':\n            pooled = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n        else:\n    \
    \        pooled = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n\n        # Head\n        z = nn.LayerNorm()(pooled)\n        z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z)\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n        if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n            return logits.squeeze(-1)\n        return logits\n\nclass DSConvMixNetwork:\n    def __init__(self, d_input, d_output, task_type, **kwargs):\n        self.network = RNANetMix(d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, **kwargs)\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, drop_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        vars = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': drop_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return vars['params']\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x,\
    \ deterministic=True)\n        if rng_key is None:\n            rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n        return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\ndef build_network_v2(d_output: int, task_type: str, hparams: dict):\n    d_input = 4\n    kwargs = dict(\n        d_model=hparams.get('d_model', 256),\n        num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks', 4),\n        kernel_size=hparams.get('kernel_size', 7),\n        dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n        pooling=hparams.get('pooling', 'attn'),\n        attn_heads=hparams.get('attn_heads', 4),\n        block_type=hparams.get('block_type', 'dsconv'),\n        dilations=tuple(hparams.get('dilations', (1, 2, 4, 8))),\n        se_ratio=hparams.get('se_ratio', 0.0),\n        positional_encoding=hparams.get('positional_encoding', True),\n        inception_kernels=tuple(hparams.get('inception_kernels', (5, 9, 15))),\n    )\n    return DSConvMixNetwork(d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output,\
    \ task_type=task_type, **kwargs)\n\n# -----------------------------\n# Required submission functions\n# -----------------------------\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'd_model': 256,\n        'num_blocks': 4,\n        'kernel_size': 7,        # paired with dilations to expand RF\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n        'pooling': 'mean',\n        'block_type': 'dilated',\n        'dilations': (1, 2, 4, 8),\n        'se_ratio': 0.0,\n        'positional_encoding': True\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    d_output = hparams.get('d_output', 1)\n    task_type = hparams.get('task_type', 'regression')\n    return build_network_v2(d_output, task_type, hparams)\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n    )\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\ndef complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n\
    \    ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n    print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation\
    \ works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 768 CPUs, 64 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: from submission\n  BASE_SEED: 42 (from submission\n\
    \  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials: 7\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 240.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune multi-dataset training...\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-On dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-On Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 1453 train, 207 val, seq_len=23\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0122 |  0.4764  | 0.4880 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 17 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\n\
    Best:0.4880 Time:13s\n[Complete] CRI-On val_metric=0.4880101957982921\n\nCRI-On training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.488010\nTraining time: 21s\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-Off dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-Off Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 14223 train, 2032 val, seq_len=46\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0005 |  0.0082  | 0.0599 \n 20  | 0.0004 |  0.0623  | 0.0663 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 21 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.0663 Time:56s\n[Complete] CRI-Off val_metric=0.0662975699841526\n\nCRI-Off training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.066298\nTraining time: 63s\n\nStarting RNA training on PRS dataset\nTask type: multilabel_regression, Output dim: 3\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nPRS Training (multilabel_regression,\
