role: model
parts:
- text: "Fantastic SOTA jump to 0.6622 with dilated DSConv + concat MHA pooling. I’ll add a triple-pooling variant (mean + max + MHA) to balance APA/PRS with MRL/ncRNA, snapshot the current best, and log an ablation summary.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/models/dsconv_mix.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n\n  def sinusoidal_positional_encoding(L: int, d_model: int):\n      pos = jnp.arange(L)[:, None]\n      i = jnp.arange(d_model)[None, :]\n      denom = jnp.power(10000.0, (2 * (i // 2)) / jnp.maximum(1.0, float(d_model)))\n      angles = pos * denom\n      pe = jnp.where((i % 2) == 0, jnp.sin(angles), jnp.cos(angles))\n      return pe\n\n  class SqueezeExcite1D(nn.Module):\n      se_ratio: float = 0.25\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          if self.se_ratio <= 0.0:\n              return x\n          C = x.shape[-1]\n          h = jnp.mean(x,\
    \ axis=1)\n          h = nn.Dense(max(1, int(C * self.se_ratio)))(h)\n          h = nn.relu(h)\n          gate = nn.Dense(C)(h)\n          gate = nn.sigmoid(gate)\n          return x * gate[:, None, :]\n\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      dilation: int = 1\n      se_ratio: float = 0.0\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          residual = x\n          y = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          y = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.d_model,\n              kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n              feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n              padding='SAME',\n              kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,)\n          )(y)\n          y = nn.gelu(y)\n          z = nn.Dense(2 * self.d_model)(y)\n          y, g = jnp.split(z, 2, axis=-1)\n          y = y * nn.sigmoid(g)\n          y = SqueezeExcite1D(self.se_ratio)(y)\n          y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(y, deterministic=deterministic)\n\
    \          return residual + y\n\n  class InceptionDSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_sizes: tuple = (5, 9, 15)\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      se_ratio: float = 0.0\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          residual = x\n          y = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          branches = []\n          for k in self.kernel_sizes:\n              b = nn.Conv(\n                  features=self.d_model,\n                  kernel_size=(k,),\n                  feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n                  padding='SAME'\n              )(y)\n              branches.append(b)\n          y = sum(branches) / len(branches)\n          y = nn.gelu(y)\n          z = nn.Dense(2 * self.d_model)(y)\n          y, g = jnp.split(z, 2, axis=-1)\n          y = y * nn.sigmoid(g)\n          y = SqueezeExcite1D(self.se_ratio)(y)\n          y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(y, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return residual + y\n\n  class\
    \ MultiHeadAttnPool1D(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      num_heads: int = 4\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          a = nn.tanh(nn.Dense(self.d_model)(h))\n          a = nn.Dense(self.num_heads)(a)\n          w = nn.softmax(a, axis=1)\n          pooled_heads = jnp.einsum('blh,blc->bhc', w, h)\n          return pooled_heads.mean(axis=1)\n\n  class AttnPool1D_Simple(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.tanh(nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x))\n          a = nn.Dense(1)(h)\n          w = nn.softmax(a, axis=1)\n          return jnp.sum(w * x, axis=1)\n\n  class ConcatMeanAttnPool1D(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          mean_pool = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)\n          attn_pool = AttnPool1D_Simple(self.d_model)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return jnp.concatenate([mean_pool,\
    \ attn_pool], axis=-1)\n\n  class ConcatMeanMHAPool1D(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      num_heads: int = 4\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          mean_pool = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)\n          attn_pool = MultiHeadAttnPool1D(self.d_model, num_heads=self.num_heads)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return jnp.concatenate([mean_pool, attn_pool], axis=-1)\n\n  class ConcatMeanMaxMHAPool1D(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      num_heads: int = 4\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          mean_pool = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)\n          max_pool = jnp.max(x, axis=1)\n          attn_pool = MultiHeadAttnPool1D(self.d_model, num_heads=self.num_heads)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return jnp.concatenate([mean_pool, max_pool, attn_pool], axis=-1)\n\n  class RNANetMix(nn.Module):\n      d_input: int = 4\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type: str = 'regression'\n      d_model: int = 256\n      num_blocks:\
    \ int = 4\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      pooling: str = 'attn'            # 'attn' | 'mean' | 'max' | 'mha' | 'concat' | 'concat_mha' | 'concat_mmh'\n      attn_heads: int = 4\n      block_type: str = 'dsconv'       # 'dsconv' | 'dilated' | 'inception'\n      dilations: tuple = (1, 2, 4, 8)\n      se_ratio: float = 0.0\n      positional_encoding: bool = True\n      inception_kernels: tuple = (5, 9, 15)\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x)\n          if self.positional_encoding:\n              L = h.shape[1]\n              h = h + sinusoidal_positional_encoding(L, self.d_model)[None, :, :]\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              if self.block_type == 'inception':\n                  h = InceptionDSConvBlock(\n                      d_model=self.d_model,\n\
    \                      kernel_sizes=self.inception_kernels,\n                      dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n                      se_ratio=self.se_ratio\n                  )(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n              else:\n                  dilation = 1 if self.block_type == 'dsconv' else self.dilations[i % len(self.dilations)]\n                  h = DSConvBlock(\n                      d_model=self.d_model,\n                      kernel_size=self.kernel_size,\n                      dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n                      dilation=dilation,\n                      se_ratio=self.se_ratio\n                  )(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          if self.pooling == 'attn':\n              pooled = MultiHeadAttnPool1D(self.d_model, num_heads=1)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif self.pooling == 'mha':\n              pooled = MultiHeadAttnPool1D(self.d_model, num_heads=self.attn_heads)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif self.pooling\
    \ == 'max':\n              pooled = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n          elif self.pooling == 'concat':\n              pooled = ConcatMeanAttnPool1D(self.d_model)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif self.pooling == 'concat_mha':\n              pooled = ConcatMeanMHAPool1D(self.d_model, num_heads=self.attn_heads)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif self.pooling == 'concat_mmh':\n              pooled = ConcatMeanMaxMHAPool1D(self.d_model, num_heads=self.attn_heads)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          else:\n              pooled = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(pooled)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n          if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n              return logits.squeeze(-1)\n          return logits\n\n  class DSConvMixNetwork:\n      def __init__(self,\
    \ d_input, d_output, task_type, **kwargs):\n          self.network = RNANetMix(d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, **kwargs)\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, drop_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          vars = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': drop_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return vars['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          if rng_key is None:\n              rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n          return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def build_network_v2(d_output: int, task_type: str, hparams: dict):\n      d_input = 4\n      kwargs = dict(\n          d_model=hparams.get('d_model', 256),\n          num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks', 4),\n          kernel_size=hparams.get('kernel_size',\
    \ 7),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n          pooling=hparams.get('pooling', 'attn'),\n          attn_heads=hparams.get('attn_heads', 4),\n          block_type=hparams.get('block_type', 'dsconv'),\n          dilations=tuple(hparams.get('dilations', (1, 2, 4, 8))),\n          se_ratio=hparams.get('se_ratio', 0.0),\n          positional_encoding=hparams.get('positional_encoding', True),\n          inception_kernels=tuple(hparams.get('inception_kernels', (5, 9, 15))),\n      )\n      return DSConvMixNetwork(d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, **kwargs)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Dilated DSConv (1,2,4,8) + Concat Mean+Max+MHA Pooling\"\ntags: \"cnn, depthwise separable, dilated conv, mean+max+attention, multi-dataset\"\nabstract: \"Triple pooling (mean+max+multi-head attention) on top of dilated DSConv to fuse robust global, salient, and focused features. Unified architecture; same hyperparameters across datasets.\"\
    \ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema')\n\n  from models.dsconv_mix import build_network_v2\n  import optax\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 4,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'pooling': 'concat_mmh',   # new triple pooling\n          'attn_heads': 4,\n          'block_type': 'dilated',\n          'dilations': (1, 2, 4, 8),\n          'se_ratio': 0.0,\n          'positional_encoding': True\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      d_output = hparams.get('d_output', 1)\n      task_type = hparams.get('task_type', 'regression')\n      return build_network_v2(d_output, task_type, hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\
    \  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/best_dilated_concat_mha.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Snapshot of best method so far (Eval 31): Dilated DSConv + Concat MHA Pooling (4 heads)\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema')\n\n  from models.dsconv_mix import build_network_v2\n  import optax\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 4,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'pooling': 'concat_mha',\n          'attn_heads': 4,\n          'block_type': 'dilated',\n          'dilations': (1, 2, 4, 8),\n          'se_ratio': 0.0,\n          'positional_encoding': True\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      d_output = hparams.get('d_output',\
    \ 1)\n      task_type = hparams.get('task_type', 'regression')\n      return build_network_v2(d_output, task_type, hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[BEST-31 SNAPSHOT] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 21 update — SOTA 0.6622 (Eval 31: Dilated DSConv + Concat MHA; heads=4).\n  Key scores:\n  - 31: Score 0.6622 | APA 0.8367 | CRI-Off 0.0858 | CRI-On 0.5176 | PRS 0.5611 | MRL 0.8288 | Modif 0.9514 | ncRNA 0.8538\n  - 24: Score 0.6477 | APA 0.8458 | CRI-Off 0.0803 | CRI-On 0.4381 | PRS 0.5650 | MRL 0.8250 | Modif 0.9519 | ncRNA 0.8277\n  - 17:\
    \ Score 0.6365 | APA 0.8465 | CRI-Off 0.0663 | CRI-On 0.4880 | PRS 0.5735 | MRL 0.8134 | Modif 0.9525 | ncRNA 0.7154\n  - 13: Score 0.6311 | APA 0.8587 | CRI-Off 0.0651 | CRI-On 0.4753 | PRS 0.5734 | MRL 0.7377 | Modif 0.9521 | ncRNA 0.7554\n  - 20: Score 0.6255 | APA 0.8365 | CRI-Off 0.0769 | CRI-On 0.4690 | PRS 0.5639 | MRL 0.6479 | Modif 0.9509 | ncRNA 0.8338\n  - 8:  Score 0.6190 | APA 0.8565 | CRI-Off 0.0605 | CRI-On 0.5288 | PRS 0.5654 | MRL 0.6807 | Modif 0.9520 | ncRNA 0.6892\n  - 22: Score 0.6180 | APA 0.8442 | CRI-Off 0.0675 | CRI-On 0.4827 | PRS 0.5701 | MRL 0.7305 | Modif 0.9513 | ncRNA 0.6800\n  - 27: Score 0.6063 | APA 0.8325 | CRI-Off 0.0775 | CRI-On 0.4417 | PRS 0.5699 | MRL 0.6303 | Modif 0.9509 | ncRNA 0.7415\n\n  Insights:\n  - Pooling: Mean pooling boosts APA/Modif; attention boosts ncRNA/CRI tasks. Concatenating mean+MHA (with dilations) yields the best average.\n  - Receptive field: Dilations (1,2,4,8) substantially lift MRL and stabilize CRISPR vs. plain kernel\
    \ sweep.\n  - Scheduling: Cosine LR warmup degraded MRL/APA; constant LR 1e-3 is more robust here.\n  - Channel attention (SE=0.25) did not help; likely over-parameterized for this setup.\n\n  Actions:\n  - Queued triple pooling (mean+max+MHA) to strengthen APA/PRS while retaining MRL/ncRNA (Eval pending).\n  - Snapshot of best code saved to storage/noema/submissions/best_dilated_concat_mha.py.\n  - Pending: 8-head concat MHA run (Eval 34). If helpful, we’ll consolidate and draft the paper with ablation table and insights on pooling vs. receptive field trade-offs.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Considering architecture adjustments**\n\nI need to be cautious with the attempt count and evaluations. \n\nI'm thinking about using \"residual mixing\" similar to gated MLP mixing, but I want to maintain a unified architecture and avoid dataset-specific methods. Maybe I could explore adding a \"Token-mixing MLP\" or using \"Conv1D with dilations\" for long-range effects. \n\nAlso, I wonder whether to try learnable positional encoding or dropout rate tuning, considering layernorm placement and examining variations with the training system as well. \n\nCan I increase BATCH_SIZE from 64 to 128 if memory allows?**Evaluating model adjustments**\n\nI'm using a CPU for the runner, but the evaluation environment has GPUs turned off. Increasing the batch size might help speed things up, but it could also degrade performance, and it's not a novel approach. \n\nThe most promising idea I've seen is to unify pooling by combining mean and MHA, which has been done before. \n\nLooking\
  \ at the metrics, the best model has lower APA compared to earlier mean pooling, but there are improvements in other areas. It seems like there's a trade-off with APA and PRS dropping while others, like MRL and ncRNA, significantly increase. \n\nThe \"concat MHA with dilated\" method shows promise, except for APA and PRS. Perhaps adapting the output head for layer-specific calibrations may help.**Exploring optimization strategies**\n\nI'm adapting through different output dimensions, but I can't alter the losses. \n\nI've noticed that the learning rate schedule hurt performance, so I’ll stick with a constant learning rate. \n\nI'm considering using d_model values of 384 or 192 to see how they balance parsimony and performance. Trying a dropout rate of 0.05 or 0.2 feels less exciting, though.\n\nMaybe I could add \"residual gating\" or a \"channel mixing MLP\" after pooling. However, gains might be minor since the current head has a pretty solid structure. \n\nAnother thought is to use\
  \ a logit transform for regression outputs, but that might complicate the distribution without tweaking the mandated training system, which typically returns raw predictions. \n\nI’m also thinking about implementing multi-scale pooling with mean, max, and attention for potential improvements.**Proposing pooling enhancements**\n\nI've already included mean and MHA pooling, but I’m considering adding max pooling to create a \"triple pooling\" approach. This might enhance robustness.\n\nAnother potential improvement could involve \"relative positional biases\" in pooling attention, though that would be heavier on implementation.\n\nI could also implement \"ECA\" (efficient channel attention) within DSConv blocks since it has minimal compute costs. The previous SE ratio of 0.25 didn’t help. ECA may offer low overhead with a 1D convolution along channels to maintain parsimony.\n\nAdditionally, I’m considering adjusting the dilation patterns to enhance coverage with options like (1, 3, 5, 7)\
  \ or (1, 2, 3, 5).**Planning next actions**\n\nI’m considering testing \"hybrid dilations\" and incorporating \"residual skip connections\" with gating across blocks since we already have residuals inside blocks. \n\nAnother thought is to add \"GLU gating\" in the DSConvBlock. I could also test a smaller kernel size of 5 instead of 7 to see if it suffices. \n\nTo keep the experiments organized, I’ll compile an analysis of the results and create a private memory record with an ablation table. I also want to store the best submission code and add a paper draft in private memory. \n\nI’m aware of the token budget and have some evaluations pending. It seems I can queue one more submission for \"triple pooling.\" I'll implement the necessary code modifications and plan to submit the new run while recording an ablation summary. It's essential to ensure everything fits within constraints and maintains high value.**Implementing new pooling option**\n\nI’m planning to replicate the DSConvMixNetwork\
  \ and build_network_v2 while adding a new pooling option called 'concat_mmh' with ConcatMeanMaxMHAPool1D. It's important to keep the existing function names intact to avoid breaking earlier code. \n\nI’ll make sure to maintain the attn_heads parameter for this pooling option and use the usual imports to ensure everything is compatible with jax and jnp. For now, I'm setting attn_heads to 4 to moderate computational load. \n\nRetrieving the latest evaluations, I’ll summarize the best scores and key insights regarding pooling improvements and the impact of mean pooling. After that, I’ll prepare to queue the triple pooling submission and plan future explorations of learned positional encoding and dropout tuning.  Lastly, I need to create the YAML submission for this run titled 'Dilated DSConv + Concat Mean+Max+MHA Pooling.'"
