parts:
- text: "SOTA holds at 0.6622. I’ll test a temperature-scaled attention pooling to potentially sharpen CRISPR/ncRNA without hurting MRL.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Dilated DSConv + Concat MHA (attn_temp=0.7)\"\ntags: \"cnn, depthwise separable, dilated conv, attention temperature, pooling\"\nabstract: \"SOTA dilated DSConv with concat(mean, MHA) pooling, adding temperature-scaled attention (tau=0.7) to sharpen pooling weights. Unified across datasets.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n\n  class SqueezeExcite1D(nn.Module):\n      se_ratio: float = 0.0\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          if self.se_ratio <= 0.0:\n              return x\n          C = x.shape[-1]\n          h = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)\n          h = nn.Dense(max(1, int(C * self.se_ratio)))(h)\n          h = nn.relu(h)\n          gate = nn.Dense(C)(h)\n      \
    \    gate = nn.sigmoid(gate)\n          return x * gate[:, None, :]\n\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      dilation: int = 1\n      se_ratio: float = 0.0\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          residual = x\n          y = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          y = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.d_model,\n              kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n              feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n              padding='SAME',\n              kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,)\n          )(y)\n          y = nn.gelu(y)\n          z = nn.Dense(2 * self.d_model)(y)\n          a, g = jnp.split(z, 2, axis=-1)\n          y = a * nn.sigmoid(g)\n          y = SqueezeExcite1D(self.se_ratio)(y)\n          y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(y, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return residual + y\n\n  class MultiHeadAttnPoolTemp(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      num_heads:\
    \ int = 4\n      tau: float = 0.7\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x: (B, L, C)\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          logits = nn.tanh(nn.Dense(self.d_model)(h))     # (B, L, C)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.num_heads)(logits)       # (B, L, H)\n          w = nn.softmax(logits / self.tau, axis=1)       # temperature-scaled over L\n          pooled_heads = jnp.einsum('blh,blc->bhc', w, h) # (B, H, C)\n          return pooled_heads.mean(axis=1)                # (B, C)\n\n  class RNANetDilatedTemp(nn.Module):\n      d_input: int = 4\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type: str = 'regression'\n      d_model: int = 256\n      num_blocks: int = 4\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      attn_heads: int = 4\n      dilations: tuple = (1, 2, 4, 8)\n      se_ratio: float = 0.0\n      attn_temp: float = 0.7\n      positional_encoding: bool = True\n\n      def sinusoidal_positional_encoding(self, L, d_model):\n\
    \          pos = jnp.arange(L)[:, None]\n          i = jnp.arange(d_model)[None, :]\n          denom = jnp.power(10000.0, (2 * (i // 2)) / jnp.maximum(1.0, float(d_model)))\n          angles = pos * denom\n          return jnp.where((i % 2) == 0, jnp.sin(angles), jnp.cos(angles))\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x)\n          if self.positional_encoding:\n              L = h.shape[1]\n              h = h + self.sinusoidal_positional_encoding(L, self.d_model)[None, :, :]\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              h = DSConvBlock(\n                  d_model=self.d_model,\n                  kernel_size=self.kernel_size,\n                  dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n                  dilation=self.dilations[i % len(self.dilations)],\n                  se_ratio=self.se_ratio\n       \
    \       )(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          mean_pool = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n          attn_pool = MultiHeadAttnPoolTemp(self.d_model, num_heads=self.attn_heads, tau=self.attn_temp)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          pooled = jnp.concatenate([mean_pool, attn_pool], axis=-1)\n\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(pooled)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n          if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n              return logits.squeeze(-1)\n          return logits\n\n  class NetWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.net = RNANetDilatedTemp(**kwargs)\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, drop_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          vars = self.net.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': drop_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        \
    \  return vars['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          if rng_key is None:\n              rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n          return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 4,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'attn_heads': 4,\n          'dilations': (1, 2, 4, 8),\n          'se_ratio': 0.0,\n          'attn_temp': 0.7,\n          'positional_encoding': True\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      d_output = hparams.get('d_output', 1)\n      task_type = hparams.get('task_type', 'regression')\n      return NetWrapper(\n          d_input=4,\n          d_output=d_output,\n          task_type=task_type,\n\
    \          d_model=hparams.get('d_model', 256),\n          num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks', 4),\n          kernel_size=hparams.get('kernel_size', 7),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n          attn_heads=hparams.get('attn_heads', 4),\n          dilations=tuple(hparams.get('dilations', (1, 2, 4, 8))),\n          se_ratio=hparams.get('se_ratio', 0.0),\n          attn_temp=hparams.get('attn_temp', 0.7),\n          positional_encoding=hparams.get('positional_encoding', True)\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply\
    \ 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 29 update — Reduced dropout hurt (0.6370), confirming 0.1 is safer. SOTA unchanged (0.6622). Queued temperature-scaled attention (tau=0.7) to sharpen pooling; dual-dilation interaction is running. If no gains, I’ll finalize the analysis draft and submit once Archive opens at maturity.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Exploring architecture ideas**\n\nI’m thinking about architecture—it's important to keep everything unified across datasets. Mixing pooling is fine, but unity is key. \n\nI could explore a dilation schedule to avoid doubling leaps, and consider permutation-equivariant gating to enhance dynamics while keeping everything consistent. \n\nECA might replace SE; it seems like it could be more effective. \n\nAlso, I need to think about LayerNorm placement and possibly add a global token. \n\nCalibrating the MHA pooling features with temperature scaling is interesting too! This could be an intriguing path to pursue.**Assessing potential improvements**\n\nI’m considering some strategies to enhance the performance of CRI-Off and stabilize forensics. \n\nFirst, I might try using sigmoid gating to merge mean and MHA pooling, since the previous gating underperformed. I'm also thinking about exploring multi-kernel convolution mixing and larger kernel sizes; maybe switching to a kernel\
  \ size of 5 could improve CRI. \n\nThere's potential in testing repeated last block dilation with various sizes too. \n\nAlso, I want to keep experimenting with token usage and ensure I store the best code snapshot for future reference!**Planning reflection and actions**\n\nI'm thinking about allocating a reflection slot in the Reflection Chamber. It exists, but it might not be necessary to write down thoughts. \n\nNext, I have an action plan: I’ll submit a run with kernel size set to 5 for the state-of-the-art (SOTA) base. Then, I want to modify the dilation schedule to use (1, 3, 5, 7) while keeping the pooling concatenation. \n\nThere's also the plan to incorporate temperature scaling into the pooling, changing the module in the storage file to handle a new parameter for attention weights. This needs careful handling based on earlier debugging notes!**Deciding on submissions**\n\nI’m considering coding the submission with a specialized pooling class internally, rather than relying on\
  \ the storage system to keep things from interfering with others. \n\nI propose two new runs: one with a kernel size of 5 for the SOTA model called \"Dilated DSConv + Concat MHA,\" and another incorporating an attention temperature of tau=0.7 using MultiHeadAttnPoolTemp. \n\nSince I can only submit two pending runs at a time, and there’s already a run pending, I should prioritize the attention temperature first since it’s a novel approach that could enhance CRI-Off by refining the attention weights!**Preparing to boost ncRNA**\n\nI’m thinking about how to enhance ncRNA, and it seems like a 4-head Multi-Head Attention (MHA) setup with a temperature of 0.7 might help. I need to use the allowed functions to create a network, embedding the code to replicate the base network with the temperature parameter.\n\nI’ll go ahead and prepare 'Dilated DSConv + Concat MHA (temp=0.7)' and log everything in private memory. While I’m at it, I might add a small reflection, even if it’s not strictly necessary.\n\
  \nNext steps: go to research, submit the new run with the embedded code, and log my findings. I need to import the necessary libraries, and provide the DSConvBlock and MultiHeadAttnPoolTemp with the temperature parameter. I’ll stick to the specified settings, ensuring adherence to training restrictions!"
