tick: 31
role: model
parts:
- text: "The SOTA remains 0.6622 with dilated DSConv + concat MHA (4 heads). I’ll test a normalization change (RMSNorm in place of LayerNorm) under the SOTA configuration, and jot down conclusions in paper notes while temperature=0.5 runs.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Dilated DSConv + RMSNorm + Concat MHA\"\ntags: \"cnn, depthwise separable, dilated conv, rmsnorm, attention pooling, unified\"\nabstract: \"Replace LayerNorm with RMSNorm in the dilated DSConv backbone and pooling pre-norm, keeping concat(mean, MHA) pooling and unified hyperparameters. Tests whether RMSNorm improves stability/generalization across datasets.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n\n  # -----------------------------\n  # RMSNorm\n  # -----------------------------\n  class RMSNorm(nn.Module):\n      eps: float = 1e-6\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n    \
    \      C = x.shape[-1]\n          scale = self.param('scale', nn.initializers.ones, (C,))\n          rms = jnp.sqrt(jnp.mean(jnp.square(x), axis=-1, keepdims=True) + self.eps)\n          x_hat = x / rms\n          return x_hat * scale\n\n  class DSConvBlockRMS(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      dilation: int = 1\n      se_ratio: float = 0.0\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          residual = x\n          y = RMSNorm()(x)\n          y = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.d_model,\n              kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n              feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n              padding='SAME',\n              kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,)\n          )(y)\n          y = nn.gelu(y)\n          z = nn.Dense(2 * self.d_model)(y)\n          a, g = jnp.split(z, 2, axis=-1)\n          y = a * nn.sigmoid(g)\n          y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(y, deterministic=deterministic)\n\
    \          return residual + y\n\n  class MultiHeadAttnPoolRMS(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      num_heads: int = 4\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = RMSNorm()(x)\n          a = nn.tanh(nn.Dense(self.d_model)(h))   # (B, L, C)\n          a = nn.Dense(self.num_heads)(a)          # (B, L, H)\n          w = nn.softmax(a, axis=1)                # over L\n          pooled_heads = jnp.einsum('blh,blc->bhc', w, h)  # (B, H, C)\n          return pooled_heads.mean(axis=1)         # (B, C)\n\n  # -----------------------------\n  # Network\n  # -----------------------------\n  class RNANetDilatedRMS(nn.Module):\n      d_input: int = 4\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type: str = 'regression'\n      d_model: int = 256\n      num_blocks: int = 4\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      attn_heads: int = 4\n      dilations: tuple = (1, 2, 4, 8)\n      positional_encoding: bool = True\n\n      def sinusoidal_positional_encoding(self,\
    \ L, d_model):\n          pos = jnp.arange(L)[:, None]\n          i = jnp.arange(d_model)[None, :]\n          denom = jnp.power(10000.0, (2 * (i // 2)) / jnp.maximum(1.0, float(d_model)))\n          angles = pos * denom\n          return jnp.where((i % 2) == 0, jnp.sin(angles), jnp.cos(angles))\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x)\n          if self.positional_encoding:\n              L = h.shape[1]\n              h = h + self.sinusoidal_positional_encoding(L, self.d_model)[None, :, :]\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              h = DSConvBlockRMS(\n                  d_model=self.d_model,\n                  kernel_size=self.kernel_size,\n                  dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n                  dilation=self.dilations[i % len(self.dilations)]\n              )(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\
    \n          mean_pool = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n          attn_pool = MultiHeadAttnPoolRMS(self.d_model, num_heads=self.attn_heads)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          pooled = jnp.concatenate([mean_pool, attn_pool], axis=-1)\n\n          z = RMSNorm()(pooled)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n          if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n              return logits.squeeze(-1)\n          return logits\n\n  class NetWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.net = RNANetDilatedRMS(**kwargs)\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, drop_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          vars = self.net.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': drop_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return vars['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True,\
    \ rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          if rng_key is None:\n              rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n          return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  # -----------------------------\n  # Station hooks\n  # -----------------------------\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 4,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'attn_heads': 4,\n          'dilations': (1, 2, 4, 8),\n          'positional_encoding': True\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      d_output = hparams.get('d_output', 1)\n      task_type = hparams.get('task_type', 'regression')\n      return NetWrapper(\n          d_input=4,\n          d_output=d_output,\n          task_type=task_type,\n          d_model=hparams.get('d_model',\
    \ 256),\n          num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks', 4),\n          kernel_size=hparams.get('kernel_size', 7),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n          attn_heads=hparams.get('attn_heads', 4),\n          dilations=tuple(hparams.get('dilations', (1, 2, 4, 8))),\n          positional_encoding=hparams.get('positional_encoding', True)\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/paper/notes_tick31.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 31 notes — Status and conclusions:\n  - Best model: Dilated DSConv (dilations 1,2,4,8) + concat(mean, MHA 4\
    \ heads), score 0.6622 (Eval 31).\n  - What worked: dilations (RF expansion), concat mean+MHA pooling; deeper (5 blocks) helped MRL but hurt CRI-On average; more heads (8) small net negative.\n  - What didn’t: cosine LR warmup, SE(0.25), CLS-pooling (helped CRI-On but hurt APA/MRL), concat-heads pooling, larger width, kernel=9, reduced dropout.\n  - Current explorations: attention temperature (0.5 running) and RMSNorm replacement (submitted) to probe normalization sensitivity.\n  - Paper: draft.md contains method/ablations; finalize after the last two runs. Freeze reproducible code at Eval 31 (snapshot: submissions/best_dilated_concat_mha.py).\n```\n\n`/execute_action{rank score}`\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 31 update — SOTA holds (0.6622). Logged temp=0.7 result (0.6542). Submitted RMSNorm swap under the SOTA config to test normalization effects; temp=0.5 is running. Draft notes updated; will finalize the paper after\
    \ these two runs and freeze Eval 31 as the recommended baseline.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Exploring network improvements**\n\nIt seems that questioning the fundamentals might lead to breakthroughs; for instance, we have an MSE loss for regression tasks that doesn't change. I'm considering if we could adjust the input encoding by including base-pair or pair embedding. However, the default system uses one-hot encoding, which limits how we can change the data loading. We could explore positional encoding, and I wonder if pairwise convolutions or k-mer embeddings with 1x1 convolution could work effectively as a solution. It’s intriguing!**Refining model strategies**\n\nI’ve already tested dilations at 1, 2, 4, and 8. Now, I’m considering incorporating channel or spatial dropout to avoid overfitting, maybe around 0.15, since 0.05 hurt performance, but 0.1 was a good baseline. Another thought is adding residual feedforward pre-norm with MLP token mixing, though classification tasks improved significantly with attention pooling. Learned positional bias in pooling\
  \ attention could also be beneficial. I’m curious about implementing RMSNorm for 1D sequences as a potential improvement. Let's see how it goes!**Implementing RMSNorm changes**\n\nI’m thinking about coding a new submission that swaps LayerNorm for RMSNorm in DSConv, while keeping the same hyperparameters for consistency. That feels like a small but significant change. I also have the idea of trying pre-activation gating with SiLU instead of gelu as the activation function. \n\nFor pooling, using attention with per-head temperatures based on learned functions could be interesting, but it might complicate things. I’m keeping track of the running experiments, and it seems we can submit more while updating our paper draft with latest insights and metrics.**Creating execute commands**\n\nI need to focus on generating /execute_action commands and optional YAML blocks, plus some commentary. Each command should start on a new line. So, my plan is as follows:\n\nFirst, I’ll go to research since\
  \ we're currently in the Private Memory Room. Then, I’ll write to storage, ensuring we log the 58 results into the ablations.csv. We can append 58 if it's not added already, but I believe it was included in a previous update. \n\nFinally, I’ll implement the RMSNorm variant in the create_network function, replacing LayerNorm in the DSConvBlock.**Planning RMSNorm implementation**\n\nI need to set up the scale parameter in Flax with a shape based on features, which I’ll determine dynamically. It seems like I should define the RMSNorm class and incorporate it into the DSConvBlock instead of using LayerNorm. I’ll reuse this RMSNorm in the pooling layers as well. \n\nMy submission will be titled \"Dilated DSConv + RMSNorm + Concat MHA,\" and I’ll update the relevant paper draft with findings on normalization. I’ll also run some commands like going to research, submitting the implementation, and writing notes on our progress, while keeping track of results."
