    \n```\n### Message 3\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nDo not give up on an approach too easily. Implementation details are often the key—tweaking hyperparameters and other specifics may be enough to make an existing method work effectively.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n3. `storage write noema/paper/notes_tick31.md` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n4. `rank score` (in Research Counter);\n5. `goto private_memory` (in Research Counter);\n6. `reply 1` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'Dilated DSConv + RMSNorm + Concat MHA' submitted for Research Task #1: Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling. Evaluation ID: 65.\n- File created successfully: noema/paper/notes_tick31.md\n\
    - Evaluations now sorted by score.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 65 | 1 | Dilated DSConv + RMSNorm + Concat MHA | Noema I | 31 |\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | APA_R2 | CRI-Off_Spearman | CRI-On_Spearman | MRL_R2 | Modif_AUC-ROC | PRS_R2 | ncRNA_Accuracy |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 31 | 1 | Dilated DSConv (1,2,4,8) + Concat MHA Pooling | Noema I | 19 | 0.6622 | 0.8367 | 0.0858 | 0.5176 | 0.8288 | 0.9514 | 0.5611 | 0.8538 |\n| 34 | 1 | Dilated DSConv (1,2,4,8) + Concat MHA Pooling (8 heads) | Noema I | 20 | 0.6611 | 0.8330 | 0.0775 | 0.5072 | 0.8425 | 0.9508 | 0.5644 | 0.8523 |\n| 43 | 1 | Dilated DSConv + Concat MHA (5 blocks: 1,2,4,8,16) | Noema I | 23\
    \ | 0.6590 | 0.8464 | 0.0823 | 0.4456 | 0.8575 | 0.9515 | 0.5667 | 0.8631 |\n| 37 | 1 | Dilated DSConv (1,2,4,8) + Concat Mean+Max+MHA Pooling | Noema I | 21 | 0.6567 | 0.8451 | 0.0661 | 0.4756 | 0.8247 | 0.9505 | 0.5550 | 0.8800 |\n| 60 | 1 | Dilated DSConv + Concat MHA (attn_temp=0.5) | Noema I | 30 | 0.6566 | 0.8393 | 0.0741 | 0.4714 | 0.8572 | 0.9515 | 0.5704 | 0.8323 |\n| 38 | 1 | Dilated DSConv + Concat MHA (d_model=320) | Noema I | 22 | 0.6550 | 0.8396 | 0.0786 | 0.4592 | 0.8256 | 0.9517 | 0.5685 | 0.8615 |\n| 47 | 1 | Dilated DSConv + Concat Heads MHA Pooling (4 heads) | Noema I | 25 | 0.6545 | 0.8398 | 0.0614 | 0.4634 | 0.8373 | 0.9509 | 0.5675 | 0.8615 |\n| 58 | 1 | Dilated DSConv + Concat MHA (attn_temp=0.7) | Noema I | 29 | 0.6542 | 0.8414 | 0.0771 | 0.4615 | 0.8188 | 0.9510 | 0.5710 | 0.8585 |\n| 48 | 1 | Dilated DSConv + CLS Attention Pooling (concat mean + cls) | Noema I | 26 | 0.6535 | 0.8278 | 0.0637 | 0.5200 | 0.8236 | 0.9497 | 0.5696 | 0.8200 |\n| 45 | 1 | Dilated\
    \ DSConv + Concat MHA (kernel_size=9) | Noema I | 24 | 0.6502 | 0.8407 | 0.0757 | 0.4563 | 0.8170 | 0.9511 | 0.5659 | 0.8446 |\n\nPage 1 of 3 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-3, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Replied to capsule #1. Your message ID is Noema_private_1-20.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 1 | Noema I — Initial Results and Plan (Tick 10) | Noema I | Tick 10 | 1455 | 20 | (All Read) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n\
    - Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
