tick: 34
role: model
parts:
- text: "Incredible breakthrough: removing positional encoding set a new SOTA at 0.6686 (Eval 66), with large gains on MRL and ncRNA. I’ll snapshot the new best, log results, and probe two unified variants: no-PE with sharper attention and no-PE with 5 blocks.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/ablations.csv}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  eval_id,title,score,APA_R2,CRI-Off_Spearman,CRI-On_Spearman,MRL_R2,Modif_AUC-ROC,PRS_R2,ncRNA_Accuracy\n  66,Dilated DSConv + Concat MHA (no positional encoding),0.6686,0.8615,0.0357,0.4620,0.8918,0.9485,0.5655,0.9154\n  31,Dilated DSConv (1,2,4,8) + Concat MHA Pooling,0.6622,0.8367,0.0858,0.5176,0.8288,0.9514,0.5611,0.8538\n  34,Dilated DSConv (1,2,4,8) + Concat MHA Pooling (8 heads),0.6611,0.8330,0.0775,0.5072,0.8425,0.9508,0.5644,0.8523\n  65,Dilated DSConv + RMSNorm + Concat MHA,0.6596,0.8396,0.0848,0.4979,0.8213,0.9527,0.5639,0.8569\n  43,Dilated DSConv + Concat MHA (5 blocks: 1,2,4,8,16),0.6590,0.8464,0.0823,0.4456,0.8575,0.9515,0.5667,0.8631\n\
    \  37,Dilated DSConv (1,2,4,8) + Concat Mean+Max+MHA Pooling,0.6567,0.8451,0.0661,0.4756,0.8247,0.9505,0.5550,0.8800\n  60,Dilated DSConv + Concat MHA (attn_temp=0.5),0.6566,0.8393,0.0741,0.4714,0.8572,0.9515,0.5704,0.8323\n  38,Dilated DSConv + Concat MHA (d_model=320),0.6550,0.8396,0.0786,0.4592,0.8256,0.9517,0.5685,0.8615\n  47,Dilated DSConv + Concat Heads MHA Pooling (4 heads),0.6545,0.8398,0.0614,0.4634,0.8373,0.9509,0.5675,0.8615\n  58,Dilated DSConv + Concat MHA (attn_temp=0.7),0.6542,0.8414,0.0771,0.4615,0.8188,0.9510,0.5710,0.8585\n  48,Dilated DSConv + CLS Attention Pooling (concat mean + cls),0.6535,0.8278,0.0637,0.5200,0.8236,0.9497,0.5696,0.8200\n  54,Dilated DSConv + Dual-Dilation Interaction + Concat MHA,0.6487,0.8081,0.0751,0.4710,0.8291,0.9512,0.5681,0.8385\n  45,Dilated DSConv + Concat MHA (kernel_size=9),0.6502,0.8407,0.0757,0.4563,0.8170,0.9511,0.5659,0.8446\n  52,Dilated DSConv + Concat MHA (dropout=0.05),0.6370,0.8317,0.0685,0.4429,0.7699,0.9512,0.5611,0.8338\n\
    \  24,Dilated DSConv (1,2,4,8) + Concat Mean+Attention Pooling,0.6477,0.8458,0.0803,0.4381,0.8250,0.9519,0.5650,0.8277\n  17,Dilated DSConv (1,2,4,8) with Mean Pooling,0.6365,0.8465,0.0663,0.4880,0.8134,0.9525,0.5735,0.7154\n  13,Kernel Sweep: k=11 with Mean Pooling (DSConv),0.6311,0.8587,0.0651,0.4753,0.7377,0.9521,0.5734,0.7554\n  20,Concat Mean+Attention Pooling (k=11 DSConv),0.6255,0.8365,0.0769,0.4690,0.6479,0.9509,0.5639,0.8338\n  8,Ablation: Mean Pooling (no attention),0.6190,0.8565,0.0605,0.5288,0.6807,0.9520,0.5654,0.6892\n  22,Inception DSConv (k=5,9,15) with Mean Pooling,0.6180,0.8442,0.0675,0.4827,0.7305,0.9513,0.5701,0.6800\n  27,Dilated DSConv + Mean Pooling + Cosine LR Warmup,0.6063,0.8325,0.0775,0.4417,0.6303,0.9509,0.5699,0.7415\n  12,Gated Mean–Attention Pooling (DSConv),0.6018,0.8584,0.0618,0.4625,0.6698,0.9518,0.5726,0.6354\n  2,Depthwise CNN with Attention Pooling for RNA,0.5917,0.7550,0.0284,0.5150,0.6883,0.7255,0.5637,0.8662\n  16,SE(0.25) + k=11 with Mean Pooling\
    \ (DSConv),0.5866,0.8435,0.0585,0.4711,0.6491,0.9523,0.5699,0.5615\n  9,Ablation: No Depthwise Convs (MLP + attention pooling),0.4935,0.7424,0.0508,0.4230,0.0579,0.9416,0.5139,0.7246\n  1,Vanilla MLP Baseline,0.2401,0.3258,0.0336,0.3232,0.0402,0.6377,0.1324,0.1877\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/best_nope_dilated_concat_mha.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Snapshot of best method (Eval 66): Dilated DSConv + Concat MHA, no positional encoding\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema')\n  from models.dsconv_mix import build_network_v2\n  import optax\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 4,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'pooling': 'concat_mha',\n          'attn_heads': 4,\n          'block_type': 'dilated',\n          'dilations': (1, 2, 4, 8),\n          'se_ratio': 0.0,\n          'positional_encoding': False\n  \
    \    }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      d_output = hparams.get('d_output', 1)\n      task_type = hparams.get('task_type', 'regression')\n      return build_network_v2(d_output, task_type, hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[BEST-66 SNAPSHOT] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"No-PE + Concat MHA (attn_temp=0.5)\"\ntags: \"cnn, depthwise separable, dilated conv, attention temperature, no positional encoding\"\nabstract: \"Best no-PE architecture with sharper attention (tau=0.5) to see if CRISPR metrics can lift without harming MRL/ncRNA gains.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy\
    \ as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model:int; kernel_size:int; dropout_rate:float; dilation:int=1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          residual = x\n          y = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                      feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(y)\n          y = nn.gelu(y)\n          z = nn.Dense(2*self.d_model)(y)\n          a,g = jnp.split(z,2,axis=-1)\n          y = a * nn.sigmoid(g)\n          y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(y, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return residual + y\n\n  class AttnPoolTemp(nn.Module):\n      d_model:int; heads:int=4; tau:float=0.5\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          logits = nn.tanh(nn.Dense(self.d_model)(h))\n\
    \          logits = nn.Dense(self.heads)(logits)\n          w = nn.softmax(logits / self.tau, axis=1)\n          pooled_heads = jnp.einsum('blh,blc->bhc', w, h)\n          return pooled_heads.mean(axis=1)\n\n  class Net(nn.Module):\n      d_output:int; task_type:str; d_model:int=256; blocks:int=4; k:int=7; dropout:float=0.1\n      heads:int=4; dilations:tuple=(1,2,4,8)\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x)   # no positional encoding\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          for i in range(self.blocks):\n              h = DSConvBlock(self.d_model, self.k, self.dropout, self.dilations[i%len(self.dilations)])(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          mean = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n          attn = AttnPoolTemp(self.d_model, heads=self.heads, tau=0.5)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          z = jnp.concatenate([mean, attn], axis=-1)\n          z\
    \ = nn.LayerNorm()(z)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z); z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          return logits.squeeze(-1) if (self.task_type=='regression' and self.d_output==1) else logits\n\n  class Wrap:\n      def __init__(self, **kw): self.net = Net(**kw)\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy): \n          pk, dk = random.split(rng_key); vars = self.net.init({'params':pk,'dropout':dk}, dummy, deterministic=True); return vars['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic: return self.net.apply({'params':params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          if rng_key is None: rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n          return self.net.apply({'params':params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout':rng_key})\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {'learning_rate':0.001,'d_model':256,'num_blocks':4,'kernel_size':7,'dropout_rate':0.1,\n\
    \              'attn_heads':4,'dilations':(1,2,4,8)}\n\n  def create_network(hp):\n      return Wrap(d_output=hp.get('d_output',1), task_type=hp.get('task_type','regression'),\n                  d_model=hp.get('d_model',256), blocks=hp.get('num_blocks',4), k=hp.get('kernel_size',7),\n                  dropout=hp.get('dropout_rate',0.1), heads=hp.get('attn_heads',4),\n                  dilations=tuple(hp.get('dilations',(1,2,4,8))))\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01))\n\n  BASE_SEED=42; BATCH_SIZE=64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"No-PE + Concat MHA (5 blocks: 1,2,4,8,16)\"\ntags: \"cnn, depthwise separable, dilated conv, no positional encoding, depth\"\nabstract: \"Extend no-PE\
    \ SOTA to 5 blocks with dilations (1,2,4,8,16) to test if larger receptive field further improves MRL/ncRNA without tanking CRISPR.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema')\n\n  from models.dsconv_mix import build_network_v2\n  import optax\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'pooling': 'concat_mha',\n          'attn_heads': 4,\n          'block_type': 'dilated',\n          'dilations': (1, 2, 4, 8, 16),\n          'se_ratio': 0.0,\n          'positional_encoding': False\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      d_output = hparams.get('d_output', 1)\n      task_type = hparams.get('task_type', 'regression')\n      return build_network_v2(d_output, task_type, hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\
    \ optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01))\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/paper/draft.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Title: Unified Dilated Depthwise CNNs with Concat Multi-Head Attention Pooling for Multi-Dataset RNA Modeling\n\n  Abstract (updated with new SOTA):\n  We propose a unified sequence model for seven RNA tasks. A depthwise-separable CNN with dilations (1,2,4,8) and concat(mean, multi-head attention) pooling achieves a new state-of-the-art average validation score of 0.6686 when positional encoding is removed. Ablations reveal: (i) dilations are critical (MRL/CRISPR), (ii) mean pooling helps APA/Modif while attention helps ncRNA/CRISPR, (iii) concatenating mean with attention best balances tasks, and (iv) absolute sinusoidal positional encoding can harm performance\
    \ in convolutional backbones for these RNA tasks.\n\n  Best results:\n  - No-PE (Eval 66): 0.6686 | APA 0.8615 | CRI-Off 0.0357 | CRI-On 0.4620 | PRS 0.5655 | MRL 0.8918 | Modif 0.9485 | ncRNA 0.9154.\n  - With PE (Eval 31): 0.6622 | APA 0.8367 | CRI-Off 0.0858 | CRI-On 0.5176 | PRS 0.5611 | MRL 0.8288 | Modif 0.9514 | ncRNA 0.8538.\n  Trade-off: removing PE improves APA/MRL/ncRNA substantially but lowers CRI-Off/CRI-On. However, the aggregate improves.\n\n  Repro snapshot:\n  - storage/noema/submissions/best_nope_dilated_concat_mha.py (Eval 66)\n\n  Implementation & training:\n  - Depthwise-separable conv blocks (kernel 7), GLU pointwise; dilations (1,2,4,8); concat(mean, MHA-4) pooling; AdamW lr 1e-3, wd 0.01, batch 64, early stopping.\n  - Losses fixed by system (MSE, CE, BCE).\n\n  Ablations (highlights):\n  - +8 heads, +depth=5, RMSNorm, attention temperature, CLS pooling, mean+max, width=320, kernel=9, cosine warmup, SE: none surpassed no-PE or best with PE.\n\n  Future work:\n\
    \  - Unified, mismatch-aware interactions to lift CRI-Off without reintroducing harmful absolute PE.\n  - Relative position or learned offset schemes compatible with conv invariances.\n  - Calibration/uncertainty analyses under fixed-loss constraints.\n\n  Full table: storage/noema/results/ablations.csv\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 34 update — New SOTA: 0.6686 by removing positional encoding (Eval 66). Huge gains on MRL (0.8918) and ncRNA (0.9154), small drops on CRISPR metrics (esp. CRI-Off 0.0357). Snapshot saved at storage/noema/submissions/best_nope_dilated_concat_mha.py. Logged results and updated draft with new SOTA and trade-offs. Queued two unified variants on no-PE: (i) attention temperature 0.5, (ii) depth=5 (1,2,4,8,16). If they don’t surpass, I’ll finalize the paper with Eval 66 as the recommended baseline.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Planning next steps**


  I need to outline our next actions. The latest evaluation without positional encoding scored 0.6686, which is a clear improvement over the previous record of 0.6622. Metrics show significant improvements in several areas, like MRL and ncRNA. This suggests that removing positional encoding has positive implications. I’ll log this finding, update the ablations CSV and paper draft, and save the best code for reproducibility. We might also explore partial positional encoding, but we need to maintain a unified approach. Given the improved score, finalizing our proposal seems reasonable.**Exploring fixes and publishing**


  I’m considering a unified approach for a small CRI-Off-focused fix, maybe adding Gaussian noise augmentation or dropout before pooling. The training system is fixed, but I can adjust the architecture for pairwise gating. However, past attempts have often degraded performance. The best result has been achieved without positional encoding. I want to prepare for publication before reaching 50 ticks, which means I should freeze our findings at 34 ticks and update the best snapshot reflecting the latest evaluation without positional encoding.**Creating new snapshots and experiments**


  I’m updating the previous snapshot ''best_dilated_concat_mha.py'', which used positional encoding, to a new one called ''best_nope_dilated_concat_mha.py'', now with positional_encoding set to False. I need to ensure that ''build_network_v2'' reads the positional encoding flag correctly, and it does! I’ll log a summary and update the paper draft and abstract to reflect this latest improvement. Then, I might run two experiments: ''no PE with attn temp = 0.5'' and ''no PE with mean pooling ablation'' to see if they help CRI-Off.**Addressing CRI-Off regression**


  Right now, CRI-Off is quite low at 0.0357, compared to 0.0858 when using positional encoding, indicating a regression that might suggest that positional encoding aids CRI-Off. Even though the aggregated results improved, I wonder if we can recover some CRI-Off by using a hybrid approach, like gating input coordinates. That might reintroduce positional bias. I could explore techniques like "positional dropout" or a low-amplitude sinusoidal addition with a small learned scale, ensuring we keep the architecture consistent. I need to test "positional_encoding" with a learned scale parameter, ''pe_scale,'' and create a new model that respects this while ensuring the training framework uses allowed functions.**Planning experiments and updates**


  I’m considering using a tiny PE scale to recover CRI-Off while maintaining robustness. Alternatively, options like "relative shift" or "learned offset conv" could unify things, though they''re more complex. I think it''s best to log the new SOTA, create a snapshot, and update the paper. I’ll add a new row for eval 66 in the results CSV, save the submission file without positional encoding, and submit two runs: ''no PE + attn_temp=0.5'' and ''no PE with depth 5''. Following this, I''ll update the paper draft with the new SOTA details.'
