thinking_content: "**Considering model architectures**\n\nI'm thinking about how to enhance our understanding of CRI-Off, which relates to Spearman correlation of sgRNA-target off-target data. It's interesting that CRI-Off could benefit from capturing segment interactions, but I wonder if the network struggles with pairwise interactions. Implementing cross-correlation or a CMA might help. Still, designing a general \"pairwise local interaction\" layer sounds promising, as it could apply across datasets without causing issues. However, I'm cautious about the overhead with new trials, especially since we're already at 35 ticks.**Exploring pooling strategies**\n\nI'm considering proposing a run with \"relative shift attention pooling\" that adds pairwise difference features along with \"two-headed pooling,\" which involves MHA with tau and top-k gating. Surprisingly, we've achieved a new state-of-the-art score of 0.6686! Next, I should log the ablations for good practice. The user might expect\
  \ this. I'm thinking of replicating the no-PE run with seed sweeps, but since the base seed is fixed at 42, I wonder if switching to 123 could help with stability while keeping the current datasets in mind.**Planning next steps with modifications**\n\nI'm aware that heavy modifications can sometimes lead to degradation. First, I think I should store a snapshot, update the paper, and note that when things mature, we’ll deposit it to the Archive. I also want to ensure the code produces the best run for reproducibility, and I've saved \"best_nope_dilated_concat_mha.py,\" which is great! \n\nNow, I can propose testing 'attn temp 0.9 or 1.2' since 0.5 improved the score a bit. I'm looking forward to seeing results from our queued tests. Maybe I can record insights in the Reflection Chamber later.**Planning evaluations and testing**\n\nI'm thinking of testing \"groupnorm vs layernorm\" with no-PE since previously, RMSNorm nearly matched with PE but didn't exceed it. Should I test RMSNorm without\
  \ PE? Maybe, but I'm cautious about token time. I could add a small dropout of 0.05, but we got poor results with reduced dropout using PE. It might differ with no-PE, so I prefer to avoid additional runs until current tests finish. My next actions are to rank the scoreboard and record results afterward, while also proposing an update to the draft with the new SOTA no-PE.**Reviewing evaluations and actions**\n\nI need to check evaluations 68 or 69, but I realize that reviewing requires an 'evaluation_id' which hasn't been introduced yet. To retrieve logs, I can use the commands '/execute_action{review 68}' and '/execute_action{review 69}'. Once I check if they’re finished, I’ll log the results and update the ablations accordingly. If they're still running, I’ll have to wait. I’ll also rank the scores again and update private memory. \n\nHere’s the streamlined list of actions:\n\n- /execute_action{goto research}\n- /execute_action{review 68}\n- /execute_action{review 69}\n- /execute_action{rank\
  \ score}"
