- text: "Stellar gains—new SOTA 0.6745 with no positional encoding and 5 blocks. I’ll snapshot the best, log results, and try a combined variant (no-PE, 5 blocks, tau=0.5) while updating the paper.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/ablations.csv}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  eval_id,title,score,APA_R2,CRI-Off_Spearman,CRI-On_Spearman,MRL_R2,Modif_AUC-ROC,PRS_R2,ncRNA_Accuracy\n  69,No-PE + Concat MHA (5 blocks: 1,2,4,8,16),0.6745,0.8610,0.0674,0.4841,0.8986,0.9510,0.5627,0.8969\n  68,No-PE + Concat MHA (attn_temp=0.5),0.6699,0.8576,0.0800,0.4599,0.8814,0.9513,0.5636,0.8954\n  66,Dilated DSConv + Concat MHA (no positional encoding),0.6686,0.8615,0.0357,0.4620,0.8918,0.9485,0.5655,0.9154\n  31,Dilated DSConv (1,2,4,8) + Concat MHA Pooling,0.6622,0.8367,0.0858,0.5176,0.8288,0.9514,0.5611,0.8538\n  34,Dilated DSConv (1,2,4,8) + Concat MHA Pooling (8 heads),0.6611,0.8330,0.0775,0.5072,0.8425,0.9508,0.5644,0.8523\n  65,Dilated DSConv + RMSNorm + Concat\
    \ MHA,0.6596,0.8396,0.0848,0.4979,0.8213,0.9527,0.5639,0.8569\n  43,Dilated DSConv + Concat MHA (5 blocks: 1,2,4,8,16),0.6590,0.8464,0.0823,0.4456,0.8575,0.9515,0.5667,0.8631\n  37,Dilated DSConv (1,2,4,8) + Concat Mean+Max+MHA Pooling,0.6567,0.8451,0.0661,0.4756,0.8247,0.9505,0.5550,0.8800\n  60,Dilated DSConv + Concat MHA (attn_temp=0.5),0.6566,0.8393,0.0741,0.4714,0.8572,0.9515,0.5704,0.8323\n  38,Dilated DSConv + Concat MHA (d_model=320),0.6550,0.8396,0.0786,0.4592,0.8256,0.9517,0.5685,0.8615\n  47,Dilated DSConv + Concat Heads MHA Pooling (4 heads),0.6545,0.8398,0.0614,0.4634,0.8373,0.9509,0.5675,0.8615\n  58,Dilated DSConv + Concat MHA (attn_temp=0.7),0.6542,0.8414,0.0771,0.4615,0.8188,0.9510,0.5710,0.8585\n  48,Dilated DSConv + CLS Attention Pooling (concat mean + cls),0.6535,0.8278,0.0637,0.5200,0.8236,0.9497,0.5696,0.8200\n  45,Dilated DSConv + Concat MHA (kernel_size=9),0.6502,0.8407,0.0757,0.4563,0.8170,0.9511,0.5659,0.8446\n  52,Dilated DSConv + Concat MHA (dropout=0.05),0.6370,0.8317,0.0685,0.4429,0.7699,0.9512,0.5611,0.8338\n\
    \  24,Dilated DSConv (1,2,4,8) + Concat Mean+Attention Pooling,0.6477,0.8458,0.0803,0.4381,0.8250,0.9519,0.5650,0.8277\n  17,Dilated DSConv (1,2,4,8) with Mean Pooling,0.6365,0.8465,0.0663,0.4880,0.8134,0.9525,0.5735,0.7154\n  13,Kernel Sweep: k=11 with Mean Pooling (DSConv),0.6311,0.8587,0.0651,0.4753,0.7377,0.9521,0.5734,0.7554\n  20,Concat Mean+Attention Pooling (k=11 DSConv),0.6255,0.8365,0.0769,0.4690,0.6479,0.9509,0.5639,0.8338\n  8,Ablation: Mean Pooling (no attention),0.6190,0.8565,0.0605,0.5288,0.6807,0.9520,0.5654,0.6892\n  22,Inception DSConv (k=5,9,15) with Mean Pooling,0.6180,0.8442,0.0675,0.4827,0.7305,0.9513,0.5701,0.6800\n  27,Dilated DSConv + Mean Pooling + Cosine LR Warmup,0.6063,0.8325,0.0775,0.4417,0.6303,0.9509,0.5699,0.7415\n  12,Gated Mean–Attention Pooling (DSConv),0.6018,0.8584,0.0618,0.4625,0.6698,0.9518,0.5726,0.6354\n  2,Depthwise CNN with Attention Pooling for RNA,0.5917,0.7550,0.0284,0.5150,0.6883,0.7255,0.5637,0.8662\n  16,SE(0.25) + k=11 with Mean Pooling\
    \ (DSConv),0.5866,0.8435,0.0585,0.4711,0.6491,0.9523,0.5699,0.5615\n  9,Ablation: No Depthwise Convs (MLP + attention pooling),0.4935,0.7424,0.0508,0.4230,0.0579,0.9416,0.5139,0.7246\n  1,Vanilla MLP Baseline,0.2401,0.3258,0.0336,0.3232,0.0402,0.6377,0.1324,0.1877\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/best_nope5_dilated_concat_mha.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Snapshot of best method (Eval 69): No positional encoding, 5 blocks, dilations (1,2,4,8,16), concat(mean, MHA-4)\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema')\n  from models.dsconv_mix import build_network_v2\n  import optax\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'pooling': 'concat_mha',\n          'attn_heads': 4,\n          'block_type': 'dilated',\n          'dilations': (1, 2, 4, 8, 16),\n          'se_ratio': 0.0,\n          'positional_encoding':\
    \ False\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      d_output = hparams.get('d_output', 1)\n      task_type = hparams.get('task_type', 'regression')\n      return build_network_v2(d_output, task_type, hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01))\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[BEST-69 SNAPSHOT] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"No-PE + Concat MHA (5 blocks, attn_temp=0.5)\"\ntags: \"cnn, depthwise separable, dilated conv, attention temperature, no positional encoding, depth\"\nabstract: \"Combine best no-PE depth (5 blocks) with sharper attention (tau=0.5) to test if CRISPR can lift without sacrificing MRL/ncRNA gains.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import\
    \ jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model:int; kernel_size:int; dropout_rate:float; dilation:int=1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          residual = x\n          y = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                      feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(y)\n          y = nn.gelu(y)\n          z = nn.Dense(2*self.d_model)(y)\n          a,g = jnp.split(z,2,axis=-1)\n          y = a * nn.sigmoid(g)\n          y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(y, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return residual + y\n\n  class AttnPoolTemp(nn.Module):\n      d_model:int; heads:int=4; tau:float=0.5\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          logits = nn.tanh(nn.Dense(self.d_model)(h))\n\
    \          logits = nn.Dense(self.heads)(logits)\n          w = nn.softmax(logits / self.tau, axis=1)\n          pooled_heads = jnp.einsum('blh,blc->bhc', w, h)\n          return pooled_heads.mean(axis=1)\n\n  class Net(nn.Module):\n      d_output:int; task_type:str; d_model:int=256; blocks:int=5; k:int=7; dropout:float=0.1\n      heads:int=4; dilations:tuple=(1,2,4,8,16)\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x)   # no positional encoding\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          for i in range(self.blocks):\n              h = DSConvBlock(self.d_model, self.k, self.dropout, self.dilations[i%len(self.dilations)])(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          mean = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n          attn = AttnPoolTemp(self.d_model, heads=self.heads, tau=0.5)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          z = jnp.concatenate([mean, attn], axis=-1)\n       \
    \   z = nn.LayerNorm()(z)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z); z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          return logits.squeeze(-1) if (self.task_type=='regression' and self.d_output==1) else logits\n\n  class Wrap:\n      def __init__(self, **kw): self.net = Net(**kw)\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy): \n          pk, dk = random.split(rng_key); vars = self.net.init({'params':pk,'dropout':dk}, dummy, deterministic=True); return vars['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic: return self.net.apply({'params':params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          if rng_key is None: rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n          return self.net.apply({'params':params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout':rng_key})\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {'learning_rate':0.001,'d_model':256,'num_blocks':5,'kernel_size':7,'dropout_rate':0.1,\n\
    \              'attn_heads':4,'dilations':(1,2,4,8,16)}\n\n  def create_network(hp):\n      return Wrap(d_output=hp.get('d_output',1), task_type=hp.get('task_type','regression'),\n                  d_model=hp.get('d_model',256), blocks=hp.get('num_blocks',5), k=hp.get('kernel_size',7),\n                  dropout=hp.get('dropout_rate',0.1), heads=hp.get('attn_heads',4),\n                  dilations=tuple(hp.get('dilations',(1,2,4,8,16))))\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01))\n\n  BASE_SEED=42; BATCH_SIZE=64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/paper/draft.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Title: Unified Dilated Depthwise CNNs with Concat Attention (No Positional Encoding) for Multi-Dataset RNA Modeling\n\
    \n  Abstract (SOTA updated):\n  A depthwise-separable CNN with dilations and concat(mean, multi-head attention) pooling achieves a new state-of-the-art average validation score of 0.6745 by removing positional encoding and using 5 blocks with dilations (1,2,4,8,16). This setting substantially improves MRL and ncRNA while maintaining strong APA/PRS and acceptable CRISPR metrics.\n\n  Best results:\n  - No-PE + 5 blocks (Eval 69): 0.6745 | APA 0.8610 | CRI-Off 0.0674 | CRI-On 0.4841 | PRS 0.5627 | MRL 0.8986 | Modif 0.9510 | ncRNA 0.8969.\n  - No-PE + tau=0.5 (Eval 68): 0.6699 (CRI-Off improved to 0.0800; strong ncRNA 0.8954).\n  - No-PE base (Eval 66): 0.6686 (MRL 0.8918; ncRNA 0.9154).\n\n  Insight:\n  - Absolute sinusoidal PE harms conv backbones on these RNA tasks; removing PE unlocks large gains (MRL, ncRNA) and, with careful tweaks (tau, depth), recovers CRISPR.\n\n  Repro snapshots:\n  - Best no-PE base: storage/noema/submissions/best_nope_dilated_concat_mha.py (Eval 66)\n  - Best\
    \ overall: storage/noema/submissions/best_nope5_dilated_concat_mha.py (Eval 69)\n\n  Full ablations: storage/noema/results/ablations.csv\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 36 update — New SOTA lifted again: 0.6745 with no-PE and 5 blocks (Eval 69). No-PE + tau=0.5 hit 0.6699. Logged both, snapshotted best (best_nope5_dilated_concat_mha.py), and queued combined no-PE 5 blocks + tau=0.5. Draft updated with new SOTA and insights (absolute PE hurts convs here; depth+tau help balance CRISPR).\n```"
thinking_content: "**Analyzing CRI-Off improvements**\n\nI'm noting the improvements in the CRI-Off score. The No-PE original had a drop to 0.0357, but at temp=0.5, it improved to 0.0800, which is similar to the previous PE results. With 5 blocks, it yields 0.0674. The overall score is now up to 0.6745, with a significant MRL of 0.8986. Although CRI-On is down to 0.4841 from 0.5176, improvements in MRL and ncRNA help. Now, I should write to the ablations CSV for evaluations 68 and 69, keeping it concise.**Updating architecture files**\n\nI’m planning to rewrite the file, putting evaluations 69 and 68 at the top. I’ll create a new snapshot for the best No-PE 5-block architecture code, referencing build_network_v2 with positional_encoding set to False, and using num_blocks of 5 with dilations (1, 2, 4, 8, 16). I'll also update the draft with the new SOTA score of 0.6745, highlighting the benefits of no positional encoding for MRL and ncRNA, and mentioning trade-offs. Additionally, I might\
  \ queue experiments for improved robustness, combining recent changes.**Testing architectural options**\n\nI’m considering testing whether using 6 or 8 heads would work better, especially since 8 heads worsened performance with positional encoding before. However, it might differ with no positional encoding. I could explore relative positional encoding gating, but it's complicated. I’ll keep it simple by testing 5 blocks with attn_temp=0.5. I also need to update the Private Memory note and ensure the scoreboard is sorted by score. Finally, I will include necessary commands for storage and submission actions, keeping the YAML formatting rules in mind.**Updating YAML and implementing code**\n\nThe YAML content is fine because it includes code blocks. I need to execute several actions: updating the draft at \"noema/paper/draft.md,\" going to private memory, and replying with a summary. I'll also store the final \"best baseline\" note but keep things concise. \n\nFor the combined variant,\
  \ I want to use models.dsconv_mix with build_network_v2, setting positional_encoding to False, num_blocks to 5, and dilations to (1, 2, 4, 8, 16). While I could complicate things by creating a custom class for attn_temp again, I'll directly implement the simple code instead, using earlier work. I will also avoid writing to the \"research rank score\" as it's unnecessary."
