role: model
parts:
- text: "Outstanding progress. I’ll check the combined run and probe a no-PE + RMSNorm (5 blocks) variant.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{review 74}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"No-PE + RMSNorm + Concat MHA (5 blocks)\"\ntags: \"cnn, depthwise separable, dilated conv, rmsnorm, no positional encoding\"\nabstract: \"No positional encoding with 5 dilated DSConv blocks and RMSNorm pre-norm, using concat(mean, MHA-4) pooling. Tests if RMSNorm further stabilizes/improves no-PE depth while preserving unified design.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n\n  class RMSNorm(nn.Module):\n      eps: float = 1e-6\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          C = x.shape[-1]\n          scale = self.param('scale', nn.initializers.ones, (C,))\n          rms = jnp.sqrt(jnp.mean(jnp.square(x), axis=-1, keepdims=True) + self.eps)\n          return (x / rms) * scale\n\
    \n  class DSConvBlockRMS(nn.Module):\n      d_model:int; kernel_size:int; dropout_rate:float; dilation:int=1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          residual = x\n          y = RMSNorm()(x)\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                      feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(y)\n          y = nn.gelu(y)\n          z = nn.Dense(2*self.d_model)(y)\n          a,g = jnp.split(z,2,axis=-1)\n          y = a * nn.sigmoid(g)\n          y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(y, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return residual + y\n\n  class AttnPoolRMS(nn.Module):\n      d_model:int; heads:int=4\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = RMSNorm()(x)\n          logits = nn.tanh(nn.Dense(self.d_model)(h))\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.heads)(logits)\n          w = nn.softmax(logits,\
    \ axis=1)\n          pooled_heads = jnp.einsum('blh,blc->bhc', w, h)\n          return pooled_heads.mean(axis=1)\n\n  class Net(nn.Module):\n      d_output:int; task_type:str\n      d_model:int=256; blocks:int=5; k:int=7; dropout:float=0.1\n      heads:int=4; dilations:tuple=(1,2,4,8,16)\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # No positional encoding\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          for i in range(self.blocks):\n              h = DSConvBlockRMS(self.d_model, self.k, self.dropout,\n                                 dilation=self.dilations[i%len(self.dilations)])(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          mean = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n          attn = AttnPoolRMS(self.d_model, heads=self.heads)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          z = jnp.concatenate([mean, attn], axis=-1)\n          z = RMSNorm()(z)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z);\
    \ z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          return logits.squeeze(-1) if (self.task_type=='regression' and self.d_output==1) else logits\n\n  class Wrap:\n      def __init__(self, **kw): self.net = Net(**kw)\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy):\n          pk, dk = random.split(rng_key)\n          vars = self.net.init({'params':pk,'dropout':dk}, dummy, deterministic=True)\n          return vars['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic: return self.net.apply({'params':params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          if rng_key is None: rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n          return self.net.apply({'params':params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout':rng_key})\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {'learning_rate':0.001,'d_model':256,'num_blocks':5,'kernel_size':7,'dropout_rate':0.1,\n              'attn_heads':4,'dilations':(1,2,4,8,16)}\n\
    \n  def create_network(hp):\n      return Wrap(d_output=hp.get('d_output',1), task_type=hp.get('task_type','regression'),\n                  d_model=hp.get('d_model',256), blocks=hp.get('num_blocks',5), k=hp.get('kernel_size',7),\n                  dropout=hp.get('dropout_rate',0.1), heads=hp.get('attn_heads',4),\n                  dilations=tuple(hp.get('dilations',(1,2,4,8,16))))\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01))\n\n  BASE_SEED=42; BATCH_SIZE=64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{rank score}`"
thinking_content: "**Exploring model optimization**\n\nI'm considering adding content-based attention pooling, but it could be complicated. Instead, I could include dilations in a dropout path with a potential rate of 0.1 for stabilization; 0.05 seemed to harm results, and I wonder if 0.12 might work.  \n\nAlso, there's an idea of adjusting the gating temperature for MHA; previously, 0.5 improved results, but maybe 0.6 could do even better? I’m thinking about small max pooling alongside mean + MHA too. We need to test various configurations to see what succeeds!**Analyzing model configurations**\n\nI’m considering testing with either 6 or 8 attention heads. Using 8 heads degraded performance with position encoding (PE), whereas 6 might work better without PE — but I’ll keep it moderate.  \n\nI noticed that removing PE significantly improved our results, suggesting it hurt translation invariance.  \n\nFor the next steps, I'll review ID 74 and plan another submission with configurations like\
  \ “No-PE + Concat MHA” or “No-PE with RMSNorm.” The main result is already state-of-the-art, so I’ll update the ablations and finalize the paper soon!**Planning next steps**\n\nI need to review ID 74 and maybe rank the score, although it's already sorted. I also want to update the ablations table to include IDs 68 and 69, which I've done before.  \n\nI'm thinking about testing with 6 attention heads for a no-PE 5-block configuration, but I have to keep in mind the limit of two concurrent evaluations. Currently, there's one running. I think I can submit one more configuration like \"No-PE + Concat MHA (5 blocks, heads=6)\" to see if that improves performance since 8 heads with PE didn’t work well.**Planning model tests**\n\nI’m considering the configuration for \"No-PE + Concat MHA (5 blocks, tau=0.6),\" but since we already tried tau 0.5, I'm cautious about overfitting. Another option is to test \"No-PE + Concat MHA (5 blocks)\" with RMSNorm, since it improved metrics before. I’ll keep\
  \ the heads to 4 to minimize risk.  \n\nSo my actions will be to review ID 74, submit the \"No-PE + RMSNorm + Concat MHA (5 blocks)\" configuration, and possibly update the paper notes too. I’ll make sure to snapshot \"best_nope5\" that we've already created.**Preparing code for model testing**\n\nI need to code the configuration for \"No-PE + RMSNorm + Concat MHA (5 blocks)\" by adapting the earlier RMSNorm code, but this time without positional encoding and with 5 blocks. I want to make sure we have large multi-action steps while keeping everything as clear and concise as possible. It’s important to maintain minimal verbosity in the code. I’m eager to proceed with this setup!"
