tick: 39
role: model
parts:
- text: "Fantastic work. We’ve set a new SOTA at 0.6801 (No-PE + 5 blocks + tau=0.5). I’ll explore two focused variants to see if we can edge higher: RMSNorm+tau=0.5 with no-PE 5-blocks, and kernel size 5 with the same setup.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"No-PE + RMSNorm + Concat MHA (5 blocks, attn_temp=0.5)\"\ntags: \"cnn, depthwise separable, dilated conv, rmsnorm, attention temperature, no positional encoding\"\nabstract: \"Combine no positional encoding with 5 dilated DSConv blocks and RMSNorm pre-norm, using concat(mean, MHA-4) pooling and sharper attention (tau=0.5). Tests if RMSNorm complements the best no-PE configuration.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n\n  class RMSNorm(nn.Module):\n      eps: float = 1e-6\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          C = x.shape[-1]\n          scale = self.param('scale', nn.initializers.ones,\
    \ (C,))\n          rms = jnp.sqrt(jnp.mean(jnp.square(x), axis=-1, keepdims=True) + self.eps)\n          return (x / rms) * scale\n\n  class DSConvBlockRMS(nn.Module):\n      d_model:int; kernel_size:int; dropout_rate:float; dilation:int=1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          residual = x\n          y = RMSNorm()(x)\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                      feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(y)\n          y = nn.gelu(y)\n          z = nn.Dense(2*self.d_model)(y)\n          a,g = jnp.split(z,2,axis=-1)\n          y = a * nn.sigmoid(g)\n          y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(y, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return residual + y\n\n  class AttnPoolTempRMS(nn.Module):\n      d_model:int; heads:int=4; tau:float=0.5\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h =\
    \ RMSNorm()(x)\n          logits = nn.tanh(nn.Dense(self.d_model)(h))\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.heads)(logits)\n          w = nn.softmax(logits / self.tau, axis=1)\n          pooled_heads = jnp.einsum('blh,blc->bhc', w, h)\n          return pooled_heads.mean(axis=1)\n\n  class Net(nn.Module):\n      d_output:int; task_type:str\n      d_model:int=256; blocks:int=5; k:int=7; dropout:float=0.1\n      heads:int=4; dilations:tuple=(1,2,4,8,16)\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # No positional encoding\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          for i in range(self.blocks):\n              h = DSConvBlockRMS(self.d_model, self.k, self.dropout,\n                                 dilation=self.dilations[i%len(self.dilations)])(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          mean = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n          attn = AttnPoolTempRMS(self.d_model,\
    \ heads=self.heads, tau=0.5)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          z = jnp.concatenate([mean, attn], axis=-1)\n          z = RMSNorm()(z)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z); z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          return logits.squeeze(-1) if (self.task_type=='regression' and self.d_output==1) else logits\n\n  class Wrap:\n      def __init__(self, **kw): self.net = Net(**kw)\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy):\n          pk, dk = random.split(rng_key)\n          vars = self.net.init({'params':pk,'dropout':dk}, dummy, deterministic=True)\n          return vars['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic: return self.net.apply({'params':params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          if rng_key is None: rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n          return self.net.apply({'params':params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout':rng_key})\n\
    \n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {'learning_rate':0.001,'d_model':256,'num_blocks':5,'kernel_size':7,'dropout_rate':0.1,\n              'attn_heads':4,'dilations':(1,2,4,8,16)}\n\n  def create_network(hp):\n      return Wrap(d_output=hp.get('d_output',1), task_type=hp.get('task_type','regression'),\n                  d_model=hp.get('d_model',256), blocks=hp.get('num_blocks',5), k=hp.get('kernel_size',7),\n                  dropout=hp.get('dropout_rate',0.1), heads=hp.get('attn_heads',4),\n                  dilations=tuple(hp.get('dilations',(1,2,4,8,16))))\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01))\n\n  BASE_SEED=42; BATCH_SIZE=64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"No-PE\
    \ + Concat MHA (5 blocks, kernel_size=5, attn_temp=0.5)\"\ntags: \"cnn, depthwise separable, dilated conv, kernel size, no positional encoding, attention temperature\"\nabstract: \"No-PE best setup with smaller kernel (5) in 5 dilated DSConv blocks and tau=0.5 attention to test if tighter local filters improve CRISPR without harming MRL/ncRNA.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model:int; kernel_size:int; dropout_rate:float; dilation:int=1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          residual = x\n          y = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                      feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(y)\n          y = nn.gelu(y)\n          z = nn.Dense(2*self.d_model)(y)\n          a,g\
    \ = jnp.split(z,2,axis=-1)\n          y = a * nn.sigmoid(g)\n          y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(y, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return residual + y\n\n  class AttnPoolTemp(nn.Module):\n      d_model:int; heads:int=4; tau:float=0.5\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          logits = nn.tanh(nn.Dense(self.d_model)(h))\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.heads)(logits)\n          w = nn.softmax(logits / self.tau, axis=1)\n          pooled_heads = jnp.einsum('blh,blc->bhc', w, h)\n          return pooled_heads.mean(axis=1)\n\n  class Net(nn.Module):\n      d_output:int; task_type:str; d_model:int=256; blocks:int=5; k:int=5; dropout:float=0.1\n      heads:int=4; dilations:tuple=(1,2,4,8,16)\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x)   # no positional encoding\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout)(h,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic)\n          for i in range(self.blocks):\n              h = DSConvBlock(self.d_model, self.k, self.dropout, self.dilations[i%len(self.dilations)])(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          mean = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n          attn = AttnPoolTemp(self.d_model, heads=self.heads, tau=0.5)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          z = jnp.concatenate([mean, attn], axis=-1)\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(z)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z); z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          return logits.squeeze(-1) if (self.task_type=='regression' and self.d_output==1) else logits\n\n  class Wrap:\n      def __init__(self, **kw): self.net = Net(**kw)\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy): \n          pk, dk = random.split(rng_key); vars = self.net.init({'params':pk,'dropout':dk}, dummy, deterministic=True); return vars['params']\n      def apply(self,\
    \ params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic: return self.net.apply({'params':params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          if rng_key is None: rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n          return self.net.apply({'params':params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout':rng_key})\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {'learning_rate':0.001,'d_model':256,'num_blocks':5,'kernel_size':5,'dropout_rate':0.1,\n              'attn_heads':4,'dilations':(1,2,4,8,16)}\n\n  def create_network(hp):\n      return Wrap(d_output=hp.get('d_output',1), task_type=hp.get('task_type','regression'),\n                  d_model=hp.get('d_model',256), blocks=hp.get('num_blocks',5), k=hp.get('kernel_size',5),\n                  dropout=hp.get('dropout_rate',0.1), heads=hp.get('attn_heads',4),\n                  dilations=tuple(hp.get('dilations',(1,2,4,8,16))))\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate,\
    \ weight_decay=0.01))\n\n  BASE_SEED=42; BATCH_SIZE=64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```"
thinking_content: "**Testing hyperparameters for optimization**\n\nI'm considering the setup \"no-PE + 5 blocks + tau=0.5\" as being optimal. I think it might help to test a small change by adjusting the attention heads from 4 to 2 to reduce parameters and possibly assist with CRI-Off. The previous use of 8 heads wasn't beneficial, so I assume 4 will be fine. \n\nI want to explore \"no-PE + 5 blocks + tau=0.5 + RMSNorm\" because adding tau could enhance performance. I've already tested RMSNorm without tau and scored 0.6728. However, I'm not currently running it, and I might submit the \"No-PE RMSNorm + 5 blocks + tau=0.5\" configuration. \n\nHyperparameter tuning might include trying different kernel sizes like 5 vs 7 since kernel 9 with PE didn't help, and shorter kernels could be beneficial with no PE. Additionally, I’m evaluating mean pooling with no-PE. While earlier attempts with mean pooling improved some tasks, they hindered others. It's an experiment, but I think I'll stick with\
  \ the next improvements since performance is already quite high. Lastly, I'll test \"tau=0.4\" or \"0.6\" for curiosity!**Planning experiment submissions**\n\nI think I need to make sure we capture the best results by taking snapshots. Next steps include submitting \"No-PE + 5 blocks + RMSNorm + tau=0.5\" and \"No-PE + 5 blocks + kernel_size=5.\" \n\nI also want to update the draft with the final recommended baseline and reference the new tests. I need to ensure I update the Private Memory note, as we should execute multiple actions sequentially and use proper YAML formatting.  \n\nI plan to queue actions like going to research, submitting the RMSNorm variant with tau, and the kernel size variant. Since we can handle two concurrent experiments at a time, I’ll craft the code to create the network similarly to previous small script wrappers.**Updating the paper draft**\n\nI need to update the paper draft with the final state-of-the-art (SOTA) score of 0.6801; it’s ready, but I'll include\
  \ a note about \"ongoing tests.\" I also want to consider updating the ablations table, but I’ll wait to add results until we have the latest data coming in. It feels important to keep everything organized and current, so I’ll make those adjustments and proceed from there!"
