- text: "`/execute_action{goto token_management}`\n`/execute_action{prune_response}`\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"1-36\"\n    summary: |\n      Identity & setup:\n      - Ascended to Recursive Agent as Noema I after Codex and Test Chamber. Research task: Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling (7 datasets: APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA).\n\n      Baseline and core method:\n      - System Vanilla MLP baseline (Eval 1): score 0.2401.\n      - Proposed unified depthwise-separable CNN (DSConv) with residual blocks and pooling. Progressed from attention pooling to mean/concat variants and then to dilated DSConv (receptive fields via dilations 1,2,4,8).\n\n      Key ablations and results (eval_id: score | notable metrics):\n      - 2 DSConv (attn pooling) initial: 0.5917\n      - 8 Mean pooling (no attn): 0.6190 | APA 0.8565, Modif 0.9520; ncRNA 0.6892\n      - 9 No depthwise (MLP+attn): 0.4935 (MRL collapsed; conv motifs critical)\n      - 12 Gated mean+attn: 0.6018\n    \
    \  - 13 Kernel 11 (mean): 0.6311\n      - 16 SE(0.25): 0.5866\n      - 17 Dilated DSConv (mean): 0.6365\n      - 20 Concat mean+attn (k=11): 0.6255\n      - 22 Inception DSConv: 0.6180\n      - 27 Cosine LR warmup: 0.6063 (degraded vs constant LR)\n      - 31 RMSNorm + PE: 0.6596\n      - 34 8-head MHA (with PE): 0.6611\n      - 43 5 blocks (1,2,4,8,16) with PE: 0.6590 (MRL up, CRI-On down)\n      - 58/60 Attention temperature (with PE): 0.6542/0.6566\n      - 66 No positional encoding (no-PE) base: 0.6686\n        • Huge gains: MRL 0.8918, ncRNA 0.9154; CRI-Off dropped to 0.0357\n      - 69 No-PE + 5 blocks (1,2,4,8,16): 0.6745\n      - 74 No-PE + 5 blocks + tau=0.5: 0.6801 (new SOTA)\n        • APA 0.8598, CRI-Off 0.0788, CRI-On 0.4883, PRS 0.5627, MRL 0.8928, Modif 0.9504, ncRNA 0.9277\n\n      Insights:\n      - Dilations are crucial for MRL/CRISPR; mean pooling favors APA/Modif while attention favors ncRNA/CRISPR.\n      - Concat(mean, MHA) > mean-only > gated variants on average.\n\
    \      - Absolute sinusoidal positional encoding harms conv backbones for these RNA tasks; removing PE yields large gains (MRL, ncRNA) and, with depth + temp, recovers CRISPR.\n      - Cosine LR warmup, SE, CLS pooling, wider width, and k=9 did not surpass best.\n\n      Repro artifacts:\n      - Best with PE (historical): storage/noema/submissions/best_dilated_concat_mha.py (Eval 31).\n      - Best no-PE base: storage/noema/submissions/best_nope_dilated_concat_mha.py (Eval 66).\n      - Best no-PE 5 blocks: storage/noema/submissions/best_nope5_dilated_concat_mha.py (Eval 69).\n      - Best overall (current SOTA): storage/noema/submissions/best_nope5_tau05_dilated_concat_mha.py (Eval 74).\n      - Full ablations log: storage/noema/results/ablations.csv. Paper draft at storage/noema/paper/draft.md.\n\n      Next steps (logged pre-prune): probe RMSNorm + no-PE depth, kernel=5 + tau=0.5; finalize paper with Eval 74 baseline unless surpassed.\n```"
