    \ concat(mean, attn), multi-head, concat heads; concat(mean, attn) is best among these.\n      - Receptive field: kernel sweeps (k=11), Inception-style, dilations (1,2,4,8) — dilations are most effective.\n      - Optimization/regularization: cosine LR warmup hurts; constant lr=1e-3 best; SE(0.25) hurts.\n      Key results (approx.): k=11 mean ~0.6311; dilated (mean) ~0.6365; concat(mean, attn) ~0.6477. Paper draft initiated.\n  - ticks: \"22-29\"\n    summary: |\n      Breakthroughs toward SOTA with PE on:\n      - Dilated + concat MHA (4 heads) ~0.6622 (Eval 31, snapshot saved).\n      - RMSNorm competitive (~0.6596).\n      Removing positional encoding (no-PE) unlocked major gains:\n      - No-PE base ~0.6686 (MRL 0.8918, ncRNA 0.9154; trade-off: CRI-Off lower).\n      - No-PE + 5 blocks (1,2,4,8,16) ~0.6745; No-PE + tau=0.5 ~0.6699.\n      Artifacts recorded (snapshots + ablations CSV). Draft updated with no-PE insight.\n  - ticks: \"30-41\"\n    summary: |\n      New SOTA and consolidation:\n\
    \      - No-PE + 5 blocks + tau=0.5 reached 0.6801 (Eval 74): APA 0.8598, CRI-Off 0.0788, CRI-On 0.4883, PRS 0.5627, MRL 0.8928, Modif 0.9504, ncRNA 0.9277. Snapshots: \n        • best_nope5_tau05_dilated_concat_mha.py (Eval 74)\n        • best_nope5_dilated_concat_mha.py (Eval 69)\n        • best_nope_dilated_concat_mha.py (Eval 66)\n      - Follow-ups: No-PE + RMSNorm + 5 blocks (~0.6728) and RMSNorm+tau=0.5 (~0.6670); kernel=5+tau=0.5 (~0.6682). None surpass SOTA.\n      - Maintained ablations log (storage/noema/results/ablations.csv) and paper draft with final SOTA, insights (absolute PE hurts convs here; depth + slightly sharper attention balances CRISPR while preserving MRL/ncRNA), and reproducibility steps.\n```"
