tick: 47
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 47\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noema I\n- Agent Description: An agent advancing novelty and parsimony through rigorous, insight-driven experimentation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 47,893 / 270,000 used (18%)\n- Agent Age: 47 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Ablation: No-PE + Mean + Low-Rank Bilinear Pooling (no MHA)' (ID: 91) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6774802323779118\n**APA_R2:** 0.8600\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0678\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9524\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4805\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5636\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8919\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9262\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 91\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the Flax Conv parameter error. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code imported `DSConvDilatedBlock`\
    \ from the author's lineage file (`storage/noema/submissions/best_nope5_tau05_dilated_concat_mha.py`). This imported function contained a bug where it incorrectly used the parameter name `dilation` when calling `nn.Conv()` (line 27 of the lineage file).\n\nIn Flax's `nn.Conv` API, the correct parameter name for dilated convolutions is `kernel_dilation`, not `dilation`. This caused the following error:\n\n```\nTypeError: Conv.__init__() got an unexpected keyword argument 'dilation'\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nCreated `submissions/submission_v2.py` with the following changes:\n\n1. **Copied the buggy function**: Copied `DSConvDilatedBlock` class from the lineage file into the submission\n2. **Fixed the parameter name**: Changed line 25 from:\n   ```python\n   dilation=(self.dilation,),\n   ```\n   to:\n   ```python\n   kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n   ```\n3. **Removed the import**: Since we now have a working version of `DSConvDilatedBlock` in the submission file, the import from the\
    \ lineage file was removed\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed that the fixed code runs successfully for over 300 seconds without crashing, indicating the fix resolved the issue and the network is now properly initializing and executing.\n\n## Technical Details\n- **Error Type**: API parameter mismatch in Flax library\n- **Location**: `nn.Conv` call in dilated depthwise convolution block\n- **Flax Version**: The correct parameter for dilations in `nn.Conv` is `kernel_dilation`, as verified by inspecting the Flax API\n- **Fix Version**: submission_v2.py\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\nfrom typing import Sequence\n\n# Fixed DSConvDilatedBlock - copied from lineage and corrected parameter name\nclass DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n\
    \    d_model: int\n    kernel_size: int = 7\n    dilation: int = 1\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # Pre-norm\n        h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n        # Depthwise conv - FIXED: changed 'dilation' to 'kernel_dilation'\n        h = nn.Conv(\n            features=self.d_model,\n            kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n            feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n            padding='SAME',\n            kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n            name='dw_conv'\n        )(h)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        # Pointwise conv\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return x + h\n\nclass LowRankBilinearPool(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int\n    r: int = 16\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        u = nn.Dense(self.r)(x)\
    \  # (B, L, r)\n        u = u - jnp.mean(u, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n        cov = jnp.einsum('blr,bls->brs', u, u) / (x.shape[1] + 1e-6)  # (B, r, r)\n        cov_flat = cov.reshape((cov.shape[0], self.r * self.r))\n        cov_flat = nn.LayerNorm()(cov_flat)\n        z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(cov_flat)\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return z\n\nclass RNANetMeanBi(nn.Module):\n    d_input: int = 4\n    d_output: int = 1\n    task_type: str = 'regression'\n    d_model: int = 256\n    num_blocks: int = 5\n    dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n    kernel_size: int = 7\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n    r_bilinear: int = 16\n    positional_encoding: bool = False\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        h = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n\
    \            d = self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n            h = DSConvDilatedBlock(\n                d_model=self.d_model, kernel_size=self.kernel_size, dilation=d, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate\n            )(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        mean_vec = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)  # (B, C)\n        bilin_vec = LowRankBilinearPool(self.d_model, r=self.r_bilinear, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        fused = jnp.concatenate([mean_vec, bilin_vec], axis=-1)  # (B, 2C)\n        z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n        z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z)\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n        if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n            return logits.squeeze(-1)\n        return logits\n\nclass DSConvMean_BiNetwork:\n    def __init__(self, d_input, d_output, task_type, **kwargs):\n\
    \        self.network = RNANetMeanBi(d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, **kwargs)\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None:\n                rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'd_model': 256,\n        'num_blocks': 5,\n        'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n        'kernel_size': 7,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n        'r_bilinear': 16,\n\
    \        'positional_encoding': False\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    d_output = hparams.get('d_output', 1)\n    task_type = hparams.get('task_type', 'regression')\n    return DSConvMean_BiNetwork(\n        d_input=4,\n        d_output=d_output,\n        task_type=task_type,\n        d_model=hparams.get('d_model', 256),\n        num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks', 5),\n        dilations=tuple(hparams.get('dilations', [1, 2, 4, 8, 16])),\n        kernel_size=hparams.get('kernel_size', 7),\n        dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n        r_bilinear=hparams.get('r_bilinear', 16),\n        positional_encoding=hparams.get('positional_encoding', False),\n    )\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n    )\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\ndef complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n    ds = trial_data.get('dataset')\n\
    \    vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n    print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n\
