    2025-10-21 13:21:25,670\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1761024085670805148\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'No-PE + Concat MHA + Low-Rank Bilinear Pooling (r=16)' (ID: 90) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6727189059398235\n**APA_R2:** 0.8616\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0614\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9518\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4408\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5649\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8931\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9354\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 90\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the Flax Conv parameter error. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code imported `DSConvDilatedBlock` from the lineage file `storage/noema/submissions/best_nope5_tau05_dilated_concat_mha.py`, which contained a bug in the Flax Conv layer usage.\n\nThe error occurred at line 27 of the lineage file:\n```python\nh = nn.Conv(\n    features=self.d_model,\n\
    \    kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n    feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n    padding='SAME',\n    dilation=(self.dilation,),  # WRONG PARAMETER NAME\n    name='dw_conv'\n)(h)\n```\n\nThe error message was:\n```\nTypeError: Conv.__init__() got an unexpected keyword argument 'dilation'\n```\n\nThe Flax `nn.Conv` layer does not accept a parameter called `dilation`. The correct parameter name is `kernel_dilation`.\n\n## Fix Applied\nI created `submissions/submission_v2.py` with the following changes:\n\n1. **Copied the buggy `DSConvDilatedBlock` class** from the lineage file into the submission\n2. **Fixed the parameter name** from `dilation=(self.dilation,)` to `kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,)`\n3. **Kept the import for `MultiHeadAttnPool1D`** since it works correctly\n\nThe fix changes line 27 from:\n```python\ndilation=(self.dilation,),  # WRONG\n```\nto:\n```python\nkernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),  # CORRECT\n```\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed that the code\
    \ has been running for over 300 seconds without crashing, which indicates the fix was successful. The evaluation is still running (training the model), which is expected behavior.\n\n## Technical Details\n- **Error Type**: Parameter name mismatch in Flax Conv layer\n- **Version Fixed**: v2\n- **Fix Location**: submissions/submission_v2.py (lines 11-34)\n- **Verification Method**: Code ran for 300+ seconds without errors\n- **Exit Code**: 0 (success)\n\nThe code is now properly configured and the neural network training can proceed without issues.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n\nfrom best_nope5_tau05_dilated_concat_mha import MultiHeadAttnPool1D\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\nfrom typing\
    \ import Sequence\n\n# Fixed version of DSConvDilatedBlock - corrected parameter name from 'dilation' to 'kernel_dilation'\nclass DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int\n    kernel_size: int = 7\n    dilation: int = 1\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # Pre-norm\n        h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n        # Depthwise conv - FIXED: changed 'dilation' to 'kernel_dilation'\n        h = nn.Conv(\n            features=self.d_model,\n            kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n            feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n            padding='SAME',\n            kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n            name='dw_conv'\n        )(h)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        # Pointwise conv\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return x + h\n\nclass LowRankBilinearPool(nn.Module):\n \
    \   d_model: int\n    r: int = 16\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # x: (B, L, C)\n        u = nn.Dense(self.r)(x)  # (B, L, r)\n        u = u - jnp.mean(u, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n        cov = jnp.einsum('blr,bls->brs', u, u) / (x.shape[1] + 1e-6)  # (B, r, r)\n        cov_flat = cov.reshape((cov.shape[0], self.r * self.r))       # (B, r*r)\n        cov_flat = nn.LayerNorm()(cov_flat)\n        z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(cov_flat)\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return z  # (B, C)\n\nclass RNANetSOTABi(nn.Module):\n    d_input: int = 4\n    d_output: int = 1\n    task_type: str = 'regression'\n    d_model: int = 256\n    num_blocks: int = 5\n    dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n    kernel_size: int = 7\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n    num_heads: int = 4\n    attn_temp: float = 0.5\n    r_bilinear: int = 16\n    positional_encoding:\
    \ bool = False\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # Input projection\n        h = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Dilated DSConv stack\n        for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n            d = self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n            h = DSConvDilatedBlock(\n                d_model=self.d_model,\n                kernel_size=self.kernel_size,\n                dilation=d,\n                dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate\n            )(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Pooling: concat(mean+MHA fused) with low-rank bilinear covariance pooling\n        mha_vec = MultiHeadAttnPool1D(\n            d_model=self.d_model, num_heads=self.num_heads, attn_temp=self.attn_temp\n        )(h, deterministic=deterministic)  # (B, C)\n        bilin_vec = LowRankBilinearPool(\n            d_model=self.d_model,\
    \ r=self.r_bilinear, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate\n        )(h, deterministic=deterministic)  # (B, C)\n\n        fused = jnp.concatenate([mha_vec, bilin_vec], axis=-1)  # (B, 2C)\n        z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n        z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z)\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n        if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n            return logits.squeeze(-1)\n        return logits\n\nclass DSConvMHA_BiNetwork:\n    def __init__(self, d_input, d_output, task_type, **kwargs):\n        self.network = RNANetSOTABi(d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, **kwargs)\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n\n \
    \   def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None:\n                rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'd_model': 256,\n        'num_blocks': 5,\n        'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n        'kernel_size': 7,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n        'num_heads': 4,\n        'attn_temp': 0.5,\n        'r_bilinear': 16,\n        'positional_encoding': False\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    d_output = hparams.get('d_output', 1)\n    task_type = hparams.get('task_type', 'regression')\n    return DSConvMHA_BiNetwork(\n        d_input=4,\n        d_output=d_output,\n        task_type=task_type,\n        d_model=hparams.get('d_model',\
    \ 256),\n        num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks', 5),\n        dilations=tuple(hparams.get('dilations', [1, 2, 4, 8, 16])),\n        kernel_size=hparams.get('kernel_size', 7),\n        dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n        num_heads=hparams.get('num_heads', 4),\n        attn_temp=hparams.get('attn_temp', 0.5),\n        r_bilinear=hparams.get('r_bilinear', 16),\n        positional_encoding=hparams.get('positional_encoding', False),\n    )\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n    )\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\ndef complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n    ds = trial_data.get('dataset')\n    vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n    print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS=''\
