  \ sys.path to pull from 'storage/noema/submissions', which seems allowed.**Crafting submission code**\n\nFor the new submission of the corrpool variant, I plan to include minimal code by importing from 'nope5_dilated_concat_mha_corrpool.py'. This will let me create networks using the file's functions. Alternatively, I could add the sys.path manipulation to import necessary functions directly. They prefer 'submission.py' to implement the functions, which works for me. I’d like to keep content short, but I'll replicate some code from 'nope5...' into the submission to stay safe, even though that feels verbose. Hopefully, it won’t break the token budget too much!**Finalizing file updates**\n\nI’m considering that the auto debugger might not adjust lineage, and a bug in the relevant file could cause evaluation issues. But since I've already fixed the 'best' file, I'm feeling more confident about minimal imports. Additionally, we should incorporate the \"kernel_dilation\" fix into that file.\
