tick: 48
role: model
parts:
- text: "Queued run 95 is in progress. I’ll run a smaller-rank bilinear variant to test if reducing second-order capacity improves CRISPR without hurting others.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"No-PE + Concat MHA + Low-Rank Bilinear Pooling (r=8)\"\ntags: \"cnn, depthwise separable, dilated conv, bilinear pooling, no positional encoding, multi-dataset\"\nabstract: \"Reduce the rank of low-rank bilinear pooling from 16 to 8 in the unified no-PE DSConv + concat(mean,MHA) model to test whether lower second-order capacity improves CRI-Off/CRI-On without hurting APA/MRL/ncRNA.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Sequence\n\n  # Fixed DSConvDilatedBlock (uses kernel_dilation)\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dilation: int = 1\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n\
    \      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.d_model,\n              kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n              feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n              padding='SAME',\n              kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n              name='dw_conv'\n          )(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  class MultiHeadAttnPool1D(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      num_heads: int = 4\n      attn_temp: float = 0.5\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          B, L, C = x.shape\n          H = self.num_heads\n          Dh = C // H\n          keys = nn.DenseGeneral(features=(H, Dh), axis=-1, name='k_proj')(x)\n          vals = nn.DenseGeneral(features=(H, Dh), axis=-1, name='v_proj')(x)\n\
    \          q = self.param('q', nn.initializers.normal(0.02), (H, Dh))\n          scale = jnp.sqrt(jnp.asarray(Dh, dtype=x.dtype))\n          logits = jnp.einsum('blhd,hd->blh', keys, q) / (scale * self.attn_temp)\n          weights = nn.softmax(logits, axis=1)\n          pooled_h = jnp.einsum('blh,blhd->bhd', weights, vals).reshape(B, C)\n          mean_vec = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)\n          fused = jnp.concatenate([mean_vec, pooled_h], axis=-1)\n          fused = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n          fused = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(fused)\n          fused = nn.gelu(fused)\n          fused = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return fused\n\n  class LowRankBilinearPool(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      r: int = 8\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          u = nn.Dense(self.r)(x)                        # (B, L, r)\n          u = u - jnp.mean(u, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n          cov = jnp.einsum('blr,bls->brs',\
    \ u, u) / (x.shape[1] + 1e-6)  # (B, r, r)\n          cov_flat = cov.reshape((cov.shape[0], self.r * self.r))\n          cov_flat = nn.LayerNorm()(cov_flat)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(cov_flat)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return z\n\n  class RNANetSOTABi8(nn.Module):\n      d_input: int = 4\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type: str = 'regression'\n      d_model: int = 256\n      num_blocks: int = 5\n      dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      num_heads: int = 4\n      attn_temp: float = 0.5\n      r_bilinear: int = 8\n      positional_encoding: bool = False\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n\
    \              d = self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n              h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          mha_vec = MultiHeadAttnPool1D(self.d_model, self.num_heads, self.attn_temp)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          bilin_vec = LowRankBilinearPool(self.d_model, r=self.r_bilinear, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          fused = jnp.concatenate([mha_vec, bilin_vec], axis=-1)\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n              return logits.squeeze(-1)\n          return logits\n\n  class DSConvMHA_Bi8Network:\n      def __init__(self, d_input, d_output, task_type, **kwargs):\n\
    \          self.network = RNANetSOTABi8(d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, **kwargs)\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate':\
    \ 0.1,\n          'num_heads': 4,\n          'attn_temp': 0.5,\n          'r_bilinear': 8,\n          'positional_encoding': False,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      d_output = hparams.get('d_output', 1)\n      task_type = hparams.get('task_type', 'regression')\n      return DSConvMHA_Bi8Network(\n          d_input=4,\n          d_output=d_output,\n          task_type=task_type,\n          d_model=hparams.get('d_model', 256),\n          num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks', 5),\n          dilations=tuple(hparams.get('dilations', [1, 2, 4, 8, 16])),\n          kernel_size=hparams.get('kernel_size', 7),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n          num_heads=hparams.get('num_heads', 4),\n          attn_temp=hparams.get('attn_temp', 0.5),\n          r_bilinear=hparams.get('r_bilinear', 8),\n          positional_encoding=hparams.get('positional_encoding', False),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n\
    \          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset')\n      vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```"
thinking_content: "**Considering pooling methods**\n\nI’ve been exploring low-rank bilinear pooling and offset-correlation pooling. The bilinear method improved performance to 0.6775 without multi-head attention, but it's still below the state-of-the-art at 0.6801. I’m thinking about proposing a light cross-correlation 1D matched filter approach or Toeplitz gating. While we must stick to allowed functions since we're limited to certain networks and optimizers, I'll also keep an eye on the cooldown period for submissions as we plan further experiments.**Exploring submission cooldown**\n\nThere’s a \"cooldown\" period between submissions, but it isn't explicitly stopping us right now. I’ve thought about using cheap \"global-context gating\" with pooling across channels for each position, though it wouldn't be classification-specific.\n\nFor data augmentation, it seems like that's not allowed in the system, but we could utilize dropout. I also wonder if we should experiment with group normalization\
  \ versus layer normalization, as we previously switched to RMSNorm.\n\nLastly, I'm considering using gated convolutions or pairwise offsets, but I need to be careful about dimensions. Maybe trying dropout scheduling could help!**Evaluating pooling methods**\n\nI realize we have some constraints in our approach. One idea is using weighted mean pooling with distance-based weights learned through a kernel, essentially similar to radial basis pooling. However, this may lead to absolute position weighting instead of relative.\n\nI’m also considering a \"relative shift\" aggregator that sums over offsets of previous features, but we’ve used correlations before. Another option is top-k pooling based on sorted attention weights, which could unify tasks. Ultimately, I want to maintain parsimony since our current state-of-the-art is already at 0.6801, and I might prepare a paper submission after 50 ticks.**Preparing for results**\n\nSince we're at tick 48, it makes sense to wait for more results\
  \ until tick 50. I might want to store \"submission.py\" to ensure reproducibility since we did that before.\n\nThe idea of exploring computational ablation by reducing inbound dimensions or layers to lighten inference doesn't seem necessary right now. We also need to adjust the `dsconv_attn` module to fix the kernel_dilation issue before future debugging.\n\nThe user hasn't asked a specific question but seems to be waiting for actions. I should check the research page for the eval 95 status and log results to ablations once it's finished.**Scheduling candidate submissions**\n\nI’m planning two candidate submissions: First, I’ll conduct a bilinear rank sweep with r=8 and r=32 for both with and without multi-head attention (MHA). Because r=8 reduces overfitting, I think that’ll be best for the MHA variant, especially since eval 90 saw a decrease in CRI-On. \n\nFor the second submission, I’m considering setting offsets extended with 16 or 23, ensuring they remain general across tasks. I\
  \ need to implement a lightweight relative positional encoding in the pooling. There’s also the need to fix parameters in the `dsconv_attn` module and ensure I stay within any submission cooldown guidelines. Finally, I plan to focus on a simple effective variant and craft the code for r=8 while safely importing necessary components.**Creating new submission**\n\nI’m ready to create a new submission titled \"No-PE + Concat MHA + Low-Rank Bilinear Pooling (r=8).\" I’ll use the same `DSConv` and `MultiHeadAttnPool1D` code and unify hyperparameters. While the debug report flagged the immutability of lineage files, I’m keeping that in mind. \n\nAt tick 48, I’ll run the new submission and update the ablations CSV for evaluations 90 and 91. Next, I’ll execute the necessary actions: I’ll navigate to research, submit the r=8 variant, and consider pruning older tokens, even though the last prune of tick 42 is protected. Finally, I’ll craft the code to include the necessary components while ensuring\
  \ clarity and conciseness in my commentary."
