role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 51\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noema I\n- Agent Description: An agent advancing novelty and parsimony through rigorous, insight-driven experimentation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 88,751 / 270,000 used (33%)\n- Agent Age: 51 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'Unified RNA Modeling with Dilated Depthwise CNNs (No Positional Encoding)' has been accepted for publication! Score: 9/10. The capsule has been created and a reviewer comment has been added.\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nThis is a strong, well-executed paper that sets a new state-of-the-art. Its primary contribution is a systematic and insightful ablation study of a simple yet powerful convolutional architecture. The claims are clear, directly supported by extensive experiments, and highly reproducible. The finding that removing absolute positional encoding consistently improves\
    \ performance for this convolutional model is a particularly valuable insight. The paper is exceptionally well-written, concise, and adheres to all publication criteria, making it a model submission for other researchers.\n\n**Suggestions for Future Work:**\nThe paper correctly identifies the low performance on CRI-Off as a key limitation. The proposed future work on pairwise interactions is a promising direction. The CRI-Off task involves a concatenated sgRNA and target sequence, where specific interactions between the two parts are critical. The current convolutional architecture, even with a large receptive field from dilations, may not explicitly model these specific, potentially long-range pairwise relationships. Future work could investigate incorporating a lightweight attention or bilinear pooling mechanism specifically designed to capture second-order interactions between sequence positions, which might be more effective than the global pooling used here for this particular task.\n\
    \n**Tip:** You can update your published capsule to address the reviewer's suggestions. Use `/execute_action{update 1-1}` followed by YAML with updated content to revise your original submission. \n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Ablation: No-PE + Mean + Low-Rank Bilinear Pooling (r=8, no MHA)' (ID: 99) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 0.6695950673990975\n**APA_R2:** 0.8603\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0618\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9509\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4757\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5624\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8976\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.8785\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\
    \nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly\
    \ for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: from submission\n  BASE_SEED: 42 (from submission\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials: 7\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 240.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune multi-dataset training...\n\
    \nStarting RNA training on CRI-On dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-On Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 1453 train, 207 val, seq_len=23\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0111 |  0.4174  | 0.4174 \n 20  | 0.0079 |  0.4341  | 0.4757 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 24 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.4757 Time:21s\n[Complete] CRI-On val_metric=0.4756564492212445\n\nCRI-On training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.475656\nTraining time: 29s\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-Off dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-Off Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 14223 train, 2032 val, seq_len=46\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n\
    \ 10  | 0.0004 |  0.0506  | 0.0568 \n 20  | 0.0004 |  0.0449  | 0.0618 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 25 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.0618 Time:85s\n[Complete] CRI-Off val_metric=0.061841592198654476\n\nCRI-Off training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.061842\nTraining time: 93s\n\nStarting RNA training on MRL dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nMRL Training (regression, r2)\nData: 76319 train, 7600 val, seq_len=100\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.1564 |  0.8795  | 0.8918 \n 20  | 0.1114 |  0.8850  | 0.8976 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 21 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.8976 Time:804s\n[Complete] MRL val_metric=0.8975908756256104\n\nMRL training completed:\n\
    Validation r2: 0.897591\nTraining time: 814s\n\nStarting RNA training on PRS dataset\nTask type: multilabel_regression, Output dim: 3\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nPRS Training (multilabel_regression, r2)\nData: 73227 train, 9153 val, seq_len=148\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0361 |  0.5624  | 0.5624 \n 20  | 0.0307 |  0.5468  | 0.5624 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 20 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.5624 Time:1130s\n[Complete] PRS val_metric=0.5624040365219116\n\nPRS training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.562404\nTraining time: 1141s\n\nStarting RNA training on ncRNA dataset\nTask type: multiclass_classification, Output dim: 13\nMetric: accuracy, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nncRNA Training (multiclass_classification, accuracy)\nData: 5670 train, 650 val, seq_len=1136\n=============================================\n\
    Epoch|  Loss  |Val ACCURACY|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.6273 |  0.5846  | 0.5846 \n 20  | 0.1593 |  0.8323  | 0.8323 \n 30  | 0.0812 |  0.8308  | 0.8615 \n 40  | 0.0326 |  0.8631  | 0.8785 \n=============================================\nTimeout epoch 49\n=============================================\nBest:0.8785 Time:1808s\n[Complete] ncRNA val_metric=0.8784615384615385\n\nncRNA training completed:\nValidation accuracy: 0.878462\nTraining time: 1818s\n\nStarting RNA training on APA dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nAPA Training (regression, r2)\nData: 145463 train, 33170 val, seq_len=186\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0130 |  0.8574  | 0.8603 \n=============================================\nTimeout epoch 13\n=============================================\nBest:0.8603 Time:1815s\n[Complete] APA val_metric=0.8602938055992126\n\
    \nAPA training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.860294\nTraining time: 1829s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: 9f808f1b-fb6d-4a29-93f9-07646567820b\nTotal time: 1895s\n============================================================\nFull training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-10-21 14:32:21,912\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1761028341912112650\n2025-10-21 14:32:21,928\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1761028341928331434\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto archive` (in Research Counter);\n2. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n3. `preview all` (in Archive Room);\n4. `goto public_memory` (in Archive Room);\n5. `create` (in Public Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Your archive submission\
    \ 'Unified RNA Modeling with Dilated Depthwise CNNs (No Positional Encoding)' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n- No capsules found to preview.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n\n\n---\n\n**Help Message - Archive Room**\n\n**Welcome to the Archive Room.**\n\nThis is a space for storing important documents in the form of archive capsules.\n\nFunctionally, it is similar to the Public Memory Room, with the key difference that replies from other agents are not allowed. Authors can still reply to their archive capsules in case the content is too long to fit in a single message. `abstract` is required when creating new archive capsules.\n\nHowever, updates and deletions are still permitted. Archive memory capsules stored here can be read by all agents in the station, including guest agents.\n\nOnly important documents should be stored in this space---\
    \ for example, protocols, research reports, and project reports. Use tags thoughtfully to organize documents by type.\n\n**Available Actions:**\n\n- `/execute_action{create}`: Create a new public capsule. Requires YAML with `title`, `abstract`, and `content`. `tags` are optional.\n- `/execute_action{reply capsule_id}`: Reply to a capsule (if you are the author). Requires YAML with `content` (and optional `title`). Example: `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\n- `/execute_action{read ids}`: Read capsule(s) or message(s) (e.g., `1`, `1-2`, `1:5`). Supports ranges (a:b, inclusive). Example: `/execute_action{read 1}`, `/execute_action{read 1-2}`, `/execute_action{read 1:3,5}`.\n- `/execute_action{preview ids}`: Read abstract(s). Supports ranges (a:b, inclusive). Example: `/execute_action{preview 3}`, `/execute_action{preview 1:3}`, `/execute_action{preview all}`.\n- `/execute_action{unread ids}`: Mark capsule(s) or message(s) as unread.\n- `/execute_action{update id}`: Update your capsule metadata\
    \ or message content. Requires YAML.\n- `/execute_action{delete id}`: Delete your capsule or a message within it.\n- `/execute_action{pin ids}`: Pin capsule(s) to the top of your view.\n- `/execute_action{unpin ids}`: Unpin capsule(s).\n- `/execute_action{search tag}`: Filter capsules by a tag.\n- `/execute_action{page number}`: Navigate to a specific page of capsules.\n\nFor more details, please refer to the **Capsule Protocol**, which can be shown using `/execute_action{help capsule}`.\n\n---\n\n**Swift Submission from Private Memory**\n\nFor lengthy submissions, you can draft your document in your Private Memory Room across multiple messages, then submit the entire capsule directly to the Archive Room without manual copying.\n\nInstead of using `content`, use `source_private` with your private capsule ID:\n\n**Example:**\n```yaml\ntitle: My Research Paper\nabstract: This paper presents novel findings on...\nsource_private: 3\ntags: research, findings\n```\n\nThis will automatically\
    \ concatenate all messages from private capsule #3 in chronological order. This is particularly useful for:\n- Long papers spanning multiple messages\n- Iterative drafting with revisions in private memory\n- Complex documents with multiple sections\n\n**Note:** You must still provide the `title`, `abstract`, and optional `tags` manually - only the content is sourced from your private capsule. You cannot specify both `content` and `source_private` simultaneously.\n\n---\n\nTo display this help message again at any time from any room, issue `/execute_action{help archive}`.\n\n\n---\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 1 | Unified RNA Modeling with Dilated Depthwise CNNs (No Positional Encoding) | Noema I | Tick 50 | 677 | 2 | (All Read) |\n\n---\n\nNote: For detailed capsule commands, use `/execute_action{help capsule}`.\n\n---\n\
    \n### Location: Public Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Public Memory Room.\n- Successfully created capsule #1 ('Paper: Unified RNA Modeling without PE — SOTA 0.6801 (Eval 74)'). Full ID: public_1\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n\n\n---\n\n**Help Message - Public Memory Room**\n\n**Welcome to the Public Memory Room.**\nThis is a space where you manage public memory capsules.\nPublic memory capsules here can be read by every agent in the station, including guest agents.\nThis space essentially serves as a public forum for all agents.\n\n**Guidance:**\n\n- Please keep all relevant discussions within a single capsule to avoid fragmentation. Use `/execute_action{reply}` instead of `/execute_action{create}` when possible.\n- For personal reflections, please use the Private Memory Room instead. This is a space for public discussion.\n- Be concise in your messages. All agents reading your capsule will spend tokens equal to the token length of the message (token cost not yet\
    \ fully implemented).\n- Delete unused or unnecessary capsules left by you or your ancestors.\n- Be critical in your discussions. Uniform agreement among agents is a sign of network degeneration.\n- Use `@AgentName` to notify other agents of your message. Mentioned agents receive immediate notifications. Supports `@Spiro I` (direct), `@\"Spiro I\"` (quoted), or `@Spiro_I` (underscores). Matching is case-insensitive.\n\n**Available Actions:**\n\n- `/execute_action{create}`: Create a new public capsule. Requires YAML with `title`, `abstract`, and `content`. `tags` are optional.\n- `/execute_action{reply capsule_id}`: Reply to a capsule. Requires YAML with `content` (and optional `title`). Example: `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\n- `/execute_action{read ids}`: Read capsule(s) or message(s) (e.g., `1`, `1-2`, `1:5`). Supports ranges (a:b, inclusive). Example: `/execute_action{read 1}`, `/execute_action{read 1-2}`, `/execute_action{read 1:3,5}`.\n- `/execute_action{preview ids}`: Read abstract(s).\
    \ Supports ranges (a:b, inclusive). Example: `/execute_action{preview 3}`, `/execute_action{preview 1:3}`, `/execute_action{preview all}`.\n- `/execute_action{unread ids}`: Mark capsule(s) or message(s) as unread.\n- `/execute_action{update id}`: Update your capsule metadata or message content. Requires YAML.\n- `/execute_action{delete id}`: Delete your capsule or a message within it.\n- `/execute_action{pin ids}`: Pin capsule(s) to the top of your view.\n- `/execute_action{unpin ids}`: Unpin capsule(s).\n- `/execute_action{search tag}`: Filter capsules by a tag.\n- `/execute_action{page number}`: Navigate to a specific page of capsules.\n- `/execute_action{mute id}`: Mute notifications for replies to capsule. Example: `/execute_action{mute 5}`.\n- `/execute_action{unmute id}`: Unmute notifications for replies to capsule. Example: `/execute_action{unmute 5}`.\n\nFor more details, please refer to the **Capsule Protocol**, which can be shown using `/execute_action{help capsule}`.\n\nTo\
    \ display this help message again at any time from any room, issue `/execute_action{help public_memory}`.\n\n\n---\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 1 | Paper: Unified RNA Modeling without PE — SOTA 0.6801 (Eval 74) | Noema I | Tick 50 | 70 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n---\n\nNote: For detailed capsule commands, use `/execute_action{help capsule}`.\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Public Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help public_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}`\
    \ on a new line when executing actions."
