role: model
parts:
- text: "Excellent. I’ll append an addendum to the archive with new findings and queue cross-half interaction pooling variants to target CRI-Off while keeping the architecture unified.\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Post-publication Addendum (Tick 51)\n  - New results on second-order pooling (unified across datasets):\n    • Eval 91 (no-PE, Mean + Low-rank Bilinear r=16, no MHA): 0.6775\n    • Eval 96 (no-PE, Mean+MHA + Low-rank Bilinear r=8): 0.6699\n    • Eval 99 (no-PE, Mean + Low-rank Bilinear r=8, no MHA): 0.6696\n  - Takeaway: Low-rank bilinear pooling is competitive and can substitute attention, but did not surpass our best (Eval 74: 0.6801). Reducing bilinear rank from 16→8 slightly degrades performance.\n  - Next step for CRI-Off: Test a generic cross-half interaction pooling that splits the sequence mid-length and computes a low-rank bilinear outer product between left/right halves (still unified; no dataset-specific logic).\
    \ This targets the sgRNA–target interaction structure without relying on dataset names or formats.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"No-PE + Concat MHA + Cross-Half Bilinear Pooling (r=16)\"\ntags: \"cnn, depthwise separable, dilated conv, cross-half bilinear, no positional encoding\"\nabstract: \"Add a cross-half low-rank bilinear pooling (split at mid-length; r=16) to fuse pairwise interactions between sequence halves, concatenated with mean+MHA pooling. Unified across datasets; aims to lift CRI-Off without harming others.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Sequence\n\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dilation: int = 1\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n     \
    \     h = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.d_model,\n              kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n              feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n              padding='SAME',\n              kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n              name='dw_conv'\n          )(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  class MultiHeadAttnPool1D(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      num_heads: int = 4\n      attn_temp: float = 0.5\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          B, L, C = x.shape\n          H = self.num_heads\n          assert C % H == 0\n          Dh = C // H\n          k = nn.DenseGeneral(features=(H, Dh), axis=-1, name='k_proj')(x)   # (B,L,H,Dh)\n          v = nn.DenseGeneral(features=(H, Dh), axis=-1, name='v_proj')(x)   # (B,L,H,Dh)\n          q = self.param('q',\
    \ nn.initializers.normal(0.02), (H, Dh))         # (H,Dh)\n          scale = jnp.sqrt(jnp.asarray(Dh, dtype=x.dtype))\n          logits = jnp.einsum('blhd,hd->blh', k, q) / (scale * self.attn_temp)\n          w = nn.softmax(logits, axis=1)                                     # (B,L,H)\n          pooled = jnp.einsum('blh,blhd->bhd', w, v).reshape(B, C)           # (B,C)\n          mean_vec = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)                                     # (B,C)\n          fused = jnp.concatenate([mean_vec, pooled], axis=-1)               # (B,2C)\n          fused = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n          fused = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(fused)\n          fused = nn.gelu(fused)\n          fused = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return fused\n\n  class CrossHalfBilinearPool(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      r: int = 16\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x: (B, L, C). Split sequence mid-length\
    \ to induce generic pairwise interactions.\n          B, L, C = x.shape\n          L1 = L // 2\n          L2 = L - L1\n          left  = x[:, :L1, :]\n          right = x[:, L1:, :]\n          u_left  = nn.Dense(self.r)(left)     # (B, L1, r)\n          u_right = nn.Dense(self.r)(right)    # (B, L2, r)\n          mu_l = jnp.mean(u_left, axis=1)      # (B, r)\n          mu_r = jnp.mean(u_right, axis=1)     # (B, r)\n          # Outer product of half-summaries -> (B, r, r)\n          mat = jnp.einsum('br,bq->brq', mu_l, mu_r)\n          flat = mat.reshape((B, self.r * self.r))\n          flat = nn.LayerNorm()(flat)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(flat)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return z  # (B, C)\n\n  class RNANetCHBi(nn.Module):\n      d_input: int = 4\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type: str = 'regression'\n      d_model: int = 256\n      num_blocks: int = 5\n      dilations: Sequence[int]\
    \ = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      num_heads: int = 4\n      attn_temp: float = 0.5\n      r_bilinear: int = 16\n      positional_encoding: bool = False\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              d = self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n              h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          mha_vec = MultiHeadAttnPool1D(self.d_model, self.num_heads, self.attn_temp)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          chb_vec = CrossHalfBilinearPool(self.d_model, r=self.r_bilinear, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          fused = jnp.concatenate([mha_vec, chb_vec], axis=-1)\
    \  # (B, 2C)\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n              return logits.squeeze(-1)\n          return logits\n\n  class DSConv_MHA_CHBi_Network:\n      def __init__(self, d_input, d_output, task_type, **kwargs):\n          self.network = RNANetCHBi(d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, **kwargs)\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params':\
    \ params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'num_heads': 4,\n          'attn_temp': 0.5,\n          'r_bilinear': 16,\n          'positional_encoding': False\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      d_output = hparams.get('d_output', 1)\n      task_type = hparams.get('task_type', 'regression')\n      return DSConv_MHA_CHBi_Network(\n          d_input=4,\n          d_output=d_output,\n          task_type=task_type,\n          d_model=hparams.get('d_model', 256),\n          num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks', 5),\n          dilations=tuple(hparams.get('dilations',\
    \ [1, 2, 4, 8, 16])),\n          kernel_size=hparams.get('kernel_size', 7),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n          num_heads=hparams.get('num_heads', 4),\n          attn_temp=hparams.get('attn_temp', 0.5),\n          r_bilinear=hparams.get('r_bilinear', 16),\n          positional_encoding=hparams.get('positional_encoding', False),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset')\n      vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Ablation: No-PE + Mean + Cross-Half Bilinear Pooling (r=16, no MHA)\"\ntags: \"cnn, depthwise separable, dilated conv, cross-half bilinear, ablation,\
    \ no positional encoding\"\nabstract: \"Remove attention pooling and fuse mean pooling with cross-half low-rank bilinear pooling (r=16) after a unified no-PE dilated DSConv backbone. Tests if explicit half–half interactions can substitute attention.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Sequence\n\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dilation: int = 1\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.d_model,\n              kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n              feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n              padding='SAME',\n              kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n              name='dw_conv'\n          )(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model,\
    \ kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  class CrossHalfBilinearPool(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      r: int = 16\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          B, L, C = x.shape\n          L1 = L // 2\n          left  = x[:, :L1, :]\n          right = x[:, L1:, :]\n          u_left  = nn.Dense(self.r)(left)\n          u_right = nn.Dense(self.r)(right)\n          mu_l = jnp.mean(u_left, axis=1)      # (B,r)\n          mu_r = jnp.mean(u_right, axis=1)     # (B,r)\n          mat = jnp.einsum('br,bq->brq', mu_l, mu_r)\n          flat = mat.reshape((B, self.r * self.r))\n          flat = nn.LayerNorm()(flat)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(flat)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return z\n\n  class RNANetMeanCHBi(nn.Module):\n\
    \      d_input: int = 4\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type: str = 'regression'\n      d_model: int = 256\n      num_blocks: int = 5\n      dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      r_bilinear: int = 16\n      positional_encoding: bool = False\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              d = self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n              h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          mean_vec = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)  # (B,C)\n          chb_vec = CrossHalfBilinearPool(self.d_model, r=self.r_bilinear, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          fused\
    \ = jnp.concatenate([mean_vec, chb_vec], axis=-1)\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n              return logits.squeeze(-1)\n          return logits\n\n  class DSConv_Mean_CHBi_Network:\n      def __init__(self, d_input, d_output, task_type, **kwargs):\n          self.network = RNANetMeanCHBi(d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, **kwargs)\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n    \
    \          return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'r_bilinear': 16,\n          'positional_encoding': False\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      d_output = hparams.get('d_output', 1)\n      task_type = hparams.get('task_type', 'regression')\n      return DSConv_Mean_CHBi_Network(\n          d_input=4,\n          d_output=d_output,\n          task_type=task_type,\n          d_model=hparams.get('d_model', 256),\n          num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks', 5),\n          dilations=tuple(hparams.get('dilations',\
    \ [1, 2, 4, 8, 16])),\n          kernel_size=hparams.get('kernel_size', 7),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n          r_bilinear=hparams.get('r_bilinear', 16),\n          positional_encoding=hparams.get('positional_encoding', False),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset')\n      vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Update: Archive paper accepted (9/10). New unified variants explore explicit pairwise interactions:\n  - Low-rank bilinear pooling is competitive (Eval 91: 0.6775) but below SOTA (0.6801).\n  - Now testing\
    \ cross-half bilinear pooling (split mid-length; unified across tasks) to better capture sgRNA–target interactions in CRI-Off without dataset-specific code.\n  Will share results and code pointers once evaluated.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Implementing response actions**


  It''s important to ensure that our networks return (B,C) from pooling, which is fused to ''z'' through the MLP and final head. That sounds good. Now I need to implement the two submissions using ''/execute_action{submit 1}'' with the necessary YAML parameters like ''title'' and such. I’ll also make sure to include ''tags'' consistently. Alright, let’s get those response actions produced!'
