thinking_content: "**Planning next actions**\n\nI need to produce the next steps in this multi-agent environment. Since we're working with the same agent, I see that we've matured and published to archive with a score of 9/10. Experiments 101 and 102 are complete now, and we can resubmit the previously attempted gating variant, which was blocked due to the two pending evaluations. So, I should submit the \"Ablation: No-PE + Mean + Cross-Half Bilinear (Gated Fusion, no MHA)\" content and also update the ablations CSV and private memory with results from evaluations 101 and 102.**Updating archive and managing tokens**\n\nI should also update the archive addendum if needed and fix the lineage script to include the gating variant, storing it appropriately. However, I have to manage the token budget carefully; I've used 107,777 tokens so far, which is about 40%. Keeping my actions concise is essential, so I’ll provide only the necessary commentary and the relevant /execute_action commands in\
  \ YAML format. I can reuse the gating variant code, ensuring dilations are correct with the kernel_dilation parameter. Also, I need to update the storage results file 'ablations.csv' with the scores: 101 at 0.6700 and 102 at 0.6526.**Clarifying numbers and practices**\n\nI need to ensure the output table reflects the correct numbers: for 101, I’ll include 0.6700, APA 0.8552, CRI-Off 0.0387, CRI-On 0.5503, MRL 0.8782, Modif 0.9490, PRS 0.5598, and ncRNA 0.8585. For evaluation 102, that would be 0.6526, APA 0.8568, CRI-Off 0.0540, CRI-On 0.4532, MRL 0.9000, Modif 0.9500, PRS 0.5638, and ncRNA 0.7908. I’ll write the gating variant code into 'noema/submissions/nope5_mean_chbi_gated.py' for reproducibility, even if it’s not strictly necessary. Also, I’m considering optimizing cross-half pooling when segments vary, and it seems the splits make sense with current dataset lengths. The performance has shown improvements, especially with CRI-On.**Exploring gating and evaluations**\n\nThe mean+cross-half\
  \ without MHA had a score of 0.6526 partly because the ncRNA dropped to 0.7908. So it seems like gating might help with maintaining classification tasks. I’m considering proposing a gating variant and perhaps a two-split based on dataset lengths while being careful to avoid dataset-specific logic. Splitting mid seems acceptable. There's also a scale parameter to think about, but the environment restricts us to 100 lines of code. Additionally, I need to check on concurrency: the latest output mentioned I don’t have any running experiments, though it seems I still have evaluations 101 and 102 pending.**Resubmitting gating variant and updates**\n\nI need to wait for the two experiments to complete before resubmitting the gating variant. Our tags are currently set to six, which is good since we need to avoid truncation. I plan to store the gating code in 'storage/noema/submissions/nope5_mean_chbi_gated.py' for reproducibility. After that, I’ll submit with imports as this reduces code duplication.\n\
  \nI’ll also update 'ablations.csv' to include evaluations 101 and 102, ensuring to maintain historical data in the file efficiently while keeping track of token usage. Let's keep it concise!**Updating ablations and submitting gating variants**\n\nI can keep the 'ablations.csv' file with only the necessary additional lines appended, without rewriting everything. It makes sense to include the core evaluations and relevant rows, totaling 21. Now I plan to submit the gating variant titled \"Ablation: No-PE + Mean + Cross-Half Bilinear (Gated Fusion, no MHA).\" \n\nI also have the option to submit a second variant with MHA, although we could just focus on one to save tokens for now. I’ll ensure to write the gating code accordingly and manage the YAML properly with quoted titles. Time to implement!"
