parts:
- text: "The learned bipartition lifted CRI-Off modestly but hurt CRI-On and overall score. I’ll log results, set a meta plan, and test content-aware pooling (dynamic, sample-specific queries) to seek CRI-Off gains without regressions.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/ablations.csv}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  eval_id,title,score,APA_R2,CRI-Off_Spearman,CRI-On_Spearman,MRL_R2,Modif_AUC-ROC,PRS_R2,ncRNA_Accuracy\n  2,Depthwise CNN with Attention Pooling for RNA,0.5917,0.7550,0.0284,0.5150,0.6883,0.7255,0.5637,0.8662\n  8,Ablation: Mean Pooling (no attention),0.6190,0.8565,0.0605,0.5288,0.6807,0.9520,0.5654,0.6892\n  9,Ablation: No Depthwise Convs (MLP + attention),0.4935,0.7424,0.0508,0.4230,0.0579,0.9416,0.5139,0.7246\n  13,Kernel Sweep k=11 (Mean Pooling),0.6311,0.8587,0.0651,0.4753,0.7377,0.9521,0.5734,0.7554\n  17,Dilated DSConv (1,2,4,8) + Mean Pooling,0.6365,0.8465,0.0663,0.4880,0.8134,0.9525,0.5735,0.7154\n  20,Concat Mean+Attention (k=11 DSConv),0.6255,0.8365,0.0769,0.4690,0.6479,0.9509,0.5639,0.8338\n\
    \  31,Dilated DSConv + Concat MHA,0.6622,0.8367,0.0858,0.5176,0.8288,0.9514,0.5611,0.8538\n  34,Dilated DSConv + Concat MHA (8 heads),0.6611,0.8330,0.0775,0.5072,0.8425,0.9508,0.5644,0.8523\n  66,No-PE Dilated DSConv + Concat MHA,0.6686,0.8615,0.0357,0.4620,0.8918,0.9485,0.5655,0.9154\n  69,No-PE + Concat MHA (5 blocks 1,2,4,8,16),0.6745,0.8610,0.0674,0.4841,0.8986,0.9510,0.5627,0.8969\n  74,No-PE + Concat MHA (5 blocks) tau=0.5,0.6801,0.8598,0.0788,0.4883,0.8928,0.9504,0.5627,0.9277\n  78,No-PE + RMSNorm + Concat MHA (5 blocks),0.6728,0.8579,0.0709,0.4805,0.8936,0.9511,0.5632,0.8923\n  83,No-PE + RMSNorm + Concat MHA (5 blocks) tau=0.5,0.6670,0.8562,0.0381,0.4666,0.8925,0.9511,0.5616,0.9031\n  84,No-PE + Concat MHA (5 blocks, k=5) tau=0.5,0.6682,0.8568,0.0790,0.4464,0.8955,0.9519,0.5632,0.8846\n  90,No-PE + Concat MHA + Low-Rank Bilinear (r=16),0.6727,0.8616,0.0614,0.4408,0.8931,0.9518,0.5649,0.9354\n  91,Ablation: No-PE + Mean + Low-Rank Bilinear (no MHA),0.6775,0.8600,0.0678,0.4805,0.8919,0.9524,0.5636,0.9262\n\
    \  95,No-PE + Concat MHA + Offset Correlation Pooling,0.6627,0.8535,0.0320,0.4589,0.8780,0.9531,0.5646,0.8985\n  96,No-PE + Concat MHA + Low-Rank Bilinear (r=8),0.6699,0.8591,0.0605,0.4573,0.8869,0.9517,0.5586,0.9154\n  99,Ablation: No-PE + Mean + Low-Rank Bilinear (r=8, no MHA),0.6696,0.8603,0.0618,0.4757,0.8976,0.9509,0.5624,0.8785\n  101,No-PE + Concat MHA + Cross-Half Bilinear (r=16),0.6700,0.8552,0.0387,0.5503,0.8782,0.9490,0.5598,0.8585\n  102,Ablation: No-PE + Mean + Cross-Half Bilinear (r=16, no MHA),0.6526,0.8568,0.0540,0.4532,0.9000,0.9500,0.5638,0.7908\n  106,Ablation: No-PE + Mean + Cross-Half Bilinear (Gated Fusion, no MHA),0.6505,0.8595,0.0463,0.4672,0.8964,0.9504,0.5539,0.7800\n  107,No-PE + Concat MHA + Learned Bipartite Bilinear (r=16),0.6589,0.8537,0.0659,0.3963,0.8852,0.9516,0.5630,0.8969\n```\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Noema Meta (Tick 56)\n  - Primary: Maintain SOTA (0.6801, Eval 74). Seek generic CRI-Off gains without harming APA/MRL/ncRNA.\n\
    \  - Working hypotheses:\n    * Content-aware pooling (dynamic queries) may improve CRISPR tasks vs fixed-query attention.\n    * Channel gating (GLU) in DSConv may sharpen motif selection (Eval 109 running).\n  - Next actions:\n    1) Submit content-aware query pooling on SOTA backbone (no-PE, 5 blocks, τ=0.5).\n    2) If weak, try small τ sweep {0.4,0.6} with content-aware pooling.\n    3) If still weak, finalize addendum on pairwise interaction negatives + CRI-On improvement (Eval 101) and close loop.\n  - Guardrails: unified architecture, no dataset-specific logic; constant lr=1e-3; batch=64; clip=1.0.\n  - Token: prune again if >75%.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"No-PE + Content-Aware Query Pooling (concat mean + CA-MHA, τ=0.5)\"\ntags: \"cnn, depthwise separable, dilated conv, content-aware pooling, no positional encoding\"\nabstract: \"Replace fixed per-head queries with sample-specific (content-aware) queries derived from global features in the no-PE\
    \ dilated DSConv backbone. Fuse with mean pooling (concat) and τ=0.5. Aims to lift CRISPR metrics without hurting overall score.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n\n  from best_nope5_tau05_dilated_concat_mha import DSConvDilatedBlock\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Sequence\n\n  class ContentQueryAttnPool1D(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      num_heads: int = 4\n      attn_temp: float = 0.5\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x: (B, L, C)\n          B, L, C = x.shape\n          H = self.num_heads\n          assert C % H == 0\n          Dh = C // H\n          k = nn.DenseGeneral(features=(H, Dh), axis=-1, name='k_proj')(x)   # (B,L,H,Dh)\n          v = nn.DenseGeneral(features=(H, Dh), axis=-1, name='v_proj')(x)   # (B,L,H,Dh)\n          # Content-aware query: derive per-sample q from global mean\
    \ features\n          g = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)                                            # (B,C)\n          q = nn.DenseGeneral(features=(H, Dh), axis=-1, name='q_proj')(g)   # (B,H,Dh)\n          scale = jnp.sqrt(jnp.asarray(Dh, dtype=x.dtype))\n          logits = jnp.einsum('blhd,bhd->blh', k, q) / (scale * self.attn_temp)\n          w = nn.softmax(logits, axis=1)                                     # (B,L,H)\n          pooled_h = jnp.einsum('blh,blhd->bhd', w, v).reshape(B, C)         # (B,C)\n          mean_vec = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)                                     # (B,C)\n          fused = jnp.concatenate([mean_vec, pooled_h], axis=-1)             # (B,2C)\n          fused = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n          fused = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(fused)\n          fused = nn.gelu(fused)\n          fused = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return fused\n\n  class RNANet_CAQP(nn.Module):\n      d_input: int = 4\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type:\
    \ str = 'regression'\n      d_model: int = 256\n      num_blocks: int = 5\n      dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      num_heads: int = 4\n      attn_temp: float = 0.5\n      positional_encoding: bool = False\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              d = self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n              h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          pooled = ContentQueryAttnPool1D(self.d_model, num_heads=self.num_heads, attn_temp=self.attn_temp)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(pooled)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n\
    \          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n              return logits.squeeze(-1)\n          return logits\n\n  class DSConv_CAQP_Network:\n      def __init__(self, d_input, d_output, task_type, **kwargs):\n          self.network = RNANet_CAQP(d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, **kwargs)\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n\
    \              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n          return {\n              'learning_rate': 0.001,\n              'd_model': 256,\n              'num_blocks': 5,\n              'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n              'kernel_size': 7,\n              'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n              'num_heads': 4,\n              'attn_temp': 0.5,\n              'positional_encoding': False\n          }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      d_output = hparams.get('d_output', 1)\n      task_type = hparams.get('task_type', 'regression')\n      return DSConv_CAQP_Network(\n          d_input=4,\n          d_output=d_output,\n          task_type=task_type,\n          d_model=hparams.get('d_model', 256),\n          num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks', 5),\n          dilations=tuple(hparams.get('dilations', [1, 2, 4, 8, 16])),\n          kernel_size=hparams.get('kernel_size', 7),\n        \
    \  dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n          num_heads=hparams.get('num_heads', 4),\n          attn_temp=hparams.get('attn_temp', 0.5),\n          positional_encoding=hparams.get('positional_encoding', False),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset')\n      vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```"
