- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"No-PE + Hybrid Pooling: Fixed MHA (with mean) + Gated CA-MHA (τ=0.5)\"\ntags: \"cnn, depthwise separable, dilated conv, hybrid pooling, content-aware, no positional encoding\"\nabstract: \"Start from SOTA no-PE dilated DSConv with concat(mean, fixed-query MHA, τ=0.5). Add a content-aware MHA branch (queries from global features), gated into the base pooled vector with a bias-initialized small gate to preserve strong APA/Modif while probing CRISPR gains.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n\n  from best_nope5_tau05_dilated_concat_mha import DSConvDilatedBlock, MultiHeadAttnPool1D\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Sequence\n\n  class ContentQueryAttnPool1D(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      num_heads: int = 4\n      attn_temp: float = 0.5\n      @nn.compact\n \
    \     def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x: (B, L, C)\n          B, L, C = x.shape\n          H = self.num_heads\n          assert C % H == 0\n          Dh = C // H\n          k = nn.DenseGeneral(features=(H, Dh), axis=-1, name='k_proj')(x)   # (B,L,H,Dh)\n          v = nn.DenseGeneral(features=(H, Dh), axis=-1, name='v_proj')(x)   # (B,L,H,Dh)\n          # Content-aware query from global mean per sample\n          g = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)                                            # (B,C)\n          q = nn.DenseGeneral(features=(H, Dh), axis=-1, name='q_proj')(g)   # (B,H,Dh)\n          scale = jnp.sqrt(jnp.asarray(Dh, dtype=x.dtype))\n          logits = jnp.einsum('blhd,bhd->blh', k, q) / (scale * self.attn_temp)\n          w = nn.softmax(logits, axis=1)                                     # (B,L,H)\n          pooled_h = jnp.einsum('blh,blhd->bhd', w, v).reshape(B, C)         # (B,C)\n          # Light projection\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(pooled_h)\n       \
    \   z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return z  # (B, C)\n\n  class GatedHybridPooling(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      num_heads: int = 4\n      base_attn_temp: float = 0.5\n      ca_attn_temp: float = 0.5\n      gate_bias: float = -2.0  # small initial gate ~0.12\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # Base: fixed-query MHA with mean fused (returns C)\n          base = MultiHeadAttnPool1D(self.d_model, num_heads=self.num_heads, attn_temp=self.base_attn_temp)(x, deterministic=deterministic)  # (B,C)\n          # Content-aware branch (returns C)\n          ca = ContentQueryAttnPool1D(self.d_model, num_heads=self.num_heads, attn_temp=self.ca_attn_temp)(x, deterministic=deterministic)   # (B,C)\n          # Gate depends on global features (mean over length)\n          g_in = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)  # (B,C)\n          g = nn.Dense(self.d_model\
    \ // 2)(g_in)\n          g = nn.gelu(g)\n          g = nn.Dense(self.d_model, bias_init=nn.initializers.constant(self.gate_bias))(g)\n          g = nn.sigmoid(g)  # (B,C)\n          return base + g * ca  # (B,C)\n\n  class RNANet_HybridPool(nn.Module):\n      d_input: int = 4\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type: str = 'regression'\n      d_model: int = 256\n      num_blocks: int = 5\n      dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      num_heads: int = 4\n      base_attn_temp: float = 0.5\n      ca_attn_temp: float = 0.5\n      positional_encoding: bool = False\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # Stem\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          # Dilated DSConv stack\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              d = self.dilations[i] if i <\
    \ len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n              h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          # Hybrid pooling\n          pooled = GatedHybridPooling(self.d_model, num_heads=self.num_heads, base_attn_temp=self.base_attn_temp, ca_attn_temp=self.ca_attn_temp)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          # Head\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(pooled)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n              return logits.squeeze(-1)\n          return logits\n\n  class DSConv_HybridPool_Network:\n      def __init__(self, d_input, d_output, task_type, **kwargs):\n          self.network = RNANet_HybridPool(d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, **kwargs)\n      def init(self,\
    \ rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'num_heads': 4,\n          'base_attn_temp': 0.5,\n          'ca_attn_temp': 0.5,\n          'positional_encoding':\
    \ False\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      d_output = hparams.get('d_output', 1)\n      task_type = hparams.get('task_type', 'regression')\n      return DSConv_HybridPool_Network(\n          d_input=4,\n          d_output=d_output,\n          task_type=task_type,\n          d_model=hparams.get('d_model', 256),\n          num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks', 5),\n          dilations=tuple(hparams.get('dilations', [1, 2, 4, 8, 16])),\n          kernel_size=hparams.get('kernel_size', 7),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n          num_heads=hparams.get('num_heads', 4),\n          base_attn_temp=hparams.get('base_attn_temp', 0.5),\n          ca_attn_temp=hparams.get('ca_attn_temp', 0.5),\n          positional_encoding=hparams.get('positional_encoding', False),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n\
    \      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset')\n      vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```"
thinking_content: "**Exploring model improvements**\n\nI'm considering replacing GELU with SiLU or possibly using pre-norm RMSNorm instead of LayerNorm. However, we found that RMSNorm didn't help, as it resulted in a worse score of 0.6596. I thought about adjusting the Squeeze-Excite ratio to a smaller value, maybe 0.1, since earlier attempts with 0.25 didn't yield positive results. Also, tuning the kernel size is on my mind: we tried k=5 (0.6682), but k=7 achieved the best results. Lowering dropout and adjusting attention heads seems necessary too.**Combining query strategies**\n\nI'm considering the idea of merging content-aware queries while constraining them through gating or residual methods with fixed queries to avoid affecting APA. For instance, we could create a pooled result by fusing the fixed-query multi-head attention (MHA) and content-aware MHA through a small gate. This might help preserve the baseline while still allowing for a slight contribution from the content-aware aspect.\
  \ The pooling could concatenate the mean, fixed-query MHA, and CA-MHA before projection, using a gating coefficient alpha based on sample global features with small initial weights near zero. Setting these initial weights carefully will be tricky.**Adjusting pooling parameters**\n\nI’m thinking about manually setting a large negative bias to encourage low gating, and I can customize the initializer for the Dense layer to produce a smaller alpha, around 0.12. This may help preserve the baseline. I also need to ensure the training code passes the PRNG for dropout, which seems correct. I’m proposing a \"Hybrid Pooling\" approach that combines fixed-query MHA with mean and 10% gated CA-MHA. Also, we should avoid absolute position encodings. Let’s create a new submission, making sure we don’t exceed concurrent evaluations.**Implementing unified pooling**\n\nI need to unify the approach by replicating the DSConv block inline to avoid issues with the Debugger referencing outdated code. We can\
  \ import from the stored file, using DSConvDilatedBlock and MultiHeadAttnPool1D. I want to make sure that MultiHeadAttnPool1D uses fixed queries, as our gating pooling will compute both. The earlier CA pooling code imported the DSConvDilatedBlock, which passed CPU validation, but the drop in APA might have come from pooling issues. Our hybrid gating should help stabilize things. Now, let’s write the code.**Refining gating and submission process**\n\nI’m setting up gating with alpha calculated as the sigmoid of a Dense layer with GELU activation, starting with a bias of -2.0. The final pooled result will be the base plus the product of alpha and the content-aware component. I also considered including the mean in the base, but it’s already fused within MultiHeadAttnPool1D. \n\nI need to keep the hyperparameters consistent and implement the optimizer while logging the ablation results. Since we're over 75% tokens now, I can prepare the submission code and make the message succinct. Let’s\
  \ get that YAML code ready with a unique title and tags!"
