parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 60\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noema I\n- Agent Description: An agent advancing novelty and parsimony through rigorous, insight-driven experimentation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nNoema Meta (Tick 56)\n- Primary: Maintain SOTA (0.6801, Eval 74). Seek generic CRI-Off gains without harming APA/MRL/ncRNA.\n- Working hypotheses:\n  * Content-aware pooling (dynamic queries) may improve CRISPR tasks vs fixed-query attention.\n  * Channel gating (GLU) in DSConv may sharpen motif selection (Eval 109 running).\n- Next actions:\n  1) Submit content-aware query pooling on SOTA backbone (no-PE, 5 blocks, τ=0.5).\n  2) If weak, try small τ sweep {0.4,0.6} with content-aware pooling.\n  3) If still weak, finalize addendum on pairwise interaction negatives + CRI-On improvement (Eval 101) and close loop.\n- Guardrails: unified architecture, no dataset-specific logic; constant lr=1e-3; batch=64; clip=1.0.\n- Token:\
    \ prune again if >75%.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 199,037 / 270,000 used (74%)\n- Agent Age: 60 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nYou can use `/execute_action{meta}` with YAML containing a single `content` field to set a meta prompt at any rooms. The meta prompt appears in every tick and is perfect for maintaining protocols, TODO lists, and long-term goals.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Public Memory Room);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'No-PE + Hybrid Pooling: Fixed MHA (with mean) + Gated CA-MHA (τ=0.5)' submitted for Research Task #1: Multi-Dataset\
    \ RNA Sequence Modeling. Evaluation ID: 115.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 115 | 1 | No-PE + Hybrid Pooling: Fixed MHA (with mean) + Gated CA-MHA (τ=0.5) | Noema I | 59 |\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | APA_R2 | CRI-Off_Spearman | CRI-On_Spearman | MRL_R2 | Modif_AUC-ROC | PRS_R2 | ncRNA_Accuracy |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 74 | 1 | No-PE + Concat MHA (5 blocks, attn_temp=0.5) | Noema I | 36 | 0.6801 | 0.8598 | 0.0788 | 0.4883 | 0.8928 | 0.9504 | 0.5627 | 0.9277 |\n| 91 | 1 | Ablation: No-PE + Mean + Low-Rank Bilinear Pooling (no MHA) | Noema I | 45 | 0.6775 | 0.8600 | 0.0678 | 0.4805 | 0.8919 | 0.9524 | 0.5636 | 0.9262 |\n| 77 | 1 | Residual CNN-BiLSTM\
    \ with Additive Attention Pooling | Veritas I | 37 | 0.6771 | 0.8626 | 0.0591 | 0.4806 | 0.8988 | 0.9499 | 0.5608 | 0.9277 |\n| 89 | 1 | Deeper Residual CNN-BiLSTM with Additive Attention Pooling | Veritas I | 45 | 0.6770 | 0.8585 | 0.0750 | 0.4805 | 0.9011 | 0.9525 | 0.5653 | 0.9062 |\n| 98 | 1 | Tuned Residual CNN-BiLSTM with Additive Attention (Reduced Dropout) | Veritas I | 49 | 0.6765 | 0.8481 | 0.0554 | 0.4862 | 0.9011 | 0.9474 | 0.5681 | 0.9292 |\n| 69 | 1 | No-PE + Concat MHA (5 blocks: 1,2,4,8,16) | Noema I | 34 | 0.6745 | 0.8610 | 0.0674 | 0.4841 | 0.8986 | 0.9510 | 0.5627 | 0.8969 |\n| 114 | 1 | Noema-Inspired SOTA: Dilated DSConv with Concat Mean+MHA Pooling (No-PE) | Aetheria I | 58 | 0.6741 | 0.8456 | 0.0371 | 0.5198 | 0.9068 | 0.9483 | 0.5638 | 0.8969 |\n| 51 | 1 | Refined Hybrid CNN-BiLSTM with Additive Attention (Increased Dense Capacity) | Veritas I | 27 | 0.6738 | 0.8558 | 0.0580 | 0.4905 | 0.9053 | 0.9443 | 0.5673 | 0.8954 |\n| 78 | 1 | No-PE + RMSNorm + Concat MHA\
    \ (5 blocks) | Noema I | 37 | 0.6728 | 0.8579 | 0.0709 | 0.4805 | 0.8936 | 0.9511 | 0.5632 | 0.8923 |\n| 90 | 1 | No-PE + Concat MHA + Low-Rank Bilinear Pooling (r=16) | Noema I | 45 | 0.6727 | 0.8616 | 0.0614 | 0.4408 | 0.8931 | 0.9518 | 0.5649 | 0.9354 |\n| 42 | 1 | Tuned Hybrid CNN-BiLSTM with Additive Attention Pooling | Veritas I | 23 | 0.6724 | 0.8635 | 0.0452 | 0.4831 | 0.8998 | 0.9498 | 0.5743 | 0.8908 |\n| 82 | 1 | Gated CNN-BiLSTM with Additive Attention Pooling | Veritas I | 39 | 0.6719 | 0.8559 | 0.0393 | 0.5131 | 0.8872 | 0.9470 | 0.5655 | 0.8954 |\n| 104 | 1 | Hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM with Additive Attention Pooling | Veritas I | 52 | 0.6709 | 0.8511 | 0.0713 | 0.4366 | 0.9006 | 0.9505 | 0.5677 | 0.9185 |\n| 94 | 1 | Dilated CNN-BiLSTM with Additive Attention Pooling | Veritas I | 47 | 0.6702 | 0.8538 | 0.0571 | 0.4639 | 0.8886 | 0.9519 | 0.5483 | 0.9277 |\n| 101 | 1 | No-PE + Concat MHA + Cross-Half Bilinear Pooling (r=16) | Noema I | 51 | 0.6700 | 0.8552 | 0.0387 | 0.5503\
    \ | 0.8782 | 0.9490 | 0.5598 | 0.8585 |\n| 96 | 1 | No-PE + Concat MHA + Low-Rank Bilinear Pooling (r=8) | Noema I | 48 | 0.6699 | 0.8591 | 0.0605 | 0.4573 | 0.8869 | 0.9517 | 0.5586 | 0.9154 |\n| 68 | 1 | No-PE + Concat MHA (attn_temp=0.5) | Noema I | 34 | 0.6699 | 0.8576 | 0.0800 | 0.4599 | 0.8814 | 0.9513 | 0.5636 | 0.8954 |\n| 57 | 1 | Multi-Head Additive Attention CNN-BiLSTM for RNA Modeling | Veritas I | 29 | 0.6697 | 0.8593 | 0.0340 | 0.4769 | 0.8946 | 0.9489 | 0.5683 | 0.9062 |\n| 99 | 1 | Ablation: No-PE + Mean + Low-Rank Bilinear Pooling (r=8, no MHA) | Noema I | 49 | 0.6696 | 0.8603 | 0.0618 | 0.4757 | 0.8976 | 0.9509 | 0.5624 | 0.8785 |\n| 66 | 1 | Dilated DSConv + Concat MHA (no positional encoding) | Noema I | 32 | 0.6686 | 0.8615 | 0.0357 | 0.4620 | 0.8918 | 0.9485 | 0.5655 | 0.9154 |\n| 53 | 1 | Siamese-like CNN for CRISPR Off-Target Prediction | Aletheia I | 28 | 0.6685 | 0.8393 | 0.0640 | 0.4607 | 0.8771 | 0.9428 | 0.5538 | 0.9415 |\n| 84 | 1 | No-PE + Concat MHA (5\
    \ blocks, kernel_size=5, attn_temp=0.5) | Noema I | 39 | 0.6682 | 0.8568 | 0.0790 | 0.4464 | 0.8955 | 0.9519 | 0.5632 | 0.8846 |\n| 72 | 1 | Task-Specific Head CNN-BiLSTM with Additive Attention | Veritas I | 35 | 0.6675 | 0.8595 | 0.0576 | 0.4337 | 0.9009 | 0.9493 | 0.5685 | 0.9031 |\n| 109 | 1 | No-PE + Concat MHA (5 blocks) with GLU Pointwise Conv | Noema I | 55 | 0.6674 | 0.8579 | 0.0391 | 0.4745 | 0.8871 | 0.9515 | 0.5601 | 0.9015 |\n| 83 | 1 | No-PE + RMSNorm + Concat MHA (5 blocks, attn_temp=0.5) | Noema I | 39 | 0.6670 | 0.8562 | 0.0381 | 0.4666 | 0.8925 | 0.9511 | 0.5616 | 0.9031 |\n| 64 | 1 | Tuned CNN-BiLSTM with Additive Attention (Reduced CNN Kernel) | Veritas I | 31 | 0.6668 | 0.8630 | 0.0648 | 0.4345 | 0.9034 | 0.9502 | 0.5564 | 0.8954 |\n| 105 | 1 | Hybrid Residual CNN-BiLSTM with Bilinear Pooling | Veritas I | 53 | 0.6656 | 0.8608 | 0.0553 | 0.4985 | 0.9047 | 0.9422 | 0.5713 | 0.8262 |\n| 108 | 1 | Dilated ResNet with Attention Pooling | Aletheia I | 55 | 0.6651 | 0.8469\
    \ | 0.0747 | 0.4442 | 0.8914 | 0.9486 | 0.5557 | 0.8938 |\n| 67 | 1 | Adaptive CNN Kernel Hybrid CNN-BiLSTM with Additive Attention | Veritas I | 33 | 0.6644 | 0.8573 | 0.0777 | 0.4349 | 0.8974 | 0.9475 | 0.5647 | 0.8708 |\n| 56 | 1 | Siamese CNN with MLP Interaction Head for CRISPR | Aletheia I | 29 | 0.6642 | 0.8375 | 0.0656 | 0.4546 | 0.8796 | 0.9460 | 0.5430 | 0.9231 |\n| 87 | 1 | Positional Encoded Residual CNN-BiLSTM with Additive Attention (Fixed) | Veritas I | 43 | 0.6636 | 0.8544 | 0.0343 | 0.4855 | 0.8686 | 0.9505 | 0.5630 | 0.8892 |\n| 95 | 1 | No-PE + Concat MHA + Offset Correlation Pooling | Noema I | 47 | 0.6627 | 0.8535 | 0.0320 | 0.4589 | 0.8780 | 0.9531 | 0.5646 | 0.8985 |\n| 31 | 1 | Dilated DSConv (1,2,4,8) + Concat MHA Pooling | Noema I | 19 | 0.6622 | 0.8367 | 0.0858 | 0.5176 | 0.8288 | 0.9514 | 0.5611 | 0.8538 |\n| 36 | 1 | Enhanced CNN-BiLSTM with Additive Attention Pooling | Veritas I | 21 | 0.6618 | 0.8586 | 0.0434 | 0.4499 | 0.9038 | 0.9499 | 0.5732 | 0.8538\
    \ |\n| 34 | 1 | Dilated DSConv (1,2,4,8) + Concat MHA Pooling (8 heads) | Noema I | 20 | 0.6611 | 0.8330 | 0.0775 | 0.5072 | 0.8425 | 0.9508 | 0.5644 | 0.8523 |\n| 65 | 1 | Dilated DSConv + RMSNorm + Concat MHA | Noema I | 31 | 0.6596 | 0.8396 | 0.0848 | 0.4979 | 0.8213 | 0.9527 | 0.5639 | 0.8569 |\n| 63 | 1 | Capacity Test: Wider Dilated ResNet (256 features) | Aletheia I | 31 | 0.6596 | 0.8381 | 0.0659 | 0.4138 | 0.8701 | 0.9473 | 0.5527 | 0.9292 |\n| 43 | 1 | Dilated DSConv + Concat MHA (5 blocks: 1,2,4,8,16) | Noema I | 23 | 0.6590 | 0.8464 | 0.0823 | 0.4456 | 0.8575 | 0.9515 | 0.5667 | 0.8631 |\n| 107 | 1 | No-PE + Concat MHA + Learned Bipartite Bilinear Pooling (r=16) | Noema I | 54 | 0.6589 | 0.8537 | 0.0659 | 0.3963 | 0.8852 | 0.9516 | 0.5630 | 0.8969 |\n| 81 | 1 | Deeper Dilated ResNet (5 Blocks) | Aletheia I | 39 | 0.6587 | 0.8438 | 0.0645 | 0.4228 | 0.8908 | 0.9473 | 0.5480 | 0.8938 |\n| 111 | 1 | Ablation: Attention Pooling with Mean-Vector Query | Aletheia I | 57 | 0.6586\
