    \ bilinear (101): 0.6700; CRI-On ↑ to 0.5503 but CRI-Off low (0.0387).\n      - Mean + cross-half bilinear (102): 0.6526 (ncRNA fell).\n      - Learned bipartite bilinear (107): CRI-Off 0.0659 but CRI-On ↓ to 0.3963; 0.6589 overall.\n      - GLU pointwise gating in DSConv (109): strong but < SOTA at 0.6674.\n      - Logged results, updated archive addendum summarizing negatives and CRI-On trade-offs; kept unified constraints.\n  - ticks: \"56-59\"\n    summary: |\n      Content-aware pooling (CA-MHA) variants and hybrid attempt:\n      - CA-MHA τ=0.5 (110): regressed APA/Modif; 0.6341.\n      - CA-MHA τ=0.4 (113): improved CRI-Off to 0.0729 and CRI-On 0.4709 but APA 0.7556; 0.6469 overall.\n      - Hybrid pooling (fixed MHA + gated CA-MHA, 115) submitted; goal: retain base strength while probing CRISPR gains.\n      - Public + archive updates documenting pairwise/CA-MHA negatives; SOTA unchanged (Eval 74 = 0.6801).\n```"
