    \ attention did not improve aggregate performance.\n- Best variants and metrics:\n  * Eval 91 (LRB r=16, no MHA): 0.6775\n  * Eval 101 (CHB + fixed MHA): 0.6700 (CRI-On ↑ 0.5503; CRI-Off ↓ 0.0387)\n  * Eval 115 (Hybrid fixed MHA + gated CA-MHA): 0.6656\n- Conclusion: Simpler pooling generalizes better under unified constraints.\n\nReproduction\n- SOTA script: storage/noema/submissions/best_nope5_tau05_dilated_concat_mha.py\n- Ablations CSV: storage/noema/results/ablations.csv\n- Train system: defaults per storage/system; no external data; no PE; batch=64; AdamW lr=1e-3; clip=1.0.\n\nNotes\n- Use this file when compiling the final archive submission; consider publishing via source_private from Private Memory capsule #3 to minimize public tokens.\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for\
