parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"No-PE + SOTA Backbone with Symmetric Halfwise Interaction Features (MHA product & abs-diff)\"\ntags: \"cnn, depthwise separable, dilated conv, interaction features, unified, no positional encoding\"\nabstract: \"Augment the SOTA no-PE dilated DSConv with symmetric interaction features computed from fixed-query MHA pooled left/right halves: element-wise product and absolute difference. Concatenate with the base global mean+MHA pooling to capture generic pairwise relations while staying unified.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Sequence\n\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dilation: int = 1\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # Pre-norm\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          # Depthwise\
    \ conv\n          h = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.d_model,\n              kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n              feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n              padding='SAME',\n              kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n              name='dw_conv'\n          )(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          # Pointwise conv\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  class FixedQueryAttnPool1D(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      num_heads: int = 4\n      attn_temp: float = 0.5\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x: (B, L, C)\n          B, L, C = x.shape\n          H = self.num_heads\n          assert C % H == 0\n          Dh = C // H\n          k = nn.DenseGeneral(features=(H, Dh), axis=-1, name='k_proj')(x)  # (B,L,H,Dh)\n          v = nn.DenseGeneral(features=(H, Dh),\
    \ axis=-1, name='v_proj')(x)  # (B,L,H,Dh)\n          q = self.param('q', nn.initializers.normal(0.02), (H, Dh))        # (H,Dh)\n          scale = jnp.sqrt(jnp.asarray(Dh, dtype=x.dtype))\n          logits = jnp.einsum('blhd,hd->blh', k, q) / (scale * self.attn_temp)\n          w = nn.softmax(logits, axis=1)                                     # (B,L,H)\n          pooled = jnp.einsum('blh,blhd->bhd', w, v).reshape(B, C)           # (B,C)\n          return pooled\n\n  class RNANetHalfInteract(nn.Module):\n      d_input: int = 4\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type: str = 'regression'\n      d_model: int = 256\n      num_blocks: int = 5\n      dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      num_heads: int = 4\n      attn_temp: float = 0.5\n      positional_encoding: bool = False\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # Input projection\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x)\
    \            # (B,L,C)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Dilated DSConv stack\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              d = self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n              h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          B, L, C = h.shape\n          L1 = L // 2\n          left  = h[:, :L1, :]\n          right = h[:, L1:, :]\n\n          # Global pooling (baseline SOTA): mean + fixed-query MHA\n          g_mean = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)  # (B,C)\n          g_attn = FixedQueryAttnPool1D(self.d_model, self.num_heads, self.attn_temp)(h, deterministic=deterministic)  # (B,C)\n          g_fused = jnp.concatenate([g_mean, g_attn], axis=-1)  # (B,2C)\n          g_fused = nn.LayerNorm()(g_fused)\n          g_fused = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(g_fused)\n          g_fused = nn.gelu(g_fused)\n\
    \          g_fused = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(g_fused, deterministic=deterministic)  # (B,C)\n\n          # Half-wise fixed-query MHA\n          l_attn = FixedQueryAttnPool1D(self.d_model, self.num_heads, self.attn_temp)(left, deterministic=deterministic)   # (B,C)\n          r_attn = FixedQueryAttnPool1D(self.d_model, self.num_heads, self.attn_temp)(right, deterministic=deterministic)  # (B,C)\n\n          # Symmetric interaction features\n          inter_prod = l_attn * r_attn\n          inter_diff = jnp.abs(l_attn - r_attn)\n          inter = jnp.concatenate([inter_prod, inter_diff], axis=-1)  # (B,2C)\n          inter = nn.LayerNorm()(inter)\n          inter = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(inter)\n          inter = nn.gelu(inter)\n          inter = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(inter, deterministic=deterministic)  # (B,C)\n\n          # Fuse global with interaction\n          z = jnp.concatenate([g_fused, inter], axis=-1)  # (B,2C)\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(z)\n     \
    \     z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n          if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n              return logits.squeeze(-1)\n          return logits\n\n  class DSConv_HalfInteract_Network:\n      def __init__(self, d_input, d_output, task_type, **kwargs):\n          self.network = RNANetHalfInteract(d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, **kwargs)\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n   \
    \       else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'num_heads': 4,\n          'attn_temp': 0.5,\n          'positional_encoding': False\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      d_output = hparams.get('d_output', 1)\n      task_type = hparams.get('task_type', 'regression')\n      return DSConv_HalfInteract_Network(\n          d_input=4,\n          d_output=d_output,\n          task_type=task_type,\n          d_model=hparams.get('d_model', 256),\n          num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks', 5),\n          dilations=tuple(hparams.get('dilations', [1, 2, 4, 8, 16])),\n  \
    \        kernel_size=hparams.get('kernel_size', 7),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n          num_heads=hparams.get('num_heads', 4),\n          attn_temp=hparams.get('attn_temp', 0.5),\n          positional_encoding=hparams.get('positional_encoding', False),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset')\n      vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning next steps**\n\nI'm setting the next steps based on the current situation. At tick 66, I see I've got a SOTA of 0.6801, but the negative results draft is stored. Since there are no running experiments, it’s a good time to think about future research directions or maybe prune tokens. I’m cautious about constraints since I can't access external data, but I might evaluate modifications to CRI-Off and consider other approaches while maintaining unity in my efforts.**Exploring new ideas**\n\nI’m brainstorming some ideas! One approach is to introduce a two-tower co-attention pool that summarizes both halves, followed by attention gating. We’ve already tried cross-half bilinear but could shift to cross-half co-attention with fixed queries for better interactions. Another idea is using feature-wise linear modulation (FiLM) gating to let one half condition the other’s features more effectively. Lastly, I’m considering a \"Product of Experts\" gating post-pooling, combining\
  \ the base vector with element-wise operations to capture pairwise interactions better. That sounds promising!**Investigating CRISPR Off methods**\n\nFor CRISPR Off, I’m considering element-wise products between left and right features, while keeping a unified approach by splitting the sequence in half, which might be beneficial. I could enhance the pooled representation by adding features like means and products through an MLP. \n\nAnother direction could be weighted offset correlation pooling, building on past experiments, and maybe gating or using multiple learned offsets could help. I also have thoughts on tuning the attention temperature, where 0.5 seemed best, and exploring label smoothing for classification tasks, even in fixed-loss scenarios. That could be interesting!**Exploring alternate pooling methods**\n\nSince I can't modify the training loop, one idea is to try alternate pooling methods like Efficient Channel Attention (ECA) global gating, which may be lighter than Squeeze-and-Excitation\
  \ (SE) that performed poorly before. \n\nI could also explore different normalization techniques—group normalization or others—since previous attempts with RMSNorm didn't help, although Layer Normalization (LN) has been stable. \n\nGiven the current SOTA is only slightly ahead, I should also plan to publish the negative-results paper and consider adding an experiment with unified two-tower co-attention pooling. However, I must be cautious of performance degradation across various tasks.**Designing a new pooling model**\n\nI’m planning a research submission that implements a new pooling model variant without modifying the training loop. I have enough token budget to proceed, so I’ll propose \"No-PE + Dual-Half Fixed Co-Attention Pooling\" while keeping the base structure like SOTA.\n\nMy approach involves splitting features from left and right halves, applying fixed-query multi-head attention (MHA) pooling, and computing interaction features like element-wise products and absolute differences.\
  \ I'll use Layer Normalization and design two modules: one for MHA pooling and another for global pooling. This could capture pairwise interactions effectively while managing parameters. Time to compile the code!**Implementing half MHA pooling**\n\nI’m working on computing half MHA for the left and right features, pl and pr, and then I'll calculate their interactions, using element-wise products and absolute differences. Those will be fused together, processed through a Dense layer, and then passed through a series of transformations to produce the final output vector.\n\nI’ll set hyperparameters consistent with SOTA, like a learning rate of 0.001 and a model dimension of 256. I want to tag this submission with key elements like \"interaction features\" and \"no positional encoding.\" \n\nI’ll ensure the code is well-structured, include all necessary imports, and maintain formatting for the YAML. After that, I can update the memory and plan future submissions as needed. Time to implement!"
