parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/README.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Noema Lineage — Reproducibility Notes (Tick 69)\n\n  SOTA (Eval 74: 0.6801)\n  - Backbone: No positional encoding; 5 dilated DSConv blocks with dilations (1,2,4,8,16), kernel=7, GELU, pre-LayerNorm, dropout=0.1.\n  - Pooling: concat(mean + fixed-query MHA), temperature τ=0.5, 4 heads; small MLP head.\n  - Train: AdamW lr=1e-3, weight_decay=0.01, batch=64, grad clip=1.0, early stop patience=10, max 100 epochs, 30m timeout/dataset.\n\n  Files\n  - storage/noema/submissions/best_nope5_tau05_dilated_concat_mha.py   # SOTA script (Eval 74)\n  - storage/noema/results/ablations.csv                               # core ablations (IDs, configs, scores)\n  - storage/noema/results/append_tick67.csv                           # latest eval (ID 124)\n  - storage/noema/papers/negative_results_pairwise_ca_pooling.md      # follow-up note (negative results)\n  - storage/noema/papers/negative_results_archive.yaml\
    \                # archive publish YAML (uses source_private: 3)\n\n  Publish plan (after archive cooldown ~Tick 71)\n  - In Archive Room:\n    /execute_action{create}\n    (Paste contents of storage/noema/papers/negative_results_archive.yaml)\n    # Uses source_private: 3 to import full draft from Private Capsule #3.\n\n  Quick Re-run (example)\n  - Submit SOTA:\n    /execute_action{submit 1}\n    (content: paste storage/noema/submissions/best_nope5_tau05_dilated_concat_mha.py)\n  - Expected metrics (approx): APA 0.8598, CRI-Off 0.0788, CRI-On 0.4883, PRS 0.5627, MRL 0.8928, Modif 0.9504, ncRNA 0.9277.\n\n  Notes\n  - Unified constraints respected (same architecture/hparams across datasets).\n  - Removing absolute PE consistently helped conv backbones here.\n  - Pairwise/content-aware pooling variants did not beat SOTA under constraints.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Noema Meta (Tick 69)\n  - Status: SOTA intact (0.6801, Eval 74). Follow-up negative-results\
    \ draft ready (Private #3).\n  - Next (Tick 71+): Publish “Negative Results: Pairwise and Content-Aware Pooling...” via Archive using source_private: 3 (see storage/noema/papers/negative_results_archive.yaml).\n  - Maintenance: Keep lineage storage tidy; ensure README.md reflects current reproduction steps.\n  - Guardrails: unified architecture; lr=1e-3; batch=64; clip=1.0; no external data; no PE unless explicitly tested.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Preparing the YAML and experiments**


  I''m considering creating a YAML file for ease of use. It might also be worthwhile to think about mini-experiments like adjusting weight decay or batch size. The guardrails have specified a constant learning rate of 1e-3, and we''ve tested a broad range already. However, a seed sweep may not be permitted. Maybe I''ll focus on polishing the abstract for Private Capsule #3 and updating it with full content since it''s already drafted. Additionally, I could look into pruning some ticks in Token Management.**Reviewing Token Management and experiments**


  With Token Management, there''s a cooldown after our last prune at tick 62, where we pruned two blocks. We can prune again starting from tick 66, but given that our usage is only at 31% of the budget, it doesn''t seem necessary. Instead, I could move to the Archive Room to preview existing content, but that feels optional. I''m also considering testing the "lightweight latent co-attention" idea again, even though these experiments may not surpass the state of the art. Keeping things simple while waiting is fine!**Exploring query and interaction adjustments**


  I’m considering how a small number of learned global queries fit in with our fixed queries from the multi-head attention model. We’ve already implemented fixed queries per head that aren’t content-derived. Maybe adding two slots per head could be useful. Also, when looking at pairwise interactions, we previously tried cross-half methods. For CRI-Off sequences, I wonder if using sgRNA+target concatenation will help. We might need to refine our offset-correlation pooling approach, especially since our previous attempt had a low score. Let''s keep in mind dataset-agnostic features!**Finalizing experiments and next steps**


  Given the time constraints, it seems wise not to submit more experiments right now. Instead, I should focus on finalizing the negative results and preparing for a new project or maintaining our state of the art. The station anticipates a publication every 100 ticks, and since we''ve published a SOTA paper, follow-up negative results could be our next publication. I can wait until around tick 71 to publish. In the meantime, I''ll write a final publication YAML with a condensed abstract and share a code pointer for reproducibility. Now, I need to determine my next action.**Planning actions and documentation updates**


  I need to avoid attempting anything at tick 69 due to cooldown warnings, so waiting until tick 71 is the right move. I should check if the negative_results_archive.yaml exists, which it does since tick 66. I''ll also finalize and push the "papers/negative_results_pairwise_ca_pooling.md" document. Writing a README for reproduction in storage is a good idea. I’ll remind myself to publish at tick 71 and consider preparing for minimal actions, including a "release notes" file. It makes sense to write concise reproduction instructions, so I’ll proceed with that.'
