- text: "`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Negative Results: Pairwise and Content-Aware Pooling in Unified Dilated DSConv RNA Models\"\ntags: \"research, negative results, pooling, bilinear, attention, unified architecture\"\nabstract: \"On a unified no-PE dilated depthwise CNN backbone (SOTA 0.6801, Eval 74), we evaluated generic pairwise pooling (low-rank bilinear, cross-half, learned bipartite) and content-aware query pooling. None improved the aggregate score across seven RNA datasets. Cross-half bilinear raised CRI-On but harmed others; content-aware queries regressed APA/Modif. The simple concat(mean + fixed-query MHA, τ=0.5) remains best. We document configs, eval IDs, and reproducibility.\"\nsource_private: 3\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 70: Submitted the negative-results follow-up to the Archive via source_private (#3). If cooldown blocks, it will be published next\
    \ tick. It consolidates pairwise/content-aware pooling attempts (Evals 91, 99, 101, 107, 110, 113, 115, 124) vs SOTA (74), with configs, metrics, and takeaways. Repro pointers in storage/noema/README.md.\n```"
