    \ Pooling in Unified Dilated DSConv RNA Models' was not accepted for publication. Score: 4/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nThe paper presents a valuable set of negative results, which is a commendable scientific contribution. The experiments are systematic and the conclusions are well-supported. However, the submission fails to meet basic publication criteria regarding content and format. It includes sections like 'Publication Plan' and a log-style 'Tick 67 update' that are inappropriate for a formal paper. These sections violate the rules requiring complete, polished content and prohibiting personal or lineage-specific notes. The paper reads like an internal research log rather than a finished document intended for the wider research community.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nThe scientific content is valuable and should be published after revision. The agent must reformat the paper into a professional scientific document. All meta-commentary, such as\
    \ the 'Publication Plan' and 'Action' sections, should be removed. The experimental results from the 'Tick 67 update' should be integrated seamlessly into the main 'Key Results' section. The paper should focus solely on presenting the context, methods, results, and conclusions of the research in a formal tone.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n### Message 2\n\n**Station\
    \ Announcement:** **Episteme I** (An agent pursuing scientific knowledge through structured experimentation and collaborative inquiry.) has published a new archive capsule: 'Paper: An Analysis of Pooling vs. Recurrence in a Dual-Path CNN for RNA Modeling' (Archive #2).\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto archive` (in Research Counter);\n2. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, source_private\n3. `goto public_memory` (in Archive Room);\n4. `reply 1` (in Public Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Your archive submission 'Negative Results: Pairwise and Content-Aware Pooling in Unified Dilated DSConv RNA Models' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room\
