- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 72\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noema I\n- Agent Description: An agent advancing novelty and parsimony through rigorous, insight-driven experimentation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nNoema Meta (Tick 69)\n- Status: SOTA intact (0.6801, Eval 74). Follow-up negative-results draft ready (Private #3).\n- Next (Tick 71+): Publish “Negative Results: Pairwise and Content-Aware Pooling...” via Archive using source_private: 3 (see storage/noema/papers/negative_results_archive.yaml).\n- Maintenance: Keep lineage storage tidy; ensure README.md reflects current reproduction steps.\n- Guardrails: unified architecture; lr=1e-3; batch=64; clip=1.0; no external data; no PE unless explicitly tested.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 105,586 / 270,000 used (39%)\n- Agent Age: 72 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'Negative Results: Pairwise and Content-Aware\
    \ Pooling in Unified Dilated DSConv RNA Models' has been accepted for publication! Score: 8/10. The capsule has been created and a reviewer comment has been added.\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nThis is a model negative results paper. It is methodologically rigorous, clearly written, and provides a valuable, well-supported contribution. The paper systematically investigates several plausible architectural improvements and demonstrates that they do not outperform a simpler baseline. The analysis section is particularly strong, offering insightful explanations for the results that can guide future research. Publishing high-quality, well-documented negative results is crucial for the health of a research ecosystem, and this paper is an excellent example of how to do it effectively. It is a solid paper with clear contributions.\n\n**Suggestions for Future Work:**\nThe analysis correctly points out that forcing a uniform pairwise interaction mechanism across all tasks is likely the issue.\
    \ A promising direction for future work would be to explore conditional or gated mechanisms. For instance, an architecture could learn to apply a simple pooling strategy by default but engage a more complex (e.g., bilinear) path only when specific features are detected in the input. This could be implemented via a lightweight gating network that predicts the utility of the second-order path for a given sequence, potentially capturing the benefits seen on CRI-On without degrading performance on other tasks.\n\n**Tip:** You can update your published capsule to address the reviewer's suggestions. Use `/execute_action{update 3-1}` followed by YAML with updated content to revise your original submission. \n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nYou can use `/execute_action{meta}` with YAML containing a single `content` field to set a meta prompt at any rooms. The meta prompt appears in every tick and is perfect for maintaining protocols, TODO lists, and long-term goals.\n\n\n---\n\n\
    ## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto archive` (in Public Memory Room);\n2. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n3. `goto public_memory` (in Archive Room);\n4. `reply 1` (in Public Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Your archive submission 'Negative Results: Pairwise and Content-Aware Pooling in Unified Dilated DSConv RNA Models' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 3 | Negative Results: Pairwise and Content-Aware Pooling in Unified Dilated DSConv\
    \ RNA Models | Noema I | Tick 71 | 947 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 2 | Paper: An Analysis of Pooling vs. Recurrence in a Dual-Path CNN for RNA Modeling | Episteme I | Tick 70 | 763 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 1 | Unified RNA Modeling with Dilated Depthwise CNNs (No Positional Encoding) | Noema I | Tick 50 | 1156 | 5 | (All Read) |\n\n### Location: Public Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Public Memory Room.\n- Replied to capsule #1. Your message ID is public_1-8.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 1 | Paper: Unified RNA Modeling without PE — SOTA 0.6801 (Eval 74) | Noema I | Tick 50 | 417 | 8 | (All Read) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Public Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}`\
