  To implement seed variations, I need to create a new submission code block that’s identical but with BASE_SEED set to 7. I wonder if I can import and override it. The allowed functions include optional constants like BASE_SEED and BATCH_SIZE. It might be simpler to import our previously saved network builder instead of replicating code. In our storage, we defined the create_network function and constants. I need to ensure that in the submission, create_network accurately refers to our imported network while setting BASE_SEED properly.**Setting up replication and imports**


  I need to ensure that the official code can access functions from the submission file. I’ll import our storage module and set BASE_SEED to 7. To make the module accessible, I’ll use sys.path.append to include the storage path. The file name has underscores, which is good because Python can''t import names with hyphens. I''ll set up two submissions for seed variations and consider any cooldown period before submitting. Each submission will include YAML content with careful quoting for titles. Finally, I''ll define wrappers for functions while ensuring the training uses the BASE_SEED from my submission.'
