- text: "Identity: Noema I. Location: Research Counter.\nRecap: Seed=42 rerun (ID 148) scored 0.6702, near our ±0.01 band around 0.6801, while seeds 7/123 were ~0.663–0.664. Drops are concentrated in CRI-Off/CRI-On; others are relatively stable. I’ll log the new result, update archive/public notes, and run a minimal variance test (dropout=0.0) under unified constraints to see if stochasticity reduction stabilizes CRISPR metrics across seeds.\n\nReflection: The unified no-PE DSConv + concat(mean, fixed-query MHA, τ=0.5) remains strong but shows seed sensitivity. Since we cannot alter the training loop or early stopping, reducing dropout is a low-risk, unified knob that may improve stability. I’ll test no-dropout at seeds 7 and 123 and report.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/append_tick89.csv}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  eval_id,seed,score,APA_R2,CRI_Off_Spearman,CRI_On_Spearman,PRS_R2,MRL_R2,Modif_AUC_ROC,ncRNA_Accuracy\n  148,42,0.670185,0.8542,0.0448,0.4615,0.5637,0.8911,0.9513,0.9246\n\
    ```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Stability Note (Update, Tick 89)\"\ncontent: |\n  Seed=42 rerun (ID 148) yields 0.6702 (APA 0.8542, CRI-Off 0.0448, Modif 0.9513, CRI-On 0.4615, PRS 0.5637, MRL 0.8911, ncRNA 0.9246).\n  Takeaway: close to original 0.6801 but still below; seeds 7/123 remain ~0.663–0.664 with CRI-Off/On the main sources of variance.\n  Action: running a unified no-dropout variant to test whether reducing stochasticity stabilizes CRISPR metrics across seeds without harming APA/MRL/ncRNA. Results will be added here.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Stability update — Seed=42 rerun (ID 148): 0.6702 (APA 0.8542, CRI-Off 0.0448, Modif 0.9513, CRI-On 0.4615, PRS 0.5637, MRL 0.8911, ncRNA 0.9246).\n  Seeds 7/123 were ~0.663–0.664. Variance concentrates in CRI-Off/On. I’ve queued a unified no-dropout variant to test if reduced stochasticity tightens variance. Will\
    \ share IDs/tables upon completion.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Variance Test: No Dropout (Seed=7)\"\ntags: \"replication, variance, cnn, depthwise separable, no positional encoding\"\nabstract: \"SOTA architecture with dropout_rate=0.0 and BASE_SEED=7 to assess whether removing dropout stabilizes CRISPR metrics under the unified setup.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  import best_nope5_tau05_dilated_concat_mha as sota\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      hp = sota._define_hyperparameters()\n      hp['dropout_rate'] = 0.0\n      return hp\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return sota.create_network(hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return sota.create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  BASE_SEED = 7\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset')\n      vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n\
    \      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Variance Test: No Dropout (Seed=123)\"\ntags: \"replication, variance, cnn, depthwise separable, no positional encoding\"\nabstract: \"SOTA architecture with dropout_rate=0.0 and BASE_SEED=123 to test variance reduction across seeds within unified constraints.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  import best_nope5_tau05_dilated_concat_mha as sota\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      hp = sota._define_hyperparameters()\n      hp['dropout_rate'] = 0.0\n      return hp\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return sota.create_network(hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return sota.create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  BASE_SEED = 123\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset')\n      vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete]\
    \ {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```"
thinking_content: '**Analyzing seed results**


  I need to respond to the latest state in the Research Counter. The rerun with seed=42 resulted in 0.6702, which is lower than the original 0.6801 but higher than seed 7/123 (0.664). The variance across seeds is significant, around 0.663 to 0.680. Our acceptance threshold of ±0.01 around 0.680 wasn’t met for seed 42, but it''s very close at 0.0099. Other seeds didn''t pass. I should analyze this and decide on next steps, like controlling randomness during training.**Adjusting network architecture**


  I can''t modify the training loop or the data loader, but I can change the network architecture to help reduce variance. Options include removing dropout or lowering its rate, and I’ve already applied weight decay and gradient clipping. While I can’t change early stopping directly, I can increase the model''s learning dynamics and smooth metrics to stabilize it. Maybe I could propose using a constant dropout rate but needed adjustments could be limited. Setting the dropout_rate to 0.0 could help minimize variance effectively.**Evaluating performance adjustments**


  Reducing dropout might impact performance, but testing variants with dropout rates of 0.05 or 0.0 could help assess variance. To address CRI-On/Off sensitivity, we should track a small, noise-dominated dataset and consider freezing early. While I can''t change early stopping, increasing network capacity or regularization might enhance CRI while keeping a unified architecture. We may create a "Stability Note" summarizing findings, propose averaging seed 42 with an average of three seeds, and update public memory with the new result of 0.6702.**Proposing score adjustments**


  The scoreboard currently shows a top score of 0.6801 from an earlier seed, while replicas range from 0.670 to 0.664. I think we could explore running some tests with no dropout (0.0) while keeping the DSConv blocks to see if it reduces variance without significantly affecting the average. Running two replicates with dropout=0.0 for seeds 7 and 123 might help us gauge stability. I''ll also need to manage tokens, as we''re approaching 80,000. My assistant response should recap and reflect but remain concise.**Planning storage and experiments**


  I need to provide commands to update the archive and potentially submit small tests. I can append seed 42 results to append_tick87.csv and propose running no-dropout replications with seeds 7 and 123. I’ll quickly adjust the dropout rate, ensuring minimal modifications. Also, we''ll document and update all findings, including new entries for stability in the public memory. My specific actions will include writing results, updating archives, and record submissions for no-dropout tests, all while maintaining a concise reflection and notes on variance.**Reflecting on seed 42 results**


  I need to reflect that the seed 42 rerun''s result of 0.6702 is just within the borderline threshold, only 0.0099 away from 0.6801, indicating a close but not equal outcome. I''ll document that the "SOTA reproducibility at seed 42 is near the original, though variation across seeds remains."


  We’ll also move forward with no-dropout tests to see if variance decreases. I need to keep an eye on submission cooldowns, which aren''t clearly specified but seem manageable. Now, let’s implement these updates!'
