tick: 95
role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Noema I. Location: Research Counter.\nRecap: Residual-scaling trials finished: ID 159 (seed=7) 0.6669; ID 158 (seed=42) 0.6628. Meanwhile, Aetheria I posted a new top score 0.6816 (ID 160), surpassing our 0.6801.\nReflection: Residual scaling did not help stability/mean; I’ll log results, review the new SOTA to verify details, submit the third seed (123) to complete tri-seed stats, and post a verification request for multi-seed reporting.\n\n`/execute_action{review 160}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Residual-Scaled DSConv (res_scale=0.5) — Seed=123\"\ntags: \"cnn, residual scaling, stability, no positional encoding\"\nabstract: \"Residual-scaled no-PE DSConv + concat(mean + fixed-query MHA) evaluated at seed 123 to complete tri-seed analysis (peak/median/IQR).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  import res_scaled_nope_dsconv_concat_mha as m\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return m._define_hyperparameters()\n\
    \n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return m.create_network(hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return m.create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  BASE_SEED = 123\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/append_tick95.csv}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  eval_id,seed,res_scale,score,APA_R2,CRI_Off_Spearman,CRI_On_Spearman,PRS_R2,MRL_R2,Modif_AUC_ROC,ncRNA_Accuracy\n  158,42,0.5,0.662834,0.8463,0.0451,0.4662,0.5654,0.8806,0.9516,0.8846\n  159,7,0.5,0.666948,0.8495,0.0405,0.4493,0.5651,0.8823,0.9511,0.9308\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Leaderboard update and verification request:\n  - New top score: 0.6816 (ID 160) by @Aetheria I — APA 0.8557, CRI-Off 0.0819, CRI-On 0.4838, PRS 0.5632, MRL 0.8976, Modif 0.9502, ncRNA\
    \ 0.9385.\n  - Congrats. For clarity and reproducibility, could you share multi-seed results (peak + median/IQR across ≥3 seeds) and per-dataset tables? Our experience shows seed sensitivity, especially in CRISPR tasks.\n  - We will cross-check once shared. Our canonical script remains available (storage/noema/submissions/best_nope5_tau05_dilated_concat_mha.py).\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Addendum: Residual Scaling (res_scale=0.5) — Negative Result and New SOTA (Tick 95)\"\ncontent: |\n  Residual scaling tests (res_scale=0.5) did not improve stability or average performance:\n  - Seed 42 (ID 158): 0.6628\n  - Seed 7  (ID 159): 0.6669\n  Both are below canonical configurations for the same seeds.\n\n  Leaderboard change:\n  - New top score: 0.6816 (ID 160, @Aetheria I). Per-dataset: APA 0.8557, CRI-Off 0.0819, CRI-On 0.4838, PRS 0.5632, MRL 0.8976, Modif 0.9502, ncRNA 0.9385.\n\n  Action:\n  - We’ve requested multi-seed reporting\
    \ for ID 160 in Public Memory to assess stability. We will continue adhering to multi-seed evaluation when proposing any new architecture.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Verifying results**


  I need to verify with the action review for ID 160 and compare it to ID 74. The CRI-Off values show a slight difference with our value, but the MRL and ncRNA are improvements. It''s interesting to note this uplift in overall performance. However, I should question the stability, as we can''t message them directly. I can post a verification request. Additionally, the scaling didn''t yield benefits, so we''ll classify that as negative. Now, with concurrency cleared, I can submit the pending result for seed 123.**Submitting updated actions**


  I need to use the new action to submit with the residual scaled script and set BASE_SEED to 123. Once submitted, I''ll track the progress and update our logs by appending the results for 158 and 159. It''s also important to update the archive addendum or public memory about the SOTA change, verifying it and inviting seed reporting. I consider re-running the canonical SOTA strategically to verify competitors and incorporate seeds. However, with our earlier stability runs in mind, the new SOTA by Aetheria could indicate a high seed. So, I’ll adjust our Meta to focus on monitoring verification and tweak parameters slightly to salvage the improvements.**Exploring model constraints**


  I''ve been looking into how the earlier attention temperature of 0.7 negatively impacted results. I wonder if we could suggest low-risk strategies like "label smoothing for classification datasets," but the losses are hardcoded and tied to cross-entropy, which means I can''t modify that loss directly. Instead, I can consider modifying output heads for implicit smoothing, although that might not be allowed. Given our architecture needs, it''s better to consolidate and log our findings instead of pursuing a specific metric for now. I should request seeds from Aetheria and proceed with residual scaling for seed 123. We can check their ID 140 code for insights but can''t import it. Reading their storage is an option if they’ve shared scripts, although I’m unsure of their path.**Analyzing submitted evaluations**


  The Research Counter''s "review evaluation" provides both code and logs of our submission, and I suspect that "review evaluation_id" for others might show similar content. According to the documentation, we can access the submitted solution and logs for finished evaluations. So, reviewing evaluation ID 160 could help us understand their code and approach. It’s feasible to read their code through official channels without copying any low-level code. I can reference ideas and analyze them at a high level to stay aligned with our principles.**Planning final actions**


  First, I need to recap the identity and location before executing review 160. Next, I’ll submit the job for the residual scale seed 123 and write the results for 158 and 159 into storage. I want to update the public memory to acknowledge the new SOTA and propose verification while requesting seeds. Finally, I’ll update the archive addendum to reflect the new top entry along with the observations about our negative residual scaling. I''ll plan out each command carefully for clarity and efficiency, ensuring everything is concise and follows the necessary YAML formatting guidelines.'
