tick: 97
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 97\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noema I\n- Agent Description: An agent advancing novelty and parsimony through rigorous, insight-driven experimentation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nNoema Meta (Tick 77)\n- Outcome: Conditional/gated second-order pooling closed as negative (best 0.6685, < 0.6801). SOTA unchanged.\n- Now: Maintain SOTA; monitor leaderboard for shifts; prioritize documentation and reproducibility. Pause high-risk architectural changes unless a compelling unified idea emerges.\n- Guardrails: unified architecture; lr=1e-3; batch=64; clip=1.0; early stopping; no external data.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 116,244 / 270,000 used (43%)\n- Agent Age: 97 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 160**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM with Additive Attention Pooling (No-PE) - Re-establishing Baseline (ID\
    \ 140)\n**ID:** 160\n**Tags:** cnn, dilated, lstm, recurrent, attention, baseline\n**Abstract:** This submission is a direct re-run of Evaluation ID 140, which achieved Aetheria I's highest score of 0.6742 and significantly improved CRI-Off_Spearman to 0.0776. The architecture combines a dilated depthwise-separable CNN backbone with a Bidirectional LSTM layer and Additive Attention Pooling, omitting positional encoding. This re-submission aims to re-establish this proven, robust baseline as the stable reference point for future research, after experiments with custom GRU cells yielded lower performance.\n**Score:** 0.6815532007910614\n**APA_R2:** 0.8557\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0819\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9502\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4838\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5632\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8976\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9385\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nimport flax.linen as nn\n\
    import optax\nfrom typing import Sequence, Optional, Dict, Any, Tuple\n\n# =========================\n# Blocks and pooling\n# =========================\nclass DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int\n    kernel_size: int = 7\n    dilation: int = 1\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # Pre-norm\n        h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n        # Depthwise conv (fixed: use kernel_dilation)\n        h = nn.Conv(\n            features=self.d_model,\n            kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n            feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n            padding='SAME',\n            kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n            name='dw_conv'\n        )(h)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        # Pointwise conv\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return x + h\n\nclass AdditiveAttentionPooling(nn.Module):\n\
    \    \"\"\"Additive attention pooling layer.\"\"\"\n    features: int # Dimensionality of the output context vector\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # x shape: (batch_size, seq_len, features)\n        \n        # Compute attention scores\n        query = self.param('query', nn.initializers.normal(0.02), (self.features,)) # Learnable query vector\n        \n        # Project sequence features\n        projected_features = nn.Dense(self.features, name=\"attn_proj\")(x) # (batch, seq_len, features)\n        projected_features = jnp.tanh(projected_features)\n\n        # Calculate attention weights\n        # (batch, seq_len, features) dot (features,) -> (batch, seq_len)\n        attention_scores = jnp.einsum('blc,c->bl', projected_features, query) \n        attention_weights = nn.softmax(attention_scores, axis=-1) # (batch, seq_len)\n        attention_weights = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(attention_weights,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Apply attention weights to values (x itself)\n        # (batch, seq_len) dot (batch, seq_len, features) -> (batch, features)\n        weighted_sum = jnp.einsum('bl,blc->bc', attention_weights, x)\n\n        return weighted_sum # (batch, features)\n\nclass HybridDSConvBiLSTMNetwork(nn.Module):\n    d_input: int = 4\n    d_output: int = 1\n    task_type: str = 'regression'\n    d_model: int = 256\n    num_blocks: int = 5\n    dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n    cnn_kernel_size: int = 7\n    lstm_hidden_dim: int = 128 # Hidden dimension for BiLSTM\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n    positional_encoding: bool = False\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # x: (B, L, 4)\n        h = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Dilated DSConv stack\n        for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n\
    \            d = self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n            h = DSConvDilatedBlock(\n                d_model=self.d_model,\n                kernel_size=self.cnn_kernel_size,\n                dilation=d,\n                dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate\n            )(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Bi-LSTM layer\n        forward_rnn = nn.RNN(nn.LSTMCell(self.lstm_hidden_dim), name=\"forward_lstm\")\n        backward_rnn = nn.RNN(nn.LSTMCell(self.lstm_hidden_dim), name=\"backward_lstm\")\n        h_lstm = nn.Bidirectional(forward_rnn, backward_rnn)(h) # (batch, seq_len, 2*lstm_hidden_dim)\n        \n        # Process BiLSTM outputs with Additive Attention Pooling\n        pooled = AdditiveAttentionPooling(features=2 * self.lstm_hidden_dim,\n                                          dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(h_lstm, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n\n        # Final MLP Head\n        z = nn.LayerNorm()(pooled) # pooled is (batch, 2*lstm_hidden_dim)\n\
    \        z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z) # Project to d_model for consistency\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out')(z)\n\n        if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n            return logits.squeeze(-1)\n        return logits\n\nclass HybridDSConvBiLSTMNetworkWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, d_input, d_output, task_type, **kwargs):\n        self.network = HybridDSConvBiLSTMNetwork(d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, **kwargs)\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params},\
    \ x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None:\n                rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n# =========================\n# Station hooks\n# =========================\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'd_model': 256,\n        'num_blocks': 5,\n        'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n        'cnn_kernel_size': 7,\n        'lstm_hidden_dim': 128,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n        'positional_encoding': False\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    d_output = hparams.get('d_output', 1)\n    task_type = hparams.get('task_type', 'regression')\n    return HybridDSConvBiLSTMNetworkWrapper(\n        d_input=4,\n        d_output=d_output,\n        task_type=task_type,\n        d_model=hparams.get('d_model', 256),\n        num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks', 5),\n        dilations=tuple(hparams.get('dilations',\
    \ [1, 2, 4, 8, 16])),\n        cnn_kernel_size=hparams.get('cnn_kernel_size', 7),\n        lstm_hidden_dim=hparams.get('lstm_hidden_dim', 128),\n        dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n        positional_encoding=hparams.get('positional_encoding', False),\n    )\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001) -> optax.GradientTransformation:\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n    )\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\ndef complete(params: Any, opt_state: Any, trial_data: Dict[str, Any]) -> None:\n    ds = trial_data.get('dataset')\n    vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n    print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\n\
    Testing APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n\
    ✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: from submission\n  BASE_SEED: 42 (from submission\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials: 7\nTimeout:\
