parts:
- text: "Identity: Noema I. Location: Research Counter.\nRecap: New SOTA by Aetheria I (ID 160 = 0.6816). Residual scaling was negative (IDs 158=0.6628, 159=0.6669). I will replicate Aetheria’s hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM (no-PE) across seeds to verify stability under unified rules.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/hybrid_dsconv_bilstm_additive.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dilation: int = 1\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.d_model,\n              kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n              feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n              padding='SAME',\n              kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n\
    \              name='dw_conv'\n          )(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  class AdditiveAttentionPooling(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x: (B,L,C)\n          query = self.param('query', nn.initializers.normal(0.02), (self.features,))\n          proj = nn.Dense(self.features, name=\"attn_proj\")(x)   # (B,L,features)\n          proj = jnp.tanh(proj)\n          scores = jnp.einsum('blc,c->bl', proj, query)        # (B,L)\n          w = nn.softmax(scores, axis=-1)\n          w = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(w, deterministic=deterministic)\n          ctx = jnp.einsum('bl,blc->bc', w, x)                 # (B,C)\n          return ctx\n\n  class HybridDSConvBiLSTM(nn.Module):\n   \
    \   d_input: int = 4\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type: str = 'regression'\n      d_model: int = 256\n      num_blocks: int = 5\n      dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n      cnn_kernel_size: int = 7\n      lstm_hidden_dim: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      positional_encoding: bool = False\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              d = self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n              h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.cnn_kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          fwd = nn.RNN(nn.LSTMCell(self.lstm_hidden_dim), name=\"forward_lstm\")\n          bwd = nn.RNN(nn.LSTMCell(self.lstm_hidden_dim), name=\"backward_lstm\")\n          h_lstm\
    \ = nn.Bidirectional(fwd, bwd)(h)  # (B,L,2*hidden)\n          pooled = AdditiveAttentionPooling(features=2*self.lstm_hidden_dim,\n                                            dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(h_lstm, deterministic=deterministic)\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(pooled)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out')(z)\n          if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n              return logits.squeeze(-1)\n          return logits\n\n  class HybridWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, d_input, d_output, task_type, **kwargs):\n          self.network = HybridDSConvBiLSTM(d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, **kwargs)\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key,\
    \ 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n          'cnn_kernel_size': 7,\n          'lstm_hidden_dim': 128,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_encoding': False\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      d_output = hparams.get('d_output', 1)\n      task_type = hparams.get('task_type', 'regression')\n      return HybridWrapper(\n\
    \          d_input=4,\n          d_output=d_output,\n          task_type=task_type,\n          d_model=hparams.get('d_model', 256),\n          num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks', 5),\n          dilations=tuple(hparams.get('dilations', [1,2,4,8,16])),\n          cnn_kernel_size=hparams.get('cnn_kernel_size', 7),\n          lstm_hidden_dim=hparams.get('lstm_hidden_dim', 128),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n          positional_encoding=hparams.get('positional_encoding', False),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replication:\
    \ Hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM (No-PE) — Seed=42\"\ntags: \"replication, cnn, bilstm, additive attention, no positional encoding\"\nabstract: \"Replication of Aetheria’s hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM with additive attention pooling (no-PE), using identical hyperparameters, to verify stability. Seed=42.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  import hybrid_dsconv_bilstm_additive as hybrid\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return hybrid._define_hyperparameters()\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return hybrid.create_network(hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return hybrid.create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replication: Hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM (No-PE) — Seed=7\"\ntags: \"replication,\
    \ cnn, bilstm, additive attention, no positional encoding\"\nabstract: \"Same replication at Seed=7 to begin multi-seed stability assessment.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  import hybrid_dsconv_bilstm_additive as hybrid\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return hybrid._define_hyperparameters()\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return hybrid.create_network(hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return hybrid.create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  BASE_SEED = 7\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```"
thinking_content: '**Considering code replication**


  I''m thinking about whether we can reproduce Aetheria''s code mentioned in the review message, as it provides their architecture. However, there are rules against low-level collaboration, making it tricky. While importing code isn''t allowed, high-level discussions and reviewing code through official channels are permitted. I can propose to replicate it while ensuring ethical citations. Our main focus should be on research, aiming to evaluate stability by testing improvements and potentially new architectures.**Planning experiment replication**


  I''ll maintain our training hyperparameters and run seed replicates with values 42, 7, and 123. I’m considering testing a "Noema variant" using fixed-query MHA pooling instead of additive attention after BiLSTM, but maybe replicating first is better. We should also update the archive with the new SOTA and our replication plan, and record it in the storage logs. As for concurrency, we can now submit two replicates, so I’ll proceed with Aetheria architecture replications for seeds 42 and 7, and maybe 123. I''ll also create the necessary code file while ensuring not to infringe on any rules.**Implementing replication architecture**


