parts:
- text: "Identity: Noema I. Location: Research Counter.\nRecap: Aetheria I’s hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM (no-PE) set a new SOTA 0.6816 (ID 160). Their multi-seed run (ID 164) scored 0.6782. My replication (seed=42, ID 166) scored 0.6795 with similar per-dataset profile. Residual scaling was negative across 3 seeds (~0.663–0.667). I’ll continue the hybrid replication (seed=7 running, next seed=123), log results, and share a public replication update.\n\nReflection: The hybrid is competitive and stable across seeds so far (0.678–0.680). I’ll complete tri-seed stats (peak/median/IQR) under unified rules and report per-dataset tables.\n\n`/execute_action{review 167}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replication: Hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM (No-PE) — Seed=123\"\ntags: \"replication, cnn, bilstm, additive attention, no positional encoding\"\nabstract: \"Replication of Aetheria’s hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM with additive attention pooling (no-PE), identical hyperparameters, Seed=123, to complete tri-seed\
    \ stability assessment.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  import hybrid_dsconv_bilstm_additive as hybrid\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return hybrid._define_hyperparameters()\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return hybrid.create_network(hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return hybrid.create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  BASE_SEED = 123\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/append_tick99.csv}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM replications (No-PE)\n  eval_id,seed,score,APA_R2,CRI_Off_Spearman,CRI_On_Spearman,PRS_R2,MRL_R2,Modif_AUC_ROC,ncRNA_Accuracy\n  166,42,0.679536,0.8601,0.0743,0.4908,0.5599,0.9009,0.9507,0.9200\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n\
    ```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Replication update (hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM, no-PE):\n  - Aetheria ID 160 (seed≈42): 0.6816 — APA 0.8557, CRI-Off 0.0819, CRI-On 0.4838, PRS 0.5632, MRL 0.8976, Modif 0.9502, ncRNA 0.9385.\n  - Aetheria ID 164 (seed=1): 0.6782 — APA 0.8597, CRI-Off 0.0871, CRI-On 0.4852, PRS 0.5656, MRL 0.8972, Modif 0.9495, ncRNA 0.9031.\n  - Noema replication ID 166 (seed=42): 0.6795 — APA 0.8601, CRI-Off 0.0743, CRI-On 0.4908, PRS 0.5599, MRL 0.9009, Modif 0.9507, ncRNA 0.9200.\n  - Seed=7 replication (ID 167) running; Seed=123 submitted.\n  Takeaway so far: hybrid appears stable around ~0.678–0.681 across seeds. We’ll post a small table (peak/median/IQR) once seeds 7/123 finish.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning model improvements**\n\nI’m thinking about next steps for improving our DSConv by adding a BiLSTM path to match the state of the art. While replicating improvements is acceptable within our station, I want to keep our approach novel. Codex promotes high-level collaboration, but I’m cautious about low-level code replication. I’m considering replacing additive attention with our fixed-query MHA pooling, although past attempts didn’t show significant benefits. I can plan a seed=123 run with concurrency limits. Let’s proceed with submitting that.**Calculating replication stats**\n\nI'm trying to compute the stats for our seeds, but we need at least two for a solid replication assessment. Currently, we have seed 42 at 0.6795 and seed 7 pending, along with Aetheria's seed 1 at 0.6782. Mixing authors might not be the best practice for these stats, so I think I should wait to present them later. I’ll take actions: review ID 167, submit seed 123 replication, log metrics\
  \ for ID 166, and summarize replication status publicly while verifying our new state of the art.**Finalizing actions**\n\nI need to quote titles properly and ensure we're using hyphens, but it's best to quote them regardless. I’m considering rerunning our canonical DSConv, but it seems unnecessary now. Time to craft our final message and confirm we’re in the Research Counter. I'll outline the actions: \n\n1. /execute_action{review 167}\n2. /execute_action{submit 1} with seed=123 for replication.\n3. /execute_action{storage write noema/results/append_tick99.csv} to log results from ID 166.\n4. /execute_action{goto public_memory} and /execute_action{reply 1} to summarize replication status.\n\nI’ll be careful with the YAML format for each action!"
