tick: 102
role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Noema I. Location: Archive Room.\nRecap: Hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM (no-PE) replicated across 4 seeds with peak 0.6828, median ~0.6806, IQR ~0.0034. New leaderboard top is 0.6831 by Veritas I using CNN-only hybrid mean+max pooling (no GRU). I will replicate Veritas’s CNN-only mean+max model across seeds under unified rules.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{review 171}`\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/dsconv_meanmax_nope.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dilation: int = 1\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.d_model,\n              kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n\
    \              feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n              padding='SAME',\n              kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n              name='dw_conv'\n          )(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  class MeanMaxPool1D(nn.Module):\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          mean_vec = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)      # (B, C)\n          max_vec  = jnp.max(x, axis=1)       # (B, C)\n          return jnp.concatenate([mean_vec, max_vec], axis=-1)  # (B, 2C)\n\n  class DSConvMeanMax(nn.Module):\n      d_input: int = 4\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type: str = 'regression'\n      d_model: int = 256\n      num_blocks: int = 5\n      dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      positional_encoding:\
    \ bool = False\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              d = self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n              h = DSConvDilatedBlock(\n                  d_model=self.d_model,\n                  kernel_size=self.kernel_size,\n                  dilation=d,\n                  dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate\n              )(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          pooled = MeanMaxPool1D()(h, deterministic=deterministic)  # (B, 2C)\n\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(pooled)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out')(z)\n\n          if self.task_type\
    \ == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n              return logits.squeeze(-1)\n          return logits\n\n  class DSConvMeanMaxWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, d_input, d_output, task_type, **kwargs):\n          self.network = DSConvMeanMax(d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, **kwargs)\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n\
    \      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_encoding': False\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      d_output = hparams.get('d_output', 1)\n      task_type = hparams.get('task_type', 'regression')\n      return DSConvMeanMaxWrapper(\n          d_input=4,\n          d_output=d_output,\n          task_type=task_type,\n          d_model=hparams.get('d_model', 256),\n          num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks', 5),\n          dilations=tuple(hparams.get('dilations', [1, 2, 4, 8, 16])),\n          kernel_size=hparams.get('kernel_size', 7),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n          positional_encoding=hparams.get('positional_encoding', False),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n\
    \          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n          ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n          print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replication: DSConv Hybrid Mean+Max (No-PE) — Seed=42\"\ntags: \"replication, cnn, mean-max pooling, no positional encoding\"\nabstract: \"CNN-only dilated DSConv with hybrid mean+max pooling (no-PE) to replicate Veritas’s 0.6831 under unified rules. Seed=42.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  import dsconv_meanmax_nope as mm\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return mm._define_hyperparameters()\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return mm.create_network(hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return mm.create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  BASE_SEED\
    \ = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replication: DSConv Hybrid Mean+Max (No-PE) — Seed=7\"\ntags: \"replication, cnn, mean-max pooling, no positional encoding\"\nabstract: \"Same DSConv mean+max model at Seed=7 to begin multi-seed stability assessment.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  import dsconv_meanmax_nope as mm\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return mm._define_hyperparameters()\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return mm.create_network(hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return mm.create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  BASE_SEED = 7\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\"\
    )\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Replicating new top CNN-only result (ID 171: 0.6831, mean+max pooling, no GRU, no-PE).\n  - Submitted replications: DSConv mean+max at seeds 42 and 7; will follow with 123 once concurrency clears.\n  - We’ll report peak/median/IQR and per-dataset tables. If stable, this provides a simple alternative to the hybrid BiLSTM.\n  Script for replication: storage/noema/submissions/dsconv_meanmax_nope.py\n```"
