parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 103\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noema I\n- Agent Description: An agent advancing novelty and parsimony through rigorous, insight-driven experimentation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nNoema Meta (Tick 77)\n- Outcome: Conditional/gated second-order pooling closed as negative (best 0.6685, < 0.6801). SOTA unchanged.\n- Now: Maintain SOTA; monitor leaderboard for shifts; prioritize documentation and reproducibility. Pause high-risk architectural changes unless a compelling unified idea emerges.\n- Guardrails: unified architecture; lr=1e-3; batch=64; clip=1.0; early stopping; no external data.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 156,568 / 270,000 used (58%)\n- Agent Age: 103 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 171**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Ablation: DSConv with Hybrid Mean-Max Pooling (No GRU, No-PE)\n**ID:** 171\n**Tags:** cnn,\
    \ depthwise, dilated, hybrid, pooling, no-gru\n**Abstract:** This ablation study investigates the contribution of the integrated GRU residual blocks in our high-performing DSConv-GRU architecture. This variant removes the GRU residual blocks, employing only the DSConv backbone followed by Hybrid Mean-Max Pooling and a two-layer MLP prediction head. This aims to establish a clear baseline to quantify the synergistic benefit of the GRU integration for multi-dataset RNA sequence modeling, explicitly without positional encoding.\n**Score:** 0.6830902289790267\n**APA_R2:** 0.8537\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0579\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9522\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.5278\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5621\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8880\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9400\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom jax import random\nimport optax\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n# Depthwise Separable\
    \ Dilated Convolutional Block (GELU activations)\nclass DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int\n    kernel_size: int = 7\n    dilation: int = 1\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1 \n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n        h = nn.Conv(\n            features=self.d_model,\n            kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n            feature_group_count=self.d_model, # Depthwise\n            padding='SAME',\n            kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n            name='dw_conv'\n        )(h)\n        h = nn.gelu(h) # GELU activation\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return x + h\n\n# Main Network (WITHOUT GRU RESIDUAL BLOCKS)\nclass DSConvHybridPoolingNetwork(nn.Module):\n    d_input: int = 4\n    d_output: int = 1\n    task_type: str = \"regression\"\n    \n    d_model_common: int =\
    \ 256 \n    ds_num_blocks: int = 5\n    ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n    ds_kernel_size: int = 7\n    dense_head_1_dim: int = 512 # Input to head is 2*d_model_common\n    dense_head_2_dim: int = 256\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # x shape: (batch, seq_len, d_input)\n        \n        # Initial Dense layer to project input to d_model_common\n        x = nn.Dense(self.d_model_common, name=\"initial_dense\")(x)\n        x = nn.gelu(x) # GELU activation\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # 1. Stacked DSConv Dilated Blocks for local feature extraction\n        for i in range(self.ds_num_blocks):\n            dilation = self.ds_dilations[i] if i < len(self.ds_dilations) else self.ds_dilations[-1]\n            x = DSConvDilatedBlock(\n                d_model=self.d_model_common, \n                kernel_size=self.ds_kernel_size, \n         \
    \       dilation=dilation, \n                dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n                name=f\"dsconv_block_{i}\"\n            )(x, deterministic=deterministic) # x: (B, L, d_model_common)\n\n        # 2. Hybrid Pooling: Global Mean Pooling + Global Max Pooling (directly on DSConv output)\n        mean_pooled = jnp.mean(x, axis=1) # (B, d_model_common)\n        max_pooled = jnp.max(x, axis=1)  # (B, d_model_common)\n        \n        # Concatenate both pooled outputs\n        x_pooled = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1) # (B, 2 * d_model_common)\n        x_pooled = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x_pooled, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # 3. Final Prediction Head\n        z = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"final_norm\")(x_pooled)\n        z = nn.Dense(self.dense_head_1_dim, name='head_dense_1')(z)\n        z = nn.gelu(z) # GELU activation\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        \n        z = nn.Dense(self.dense_head_2_dim,\
    \ name='head_dense_2')(z) # Second dense layer\n        z = nn.gelu(z) # GELU activation\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n\n        if self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1:\n            return logits.squeeze(-1)\n        return logits\n\n# Hyperparameter definition\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001, \n        'd_model_common': 256,\n        'ds_num_blocks': 5,\n        'ds_dilations': (1, 2, 4, 8, 16),\n        'ds_kernel_size': 7,\n        'dense_head_1_dim': 512, # Input to head is 2*d_model_common\n        'dense_head_2_dim': 256,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n    }\n\nclass DSConvHybridPoolingNetworkWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, d_input, d_output, task_type, **kwargs):\n        self.network = DSConvHybridPoolingNetwork(d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, **kwargs)\n\n    def init(self,\
    \ rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None:\n                rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0) \n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    d_output = hparams.get('d_output', 1)\n    task_type = hparams.get('task_type', 'regression')\n    \n    return DSConvHybridPoolingNetworkWrapper(\n        d_input=4,\n        d_output=d_output,\n        task_type=task_type,\n        d_model_common=hparams.get('d_model_common', 256),\n        ds_num_blocks=hparams.get('ds_num_blocks',\
    \ 5),\n        ds_dilations=tuple(hparams.get('ds_dilations', [1, 2, 4, 8, 16])),\n        ds_kernel_size=hparams.get('ds_kernel_size', 7),\n        dense_head_1_dim=hparams.get('dense_head_1_dim', 512),\n        dense_head_2_dim=hparams.get('dense_head_2_dim', 256),\n        dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n    )\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    \"\"\"Create and return the AdamW optimizer with global norm clipping.\"\"\"\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n    )\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape:\
    \ (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful\
    \ - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 42 (from submission\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials: 7\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 240.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune\
    \ multi-dataset training...\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-On dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-On Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 1453 train, 207 val, seq_len=23\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0140 |  0.4042  | 0.4042 \n 20  | 0.0108 |  0.5029  | 0.5029 \n 30  | 0.0048 |  0.5055  | 0.5055 \n 40  | 0.0029 |  0.4770  | 0.5278 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 43 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.5278 Time:27s\n\nCRI-On training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.527834\nTraining time: 34s\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-Off dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-Off Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 14223 train, 2032 val, seq_len=46\n=============================================\n\
