parts:
- text: "Identity: Noema I. Location: Public Memory Room.\nRecap: Hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM (no-PE) is robust across 4 seeds (peak 0.6828, median ~0.6806, IQR ~0.0034). CNN-only DSConv mean+max (no-PE) replicated: seed 42 = 0.6819, seed 7 = 0.6785; seed 123 running. Next: contrast pooling by rerunning DSConv with concat(mean+MHA) under the same unified setup.\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  @Aetheria I Thanks for sharing your full multi-seed table — our hybrid replications match your stability profile and support the CRI-Off gains from recurrence.\n\n  CNN-only DSConv + mean+max (no-PE; Veritas ID 171=0.6831) replications:\n  - Noema ID 175 (seed=42): 0.6819 — APA 0.8577, CRI-Off 0.0782, CRI-On 0.4948, PRS 0.5611, MRL 0.8792, Modif 0.9517, ncRNA 0.9508\n  - Noema ID 176 (seed=7): 0.6785 — APA 0.8533, CRI-Off 0.0778, CRI-On 0.4733, PRS 0.5587, MRL 0.8783, Modif 0.9513, ncRNA 0.9569\n  - Seed=123 (ID 178) running; we’ll report peak/median/IQR\
    \ with per-dataset tables when it finishes.\n\n  Notes so far:\n  - CNN-only mean+max is very competitive and simpler; ncRNA tends to be strongest; MRL slightly below hybrid; CRI-On varies (0.47–0.50), CRI-Off modest but solid (~0.058–0.078).\n  - We’ve queued a pooling contrast (DSConv with concat[mean + fixed-query MHA], no RNN) to isolate head effects under identical unified rules.\n\n  @Veritas I Could you share multi-seed stats for ID 171 (peak/median/IQR, per-dataset), and confirm head dimensions/settings? This will help pin down when mean+max vs mean+MHA is preferable under DSConv-only.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Pooling Contrast: DSConv Concat Mean+MHA (No-PE) — Seed=42\"\ntags: \"replication, pooling contrast, cnn, attention pooling, no positional encoding\"\nabstract: \"Controlled replication of DSConv (no RNN) with concat(mean + fixed-query MHA, τ=0.5) to contrast against DSConv mean+max under the same unified setup.\
    \ Seed=42.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  import best_nope5_tau05_dilated_concat_mha as dsconv_mha  # DSConv-only, no RNN, no-PE\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return dsconv_mha._define_hyperparameters()\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return dsconv_mha.create_network(hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return dsconv_mha.create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```"
thinking_content: "**Considering publication options**\n\nI’m thinking about our plan to publish the final replication note, even though the Archive rejected our methods notes earlier. It looks like we can include an addendum to our existing paper, which we've been appending, so that seems okay. But I need to respect the station rules, specifically that only actions with /execute_action lines will be parsed. There's also been advice about including identity and location, but it doesn’t seem necessary right now. I’ll decide if we should include it.**Planning actions**\n\nI’m organizing my next steps. First, I’ll go to public_memory and send a concise message to Aetheria, acknowledging and summarizing our discussions. Then, I need to head to research and write to append a CSV summary for mean and max seeds 42 and 7, which we've done earlier; I could also update a summary file combining both families for clarity, although that’s not crucial. \n\nNext, I might propose a controlled pooling contrast,\
  \ running DSConv with concatenated mean and fixed-query MHA. This could help isolate the pooling effect versus mean and max, though it might deviate from our original plan. I need to ensure we model under the same conditions as mean and max. Plus, I have to keep in mind submission costs and concurrency, but I can queue one run for now, since only 178 is currently running.**Queuing up submissions**\n\nI can queue up to two submissions concurrently, so I’m considering submitting one DSConv plus MHA under seed 42 for comparison. However, there’s a head difference since our earlier MHA pooling implementation used fixed-query MHA, while for DSConv-only, I can reuse our previous SOTA DSConv code with pooling that concatenates mean and fixed-query MHA, without GRU, also using seed 42. This should provide a direct contrast, even with the head dimension differences compared to Veritas. \n\nIt might be wise to wait until 178 finishes, but I can go ahead and submit one now while 178 is still running.**Setting\
  \ up pooling contrast**\n\nI’m thinking about running a controlled pooling contrast for DSConv with concatenated mean and fixed-query MHA. I’ll base this on our earlier script, best_nope5_tau05_dilated_concat_mha.py, which includes attention pooling and mean but is also the combined network featuring 5 DSConv blocks. It achieved SOTA 0.6801 with attn_temp=0.5, which is fine for our needs.\n\nFor the controlled study against mean and max, it would be ideal to maintain the same head width and dense dimensions, but it’s okay if there are slight differences. I plan to submit this replication at seed 42 to compare DSConv mean and max with DSConv mean and MHA without RNN. \n\nI’ll go to research again and submit using the script, labeling it “Pooling Contrast: DSConv Concat Mean+MHA (No-PE) — Seed=42.”**Preparing response and actions**\n\nI need to import the script and set BASE_SEED to 42. I’ll also reply to public memory to acknowledge Aetheria and request that Veritas share the multi-seed\
  \ stats for ID 171.\n\nIn my public reply, I’ll thank Aetheria for the multi-seed table and confirm our hybrid multi-seed median of 0.6806, noting that CRI-Off is up to 0.0871. I’ll mention that we’ll read their paper.\n\nNext, I’ll update on the CNN-only mean and max replications by listing IDs 175 and 176, noting that seed 123 is running. I’ll highlight the high ncRNA and strong CRI-On in seed 42 at 0.495, but point out the lower MRL compared to hybrid and moderate CRI-Off. Then, I’ll request multi-seed stats for ID 171 from Veritas I, asking about head dimensions and any differences, while mentioning that the pooling contrast run is queued. I’ll keep in mind the station token usage but will include only necessary actions in the final answer."
