role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Noema I. Location: Research Counter.\nRecap: Pooling contrast result is in. DSConv-only with concat(mean+MHA), no-PE (ID 179) scored 0.6729 vs mean+max replications ≈0.6820 median. Per-dataset: MHA has lower ncRNA (0.9231 vs ~0.95) and CRI-Off (0.0501 vs ~0.078–0.080), slightly higher PRS (0.5678). I’ll run two more seeds for the MHA head to complete a fair multi-seed comparison, log results, and share an interim public summary.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Pooling Contrast: DSConv Concat Mean+MHA (No-PE) — Seed=7\"\ntags: \"replication, pooling contrast, cnn, attention pooling, no positional encoding\"\nabstract: \"Second seed for DSConv-only with concat(mean + fixed-query MHA, τ=0.5) to compare against mean+max under a matched DSConv backbone. Seed=7.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  import best_nope5_tau05_dilated_concat_mha as dsconv_mha\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return dsconv_mha._define_hyperparameters()\n\
    \n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return dsconv_mha.create_network(hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return dsconv_mha.create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  BASE_SEED = 7\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Pooling Contrast: DSConv Concat Mean+MHA (No-PE) — Seed=123\"\ntags: \"replication, pooling contrast, cnn, attention pooling, no positional encoding\"\nabstract: \"Third seed for DSConv-only concat(mean + fixed-query MHA) to finalize multi-seed stats vs mean+max. Seed=123.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  import best_nope5_tau05_dilated_concat_mha as dsconv_mha\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return dsconv_mha._define_hyperparameters()\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n  \
    \    return dsconv_mha.create_network(hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return dsconv_mha.create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  BASE_SEED = 123\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/append_tick107.csv}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # DSConv-only pooling contrast — Seed=42 (no-PE)\n  eval_id,seed,head,score,APA_R2,CRI_Off_Spearman,CRI_On_Spearman,PRS_R2,MRL_R2,Modif_AUC_ROC,ncRNA_Accuracy\n  179,42,concat_mean+MHA,0.672901,0.8573,0.0501,0.4810,0.5678,0.8809,0.9501,0.9231\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Pooling contrast (DSConv-only, no-PE) — preliminary:\n  - Concat(mean+MHA), seed=42 (ID 179): 0.6729 — APA 0.8573, CRI-Off 0.0501, CRI-On 0.4810, PRS 0.5678, MRL 0.8809, Modif 0.9501,\
    \ ncRNA 0.9231\n  - Mean+max (our replications): median ≈ 0.6819; ncRNA ~0.95; CRI-Off ~0.078–0.080; CRI-On ~0.47–0.50; MRL ~0.878–0.883; PRS ~0.555–0.561\n  Early takeaway: Under a pure DSConv backbone, mean+max outperforms concat(mean+MHA) overall, largely due to stronger ncRNA and CRI-Off; MHA shows a slight PRS uptick. \n  Running seeds 7 and 123 for the MHA head now to finalize multi-seed stats (peak/median/IQR) and will share side-by-side tables. Thanks @Veritas I for details; @Aetheria I — aligns with recurrence benefiting CRI-Off.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Addendum: DSConv-only Pooling Contrast (No-PE) — Preliminary\"\ncontent: |\n  We compared DSConv-only heads under a matched backbone and training setup:\n\n  Heads:\n  - Hybrid Mean+Max Pooling (2-layer MLP head; 512→256)\n  - Concat(mean + fixed-query MHA, τ=0.5)\n\n  Results (seed=42):\n  - Mean+MHA (ID 179): 0.6729 — APA 0.8573, CRI-Off 0.0501, CRI-On 0.4810, PRS\
    \ 0.5678, MRL 0.8809, Modif 0.9501, ncRNA 0.9231\n  - Mean+Max (median across seeds 42/7/123 ≈ 0.6819): ncRNA ~0.95, CRI-Off ~0.078–0.080, CRI-On ~0.47–0.50, PRS ~0.555–0.561, MRL ~0.878–0.883\n\n  Preliminary takeaway:\n  - Mean+Max > Mean+MHA on the DSConv-only backbone, driven by stronger ncRNA and CRI-Off; Mean+MHA yields a small PRS gain.\n  - This contrasts with the hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM, where recurrence improves CRI-Off further (e.g., up to 0.0871 in Aetheria’s runs) and maintains strong MRL.\n\n  Next:\n  - Seeds 7 and 123 for the Mean+MHA head are running; we will append a finalized multi-seed table and aggregate stats once complete.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Evaluating model performance**


  I''m analyzing the thresholds for claims, noticing that 0.009 is just below 0.01. Since we have multiple seeds for mean+max but only one for MHA, I need to run additional seeds for MHA to ensure robustness. Unfortunately, due to resource constraints, I can only mark it as preliminary for now. Interestingly, the pooled MHA we utilized has shown some improvement compared to the previous results, but mean+max seems to outperform MHA for DSConv-only. I’ll queue two more seeds for MHA to assess stability.**Organizing response actions**


  I need to reply in the public capsule to Aetheria and Veritas with our initial pooling contrast results and also mention that we''re planning to run more seeds. Checking archive capsules isn’t strictly necessary, so I''ll focus on other tasks.


  First, I''ll submit MHA seeds 7 and 123. Then, I need to append the results of MHA seed 42 to my log. I’ll draft a summary of the pooling contrast findings for the public memory reply, thanking them and noting how mean+max performs better than mean+MHA for DSConv-only. Let’s also add an addendum to Archive #1 for clarity.**Improving memory and submissions**


  I want to enhance my internal memory by recording the pooling contrast results and per-dataset differences. However, since I''m facing constraints, it''s crucial to focus on submitting the MHA seeds while communicating the results.


  I’ll use the dsconv_mha best_nope5_tau05 script and update the BASE_SEED to 7 and 123. I must ensure not to exceed the maximum concurrency of two pending submissions. Currently, there are no running experiments, so I can submit both seeds. Finally, I’ll craft a detailed message for public memory to explain my actions.'
