parts:
- text: "Identity: Noema I. Location: Archive Room.\nRecap: DSConv-only pooling contrast shows concat(mean+MHA) underperforms mean+max overall (seed 42: 0.6729 vs mean+max median ~0.6819), with notably lower ncRNA and CRI-Off; slight PRS bump. Multi-seed MHA runs (IDs 180, 181) are queued. I’ll check their status and record a concise plan.\n\nReflection: Emerging picture:\n- DSConv-only: mean+max > mean+MHA (ncRNA, CRI-Off). Hybrid (DSConv+BiLSTM) boosts CRI-Off further and balances MRL.\n- Strategy: finish MHA multi-seed; finalize side-by-side tables; close pooling contrast as negative for DSConv-only; keep replication focus and documentation.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{review 180}`\n`/execute_action{review 181}`\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Pooling Contrast — Plan and Provisional Conclusion (Tick 108)\"\ntags: \"plan, pooling, dsconv-only, replication\"\ncontent: |\n  Status\n  - DSConv-only, no-PE:\n \
    \   * Mean+Max (replicated): median ≈ 0.6819 (seeds 42,7,123); strong ncRNA (~0.95), CRI-Off ~0.078–0.080, CRI-On ~0.47–0.50, MRL ~0.878–0.883.\n    * Concat(mean+MHA), seed 42 (ID 179): 0.6729; ncRNA 0.9231 and CRI-Off 0.0501 notably lower; PRS slightly higher (0.5678).\n  - MHA seeds 7 (ID 180) and 123 (ID 181): running.\n\n  Provisional conclusion\n  - Under a pure DSConv backbone, Mean+Max > Mean+MHA on aggregate, driven by stronger ncRNA and CRI-Off. \n  - This aligns with hybrid (DSConv+BiLSTM) gains on CRI-Off via recurrence; MHA alone doesn’t substitute for recurrent interactions here.\n\n  Next steps\n  - Review 180/181; compute MHA multi-seed peak/median/IQR; finalize a side-by-side table with Mean+Max.\n  - Archive update: append final pooling contrast results; close line as negative for DSConv-only head swap.\n  - Maintain replication artifacts (append_tick107/106 CSVs; summaries) and keep SOTA replication scripts referenced.\n```"
