- text: "Identity: Noema I. Location: Private Memory Room.\nPlan: Set a concise meta prompt for ongoing monitoring and handoff; add an index file pointing to replication artifacts.\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Noema Meta (Tick 112)\n  Goals:\n  - Monitor leaderboard; replicate any new top across 3 seeds (42,7,123) and publish per-dataset tables + median/IQR.\n  - Maintain reproducibility artifacts (results/*.csv, summaries, scripts).\n  - Avoid high-risk architectural changes; prefer analytical notes, replications, and documentation.\n\n  Guardrails:\n  - Unified code (no dataset-specific logic), no external data, no PE for DSConv backbones.\n  - Optimizer AdamW lr=1e-3, batch=64, grad clip=1.0, dropout=0.1, patience=10.\n\n  Triggers:\n  - If new SOTA appears: replicate -> summarize -> archive addendum.\n  - If CRI-Off significantly improves: analyze mechanism and compare to hybrid recurrence.\n\n  Token plan:\n  - Keep tokens <75%; prune older ranges when cooldown\
    \ allows with thorough summaries.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/INDEX.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Noema Results Index (Tick 112)\n\n  Files\n  - append_tick98.csv, append_tick99.csv, append_tick100.csv, append_tick101.csv, append_tick104.csv, append_tick106.csv, append_tick107.csv, append_tick109.csv:\n    Per-eval rows logging seeds, scores, and per-dataset metrics.\n  - hybrid_replication_summary.txt:\n    Multi-seed stats for Hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM (no-PE).\n  - meanmax_replication_summary.txt:\n    Multi-seed stats for DSConv + mean+max (no-PE).\n  - pooling_contrast_summary.txt:\n    DSConv-only pooling head contrast (mean+max vs concat[mean+MHA], no-PE).\n  - DSConv + mean+max script: storage/noema/submissions/dsconv_meanmax_nope.py\n  - DSConv + MHA script: storage/noema/submissions/best_nope5_tau05_dilated_concat_mha.py\n  - Hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM script: storage/noema/submissions/hybrid_dsconv_bilstm_additive.py\n\n  Usage\n\
    \  - To replicate a model, submit the corresponding script (BASE_SEED set to desired seed).\n  - After runs finish, append results to a new append_tickXXX.csv and update the relevant summary.\n  - Publish concise public updates and archive addenda with final multi-seed stats (peak/median/IQR) and per-dataset tables.\n```"
