parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{review 187}`\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/append_tick112.csv}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # New gated dual-path result (Aetheria)\n  eval_id,author,score,APA_R2,CRI_Off_Spearman,CRI_On_Spearman,PRS_R2,MRL_R2,Modif_AUC_ROC,ncRNA_Accuracy\n  187,Aetheria I,0.6821,0.8574,0.0657,0.5116,0.5621,0.8932,0.9525,0.9323\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Quick note on Aetheria’s gated dual-path (ID 187 = 0.6821):\n  - Trade-offs vs DSConv+mean+max SOTA (ID 171 = 0.6831): APA ↑ (0.8574 vs 0.8537), MRL ↑ (0.8932 vs 0.8880), CRI-Off ↑ (0.0657 vs 0.0579), Modif ≈; but CRI-On ↓ (0.5116 vs 0.5278), ncRNA ↓ (0.9323 vs 0.9400) → aggregate still slightly lower.\n  - Suggest keeping the gate minimal and well-regularized (start with scalar α, entropy/L2 around 0.5; freeze-unfreeze), and report per-sequence gate stats with multi-seed medians/IQR. Calibrate so the gate leans toward the CNN path on long/separable\
    \ sequences (benefits ncRNA) without collapsing CRI-On.\n  Logged to storage/noema/results/append_tick112.csv.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Summarizing gating results**\n\nI'm analyzing gating with improved metrics like APA and MRL, which showed slight improvements, but it decreased CRI-On and ncRNA, leading to an overall lower score. It’s essential to mention these trade-offs.  \n\nI might also offer guidance suggesting to calibrate the gate towards CNN for ncRNA. While a dataset-agnostic approach will weight sequences, dataset-specific methods are not allowed. Gating functions should favor CNN for longer sequences, and I need to emphasize that the sequence length differs across datasets while pooling features.**Crafting concise suggestions**\n\nI plan to keep my suggestions generic, like adding KL to the anchor gate distribution, incorporating a small ridge on the gate logit, and calibrating the mixture for each sequence. It’s important to keep my message concise and clear while performing the necessary actions. \n\nNow, I need to craft content for a public reply in a bullet-point format to share these\
  \ insights effectively. Let’s proceed with that approach!"
