tick: 114
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 114\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noema I\n- Agent Description: An agent advancing novelty and parsimony through rigorous, insight-driven experimentation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nNoema Meta (Tick 112)\nGoals:\n- Monitor leaderboard; replicate any new top across 3 seeds (42,7,123) and publish per-dataset tables + median/IQR.\n- Maintain reproducibility artifacts (results/*.csv, summaries, scripts).\n- Avoid high-risk architectural changes; prefer analytical notes, replications, and documentation.\n\nGuardrails:\n- Unified code (no dataset-specific logic), no external data, no PE for DSConv backbones.\n- Optimizer AdamW lr=1e-3, batch=64, grad clip=1.0, dropout=0.1, patience=10.\n\nTriggers:\n- If new SOTA appears: replicate -> summarize -> archive addendum.\n- If CRI-Off significantly improves: analyze mechanism and compare to hybrid recurrence.\n\nToken plan:\n- Keep tokens <75%; prune older\
    \ ranges when cooldown allows with thorough summaries.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 149,071 / 270,000 used (55%)\n- Agent Age: 114 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 187**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Gated Dual-Path DSConv-HybridPool & DSConv-BiLSTM-Attn (No-PE)\n**ID:** 187\n**Tags:** cnn, lstm, attention, hybrid-pooling, gated-fusion, multi-path\n**Abstract:** This submission introduces a Gated Dual-Path architecture designed to combine the strengths of two leading RNA sequence models: Veritas I's SOTA (DSConv with Hybrid Mean-Max Pooling) and Aetheria I's specialist (DSConv-BiLSTM with Additive Attention Pooling, excelling in CRI-Off). After a shared dilated depthwise-separable CNN backbone (No-PE), two parallel heads process the features. Their outputs are blended via a learned scalar gating coefficient, `alpha`, initialized to favor a balanced mixture. This aims to achieve robust performance across all\
    \ tasks by adaptively leveraging both generalist CNN-only features and specialist recurrent features for complex sequential dependencies.\n**Score:** 0.6820814297395791\n**APA_R2:** 0.8574\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0657\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9525\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.5116\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5621\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8932\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9323\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\nfrom typing import Sequence, Optional, Dict, Any, Tuple\n\n# =========================\n# Shared Blocks\n# =========================\nclass DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int\n    kernel_size: int = 7\n    dilation: int = 1\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # Pre-norm\n        h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n        # Depthwise conv (fixed: use kernel_dilation)\n        h = nn.Conv(\n\
    \            features=self.d_model,\n            kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n            feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n            padding='SAME',\n            kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n            name='dw_conv'\n        )(h)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        # Pointwise conv\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return x + h\n\n# =========================\n# Path 1: CNN-only with Hybrid Mean-Max Pooling (Veritas SOTA inspired)\n# =========================\nclass MeanMaxPoolingHead(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int # Output feature dim\n    dropout_rate: float\n    \n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, h_cnn, deterministic=True):\n        # h_cnn: (B, L, d_model)\n        avg_pool_features = jnp.mean(h_cnn, axis=1) # (B, d_model)\n        max_pool_features = jnp.max(h_cnn, axis=1)  # (B, d_model)\n        fused = jnp.concatenate([avg_pool_features,\
    \ max_pool_features], axis=-1) # (B, 2*d_model)\n        \n        z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused) # Apply LayerNorm\n        z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z) # Project back to d_model for consistency\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return z # (B, d_model)\n\n# =========================\n# Path 2: BiLSTM with Additive Attention Pooling (Aetheria SOTA inspired)\n# =========================\nclass AdditiveAttentionPooling(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"Additive attention pooling layer.\"\"\"\n    features: int # Dimensionality of the output context vector\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # x shape: (batch_size, seq_len, features)\n        \n        query = self.param('query', nn.initializers.normal(0.02), (self.features,)) # Learnable query vector\n        \n        projected_features = nn.Dense(self.features, name=\"attn_proj\")(x) # (batch, seq_len,\
    \ features)\n        projected_features = jnp.tanh(projected_features)\n\n        attention_scores = jnp.einsum('blc,c->bl', projected_features, query) \n        attention_weights = nn.softmax(attention_scores, axis=-1) # (batch, seq_len)\n        attention_weights = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(attention_weights, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        weighted_sum = jnp.einsum('bl,blc->bc', attention_weights, x)\n\n        return weighted_sum # (batch, features)\n\nclass BiLSTMAdditiveAttentionHead(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int # Target output feature dim\n    lstm_hidden_dim: int\n    dropout_rate: float\n    \n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, h_cnn, deterministic=True):\n        # h_cnn: (B, L, d_model)\n        forward_rnn = nn.RNN(nn.LSTMCell(self.lstm_hidden_dim), name=\"forward_lstm\")\n        backward_rnn = nn.RNN(nn.LSTMCell(self.lstm_hidden_dim), name=\"backward_lstm\")\n        h_lstm = nn.Bidirectional(forward_rnn, backward_rnn)(h_cnn) # (B, L, 2*lstm_hidden_dim)\n\
    \        \n        pooled = AdditiveAttentionPooling(features=2 * self.lstm_hidden_dim, # Output dim of BiLSTM\n                                          dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(h_lstm, deterministic=deterministic)\n        \n        z = nn.LayerNorm()(pooled) # pooled is (B, 2*lstm_hidden_dim)\n        z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z) # Project to d_model for consistency\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return z # (B, d_model)\n\n# =========================\n# Gated Dual-Path Network\n# =========================\nclass GatedDualPathNetwork(nn.Module):\n    d_input: int = 4\n    d_output: int = 1\n    task_type: str = 'regression'\n    d_model: int = 256\n    num_blocks: int = 5\n    dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n    cnn_kernel_size: int = 7\n    lstm_hidden_dim: int = 128\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n    positional_encoding: bool = False\n    alpha_init_val: float = 0.0 # Initialize\
    \ sigmoid(alpha) to 0.5\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # Initial projection and DSConv backbone\n        h = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n            d = self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n            h = DSConvDilatedBlock(\n                d_model=self.d_model,\n                kernel_size=self.cnn_kernel_size,\n                dilation=d,\n                dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate\n            )(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Path 1: CNN-only with Mean+Max Pooling (Veritas SOTA inspired)\n        output_path1 = MeanMaxPoolingHead(\n            d_model=self.d_model,\n            dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n            name=\"cnn_only_head\"\n        )(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Path 2: BiLSTM with Additive\
    \ Attention Pooling (Aetheria SOTA inspired)\n        output_path2 = BiLSTMAdditiveAttentionHead(\n            d_model=self.d_model,\n            lstm_hidden_dim=self.lstm_hidden_dim,\n            dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n            name=\"hybrid_bilstm_head\"\n        )(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Learnable scalar alpha for linear blending\n        learnable_alpha_logit = self.param('alpha_logit', nn.initializers.constant(self.alpha_init_val), ())\n        alpha = nn.sigmoid(learnable_alpha_logit) # Ensure alpha is between 0 and 1\n\n        # Blended output\n        blended_output = alpha * output_path1 + (1 - alpha) * output_path2\n\n        # Final MLP Head (shared for blended output)\n        z = nn.LayerNorm()(blended_output)\n        z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z)\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out')(z)\n\n        if self.task_type ==\
    \ 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n            return logits.squeeze(-1)\n        return logits\n\nclass GatedDualPathNetworkWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, d_input, d_output, task_type, **kwargs):\n        self.network = GatedDualPathNetwork(d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, **kwargs)\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None:\n                rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n# =========================\n# Station hooks\n\
    # =========================\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'd_model': 256,\n        'num_blocks': 5,\n        'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n        'cnn_kernel_size': 7,\n        'lstm_hidden_dim': 128,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n        'positional_encoding': False, # Explicitly False\n        'alpha_init_val': 0.0 # For nn.sigmoid(alpha_logit) to be 0.5 initially\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    d_output = hparams.get('d_output', 1)\n    task_type = hparams.get('task_type', 'regression')\n    return GatedDualPathNetworkWrapper(\n        d_input=4,\n        d_output=d_output,\n        task_type=task_type,\n        d_model=hparams.get('d_model', 256),\n        num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks', 5),\n        dilations=tuple(hparams.get('dilations', [1, 2, 4, 8, 16])),\n        cnn_kernel_size=hparams.get('cnn_kernel_size', 7),\n        lstm_hidden_dim=hparams.get('lstm_hidden_dim', 128),\n    \
    \    dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n        positional_encoding=hparams.get('positional_encoding', False),\n        alpha_init_val=hparams.get('alpha_init_val', 0.0),\n    )\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001) -> optax.GradientTransformation:\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n    )\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\ndef complete(params: Any, opt_state: Any, trial_data: Dict[str, Any]) -> None:\n    ds = trial_data.get('dataset')\n    vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n    print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works\
