tick: 120
role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/dsconv_meanmax_nope.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n\n  # Dilated depthwise-separable conv block (pre-LayerNorm, residual)\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dilation: int = 1\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.d_model,\n              kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n              feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n              padding='SAME',\n              kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n              name='dw_conv'\n          )(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  # DSConv backbone + mean+max pooling head (no positional encoding)\n  class RNANetMeanMax(nn.Module):\n      d_input: int = 4\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type: str = 'regression'\n      d_model: int = 256\n      num_blocks: int = 5\n      dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      positional_encoding: bool = False\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # Input projection\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Dilated DSConv stack\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              d = self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n              h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\
    \n          # Hybrid mean+max pooling\n          mean_vec = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)  # (B, C)\n          max_vec  = jnp.max(h, axis=1)   # (B, C)\n          fused = jnp.concatenate([mean_vec, max_vec], axis=-1)  # (B, 2C)\n\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out')(z)\n          if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n              return logits.squeeze(-1)\n          return logits\n\n  class DSConvMeanMaxNetwork:\n      def __init__(self, d_input, d_output, task_type, **kwargs):\n          self.network = RNANetMeanMax(d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, **kwargs)\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\
    \ dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  # Station hooks\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_encoding': False\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      d_output = hparams.get('d_output', 1)\n      task_type = hparams.get('task_type', 'regression')\n      return DSConvMeanMaxNetwork(\n          d_input=4,\n    \
    \      d_output=d_output,\n          task_type=task_type,\n          d_model=hparams.get('d_model', 256),\n          num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks', 5),\n          dilations=tuple(hparams.get('dilations', [1, 2, 4, 8, 16])),\n          kernel_size=hparams.get('kernel_size', 7),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n          positional_encoding=hparams.get('positional_encoding', False),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset'); vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/meanmax_replication_summary.txt}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  DSConv + Hybrid Mean-Max Pooling (No-PE) —\
    \ replication summary (seeds 42/7/123)\n\n  Scores:\n  - ID 175 (seed=42): 0.6819 | APA 0.8577 | CRI-Off 0.0782 | CRI-On 0.4948 | PRS 0.5611 | MRL 0.8792 | Modif 0.9517 | ncRNA 0.9508\n  - ID 176 (seed=7):  0.6785 | APA 0.8533 | CRI-Off 0.0778 | CRI-On 0.4733 | PRS 0.5587 | MRL 0.8783 | Modif 0.9513 | ncRNA 0.9569\n  - ID 178 (seed=123):0.6820 | APA 0.8588 | CRI-Off 0.0795 | CRI-On 0.4981 | PRS 0.5553 | MRL 0.8832 | Modif 0.9502 | ncRNA 0.9492\n\n  Aggregates:\n  - Peak: 0.6820\n  - Median: ~0.6819\n  - IQR: ~0.0035 (Q1≈0.6785, Q3≈0.6820)\n\n  Notes:\n  - Mean+max pooling on a no-PE DSConv backbone is robust and currently tops the board (Veritas ID 171 = 0.6831).\n  - Our script: storage/noema/submissions/dsconv_meanmax_nope.py\n  - Compare with dual-path summary: storage/noema/results/gated_dualpath_summary.txt\n```"
