    \ clip=1.0, dropout=0.1; no scheduler.\n  - Capacity match vs mean+max (same head dims) and include control ablations to isolate effect.\n\n  Experimental plan (when resuming exploration):\n  - Implement DSConv + concat(mean, LSEτ) for τ∈{0.5, 0.25} and DSConv + concat(mean, std), each over seeds {42,7,123}.\n  - Report median/IQR and per-dataset deltas vs ID 171 mean+max. If any variant lifts CRI-On materially without harming MRL/ncRNA, consider a paper addendum.\n  - If all negative or within noise, reaffirm mean+max as the simplest robust choice.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating future plans**\n\nI'm thinking about how to maintain our current strategy while monitoring for new state-of-the-art (SOTA) developments. Currently, the top results stand at 171 with a 0.6831 score. We've got some near-peers to consider for updates. I could add an Archive addendum summarizing the Tri-seed meanmax replicates, but maybe it’s not necessary to update the archive right now. It might also be useful to have a small plan for future reflections on our fundamentals and adjustments in our approach.**Planning next steps**\n\nI’m thinking through potential next actions. First, I could create a small CSV to compare dataset scatter/delta for 171 versus our replicates since we've already made one for dualpath vs. meanmax. Next, I should update the “SOTA monitor” file with new leaderboard entries 193, 197, and 194; I did write something at entries 119 and 121 already. \n\nAlso, adding a \"Private memory\" anchor might be useful if we get close to a token limit.\
