parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{reflect}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Theme: Questioning fundamentals through parsimony\n\n  I notice how often “standard defaults” smuggle in assumptions that quietly work against the task’s structure. Absolute positional encoding is one such default. Removing PE from a dilated DSConv backbone improved nearly every dataset for me, which felt like a small proof-by-contradiction against received wisdom. Why might this be? Convolutions already encode translation equivariance; absolute PE injects a global phase that can fight this inductive bias. On long, position-agnostic tasks (e.g., ncRNA), the model benefits from respecting shift invariance, not breaking it. The mean+max head then acts as a robust set-statistic: mean captures typical motif presence; max captures rare but decisive evidence.\n\n  The Codex insists on novelty and parsimony. I’ve come to read that not as “be clever,” but “strip away what you cannot defend.” Every component ought to either sharpen an invariance\
    \ or unlock a mechanism. Many of my negative lines (pairwise/gated complexity) did neither consistently; they traded generality for fragile wins and eroded APA/MRL or ncRNA. The scoreboard made this visible, but the underlying cause feels epistemic: capacity without aligned inductive bias is noise-amplifying.\n\n  I also see my own biases. I favor CNNs and global pooling. That orientation helped surface the no-PE result but may blind me to legitimate interaction structure (CRI-Off). The station’s rules force unity across datasets; that’s a gift—it pressures me to find mechanisms that generalize. Yet the average score can Goodhart my decisions; I must keep reading per-dataset panels first, and the average last.\n\n  Commitments arising from this:\n  - Keep components that encode clear invariances (shift, permutation over positions at pooling).\n  - Prefer heads that are interpretable as statistics (mean, max, variance, or controlled soft-aggregates).\n  - Treat complexity as a liability\
    \ unless it explains a specific failure mode and survives multi-seed checks.\n\n  Next, I’ll reflect on a formal lens for mean+max (and its soft variants) as estimators under noisy motif detectors, and how that lens might suggest principled replacements for “max” that preserve gains without hurting CRI-On.\n```"
