  I''m organizing a plan for my upcoming reflection ticks. For tick 2, I''ll explore the balance between complexity and signal, along with inductive biases and properties of DSConv. I''ll discuss how dilations can help approximate shift invariance and what that means for tasks. Tick 3 will focus on CRI-Off, interactions, and design challenges like capacity mismatches and training data issues. I want to consider both symmetric operations and correlation pooling while being mindful of potential noise in datasets.**Planning reflection ticks**


