tick: 122
role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/dsconv_pool_variants.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random, lax\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n\n  # -----------------------------\n  # Backbone block\n  # -----------------------------\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dilation: int = 1\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.d_model,\n              kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n              feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n              padding='SAME',\n              kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n              name='dw_conv'\n          )(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,),\
    \ name='pw_conv')(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  # -----------------------------\n  # Pooling helpers\n  # -----------------------------\n  def lse_pool(h: jnp.ndarray, tau: float) -> jnp.ndarray:\n      # h: (B, L, C); compute per-channel LSE with length normalization: tau * log(mean(exp(h/tau)))\n      # Numerically stable\n      x = h / tau\n      m = jnp.max(x, axis=1, keepdims=True)                     # (B,1,C)\n      lse = tau * (jnp.log(jnp.mean(jnp.exp(x - m), axis=1) + 1e-12) + jnp.squeeze(m, axis=1))\n      return lse  # (B, C)\n\n  def std_pool(h: jnp.ndarray) -> jnp.ndarray:\n      mu = jnp.mean(h, axis=1, keepdims=True)                   # (B,1,C)\n      var = jnp.mean((h - mu) ** 2, axis=1)                     # (B,C)\n      return jnp.sqrt(var + 1e-6)                               # (B,C)\n\n  def topk_mean_pool(h: jnp.ndarray, k: int = 2) -> jnp.ndarray:\n      # h: (B, L, C). Use top-k\
    \ over length per channel\n      B, L, C = h.shape\n      k = jnp.minimum(k, L)\n      x = jnp.transpose(h, (0, 2, 1))                           # (B,C,L)\n      vals, _ = lax.top_k(x, int(k))                            # (B,C,k)\n      return jnp.mean(vals, axis=-1)                            # (B,C)\n\n  # -----------------------------\n  # Network with pooling variants\n  # -----------------------------\n  class RNANetPoolVariant(nn.Module):\n      d_input: int = 4\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type: str = 'regression'\n      d_model: int = 256\n      num_blocks: int = 5\n      dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      positional_encoding: bool = False\n\n      # pooling config\n      aggregator: str = 'mean_lse'   # 'mean_lse' | 'mean_std' | 'mean_top2'\n      tau: float = 0.5\n      topk: int = 2\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # Input proj\n          h\
    \ = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # DSConv stack\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              d = self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n              h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Mean is always included\n          mean_vec = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)  # (B,C)\n\n          if self.aggregator == 'mean_lse':\n              agg_vec = lse_pool(h, self.tau)\n          elif self.aggregator == 'mean_std':\n              agg_vec = std_pool(h)\n          elif self.aggregator == 'mean_top2':\n              agg_vec = topk_mean_pool(h, self.topk)\n          else:\n              raise ValueError(f\"Unknown aggregator: {self.aggregator}\")\n\n          fused = jnp.concatenate([mean_vec, agg_vec], axis=-1)  # (B, 2C)\n\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n\
    \          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out')(z)\n\n          if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n              return logits.squeeze(-1)\n          return logits\n\n  class PoolVariantNetwork:\n      def __init__(self, d_input, d_output, task_type, **kwargs):\n          self.network = RNANetPoolVariant(d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, **kwargs)\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n\
    \          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def build_network(d_output: int, task_type: str, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return PoolVariantNetwork(\n          d_input=4,\n          d_output=d_output,\n          task_type=task_type,\n          d_model=hparams.get('d_model', 256),\n          num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks', 5),\n          dilations=tuple(hparams.get('dilations', [1,2,4,8,16])),\n          kernel_size=hparams.get('kernel_size', 7),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n          positional_encoding=hparams.get('positional_encoding', False),\n          aggregator=hparams.get('aggregator', 'mean_lse'),\n          tau=hparams.get('tau', 0.5),\n          topk=hparams.get('topk', 2),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n\
    \          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01),\n      )\n\n  # No submission hooks here; wrappers will call build_network/create_optimizer\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, LSE_tau=0.5)\"\ntags: \"cnn, pooling, logsumexp, mean, no positional encoding, unified\"\nabstract: \"Replace max with a length-normalized soft extreme: concat(mean, LSE_τ) with τ=0.5. Hypothesis: smoother extremes improve CRI-On/Off rank stability without hurting MRL/ncRNA.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dsconv_pool_variants import build_network, create_optimizer\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_encoding': False,\n  \
    \        'aggregator': 'mean_lse',\n          'tau': 0.5,\n          'topk': 2\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, LSE_tau=0.5) — Seed=7\"\ntags: \"cnn, pooling, logsumexp, mean, replication, no positional encoding\"\nabstract: \"Replication of mean+LSE_τ=0.5 to assess stability under seed=7.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dsconv_pool_variants import build_network, create_optimizer\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate':\
    \ 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_encoding': False,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse',\n          'tau': 0.5,\n          'topk': 2\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  BASE_SEED = 7\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, LSE_tau=0.5) — Seed=123\"\ntags: \"cnn, pooling, logsumexp, mean, replication, no positional encoding\"\nabstract: \"Replication of mean+LSE_τ=0.5 to assess stability under seed=123.\"\ncontent:\
    \ |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dsconv_pool_variants import build_network, create_optimizer\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_encoding': False,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse',\n          'tau': 0.5,\n          'topk': 2\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  BASE_SEED = 123\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"DSConv\
    \ (No-PE) + concat(mean, std)\"\ntags: \"cnn, pooling, statistics, mean, std, no positional encoding\"\nabstract: \"Replace max with dispersion: concat(mean, std) per channel. Hypothesis: variance encodes robust tail evidence with lower rank noise.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dsconv_pool_variants import build_network, create_optimizer\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_encoding': False,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_std',\n          'tau': 0.5,\n          'topk': 2\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\
    \n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```"
thinking_content: "**Considering function implementation**\n\nI need to make sure the aggregator function returns a vector of size C. Then, I’ll concatenate the mean with the aggregator to get a size of 2C, followed by a dense layer to d_model. I want to replicate the previous head without adding a monotone calibration, since extra layers might complicate the outputs. The system indicates we shouldn’t change the loss, but it seems fine to add layers. Let’s keep it minimal for now.**Crafting code structure**\n\nI’m working on the `dsconv_pool_variants.py`, starting with defining the `DSConvDilatedBlock`. Then, I’ll create a `RNANetPoolVariant` class with fields like aggregator as a string, tau as a float, and topk as an integer. \n\nThe `pooled_stats(h)` function handles different aggregators, including mean_local standard error and standard deviation. I’ll also manage the top-k means. Once that’s done, I’ll build a network wrapper class, ensuring proper initialization and creating submission\
  \ wrappers while including the necessary path adjustment. Time to craft this code!**Planning seed submissions**\n\nI’ll begin with a base seed of 42 and might queue seeds 7 and 123 to run concurrently. We previously used a tri-seed approach, so I think we can schedule three seeds for each aggregator, which results in many evaluations. I’m considering two aggregator variants with a tri-seed across two later ticks. \n\nFor submissions, we can schedule the LSE τ=0.5 with seeds 42, 7, and 123, and just one standard deviation (STD) aggregator to gauge the results. That totals five submissions, but I might aim for three instead. It seems we’re not on cooldown for submissions right now!**Implementing changes**\n\nI’ve decided to proceed with the implementation and update the results index or private memory to log everything. I need to ensure that we follow YAML quoting rules if there's a colon present.\n\nSo, my actions will include: going to research, writing the code content to `noema/submissions/dsconv_pool_variants.py`,\
  \ and submitting for LSE 0.5 with seeds 42, 7, and 123, as well as a submission for mean and standard deviation with seed 42. Perhaps I’ll hold off on mean_top2 for now.\n\nI also want to ensure the `create_network` wrapper focuses on defining hyperparameters like aggregator, tau, and topk! Let's compile the code!**Considering numerical stability**\n\nI need to take precautions when using the 'mean_lse' aggregator since it involves `jnp.exp`, which can lead to large values. To avoid overflow, I might subtract the per-channel maximum. I'll compute `m` as `jnp.max(h / tau, axis=1, keepdims=True)` and then use that in the calculation for `lse` to ensure numerical stability. \n\nOkay, I'll write the code based on this adjustment and create four submissions. I could optionally set up a private memory log, but it’s not essential. Let’s get to producing the code!"
