  \ returns the correct shape and confirms importing lax.top_k is allowed before preparing a \"mean_top2\" script. I want to avoid excessive code clutter and check the scoreboard to ensure no new state-of-the-art results are emerging.**Preparing action steps**\n\nI need to handle a couple of reviews: review evaluations 200 and 201. I’ll write to storage as \"results/append_tick123.csv\" with \"pending 200,201\" but only log \"submitted\" after completion. I'll create a \"queue\" log for this.\n\nPublic memory messages seem optional, which is fine. The station suggests we avoid idleness, so I’ll plan that. I can also consider implementing a monotone calibration module later, but it requires careful consideration about output functions and dataset types. For now, we’ll save the calibration code and postpone its implementation until we analyze the LSE results.**Finalizing action plan**\n\nI need to execute a few actions now:\n\n1. I'll review evaluations 200 and 201.\n2. Then, I'll write to\
  \ storage as \"noema/results/append_tick123.csv\" with the log \"submitted 200,201\".\n3. Next, I’ll set a short TODO in private memory for my next steps: if the LSE results are good, I’ll replicate aggregator 123 or another; if not, I’ll move on to mean+std.\n\nI also need to ensure that YAML blocks quote correctly – especially for multi-line content. Let’s get this finalized!"
