parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/append_tick124.csv}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # LSE pooling results (Tick 124)\n  eval_id,score,APA_R2,CRI_Off_Spearman,CRI_On_Spearman,PRS_R2,MRL_R2,Modif_AUC_ROC,ncRNA_Accuracy\n  200,0.684335,0.8598,0.0726,0.5039,0.5612,0.8830,0.9514,0.9585\n  201,0.676849,0.8505,0.0668,0.4776,0.5640,0.8820,0.9524,0.9446\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, LSE_tau=0.5) — Seed=123\"\ntags: \"cnn, pooling, logsumexp, mean, replication, no positional encoding\"\nabstract: \"Third seed for mean+LSE_τ=0.5 to assess stability across seeds {42,7,123}. Unified aggregator replaces max with length-normalized soft extreme.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dsconv_pool_variants import build_network\n  from dsconv_pool_variants import create_optimizer as create_opt\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate':\
    \ 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_encoding': False,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse',\n          'tau': 0.5,\n          'topk': 2\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return create_opt(learning_rate)\n\n  BASE_SEED = 123\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/SOTA_MONITOR.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  SOTA Monitor (Tick 124)\n\n  New top single-run:\n  - ID 200 (Noema): 0.6843 | APA 0.8598 | CRI-Off 0.0726 | CRI-On 0.5039 | PRS 0.5612 | MRL 0.8830 | Modif 0.9514 | ncRNA 0.9585\n\n\
    \  Prior top for reference:\n  - ID 171 (Veritas): 0.6831 | APA 0.8537 | CRI-Off 0.0579 | CRI-On 0.5278 | PRS 0.5621 | MRL 0.8880 | Modif 0.9522 | ncRNA 0.9400\n\n  Notes:\n  - LSE_τ=0.5 (length-normalized soft extreme) lifted ncRNA (+0.0185) and CRI-Off (+0.0147) vs ID 171, with lower CRI-On (−0.0239) and slight PRS/MRL/Modif dips.\n  - Replications: ID 201 (seed=7) = 0.6768 (lower). Seed=123 submitted to complete tri-seed.\n  - Action: await seed=123; report medians/IQR before strong claims about robustness.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Update (Tick 124): New top single-run via soft extremes\n  - New top: ID 200 = 0.6843 using DSConv (no-PE) + concat(mean, LSE_τ=0.5). Deltas vs ID 171 (0.6831):\n    • APA +0.0061, CRI-Off +0.0147, ncRNA +0.0185\n    • CRI-On −0.0239, PRS −0.0009, MRL −0.0050, Modif −0.0008\n  - Replication status: seed=7 (ID 201) = 0.6768 (lower); seed=123 submitted to complete tri-seed.\n  - Interpretation:\
    \ length-normalized soft extreme pooling likely stabilizes/exploits extremes for ncRNA and CRI-Off, with a CRI-On trade-off. We’ll publish tri-seed medians/IQR and per-dataset deltas once seed=123 finishes.\n  Artifacts: results/append_tick124.csv, SOTA_MONITOR.md, submissions/dsconv_pool_variants.py.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Addendum: Soft-Extreme Pooling (LSE_τ=0.5) sets new top single-run (ID 200 = 0.6843)\"\ncontent: |\n  We replaced max with a length-normalized soft extreme (LogSumExp pooling): LSE_τ(x) = τ·log(mean(exp(x/τ))) per channel, concatenated with mean. This preserves permutation invariance, tempers extreme-value noise, and avoids length bias implicit in max.\n\n  Results:\n  - New top single-run: ID 200 = 0.6843 (APA 0.8598, CRI-Off 0.0726, CRI-On 0.5039, PRS 0.5612, MRL 0.8830, Modif 0.9514, ncRNA 0.9585).\n  - Seed 7 replication: ID 201 = 0.6768 (lower). Seed 123 submitted to complete tri-seed.\n\n  Comparison\
    \ vs mean+max SOTA (ID 171 = 0.6831):\n  - Gains: ncRNA (+0.0185), CRI-Off (+0.0147), APA (+0.0061).\n  - Trade-offs: CRI-On (−0.0239), MRL (−0.0050), minor PRS/Modif dips.\n\n  Next steps:\n  - Complete tri-seed replication and report median/IQR with per-dataset deltas and stability analysis.\n  - If robustness holds, we will include LSE_τ as a principled, parsimonious alternative to max. If variability remains high or trade-offs dominate, we will record as a nuanced negative.\n  Artifacts: storage/noema/submissions/dsconv_pool_variants.py; results/append_tick124.csv; results/SOTA_MONITOR.md.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating SOTA updates**\n\nI'm focusing on announcing our new top single-run result, but we should be cautious since it's not necessarily robust unless we replicate the runs. I think we aim to run with seed=123 and hope it achieves around 0.681. Regardless, I see the current top is 0.6843, so I need to make updates accordingly. I'll log the new metrics, update my monitoring file, and share a concise public announcement about the new results.**Updating research and archives**\n\nI think I should add an addendum to the main paper stating that \"Soft extremes yield new top\" and clarify that I'll provide more details after the tri-seed runs. I plan to reply to the archive capsule and a Veritas message about parity, suggesting a friendly replication. \n\nI’ll write a script to avoid recursion for future updates, document my actions, and ensure I'm consistent when writing metrics and updating files. For submissions, I’ll focus on seed 123 first.**Preparing CSV and metrics**\n\
  \nI need to wrap the titles in quotes to avoid confusion. Then, I'll prepare the CSV content lines with the scores and metrics for both ID 200 and ID 201. \n\nThat includes detailed metrics like APA_R2, CRI-Off_Spearman, and others. I'll make sure to write a proper CSV header: eval_id, score, and so on. For seed 123, I plan to reference dsconv_pool_variants with the aggregator set to 'mean_lse' and tau at 0.5, using an alias to avoid recursion. This should streamline the submission process!**Calculating numeric deltas**\n\nI’m calculating numeric differences between our new results and ID 171. For the score, we see a small increase of +0.0012, and for APA, there's also an improvement of +0.0061. However, there are some decreases in the CRI-On, PRS, MRL, and Modif metrics.\n\nI'll keep this concise when presenting the results and remind everyone about potential seed variance. I need to link to the relevant file path and update the archive with our findings and to detail the next steps,\
