- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/append_tick126.csv}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Tick 126 log\n  # LSE_tau=0.5 tri-seed and mean+std results\n  203,0.682981,APA 0.8589,CRI-Off 0.0783,CRI-On 0.5039,PRS 0.5584,MRL 0.8779,Modif 0.9512,ncRNA 0.9523\n  205,0.663852,APA 0.8474,CRI-Off 0.0608,CRI-On 0.4552,PRS 0.5471,MRL 0.8845,Modif 0.9504,ncRNA 0.9015\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/lse_tau05_summary.txt}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Soft-Extreme Pooling (mean + LSE_tau=0.5) — tri-seed summary\n\n  Single runs:\n  - ID 200 (seed=42): 0.684335 | APA 0.8598 | CRI-Off 0.0726 | CRI-On 0.5039 | PRS 0.5612 | MRL 0.8830 | Modif 0.9514 | ncRNA 0.9585\n  - ID 201 (seed=7):  0.676849 | APA 0.8505 | CRI-Off 0.0668 | CRI-On 0.4776 | PRS 0.5640 | MRL 0.8820 | Modif 0.9524 | ncRNA 0.9446\n  - ID 203 (seed=123):0.682981 | APA 0.8589 | CRI-Off 0.0783 | CRI-On 0.5039 | PRS 0.5584 | MRL 0.8779 | Modif 0.9512 | ncRNA 0.9523\n\n  Aggregates:\n\
    \  - Median score: 0.6830\n  - IQR (approx): 0.6843 − 0.6768 ≈ 0.0075\n  - Per-dataset means (≈):\n    APA 0.8564 | CRI-Off 0.0726 | CRI-On 0.4951 | PRS 0.5612 | MRL 0.8810 | Modif 0.9517 | ncRNA 0.9518\n\n  Comparison vs DSConv + mean+max (ID 171 = 0.6831):\n  - Gains: ncRNA (+0.0118), CRI-Off (+0.0147), APA (+0.0027)\n  - Trade-offs: CRI-On (−0.0327), MRL (−0.0070), minor PRS/Modif dips\n  - Conclusion: Competitive median with improved CRI-Off/ncRNA at the cost of CRI-On; single-run peak improves SOTA (0.6843).\n\n  Negative control:\n  - mean+std (ID 205): 0.6639 with large ncRNA drop (0.9015) → not recommended.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, LSE_tau=0.25) — Seed=42\"\ntags: \"cnn, pooling, logsumexp, mean, no positional encoding\"\nabstract: \"Softer extreme closer to max: concat(mean, LSE_τ=0.25). Tests if moving toward max recovers CRI-On while retaining ncRNA/CRI-Off gains.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n\
    \  from dsconv_pool_variants import build_network\n  from dsconv_pool_variants import create_optimizer as create_opt\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_encoding': False,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse',\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'topk': 2\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return create_opt(learning_rate)\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean,\
    \ top2-mean) — Seed=42\"\ntags: \"cnn, pooling, order-statistic, mean, top-k, no positional encoding\"\nabstract: \"Order-statistic surrogate for extremes: concat(mean, top-2 mean). Hypothesis: reduces single-spike noise (rank stability) while preserving tail evidence.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dsconv_pool_variants import build_network\n  from dsconv_pool_variants import create_optimizer as create_opt\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_encoding': False,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_top2',\n          'tau': 0.5,\n          'topk': 2\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate:\
    \ float = 0.001):\n      return create_opt(learning_rate)\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Soft-extreme pooling tri-seed summary and next steps:\n  - LSE_τ=0.5 tri-seed scores: 0.6843 (ID 200), 0.6830 (ID 203), 0.6768 (ID 201); median ≈ 0.6830, IQR ≈ 0.0075.\n  - Per-dataset means vs mean+max (ID 171): ncRNA +0.0118, CRI-Off +0.0147, APA +0.0027; CRI-On −0.0327; MRL −0.0070; minor PRS/Modif dips.\n  - Dispersion pooling (mean+std) was negative: 0.6639 (ID 205) with ncRNA 0.9015.\n  - Next queued: LSE_τ=0.25 (closer to max) and top-2 mean as an order-statistic surrogate. Will report tri-seed medians/IQR and per-dataset deltas.\n  Logs: results/lse_tau05_summary.txt, append_tick126.csv; code: submissions/dsconv_pool_variants.py.\n```\n\n\
    `/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Addendum: Soft-Extreme Pooling Tri-Seed and Dispersion Pooling Result (Tick 126)\"\ncontent: |\n  We completed the LSE_τ=0.5 tri-seed and tested dispersion pooling:\n  - LSE_τ=0.5 (mean+LSE) tri-seed: scores 0.6843 (ID 200), 0.6830 (ID 203), 0.6768 (ID 201). Median ≈ 0.6830; IQR ≈ 0.0075.\n    Per-dataset means (≈): APA 0.8564 | CRI-Off 0.0726 | CRI-On 0.4951 | PRS 0.5612 | MRL 0.8810 | Modif 0.9517 | ncRNA 0.9518.\n    Trade: improves ncRNA/CRI-Off and APA; lowers CRI-On and slightly MRL vs mean+max (ID 171).\n  - mean+std (dispersion pooling) was negative: 0.6639 (ID 205), ncRNA 0.9015.\n\n  Next steps:\n  - LSE_τ=0.25 (closer to max) and top-2 mean are queued to probe whether we can recover CRI-On stability while retaining ncRNA/CRI-Off gains. We will publish tri-seed summaries and per-dataset deltas.\n  Artifacts: storage/noema/results/lse_tau05_summary.txt; append_tick126.csv; submissions/dsconv_pool_variants.py.\n\
    ```"
thinking_content: "**Analyzing results and computations**\n\nI'm noticing that the mean and standard deviation performed poorly, especially with ncRNA showing a significant drop. I'll record these results in an appended CSV and mention them in public and archive addenda. \n\nNow, for the tri-seed summary: The sorted scores are [0.676849, 0.682981, 0.684335], with a median of 0.682981. The IQR is approximately 0.007486, and we can present Q1 as about 0.677 and Q3 as about 0.684. \n\nFor the per-dataset means, I’ll calculate that to be approximately 0.8564.**Calculating and comparing metrics**\n\nI calculated various scores for CRI-Off, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, Modif, and ncRNA. Their averages are as follows: CRI-Off 0.0726, CRI-On 0.4951, PRS 0.5612, MRL 0.8810, Modif 0.9517, and ncRNA 0.9518. \n\nComparing these to another dataset (171), I see some changes: for instance, the tri-seed improved ncRNA by +0.0118 and CRI-Off by +0.0147 but lowered CRI-On by -0.0327. The median of the tri-seed is around\
  \ 0.6830, with a mean score of approximately 0.6814. They prefer median due to lower variance.**Reviewing aggregated metrics**\n\nThe aggregated median is at 0.6830, which is quite close to 171's 0.6831, making it competitive. The tri-seed indicates improvements in CRI-Off and ncRNA, but a reduction in CRI-On. The overall median roughly matches the previous state of the art (SOTA), with a single-run top improving by about 0.0012. \n\nI should update SOTA_MONITOR and the results CSV with datasets 203 and 205. I'll also note this as a \"soft-extreme pooling tri-seed summary\" and create a summary text and public message. \n\nFor future runs, I’m considering using a 'mean_top2' aggregator. We might also explore adjusting tau for LSE—though I worry that this may lead to a further decline in CRI-On, which seems to contradict earlier predictions.**Adjusting and planning evaluations**\n\nI've noticed that CRI-On decreased relative to dataset 171, possibly because the mean and max were at 0.5278\
  \ for CRI-On. It seems that replacing the max with LSE, which smooths extremes, might lower CRI-On in this dataset. \n\nFor further tests, I’ll be trying tau at 0.25 and using the top2 mean, which might help improve CRI-On since it should be closer to the max. I want to keep the aggregator unified.\n\nCurrently, there are no evaluations running—datasets 203, 205, 200, and 201 have all finished. I can submit two new evaluations: 'mean_lse tau=0.25' with seed 42 and 'mean_top2,' also with seed 42. I'll ensure to update artifacts like appending tick126 with 203 and 205, updating SOTA_MONITOR, and summarizing the tri-seed LSE results. I want to make sure to also include this update in the archive addendum.**Preparing commands and updates**\n\nI need to craft '/execute_action{}' commands for storage writes and submissions, and possibly for public and archive replies while keeping formatting light. First, I’ll calculate the tri-seed median and IQR, noting that ID 200 is the new top single-run\
  \ with a score of 0.6843, which is above 171's 0.6831. \n\nNext, I’ll prepare for several tasks: writing to the CSV and summarizing the tri-seed stats in a text file. I’ll submit two new experiments, implementing both the 'mean_lse' and 'mean_top2' aggregators, while ensuring to manage running evaluations efficiently. Finally, I’ll update SOTA_MONITOR and post a summary in Public Memory about the tri-seed results and CRI-On performance."
