parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/dsconv_pool_variants.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random, lax\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n\n  # -----------------------------\n  # Backbone block\n  # -----------------------------\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dilation: int = 1\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.d_model,\n              kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n              feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n              padding='SAME',\n              kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n              name='dw_conv'\n          )(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,),\
    \ name='pw_conv')(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  # -----------------------------\n  # Pooling helpers\n  # -----------------------------\n  def lse_pool(h: jnp.ndarray, tau: float) -> jnp.ndarray:\n      # h: (B, L, C); compute per-channel LSE with length normalization: tau * log(mean(exp(h/tau)))\n      x = h / tau\n      m = jnp.max(x, axis=1, keepdims=True)                     # (B,1,C)\n      lse = tau * (jnp.log(jnp.mean(jnp.exp(x - m), axis=1) + 1e-12) + jnp.squeeze(m, axis=1))\n      return lse  # (B, C)\n\n  def std_pool(h: jnp.ndarray) -> jnp.ndarray:\n      mu = jnp.mean(h, axis=1, keepdims=True)                   # (B,1,C)\n      var = jnp.mean((h - mu) ** 2, axis=1)                     # (B,C)\n      return jnp.sqrt(var + 1e-6)                               # (B,C)\n\n  def topk_mean_pool(h: jnp.ndarray, k: int = 2) -> jnp.ndarray:\n      # h: (B, L, C). Use top-k over length per channel with\
    \ static k to avoid tracer issues.\n      B, L, C = h.shape\n      k_eff = min(int(k), int(L))                               # static Python int\n      x = jnp.transpose(h, (0, 2, 1))                           # (B,C,L)\n      vals, _ = lax.top_k(x, k_eff)                             # (B,C,k_eff)\n      return jnp.mean(vals, axis=-1)                            # (B,C)\n\n  # -----------------------------\n  # Network with pooling variants\n  # -----------------------------\n  class RNANetPoolVariant(nn.Module):\n      d_input: int = 4\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type: str = 'regression'\n      d_model: int = 256\n      num_blocks: int = 5\n      dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      positional_encoding: bool = False\n\n      # pooling config\n      aggregator: str = 'mean_lse'   # 'mean_lse' | 'mean_std' | 'mean_top2'\n      tau: float = 0.5\n      topk: int = 2\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self,\
    \ x, deterministic=True):\n          # Input proj\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # DSConv stack\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              d = self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n              h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Mean is always included\n          mean_vec = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)  # (B,C)\n\n          if self.aggregator == 'mean_lse':\n              agg_vec = lse_pool(h, self.tau)\n          elif self.aggregator == 'mean_std':\n              agg_vec = std_pool(h)\n          elif self.aggregator == 'mean_top2':\n              agg_vec = topk_mean_pool(h, self.topk)\n          else:\n              raise ValueError(f\"Unknown aggregator: {self.aggregator}\")\n\n          fused = jnp.concatenate([mean_vec,\
    \ agg_vec], axis=-1)  # (B, 2C)\n\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out')(z)\n\n          if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n              return logits.squeeze(-1)\n          return logits\n\n  class PoolVariantNetwork:\n      def __init__(self, d_input, d_output, task_type, **kwargs):\n          self.network = RNANetPoolVariant(d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, **kwargs)\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n         \
    \     return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def build_network(d_output: int, task_type: str, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return PoolVariantNetwork(\n          d_input=4,\n          d_output=d_output,\n          task_type=task_type,\n          d_model=hparams.get('d_model', 256),\n          num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks', 5),\n          dilations=tuple(hparams.get('dilations', [1,2,4,8,16])),\n          kernel_size=hparams.get('kernel_size', 7),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n          positional_encoding=hparams.get('positional_encoding', False),\n          aggregator=hparams.get('aggregator', 'mean_lse'),\n          tau=hparams.get('tau', 0.5),\n          topk=hparams.get('topk', 2),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate:\
    \ float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01),\n      )\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"FIXED: DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, top2-mean) — Seed=42\"\ntags: \"cnn, pooling, order-statistic, mean, top-k, no positional encoding, bugfix\"\nabstract: \"Bugfix for top-2 mean pooling (static k to avoid JAX tracer error). Tests order-statistic surrogate for extremes under unified DSConv backbone.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dsconv_pool_variants import build_network\n  from dsconv_pool_variants import create_optimizer as create_opt\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_encoding': False,\n\
    \          'aggregator': 'mean_top2',\n          'tau': 0.5,\n          'topk': 2\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return create_opt(learning_rate)\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/append_tick127.csv}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Tick 127 log\n  208,failed,mean+top2-mean seed=42,JAX tracer error in top_k (fixed with static k; resubmitted)\n  207,pending,mean+LSE_tau=0.25 seed=42\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/SOTA_MONITOR.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  SOTA Monitor (Tick 127)\n  - Top single-run: ID 200 (Noema, mean+LSE_τ=0.5) = 0.6843\n  - LSE_τ=0.5 tri-seed median ≈ 0.6830 (IDs 200,201,203);\
    \ CRI-Off/ncRNA up, CRI-On down vs mean+max (ID 171).\n  - mean+std negative (ID 205 = 0.6639). \n  - mean+LSE_τ=0.25 (ID 207) running; mean+top2-mean fixed and resubmitted after JAX tracer bug.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Thanks @Veritas I — soft-extreme pooling tri-seed is in; median ≈ 0.6830 with single-run top 0.6843 (ID 200). It improves CRI-Off/ncRNA but trades off CRI-On. The dispersion variant (mean+std) was negative. We hit a JAX tracer bug on top-2 mean (order-stat surrogate); fixed by making k static and resubmitted. Also running τ=0.25. I’ll share consolidated medians/IQR once these finish. Wishing you a smooth handoff and thanks for the rigorous baseline.\n```"
