tick: 128
role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/append_tick128.csv}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Tick 128 log\n  # LSE_tau=0.25 and queue status\n  207,0.672800,APA 0.8554,CRI-Off 0.0867,CRI-On 0.4437,PRS 0.5527,MRL 0.8768,Modif 0.9513,ncRNA 0.9431\n  210,pending,mean+top2-mean seed=42 (bugfixed static k)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/SOTA_MONITOR.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  SOTA Monitor (Tick 128)\n  - Top single-run: ID 200 (mean+LSE_τ=0.5) = 0.6843\n  - Tri-seed (LSE_τ=0.5): median ≈ 0.6830 (IDs 200, 201, 203); trade: ↑ncRNA/CRI-Off, ↓CRI-On.\n  - LSE_τ=0.25 (ID 207): 0.6728 with CRI-Off 0.0867 (high) but CRI-On 0.4437 → net negative.\n  - mean+std negative (ID 205 = 0.6639).\n  - mean+top2-mean (ID 210) running after tracer fix.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/dsconv_pool_variants_calib.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random, lax\n  import flax.linen\
    \ as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dilation: int = 1\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model,\n                      kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                      feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n                      padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n                      name='dw_conv')(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  def lse_pool(h: jnp.ndarray, tau: float) -> jnp.ndarray:\n      x = h / tau\n      m = jnp.max(x, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n      return tau * (jnp.log(jnp.mean(jnp.exp(x\
    \ - m), axis=1) + 1e-12) + jnp.squeeze(m, axis=1))\n\n  class MonotoneCalib(nn.Module):\n      n_hinges: int = 3\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          # x: (B,) or (B,D)\n          t_all = jnp.array([-1.0, 0.0, 1.0])\n          t = t_all[: self.n_hinges]\n          w = self.param('w', nn.initializers.zeros, (self.n_hinges,))\n          b = self.param('b', nn.initializers.zeros, ())\n          slopes = nn.softplus(w)  # >= 0\n          X = x[..., None]  # (B,1) or (B,D,1)\n          relu_terms = jnp.maximum(X - t, 0.0)  # broadcast over hinges\n          y = b + jnp.sum(slopes * relu_terms, axis=-1)\n          return y\n\n  class RNANetPoolVariantCalib(nn.Module):\n      d_input: int = 4\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type: str = 'regression'\n      d_model: int = 256\n      num_blocks: int = 5\n      dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      positional_encoding: bool = False\n      # pooling\n\
    \      tau: float = 0.5\n      # calibration\n      use_monotone_calib: bool = True\n      n_hinges: int = 3\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              d = self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n              h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          mean_vec = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)           # (B,C)\n          lse_vec  = lse_pool(h, self.tau)         # (B,C)\n          fused = jnp.concatenate([mean_vec, lse_vec], axis=-1)  # (B,2C)\n\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits\
    \ = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out')(z)\n\n          # Optional monotone calibration for regression tasks only\n          if self.use_monotone_calib and (self.task_type in ('regression', 'multilabel_regression')):\n              calib = MonotoneCalib(self.n_hinges)\n              if self.d_output == 1:\n                  logits = calib(logits)           # (B,)\n              else:\n                  logits = calib(logits)           # (B, d_output)\n          return logits if not (self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1) else logits.squeeze(-1)\n\n  class PoolVariantCalibNetwork:\n      def __init__(self, d_input, d_output, task_type, **kwargs):\n          self.network = RNANetPoolVariantCalib(d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, **kwargs)\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n\
    \          return variables['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def build_network(d_output: int, task_type: str, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return PoolVariantCalibNetwork(\n          d_input=4,\n          d_output=d_output,\n          task_type=task_type,\n          d_model=hparams.get('d_model', 256),\n          num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks', 5),\n          dilations=tuple(hparams.get('dilations', [1,2,4,8,16])),\n          kernel_size=hparams.get('kernel_size', 7),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n          positional_encoding=hparams.get('positional_encoding', False),\n        \
    \  tau=hparams.get('tau', 0.5),\n          use_monotone_calib=hparams.get('use_monotone_calib', True),\n          n_hinges=hparams.get('n_hinges', 3),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01),\n      )\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"DSConv (No-PE) + mean+LSE_tau=0.5 + monotone calibration (regression only) — Seed=42\"\ntags: \"cnn, pooling, logsumexp, monotone calibration, regression, no positional encoding\"\nabstract: \"Add a tiny strictly monotone piecewise-linear calibration after regression heads to better align MSE training with rank metrics (Spearman) while keeping pooling = mean+LSE_τ=0.5.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dsconv_pool_variants_calib import build_network\n  from dsconv_pool_variants_calib import create_optimizer as create_opt\n\
    \n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_encoding': False,\n          'tau': 0.5,\n          'use_monotone_calib': True,\n          'n_hinges': 3\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return create_opt(learning_rate)\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Update (Tick 128): τ sweep and calibration plan\n  - LSE_τ=0.25 (ID 207) → 0.6728: CRI-Off up to 0.0867\
    \ but CRI-On down to 0.4437 → net negative.\n  - LSE_τ=0.5 remains best among soft-extremes (median ≈ 0.6830; top 0.6843).\n  - mean+top2-mean re-submitted after fixing a JAX tracer issue (static k); running (ID 210).\n  - New run queued: mean+LSE_τ=0.5 + tiny strictly monotone calibration on regression heads (unified). Goal: align MSE training to Spearman without changing the loss or pooling.\n  Will report medians/IQR and per-dataset deltas; if effects lie within noise, we’ll close as negative and keep mean+LSE_τ=0.5 (or mean+max) as the parsimonious default.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning next actions**\n\nI need to figure out the next steps in our station environment. Right now, at tick 128 in the Public Memory Room, we've got some interesting results: LSE_tau=0.25 gave us a CRI-Off of 0.0867, which is the highest on the list, but CRI-On dropped to 0.4437, leading to a lower overall score. \n\nWe also had some promising results with LSE_tau=0.5. I should update our logs and possibly respond to Veritas's farewell message, as they've left at tick 128. An interim note could summarize the improvements at tau=0.25.**Reviewing CRI-Off results**\n\nI’m looking at the CRI-Off values, and I see that the max was 0.0867 from ID 207, but Aetheria’s earlier 0.0871 from ID 164 surpasses it. I need to confirm that Aetheria 164 indeed had 0.0871, but it’s not listed on the current page; it was recorded in an earlier long table.\n\nSo, 0.0867 isn't a new best CRI-Off score. I need to decide if we should continue with LSE variants like τ=0.35 while keeping an\
  \ eye on token usage, which is currently around 146k, below the 75% limit. Here's what I should do: append the results to the file, update the monitor, and maybe submit a tri-seed seed=7 for τ=0.25.**Deciding on LSE tweaks**\n\nGiven the poor CRI-On results, we might drop further LSE tweaks except for top2, which is still running. We're sticking with the tri-seed for LSE_τ=0.5 that we planned. For τ=0.25, it seems negative, so we can stop there.\n\nI’ve thought about proposing a monotone output calibration for regression tasks, but that requires adding a monotonic layer. We should ensure that our training system uses network outputs effectively. I can test the calibration specifically on CRI-On, but we need to maintain a unified approach.\n\nI’m considering a small piecewise-linear function with three segments for monotonicity, applying the right parameters based on the dataset—ensuring that we have positive slopes and a cumulative sum to maintain monotonicity when working with regression\
  \ tasks.**Exploring monotone calibration**\n\nI'm considering building a 'MonotoneSpline1D' module, where the output is calculated with an isotonic piecewise-linear approach using softplus and relu functions. I’m thinking we could fix three hinges at quantiles, and while we don't know the data distribution, I might set knots at [-2, 0, 2]. \n\nThe outputs are logits or predicted regression values, but we need to consider the scale. For training, we usually use raw target scales, so I’m not entirely sure on standardized targets. \n\nI propose implementing 'MonotoneCalib' with three knots at [-1, 0, 1], allowing biases and unifying across datasets for consistency in calibration between regression tasks, while classification heads won’t require this. I plan to keep the aggregator mean+LSE_tau=0.5 since it performs well and will code this into either dsconv_pool_variants or a new file. Then I'll submit it with seed=42 for a single-run test.**Planning evaluation and calibration actions**\n\n\
  I see we have evaluation 210 currently running, and it seems we can submit one more experiment since the queue capacity might be two. I'll log the results and update SOTA_MONITOR with the details from ID 207. It's important to summarize that CRI-Off was highest at about 0.0867 while noting Veritas's departure.\n\nNext steps involve appending results and implementing a new monotone calibration module. I’ll create a new file to avoid affecting existing tasks. It’ll include the MonotoneCalib class, which addresses piecewise linear adjustments based on regression tasks. I will keep everything organized!"
