tick: 129
role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/append_tick129.csv}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Tick 129 log\n  # mean+top2-mean result (bugfixed static k)\n  210,0.675650,APA 0.8587,CRI-Off 0.0694,CRI-On 0.4562,PRS 0.5572,MRL 0.8871,Modif 0.9518,ncRNA 0.9492\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/SOTA_MONITOR.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  SOTA Monitor (Tick 129)\n  - Top single-run: ID 200 (mean+LSE_τ=0.5) = 0.6843\n  - LSE_τ=0.5 tri-seed: median ≈ 0.6830 (IDs 200, 201, 203); trade: ↑ncRNA/CRI-Off, ↓CRI-On vs mean+max (ID 171).\n  - LSE_τ=0.25 (ID 207): 0.6728 — CRI-Off 0.0867 (high) but CRI-On 0.4437 → net negative.\n  - mean+top2-mean (ID 210): 0.6756 — balanced but below LSE_τ=0.5; CRI-On 0.4562, CRI-Off 0.0694.\n  - mean+std negative (ID 205 = 0.6639).\n  - Calibration run (mean+LSE_τ=0.5 + monotone regression calibration) running: ID 212.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"DSConv (No-PE) + mean+LSE_tau=0.5 + monotone\
    \ calibration — Seed=7\"\ntags: \"cnn, pooling, logsumexp, monotone calibration, regression, replication\"\nabstract: \"Replication of mean+LSE_τ=0.5 with tiny strictly monotone calibration on regression heads to assess stability and potential Spearman gains. Seed=7.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dsconv_pool_variants_calib import build_network\n  from dsconv_pool_variants_calib import create_optimizer as create_opt\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_encoding': False,\n          'tau': 0.5,\n          'use_monotone_calib': True,\n          'n_hinges': 3\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def\
    \ create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return create_opt(learning_rate)\n\n  BASE_SEED = 7\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Quick update (Tick 129):\n  - mean+top2-mean (order-stat surrogate) = 0.6756 (ID 210): CRI-On 0.4562, CRI-Off 0.0694, ncRNA 0.9492 — below mean+LSE_τ=0.5.\n  - LSE_τ=0.25 was net negative (0.6728, ID 207): CRI-Off high but CRI-On low.\n  - Best among soft-extremes remains LSE_τ=0.5: single-run 0.6843 (ID 200), median ≈ 0.6830 tri-seed.\n  - Running: mean+LSE_τ=0.5 + tiny monotone calibration for regression heads (IDs 212, new replication queued). Goal: nudge Spearman without hurting other panels.\n  Logs updated in results/*; code in submissions/dsconv_pool_variants*."
thinking_content: I’m thinking about whether I should create a results summary file and a calibrations plan file, though that’s optional. I need to be cautious with YAML, especially with special characters like colons. Using a block with ‘|’ helps avoid any quoting issues. I must also keep an eye out for the create_optimizer bug and set up the wrapper properly. Finally, I need to import from dsconv_pool_variants_calib for the composition. Alright, let's compose this!
