parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/append_tick130.csv}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Tick 130 log\n  # Monotone calibration (mean+LSE_tau=0.5) results\n  212,0.271239,APA -0.0013,CRI-Off 0.0000,CRI-On 0.0000,PRS -0.0000,MRL -0.0010,Modif 0.9518,ncRNA 0.9492\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/SOTA_MONITOR.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  SOTA Monitor (Tick 130)\n  - Top single-run: ID 200 (mean+LSE_τ=0.5) = 0.6843\n  - Tri-seed (LSE_τ=0.5): median ≈ 0.6830 (IDs 200, 201, 203); trade: ↑ncRNA/CRI-Off, ↓CRI-On vs mean+max (ID 171).\n  - LSE_τ=0.25 (ID 207): 0.6728 — CRI-Off 0.0867 (high) but CRI-On 0.4437 → net negative.\n  - mean+top2-mean (ID 210): 0.6756 — below LSE_τ=0.5.\n  - mean+std (ID 205): 0.6639 — negative (ncRNA collapse).\n  - Monotone calibration (regression heads) with mean+LSE_τ=0.5 (ID 212): catastrophic for regression panels (Spearman ~0, R² ≈ 0), classification intact. Line closed as negative.\n  - Running: calibration\
    \ replication (ID 214) — expect similar; will record then stop.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Negative result: Monotone regression calibration with mean+LSE_τ=0.5 (ID 212) collapsed regression panels (Spearman ~0 for CRI-On/Off; R² ≈ 0 for APA/PRS/MRL) while classification stayed intact. Likely caused by degenerate output dynamics under the tiny spline; regardless, the unified variant is not robust. I’m treating calibration as negative and closing the line after the queued replication (ID 214). Best remains mean+LSE_τ=0.5 (median ≈ 0.6830; top 0.6843, ID 200).\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Addendum: Monotone Calibration — Negative Result (Tick 130)\"\ncontent: |\n  We tested a tiny strictly monotone piecewise-linear calibration module after regression heads (paired with mean+LSE_τ=0.5 pooling) to better align MSE with Spearman. Result: catastrophic degradation\
    \ on regression panels (ID 212): CRI-On/Off Spearman ~0, APA/PRS/MRL R² ≈ 0; classification panels (Modif/ncRNA) were unaffected as intended. This suggests the calibration introduced degenerate output dynamics under our unified constraints and training regime.\n\n  Conclusion: treat monotone calibration as a negative under the unified DSConv setting. We retain soft-extreme pooling without calibration as the parsimonious choice (tri-seed median ≈ 0.6830; top single-run 0.6843).\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning actions for calibration**\n\nI'm considering a few actions here, like recording metrics in a file and updating the SOTA_MONITOR with notes on calibration. Notably, the regression metrics have collapsed, but classification seems unaffected. \n\nI should compose a public response summarizing these findings and reaffirm that LSE_τ=0.5 is the best option. I think an archive addendum summarizing negative calibration could be useful, and we might want to adjust the calibrator’s identity initialization too. I'll ensure everything remains concise for clarity and focus on what the user expects.**Planning subsequent actions**\n\nI’m thinking about the next steps to take. First, I need to go to research and record some negative metrics in the append_tick130.csv file. Then, I’ll update the SOTA_MONITOR accordingly. I want to draft a public reply summarizing the negative calibration results and create a brief addendum for the archive. If needed, I could queue no new experiments\
  \ due to slot limitations, but maybe I won't do that. I need to handle the YAML carefully, especially with quoting the negative numbers for the CSV."
