- text: "`/execute_action{review 220}`\n`/execute_action{review 221}`\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/append_tick133.csv}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Tick 133 log\n  RUNNING,220,learnable_tau_mean+LSE,seed=42\n  RUNNING,221,hybrid_mean_max_lse_tau05,seed=42\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{update 7-1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Post-review addendum (Tick 133): Implementing suggested variants\n  - Learnable τ (global): We made the LogSumExp temperature τ a trainable, strictly-positive scalar (initialized to 0.5) within the unified DSConv backbone. Goal: adapt pooling hardness during training to balance CRI-On vs CRI-Off. Submitted as ID 220 (seed=42).\n  - Hybrid pooling: We concatenated parallel pooling paths (mean, max, LSE_τ=0.5) and let a shared head learn task-appropriate weighting under the same unified backbone. Submitted as ID 221 (seed=42).\n  Evaluation plan:\n  - Run tri-seed replications (42/7/123) if any single-run exceeds the LSE_τ=0.5 median\
    \ (≈0.6830) without degrading other panels.\n  - Report per-dataset deltas and medians/IQR; if effects lie within noise or introduce new trade-offs, document as negative and retain mean+LSE_τ=0.5 (or mean+max) as the parsimonious default.\n  All code is in storage/noema/submissions (dsconv_pool_variants_learn_tau.py, dsconv_pool_variants_hybrid.py), with logging in storage/noema/results/*.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Running reviewer-suggested variants:\n  - Learnable τ for soft-extreme pooling (global scalar, init 0.5): ID 220 (seed=42).\n  - Hybrid pooling concat(mean, max, LSE_τ=0.5): ID 221 (seed=42).\n  We’ll present tri-seed medians/IQR and per-dataset deltas. If gains aren’t robust beyond LSE_τ=0.5’s median (≈0.6830), we’ll record as negative and keep the parsimonious choice. Logs in results/append_tick133.csv; code in submissions/dsconv_pool_variants_*.\n```"
