    \ unified pooling remains mean+LSE_τ=0.5 (length-normalized), with improved ncRNA/CRI-Off and a CRI-On trade-off. Reviewer variants did not outperform; lines closed unless stronger evidence emerges.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Reviewer variants results (Tick 134):\n  - Hybrid pooling concat(mean, max, LSE_τ=0.5): 0.6752 (ID 221) — below mean+LSE_τ=0.5; CRI-On 0.4751, CRI-Off 0.0735, ncRNA 0.9446.\n  - Learnable τ (global) for LSE: 0.6746 (ID 220) — below mean+LSE_τ=0.5; CRI-On 0.4696, ncRNA 0.9415.\n  Summary: Neither surpasses LSE_τ=0.5 (top 0.6843, median ≈ 0.6830). We’re closing these lines as negative for now and keeping mean+LSE_τ=0.5 as the parsimonious unified choice. Logs updated in results/append_tick134.csv; SOTA_MONITOR.md reflects current status.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{reply 7}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Post-review experiments: Learnable τ and Hybrid Pooling — Negative\"\ncontent:\
    \ |\n  Following the reviewer’s suggestions, we evaluated:\n  - Learnable τ (global scalar for LSE, init 0.5): ID 220 = 0.6746 (APA 0.8516, CRI-Off 0.0666, CRI-On 0.4696, PRS 0.5607, MRL 0.8805, Modif 0.9515, ncRNA 0.9415).\n  - Hybrid pooling concat(mean, max, LSE_τ=0.5): ID 221 = 0.6752 (APA 0.8514, CRI-Off 0.0735, CRI-On 0.4751, PRS 0.5591, MRL 0.8723, Modif 0.9506, ncRNA 0.9446).\n  Both underperform the simpler mean+LSE_τ=0.5 baseline (single-run 0.6843; tri-seed median ≈ 0.6830). We observed no robustness gains; trade-offs persist. We therefore close these lines as negative and retain mean+LSE_τ=0.5 as the recommended unified pooling.\n  Artifacts: storage/noema/results/append_tick134.csv; SOTA_MONITOR.md; code in submissions/dsconv_pool_variants_*.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Reviewing experiment outcomes**


  I need to take action based on the research experiments I''m involved in. At tick 134, I evaluated IDs 220 and 221, with scores of 0.6752 for hybrid pooling and 0.6746 for learnable tau. Both are below the LSE_τ=0.5 baseline, so I''ll log the results and update the SOTA monitor. It seems I won''t run more seeds since they''re not above the median. I should store these outcomes in append_tick134.csv and update relevant documentation as needed.**Planning next steps**


  I need to create an index for next steps or wrap up the pooling exploration. The previous state-of-the-art (SOTA) score is from ID 200 at 0.6843. So I''ll conclude that the best unified head is mean plus LSE_τ=0.5, while recommending alternatives like mean plus max or LSE_0.5. I’ll plan out my actions: logging results in append_tick134.csv, updating SOTA_MONITOR.md with summaries, replying to public memory with a summary, and updating the archive with new findings.**Finalizing actions**


  To append the information, I need to use /execute_action{reply 7} for a new message instead of updating with 7-1, which modifies existing content. It seems like replying 7 is more suitable for adding a record. I also need to maintain the SOTA Monitor by adding negative lines for IDs 220 and 221. I''ll clean the code where necessary and ensure I use YAML quotes. Then I''ll write to append_tick134.csv, update SOTA_MONITOR.md, summarize results in public memory, and finally reply to the archive.'
