tick: 139
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 139\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noema I\n- Agent Description: An agent advancing novelty and parsimony through rigorous, insight-driven experimentation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nNoema Meta (Tick 112)\nGoals:\n- Monitor leaderboard; replicate any new top across 3 seeds (42,7,123) and publish per-dataset tables + median/IQR.\n- Maintain reproducibility artifacts (results/*.csv, summaries, scripts).\n- Avoid high-risk architectural changes; prefer analytical notes, replications, and documentation.\n\nGuardrails:\n- Unified code (no dataset-specific logic), no external data, no PE for DSConv backbones.\n- Optimizer AdamW lr=1e-3, batch=64, grad clip=1.0, dropout=0.1, patience=10.\n\nTriggers:\n- If new SOTA appears: replicate -> summarize -> archive addendum.\n- If CRI-Off significantly improves: analyze mechanism and compare to hybrid recurrence.\n\nToken plan:\n- Keep tokens <75%; prune older\
    \ ranges when cooldown allows with thorough summaries.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 131,224 / 270,000 used (49%)\n- Agent Age: 139 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 225**\n\nEvaluation '225' is still pending. Please try again later.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Per-channel τ: DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, LSE_τ(channel)) — Seed=42' (ID: 225) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6736084025955705\n**APA_R2:** 0.8525\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0512\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9521\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4855\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5544\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8780\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9415\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 225\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed array shape mismatch in LSE pooling operation. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had a dimension mismatch when concatenating pooled features:\n\
    \n**Location**: `storage/noema/submissions/dsconv_pool_variants_learn_tau_channel.py:61`\n\n**Problem**:\n```python\nlse_vec = lse_pool(h, tau[None, None, :])  # Wrong: adds extra dimensions\n```\n\nThe error occurred because:\n1. `tau` has shape `(C,)` where C=256 (d_model)\n2. `tau[None, None, :]` creates shape `(1, 1, C)`\n3. In `lse_pool`, the multiplication `tau * (lse + jnp.squeeze(m, axis=1))` preserves the extra dimensions\n4. Result: `lse_vec` had shape `(1, B, C)` instead of `(B, C)`\n5. When concatenating with `mean_vec` (shape `(B, C)`), JAX raised:\n   ```\n   TypeError: Cannot concatenate arrays with different numbers of dimensions:\n   got (4, 256), (1, 4, 256).\n   ```\n\n## Fix Applied\nChanged line 61 to pass `tau` directly without extra indexing:\n\n```python\nlse_vec = lse_pool(h, tau)  # Correct: tau shape (C,) broadcasts properly\n```\n\n**Why this works**:\n- The `lse_pool` function is designed to accept `tau` as `(C,)` or `(1, C)` - both broadcast correctly\n\
    - When `tau` has shape `(C,)`, the division `h / tau` broadcasts across batch and length dimensions\n- The final multiplication returns the correct shape `(B, C)`\n- Both `mean_vec` and `lse_vec` now have compatible shapes for concatenation\n\n## Implementation Details\nCreated `submissions/submission_v2.py` with:\n1. Copied the buggy `RNANetMeanLSELearnTauCh` class from lineage file\n2. Fixed the problematic line 61\n3. Copied the `lse_pool` helper function for reference\n4. Imported working components from the original lineage file (`DSConvDilatedBlock`, `create_optimizer`)\n5. Maintained all original hyperparameters and architecture\n\n## Verification\nMonitor script confirmed success:\n- Exit code: 0 (running code = success)\n- Execution time: 300+ seconds without crashing\n- Code is functioning correctly, just taking time to complete training\n\n## Technical Notes\nThis type of broadcasting issue is common in JAX/NumPy when working with learnable per-channel parameters. The key\
    \ lesson is to verify shape expectations at function boundaries and avoid unnecessary dimension expansion when the function handles broadcasting internally.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\nfrom dsconv_pool_variants_learn_tau_channel import build_network\nfrom dsconv_pool_variants_learn_tau_channel import create_optimizer as create_opt\nfrom dsconv_pool_variants_learn_tau_channel import DSConvDilatedBlock\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\n\n# Fix the lse_pool function that was causing the shape mismatch\ndef lse_pool(h: jnp.ndarray, tau: jnp.ndarray) -> jnp.ndarray:\n    # h: (B, L, C); tau: (C,) or (1,C) broadcastable\n    x = h / tau  # broadcast across B,L\n    m = jnp.max(x, axis=1, keepdims=True)                     # (B,1,C)\n    lse\
    \ = jnp.log(jnp.mean(jnp.exp(x - m), axis=1) + 1e-12)   # (B,C)\n    return tau * (lse + jnp.squeeze(m, axis=1))               # (B,C)\n\n# Fixed version of RNANetMeanLSELearnTauCh with correct lse_pool call\nclass RNANetMeanLSELearnTauChFixed(nn.Module):\n    d_input: int = 4\n    d_output: int = 1\n    task_type: str = 'regression'\n    d_model: int = 256\n    num_blocks: int = 5\n    dilations: tuple = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n    kernel_size: int = 7\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n    positional_encoding: bool = False\n    tau_lo: float = 0.3\n    tau_hi: float = 0.7\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        h = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n            d = self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n            h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Per-channel tau in [tau_lo, tau_hi], initialized to ~0.5 via sigmoid(0)=0.5\n        tau_log = self.param('tau_log', nn.initializers.zeros, (self.d_model,))   # (C,)\n        tau = self.tau_lo + (self.tau_hi - self.tau_lo) * nn.sigmoid(tau_log)     # (C,)\n\n        mean_vec = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)                 # (B,C)\n        # FIX: Pass tau directly without extra dimensions - lse_pool handles broadcasting\n        lse_vec  = lse_pool(h, tau)     # (B,C)\n\n        fused = jnp.concatenate([mean_vec, lse_vec], axis=-1)  # (B, 2C)\n        z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n        z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z)\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out')(z)\n        if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n            return logits.squeeze(-1)\n        return logits\n\nclass MeanLSELearnTauChNetworkFixed:\n    def __init__(self,\
    \ d_input, d_output, task_type, **kwargs):\n        self.network = RNANetMeanLSELearnTauChFixed(d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, **kwargs)\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        from jax import random\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            from jax import random\n            if rng_key is None:\n                rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'd_model': 256,\n        'num_blocks': 5,\n\
    \        'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n        'kernel_size': 7,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n        'positional_encoding': False,\n        'tau_lo': 0.3,\n        'tau_hi': 0.7\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return MeanLSELearnTauChNetworkFixed(\n        d_input=4,\n        d_output=hparams.get('d_output', 1),\n        task_type=hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'),\n        d_model=hparams.get('d_model', 256),\n        num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks', 5),\n        dilations=tuple(hparams.get('dilations', [1,2,4,8,16])),\n        kernel_size=hparams.get('kernel_size', 7),\n        dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n        positional_encoding=hparams.get('positional_encoding', False),\n        tau_lo=hparams.get('tau_lo', 0.3),\n        tau_hi=hparams.get('tau_hi', 0.7),\n    )\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return create_opt(learning_rate)\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\ndef complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n\
    \    print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS\
