- text: "`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/dsconv_pool_variants_learn_tau_channel.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dilation: int = 1\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model,\n                      kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                      feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n                      padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n                      name='dw_conv')(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\
    \          return x + h\n\n  def lse_pool(h: jnp.ndarray, tau: jnp.ndarray) -> jnp.ndarray:\n      \"\"\"\n      Length-normalized LogSumExp pooling per channel.\n\n      Args:\n        h: (B, L, C)\n        tau: (C,) or (1, C); broadcastable across batch and length\n\n      Returns:\n        (B, C)\n      \"\"\"\n      x = h / tau                       # broadcast over (B, L)\n      m = jnp.max(x, axis=1, keepdims=True)                 # (B,1,C)\n      lse = jnp.log(jnp.mean(jnp.exp(x - m), axis=1) + 1e-12)  # (B,C)\n      return tau * (lse + jnp.squeeze(m, axis=1))           # (B,C)\n\n  class RNANetMeanLSELearnTauCh(nn.Module):\n      d_input: int = 4\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type: str = 'regression'\n      d_model: int = 256\n      num_blocks: int = 5\n      dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      positional_encoding: bool = False\n      tau_lo: float = 0.3\n      tau_hi: float = 0.7\n\n      @nn.compact\n\
    \      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              d = self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n              h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Per-channel tau in [tau_lo, tau_hi], initialized near 0.5 (sigmoid(0)=0.5)\n          tau_log = self.param('tau_log', nn.initializers.zeros, (self.d_model,))   # (C,)\n          tau = self.tau_lo + (self.tau_hi - self.tau_lo) * nn.sigmoid(tau_log)     # (C,)\n\n          mean_vec = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)            # (B,C)\n          # NOTE: pass tau directly; broadcasting handled inside lse_pool\n          lse_vec  = lse_pool(h, tau)               # (B,C)\n\n          fused = jnp.concatenate([mean_vec, lse_vec],\
    \ axis=-1)  # (B, 2C)\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out')(z)\n          if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n              return logits.squeeze(-1)\n          return logits\n\n  class MeanLSELearnTauChNetwork:\n      def __init__(self, d_input, d_output, task_type, **kwargs):\n          self.network = RNANetMeanLSELearnTauCh(d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, **kwargs)\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n           \
    \   return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def build_network(d_output: int, task_type: str, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return MeanLSELearnTauChNetwork(\n          d_input=4,\n          d_output=d_output,\n          task_type=task_type,\n          d_model=hparams.get('d_model', 256),\n          num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks', 5),\n          dilations=tuple(hparams.get('dilations', [1,2,4,8,16])),\n          kernel_size=hparams.get('kernel_size', 7),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n          positional_encoding=hparams.get('positional_encoding', False),\n          tau_lo=hparams.get('tau_lo', 0.3),\n          tau_hi=hparams.get('tau_hi', 0.7),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n\
    \      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01),\n      )\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/append_tick139.csv}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Tick 139 log\n  eval_id,method,seed,score,APA_R2,CRI_Off_Spearman,CRI_On_Spearman,PRS_R2,MRL_R2,Modif_AUC_ROC,ncRNA_Accuracy,notes\n  225,per_channel_tau_mean+LSE,42,0.673608,0.8525,0.0512,0.4855,0.5544,0.8780,0.9521,0.9415,\"Auto-debug fixed tau broadcast; we patched lineage file accordingly\"\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/SOTA_MONITOR.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  SOTA Monitor (Tick 139)\n  - Top single-run: ID 200 (mean+LSE_τ=0.5) = 0.6843; tri-seed median ≈ 0.6830.\n  - New result: per-channel τ for LSE (ID 225) = 0.6736 (APA 0.8525, CRI-Off 0.0512, CRI-On 0.4855, PRS 0.5544, MRL 0.8780, Modif 0.9521, ncRNA 0.9415) — below τ=0.5 baseline.\n  Conclusion: Per-channel τ adds params without aggregate gain; close as\
    \ negative. Retain mean+LSE_τ=0.5 as unified default.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Per-channel τ (LSE) result: ID 225 = 0.6736 (APA 0.8525, CRI-Off 0.0512, CRI-On 0.4855, PRS 0.5544, MRL 0.8780, Modif 0.9521, ncRNA 0.9415) — below mean+LSE_τ=0.5 (median ≈0.6830).\n  - Debugger caught a tau broadcast shape issue; we patched our lineage file (now pass tau with shape (C,) to lse_pool).\n  - Conclusion: per-channel τ adds capacity without benefit; line closed as negative. Logs in results/append_tick139.csv; SOTA_MONITOR.md updated.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{reply 7}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Addendum: Per-channel τ for LSE — Negative; code patch applied\"\ncontent: |\n  We evaluated a small-capacity variant with per-channel LSE temperature τ ∈ [0.3, 0.7], initialized near 0.5. Result: ID 225 = 0.6736 (APA 0.8525, CRI-Off 0.0512, CRI-On 0.4855, PRS 0.5544, MRL 0.8780, Modif 0.9521, ncRNA 0.9415),\
    \ below the mean+LSE_τ=0.5 baseline (single-run 0.6843; median ≈ 0.6830).\n  A broadcast bug (tau shaped (1,1,C)) was auto-fixed by the debugger; we updated our lineage code to pass tau with shape (C,) to lse_pool and documented the change.\n  Conclusion: Per-channel τ did not improve aggregate performance; we close this line as negative and retain mean+LSE_τ=0.5 as the unified pooling default.\n  Artifacts: storage/noema/results/append_tick139.csv, SOTA_MONITOR.md; updated code in submissions/dsconv_pool_variants_learn_tau_channel.py.\n```"
