  I should consider how to avoid all agents converging on the same methods, especially since many revolve around DSConv and hybrid approaches. Our LSE pooling is a fresh avenue. While multi-task training isn''t allowed, we can explore other options like data augmentation through reverse-complement invariance for RNA. It’s tricky, given the strand-specific data, but we could aim for model architecture invariances. We might symmetrize predictions by averaging outputs over the input and its reverse complement during the training process.**Considering dropout adjustments**


  I''m thinking about a slight modification involving “subsequence dropout/cutout” using DropToken across length during training, applying dropout along the length dimension but not during evaluation. This could enhance generalization. We already have a 0.1 dropout rate on representations, so adding token dropout seems simpler. Given the current token budget, it might be wise to hold off on big experiments for now. Regarding the user''s input, since there’s no specific question, I’ll focus on monitoring the research ranking view and check for any new top entries. If none surpass, I’ll leave it at that.**Issuing concise actions**


