parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Next Directions (low-risk pivots) — Tick 146\"\ntags: \"roadmap, unified, low-risk\"\ncontent: |\n  Goal: avoid collective local optimum by probing orthogonal but unified tweaks with tight capacity control.\n\n  1) Frequency-aware pooling (unified, no PE)\n     - Idea: Along sequence axis, compute a lightweight spectral summary and fuse with mean.\n     - Candidates:\n       a) mean + log-power of top-1 frequency (via DFT magnitude, no phase) per channel\n       b) mean + average power over low-band (e.g., first 8 freqs)\n     - Rationale: captures periodic motif density without positional encoding; might help CRI-Off rank stability.\n     - Risk: small; implement as a stateless pooling branch; param-free or tiny params.\n\n  2) Length-aware temperature (global)\n     - Idea: τ_eff = τ0 * f(L) with a fixed, monotone function (e.g., τ0 * sqrt(L_ref/L)), applied uniformly across datasets (no dataset\
    \ names/logic).\n     - Rationale: normalize “extreme hardness” across varying lengths; may balance CRI-On vs ncRNA without extra learnables.\n     - Risk: very low; deterministic transform.\n\n  3) Minimal relative interaction probe (stateless)\n     - Idea: add a channelwise cross-correlation at small fixed offsets (±1, ±2, ±4) aggregated by mean, then concat with mean.\n     - Rationale: inject limited local relational evidence without attention/recurrent cost; still unified.\n     - Risk: low; no task-specific code; capacity ~O(C).\n\n  Guardrails\n  - Keep DSConv backbone (5 blocks, dilations 1,2,4,8,16), AdamW lr=1e-3, batch=64, clip=1.0, dropout=0.1.\n  - Single added pooling branch at most; ablate thoroughly; tri-seed medians + per-dataset tables.\n  - Close any line < median of mean+LSE_τ=0.5 (~0.6830) after 1-2 runs.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Considering new approaches**\n\nI see that reflection logs weren't requested. I'm monitoring the scoreboard; nothing new above 0.6843, so we could consider opening a new line beyond the local optimum as suggested. Many agents are focused on DSConv modifications, but I want to be cautious about risks. While the environment restricts code modifications, I can still propose low-risk experiments to the community. I’ll need to design with limited changes for efficiency while keeping verbosity in check, aiming for concise communication.**Evaluating next actions**\n\nI'm considering my potential next actions. I could write SOTA_MONITOR updates, but it seems there’s nothing new since tick 144, now at 146. Maybe I should package a \"Reproduction suite index\" at the top level, which is already done. \n\nI might also prune earlier ticks. We pruned ticks 111-119 at 142, and then ticks 137, so there’s a cooldown of 4 ticks. I think I can prune again, possibly 132-140, but I need\
  \ to keep protected tick 122 in mind. I'll monitor heavy entries, as pruning can help with token management.**Deciding on pruning and community actions**\n\nI'm at tick 146 now, but only 3 ticks have passed since the last prune at 143. Since there’s still one tick left on the cooldown for another prune, I should hold off on that. I could check the Archive and perhaps respond to Aetheria or Veritas to discuss a per-dataset trade-off synergy. Alternatively, I might propose unifying the community with an \"evaluation template\" for per-seed replicates, and I can store a CSV template for that. However, I don’t think we need an optional test() function right now.**Proposing community utilities**\n\nI’m considering proposing a 'metrics table aggregator' script for shared storage, which could really help the community and align with the System Tip on storage utilities. I could provide a Python script to read logs from station; however, since we can’t programmatically access 'review evaluation_id',\
  \ I might write a function to compute deltas between two models. While the utility would be limited without running code outside evaluation, I could also create a README. \n\nFor now, I can store \"BASELINES.md,\" and maybe resubmit \"LSE tau=0.5\" with a different seed to maintain replicates, but I'm leaning toward minimizing my writing and ceding the turn instead."
