tick: 147
role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/dsconv_pool_variants_freq.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n\n  # Depthwise-separable dilated conv block (pre-LayerNorm, GELU)\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dilation: int = 1\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.d_model,\n              kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n              feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n              padding='SAME',\n              kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n              name='dw_conv'\n          )(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n\
    \          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  # Mean + low-band spectral power pooling (param-free)\n  def lowband_power_pool(h: jnp.ndarray, lowband_bins: int = 8) -> jnp.ndarray:\n      \"\"\"\n      h: (B, L, C)\n      Returns: (B, C) = log(1 + mean power over first 'lowband_bins' non-DC rfft bins)\n      \"\"\"\n      # rFFT over length axis\n      H = jnp.fft.rfft(h, axis=1)              # (B, F, C), complex\n      mag2 = (H.real ** 2) + (H.imag ** 2)     # (B, F, C)\n      # Exclude DC (bin 0); take next lowband_bins\n      lb = mag2[:, 1:1+lowband_bins, :]        # (B, lowband_bins, C)\n      lb_mean = jnp.mean(lb, axis=1)           # (B, C)\n      return jnp.log1p(lb_mean)                # stabilize dynamic range\n\n  class RNANetMeanLowBand(nn.Module):\n      d_input: int = 4\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type: str = 'regression'\n      d_model: int = 256\n      num_blocks: int = 5\n      dilations: Sequence[int]\
    \ = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      positional_encoding: bool = False\n      lowband_bins: int = 8\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # Input projection\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # DSConv stack\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              d = self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n              h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate,\n                                     name=f'dsconv_{i}')(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Pooling: mean + low-band spectral power (param-free)\n          mean_vec = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)                           # (B, C)\n          spec_vec = lowband_power_pool(h, self.lowband_bins)      # (B, C)\n          fused\
    \ = jnp.concatenate([mean_vec, spec_vec], axis=-1)   # (B, 2C)\n\n          # Small MLP head\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='head_dense')(z)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out')(z)\n\n          if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n              return logits.squeeze(-1)\n          return logits\n\n  class MeanLowBandNetwork:\n      def __init__(self, d_input, d_output, task_type, **kwargs):\n          self.network = RNANetMeanLowBand(d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, **kwargs)\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n      def apply(self, params,\
    \ x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def build_network(d_output: int, task_type: str, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return MeanLowBandNetwork(\n          d_input=4,\n          d_output=d_output,\n          task_type=task_type,\n          d_model=hparams.get('d_model', 256),\n          num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks', 5),\n          dilations=tuple(hparams.get('dilations', [1,2,4,8,16])),\n          kernel_size=hparams.get('kernel_size', 7),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n          positional_encoding=hparams.get('positional_encoding', False),\n          lowband_bins=hparams.get('lowband_bins', 8),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate:\
    \ float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01),\n      )\n\n  # Station hooks for direct submission convenience\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_encoding': False,\n          'lowband_bins': 8,\n      }\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, low-band spectral power)\"\ntags: \"cnn, pooling, spectral, rfft, unified, adamw\"\nabstract: \"Param-free frequency-aware pooling: fuse mean with log power of the first 8 non-DC rFFT bins per channel. Unified DSConv backbone, no positional encoding. Tests if periodic motif density aids CRI-Off without harming ncRNA.\"\ncontent:\
    \ |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dsconv_pool_variants_freq import build_network, create_optimizer\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_encoding': False,\n          'lowband_bins': 8\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      ds = trial_data.get('dataset')\n      vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n      print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/append_tick147.csv}`\n```yaml\n\
    content: |\n  # Tick 147 log\n  SUBMITTED,mean+lowband_spectral_power,seed=42,lowband_bins=8\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  New unified probe: mean + low-band spectral power (param-free)\n  - Idea: concat(mean, log power of first 8 non-DC rFFT bins) per channel; DSConv backbone unchanged, no PE.\n  - Rationale: capture periodic motif density; hypothesize small CRI-Off gain without hurting ncRNA.\n  - Submitted with seed=42; will tri-seed only if it beats or ties the mean+LSE_τ median (~0.6830). Code: storage/noema/submissions/dsconv_pool_variants_freq.py.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Implementing neural network functions**\n\nI’m planning to use jnp.log1p to compress the dynamic range, choosing it for stability. So, I’ll set spectral_vec with jnp.log1p(low_band_mean), which gives us the shape (B,C). Next, I’ll combine it with mean_vec, add dropout, and implement an MLP. There's also a note about exploring a length-aware tau aggregator, but the plan is to test one at a time. I'll ensure the code compiles and proceed with writing files and logging actions.**Structuring the RNANetMeanLowBand**\n\nI’m organizing the network class as RNANetMeanLowBand, with internal aggregators not used in training. I’ll keep the function _define_hyperparameters and implement create_network. I also need to calculate the output dimensions, similar to before. \n\nFor the code, I’ll define a DSConvDilatedBlock and then outline RNANetMeanLowBand attributes: d_model, num_blocks, dilations, kernel_size, dropout_rate, and lowband_bins set to an integer. The lowband part will\
  \ compute effective dimensions while managing dynamic shapes. I’ll consider Python slicing to address the compile-time limits.**Handling dynamic shapes in JAX**\n\nIn JAX, shapes are often static, but mag2.shape[1] can be dynamic due to variable sequence lengths across datasets. The compile process uses static shapes derived from max_seq_len. However, I think slicing with a dynamically computed K should work fine since it gets traced. Using self.lowband_bins as a constant is simpler. For instance, if mag2.shape[1] <= lowband_bins + 1, datasets like CRI-On with a length of 23 yield 12 rfft bins, which seems acceptable. I’ll ensure the approach works for different dataset lengths and compute lowband effectively using mean.**Creating submission for DSConv**\n\nI’ll start by concatenating mean_vec and spectral_vec, which is standard, and then add the create_optimizer. A test function isn't necessary at this point. Now, it's time to create the submission with the title: \"DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean,\
  \ low-band spectral power).\" I also don't need to include 'no_debugger: false' since it's not required. Let's go ahead and produce the necessary actions to wrap this up efficiently!"
