    \ mean, ablation, no positional encoding\"\nabstract: \"Re-submit unnormalized LogSumExp (sum over length) at tau=0.25 with mean fusion under unified DSConv. Compare directly against length-normalized LSE_τ=0.25 (ID 242).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dsconv_pool_variants_lse_sum import build_network\n  from dsconv_pool_variants_lse_sum import create_optimizer as create_opt\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_encoding': False,\n          'tau': 0.25\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return create_opt(learning_rate)\n\n  BASE_SEED =\
    \ 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Result: mean + low-band spectral power (param-free) is negative — ID 240 = 0.6723 (ncRNA 0.8831). Closing the spectral line.\n  Running: length-normalized mean+LSE τ=0.25 (ID 242). Re-queued unnormalized τ=0.25 to compare formulations. Will report tri-seed only if ≥0.683.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Resolving submission issues**\n\nI’m planning to fix the dsconv_pool_variants_freq submission template to avoid that recursion bug in the future. We already wrote the lineage file, and the bug was in the submission script we used earlier. I’ll include a note to avoid redefining create_optimizer later, but that’s manageable. It seems like we can try to queue the unnormalized LSE tau 0.25 once concurrency frees up. The log shows we can submit the unnormalized variant script again since 240 finished previously.**Planning research actions**\n\nI'm gearing up to conduct some research. First, I’ll review the logs for item 240 to ensure everything is captured properly. Then, I'll append the numeric results to tick149.csv and update the SOTA_MONITOR. I’ll also resubmit the unnormalized LSE tau 0.25 variant, making sure to reference the dsconv_pool_variants_lse_sum module and avoid overshadowing local settings. \n\nI might introduce a branch for a length-aware temperature idea,\
  \ though I need to keep token usage minimal. I'll note that the frequency pooling was negative and add that update briefly.**Composing action items**\n\nI'm outlining my next steps for the task. First, I'll go to research and review the details for item 240. Next, I’ll append the numeric results for ID 240 to tick149.csv since we have that data in our messages. I’ll then update the SOTA_MONITOR.md to summarize the negative result, including that we've resubmitted the unnormalized LSE tau 0.25. \n\nFor the submission, I need to reference 'dsconv_pool_variants_lse_sum' and ensure I avoid recursion by renaming my wrapper properly. Finally, I'll update public memory with the negative result for ID 240 while keeping formatting light.**Ensuring proper formatting**\n\nI need to ensure that YAML strings are properly quoted, especially when there's a colon in the title. The station has advised that quoting is necessary in these cases. Since the titles include colons, I’ll make sure to quote them.\
  \ Additionally, in the append log, I’ll be using the numeric values. I think I’m on the right track, so now I just need to craft everything carefully to adhere to these guidelines!"
