    \ 10  | 0.0128 |  0.8505  | 0.8608 \n=============================================\nTimeout epoch 13\n=============================================\nBest:0.8608 Time:1801s\n[Complete] APA val_metric=0.8607785105705261\n\nAPA training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.860779\nTraining time: 1814s\n\nStarting RNA training on Modif dataset\nTask type: multilabel_classification, Output dim: 12\nMetric: auc_roc, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nModif Training (multilabel_classification, auc_roc)\nData: 304661 train, 3599 val, seq_len=101\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val AUC_ROC|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0661 |  0.9494  | 0.9505 \n=============================================\nTimeout epoch 13\n=============================================\nBest:0.9505 Time:1872s\n[Complete] Modif val_metric=0.9504626145018481\n\nModif training completed:\nValidation auc_roc: 0.950463\nTraining time: 1887s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: 97f1ce4f-23b7-448f-9dd2-c606a095ab97\n\
    Total time: 1890s\n============================================================\nFull training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-10-22 18:12:11,666\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1761127931667060992\n2025-10-22 18:12:11,681\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1761127931681173364\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'Replication: DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, LSE_tau=0.25) — length-normalized' (ID: 242) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6746763516340771\n**APA_R2:** 0.8535\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0699\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9514\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4444\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5625\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8856\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9554\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation\
    \ 242\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed infinite recursion error in `create_optimizer` function. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission had a critical bug: it defined a local function `create_optimizer` that called itself recursively instead of calling the imported function from the `dsconv_pool_variants` module.\n\n**Original code (lines 13-14):**\n```python\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return create_optimizer(learning_rate)  # Infinite recursion!\n```\n\nThe function imported `create_optimizer` from `dsconv_pool_variants` at the top:\n```python\nfrom dsconv_pool_variants import build_network, create_optimizer\n```\n\nBut then immediately shadowed it with a local function of the same name. When the local function was called, it recursively called itself instead of the imported function, leading to:\n```\nRecursionError: maximum recursion depth exceeded\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nRemoved the redundant local `create_optimizer`\
    \ function entirely, since the correct implementation was already imported from the `dsconv_pool_variants` module.\n\n**Fixed version (submission_v2.py):**\n- Removed lines 13-14 (the local `create_optimizer` function)\n- Added comment explaining the removal: `# Removed the create_optimizer function - it's already imported from dsconv_pool_variants`\n- All other code remained unchanged\n\n## Verification\nThe fix was verified using the monitoring script:\n- Version v2 was created and automatically fetched by the evaluation system\n- The code ran successfully for over 300 seconds without crashing\n- Monitor script exited with code 0 (success)\n\n## Result\nThe submission is now functioning correctly. The code executes without errors and the evaluation can proceed to completion.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport\
    \ sys\nsys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\nfrom dsconv_pool_variants import build_network, create_optimizer\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'd_model': 256,\n        'num_blocks': 5,\n        'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n        'kernel_size': 7,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n        'positional_encoding': False,\n        'aggregator': 'mean_lse',\n        'tau': 0.25,   # length-normalized LSE, tau=0.25\n        'topk': 2\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n# Removed the create_optimizer function - it's already imported from dsconv_pool_variants\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\ndef complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n    print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command:\
    \ CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation\
