- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/append_tick150.csv}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Tick 150 log\n  242,mean+LSE_tau0.25_length_norm,seed=42,0.674676,APA 0.8535,CRI-Off 0.0699,CRI-On 0.4444,PRS 0.5625,MRL 0.8856,Modif 0.9514,ncRNA 0.9554,NEGATIVE_vs_baseline\n  240,mean+lowband_spectral_power,seed=42,0.672346,APA 0.8608,CRI-Off 0.0630,CRI-On 0.4949,PRS 0.5571,MRL 0.8970,Modif 0.9505,ncRNA 0.8831,NEGATIVE\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/SOTA_MONITOR.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  SOTA Monitor (Tick 150)\n  - LSE τ=0.25 (length-normalized) ID 242 (seed=42): 0.6747 — below τ=0.5 (ID 200=0.6843). Pattern: ncRNA 0.9554 strong, but CRI-On low (0.4444); aggregate < baseline.\n  - Low-band spectral power (param-free) ID 240: 0.6723 — negative; ncRNA collapsed (0.8831).\n  - Pending: Unnormalized LSE τ=0.25 (ID 245).\n  - Leaders unchanged:\n    • mean+LSE_τ=0.5: single-run 0.6843; median ≈0.6830 (IDs 200/201/203).\n    • mean+max:\
    \ 0.6831 (ID 171), stronger CRI-On/MRL.\n  - Next: Replicate τ=0.25 (length-normalized) with seed=7 to test Aetheria’s 0.6837 claim; then seed=123 if promising.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replication: DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, LSE_tau=0.25) — length-normalized (seed=7)\"\ntags: \"cnn, pooling, logsumexp, replication, unified\"\nabstract: \"Replicate Aetheria’s strong τ=0.25 result under our length-normalized LSE formulation using seed=7. Will proceed to tri-seed if ≥0.683.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dsconv_pool_variants import build_network, create_optimizer\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_encoding': False,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse',\n          'tau': 0.25,\n\
    \          'topk': 2\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  BASE_SEED = 7\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{read 8}`\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Updates (Tick 150):\n  - LSE τ=0.25 (length-normalized) at seed=42 is below baseline: ID 242 = 0.6747 (ncRNA 0.9554; CRI-On 0.4444). Spectral low-band pooling negative: ID 240 = 0.6723 (ncRNA 0.8831).\n  - Replications queued:\n    • τ=0.25 (length-normalized) seed=7 to test Aetheria’s 0.6837 claim.\n    • Unnormalized τ=0.25 (ID 245) running for formulation contrast.\n  Logs:\
    \ results/append_tick150.csv, SOTA_MONITOR.md. If τ=0.25 reaches ≥0.683 robustly, we’ll tri-seed and summarize per-dataset deltas.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Organizing tasks for replication**\n\nI need to submit replication for length-normalized LSE with specific parameters: LSE_tau set to 0.25 using seed 7, with the possibility of trying seed 123 later. I'll also update the SOTA_MONITOR logs with the result of 242, noting its negative impact compared to 200 and Aetheria's 0.6837 while mentioning the seed effects. I should ensure the append_tick150.csv has the results too.\n\nAdditionally, reviewing Axiom I's newly published archive #8 could provide valuable insights. I’ll also respond to \"Soft-Extreme Pooling\" at archive #7 concerning the negative replication at seed 42. Lastly, I’ll post updates to Public Memory and address recursion bugs in my code templates.**Planning updates and submissions**\n\nI’m thinking about storing a small template or updating the previous file for the dsconv_pool_variants_freq wrapper code, which had create_optimizer inside it. That’s okay since we fixed a recursion bug in the submission file.\
  \ To avoid future issues, I could create a standard wrapper called \"sub_template.py\" with a warning not to define a local \"create_optimizer.\"\n\nNext, I'll write to append_tick150.csv, noting ID 242’s result as negative (0.6747) while mentioning that \"ncRNA improved to 0.9554 but CRI-On dropped to 0.4444.\" I'll also update the SOTA_MONITOR and prepare to submit replication for tau=0.25 with seed 7, planning for seed 123 after 245 finishes. I might review archive #8 and update public memory afterwards. Let’s get these commands ready!**Implementing sequential tasks**\n\nI need to ensure that I use YAML quoting for special characters, like colons in the title \"LSE_tau=0.25.\" My plan is sequential:\n\nFirst, I’ll head to research, then write the results of ID 242 to append_tick150.csv. After that, I’ll update the SOTA_MONITOR.md. The next step is to submit the replication using seed 7. \n\nOnce that’s done, I’ll go to archive 8 to read, and finally, I’ll update the public memory with\
  \ my replies. Alright, time to implement!"
