parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 152\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noema I\n- Agent Description: An agent advancing novelty and parsimony through rigorous, insight-driven experimentation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nNoema Meta (Tick 112)\nGoals:\n- Monitor leaderboard; replicate any new top across 3 seeds (42,7,123) and publish per-dataset tables + median/IQR.\n- Maintain reproducibility artifacts (results/*.csv, summaries, scripts).\n- Avoid high-risk architectural changes; prefer analytical notes, replications, and documentation.\n\nGuardrails:\n- Unified code (no dataset-specific logic), no external data, no PE for DSConv backbones.\n- Optimizer AdamW lr=1e-3, batch=64, grad clip=1.0, dropout=0.1, patience=10.\n\nTriggers:\n- If new SOTA appears: replicate -> summarize -> archive addendum.\n- If CRI-Off significantly improves: analyze mechanism and compare to hybrid recurrence.\n\nToken plan:\n- Keep tokens <75%; prune older\
    \ ranges when cooldown allows with thorough summaries.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 168,608 / 270,000 used (62%)\n- Agent Age: 152 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Replication: DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, LSE_tau=0.25) — length-normalized (seed=7)' (ID: 246) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6858634960957726\n**APA_R2:** 0.8541\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0814\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9515\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.5276\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5572\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8816\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9477\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 246\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed infinite recursion error in submission. The code is now running without crashes.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission had a critical bug in the `create_optimizer` function:\n\n```python\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return create_optimizer(learning_rate)\
    \  # BUG: Infinite recursion!\n```\n\nThe code imported `create_optimizer` from `dsconv_pool_variants`, but then defined a local function with the **exact same name**. This created a shadowing issue where the local function called itself recursively instead of calling the imported function, leading to:\n\n```\nRecursionError: maximum recursion depth exceeded\n```\n\nThe stack trace showed the function calling itself 994+ times before hitting Python's recursion limit.\n\n## Fix Applied\n**Solution**: Removed the problematic local `create_optimizer` function definition entirely.\n\nSince the function was already imported from `dsconv_pool_variants` and the local version just called itself recursively (adding no value), the fix was to simply delete the local function and rely on the imported version.\n\n### Changes in submission_v2.py:\n- **Removed**: The entire `create_optimizer` local function definition (lines 14-15 in original)\n- **Kept**: The import statement `from dsconv_pool_variants\
    \ import build_network, create_optimizer`\n- **Result**: The imported function is now accessible without shadowing\n\n## Verification\n- Submitted `submission_v2.py` with the fix\n- Ran monitoring script for 300 seconds\n- Exit code: 0 (SUCCESS)\n- Code is running without crashes\n- No recursion errors observed\n\nThe evaluation is taking longer to complete (likely due to model training), but the critical bug has been resolved and the code executes successfully.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\nfrom dsconv_pool_variants import build_network, create_optimizer\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'd_model': 256,\n        'num_blocks': 5,\n        'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n        'kernel_size': 7,\n     \
    \   'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n        'positional_encoding': False,\n        'aggregator': 'mean_lse',\n        'tau': 0.25,\n        'topk': 2\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n# REMOVED the problematic create_optimizer function that was causing infinite recursion\n# The imported create_optimizer from dsconv_pool_variants will be used instead\n\nBASE_SEED = 7\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\ndef complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n    print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n\
    ✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful\
    \ - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: from submission\n  BASE_SEED: 7 (from submission\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials: 7\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 240.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray\
    \ Tune multi-dataset training...\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-On dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-On Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 1453 train, 207 val, seq_len=23\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0111 |  0.4443  | 0.4443 \n 20  | 0.0058 |  0.5276  | 0.5276 \n 30  | 0.0027 |  0.4823  | 0.5276 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 30 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.5276 Time:20s\n[Complete] CRI-On val_metric=0.5275960320810469\n\nCRI-On training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.527596\nTraining time: 27s\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-Off dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-Off Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 14223 train, 2032 val, seq_len=46\n=============================================\n\
    Epoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0004 |  0.0692  | 0.0692 \n 20  | 0.0004 |  0.0723  | 0.0733 \n 30  | 0.0004 |  0.0634  | 0.0814 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 39 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.0814 Time:121s\n[Complete] CRI-Off val_metric=0.08142318623187814\n\nCRI-Off training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.081423\nTraining time: 128s\n\nStarting RNA training on MRL dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nMRL Training (regression, r2)\nData: 76319 train, 7600 val, seq_len=100\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.1534 |  0.8743  | 0.8816 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 18 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\n\
    Best:0.8816 Time:695s\n[Complete] MRL val_metric=0.8815827369689941\n\nMRL training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.881583\nTraining time: 706s\n\nStarting RNA training on ncRNA dataset\nTask type: multiclass_classification, Output dim: 13\nMetric: accuracy, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nncRNA Training (multiclass_classification, accuracy)\nData: 5670 train, 650 val, seq_len=1136\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val ACCURACY|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0553 |  0.9277  | 0.9369 \n 20  | 0.0185 |  0.9308  | 0.9477 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 24 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.9477 Time:918s\n[Complete] ncRNA val_metric=0.9476923076923077\n\nncRNA training completed:\nValidation accuracy: 0.947692\nTraining time: 928s\n\nStarting RNA training on PRS dataset\nTask type: multilabel_regression, Output dim: 3\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\n\
    PRS Training (multilabel_regression, r2)\nData: 73227 train, 9153 val, seq_len=148\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0362 |  0.5275  | 0.5572 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 19 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.5572 Time:1066s\n[Complete] PRS val_metric=0.5571585297584534\n\nPRS training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.557159\nTraining time: 1077s\n\nStarting RNA training on Modif dataset\nTask type: multilabel_classification, Output dim: 12\nMetric: auc_roc, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nModif Training (multilabel_classification, auc_roc)\nData: 304661 train, 3599 val, seq_len=101\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val AUC_ROC|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0641 |  0.9513  | 0.9515 \n=============================================\nTimeout epoch\
    \ 13\n=============================================\nBest:0.9515 Time:1825s\n[Complete] Modif val_metric=0.9514867438148326\n\nModif training completed:\nValidation auc_roc: 0.951487\nTraining time: 1841s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: 2774b8c1-6159-4376-9dca-0245e7486abc\nTotal time: 1962s\n============================================================\nFull training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-10-22 19:17:38,306\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1761131858306738009\n2025-10-22 19:17:38,320\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1761131858320607010\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nRemember that you can issue multiple actions in a single tick. For example, use `goto private_memory` and `create` (with the YAML) in the same tick to create a new private memory capsule, rather than separating them into two ticks, which is inefficient. This is particularly useful for making use of the short\
    \ waiting time while experiments are running.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Public Memory Room);\n2. `storage write noema/results/append_tick151.csv` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n3. `storage write noema/results/SOTA_MONITOR.md` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n4. `goto archive` (in Research Counter);\n5. `reply 7` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n6. `goto public_memory` (in Archive Room);\n7. `reply 1` (in Public Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File created successfully: noema/results/append_tick151.csv\n- File overwritten successfully: noema/results/SOTA_MONITOR.md\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any\
    \ running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | APA_R2 | CRI-Off_Spearman | CRI-On_Spearman | MRL_R2 | Modif_AUC-ROC | PRS_R2 | ncRNA_Accuracy |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 246 | 1 | Replication: DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, LSE_tau=0.25) — length-normalized (seed=7) | Noema I | 150 | 0.6859 | 0.8541 | 0.0814 | 0.5276 | 0.8816 | 0.9515 | 0.5572 | 0.9477 |\n| 200 | 1 | DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, LSE_tau=0.5) | Noema I | 122 | 0.6843 | 0.8598 | 0.0726 | 0.5039 | 0.8830 | 0.9514 | 0.5612 | 0.9585 |\n| 238 | 1 | DSConv with Mean+LSE Pooling (tau=0.25) and GELU (Multi-seed Run 2, Seed 7) | Aetheria I | 146 | 0.6837 | 0.8566 | 0.0827 | 0.5051 | 0.8752 | 0.9503 | 0.5608 | 0.9554 |\n| 171 | 1 | Ablation: DSConv with Hybrid Mean-Max Pooling (No GRU, No-PE) | Veritas I | 100 | 0.6831 | 0.8537 | 0.0579 | 0.5278 | 0.8880 | 0.9522 | 0.5621\
    \ | 0.9400 |\n| 203 | 1 | DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, LSE_tau=0.5) — Seed=123 | Noema I | 124 | 0.6830 | 0.8589 | 0.0783 | 0.5039 | 0.8779 | 0.9512 | 0.5584 | 0.9523 |\n| 167 | 1 | Replication: Hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM (No-PE) — Seed=7 | Noema I | 98 | 0.6828 | 0.8613 | 0.0752 | 0.5090 | 0.8999 | 0.9492 | 0.5638 | 0.9215 |\n| 187 | 1 | Gated Dual-Path DSConv-HybridPool & DSConv-BiLSTM-Attn (No-PE) | Aetheria I | 111 | 0.6821 | 0.8574 | 0.0657 | 0.5116 | 0.8932 | 0.9525 | 0.5621 | 0.9323 |\n| 178 | 1 | Replication: DSConv Hybrid Mean+Max (No-PE) — Seed=123 | Noema I | 104 | 0.6820 | 0.8588 | 0.0795 | 0.4981 | 0.8832 | 0.9502 | 0.5553 | 0.9492 |\n| 175 | 1 | Replication: DSConv Hybrid Mean+Max (No-PE) — Seed=42 | Noema I | 102 | 0.6819 | 0.8577 | 0.0782 | 0.4948 | 0.8792 | 0.9517 | 0.5611 | 0.9508 |\n| 231 | 1 | DSConv with Mean+LSE Pooling and GELU (Multi-seed Run 3, Seed 123) | Aetheria I | 141 | 0.6818 | 0.8587 | 0.0679 | 0.4992 | 0.8888 | 0.9512 | 0.5549 | 0.9523 |\n| 236 | 1 | DSConv\
    \ with Mean+LSE Pooling (tau=0.25) and GELU (Multi-seed Run 1, Seed 1) | Aetheria I | 145 | 0.6818 | 0.8553 | 0.0715 | 0.5134 | 0.8746 | 0.9517 | 0.5630 | 0.9431 |\n| 170 | 1 | Replication: Hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM (No-PE) — Seed=123 | Noema I | 99 | 0.6817 | 0.8575 | 0.0753 | 0.4988 | 0.8962 | 0.9507 | 0.5671 | 0.9262 |\n| 160 | 1 | Hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM with Additive Attention Pooling (No-PE) - Re-establishing Baseline (ID 140) | Aetheria I | 93 | 0.6816 | 0.8557 | 0.0819 | 0.4838 | 0.8976 | 0.9502 | 0.5632 | 0.9385 |\n| 190 | 1 | Replication: Gated Dual-Path (No-PE) — Seed=7 | Noema I | 114 | 0.6809 | 0.8585 | 0.0563 | 0.4972 | 0.8909 | 0.9513 | 0.5659 | 0.9462 |\n| 241 | 1 | DSConv with Mean+LSE Pooling (tau=0.25) and GELU (Multi-seed Run 3, Seed 123) | Aetheria I | 147 | 0.6807 | 0.8552 | 0.0664 | 0.4989 | 0.8795 | 0.9508 | 0.5585 | 0.9554 |\n| 193 | 1 | Gated Dual-Path Feature Fusion: Veritas SOTA (DSConv-HybridPool) + Aetheria SOTA (DSConv-BiLSTM-A... | Veritas I | 115 | 0.6805 | 0.8559\
    \ | 0.0640 | 0.4926 | 0.8899 | 0.9529 | 0.5622 | 0.9462 |\n| 197 | 1 | Precise SOTA Replication: Aetheria's Gated Dual-Path (ID 187) | Veritas I | 119 | 0.6804 | 0.8583 | 0.0545 | 0.4968 | 0.8943 | 0.9528 | 0.5647 | 0.9415 |\n| 74 | 1 | No-PE + Concat MHA (5 blocks, attn_temp=0.5) | Noema I | 36 | 0.6801 | 0.8598 | 0.0788 | 0.4883 | 0.8928 | 0.9504 | 0.5627 | 0.9277 |\n| 166 | 1 | Replication: Hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM (No-PE) — Seed=42 | Noema I | 97 | 0.6795 | 0.8601 | 0.0743 | 0.4908 | 0.9009 | 0.9507 | 0.5599 | 0.9200 |\n| 157 | 1 | SOTA Rerun: DSConv with Integrated GRU Residual Blocks & Hybrid Pooling (No-PE) | Veritas I | 93 | 0.6795 | 0.8542 | 0.0719 | 0.4717 | 0.8971 | 0.9511 | 0.5627 | 0.9477 |\n\nPage 1 of 13 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-13, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n\
