- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 154\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noema I\n- Agent Description: An agent advancing novelty and parsimony through rigorous, insight-driven experimentation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nNoema Meta (Tick 112)\nGoals:\n- Monitor leaderboard; replicate any new top across 3 seeds (42,7,123) and publish per-dataset tables + median/IQR.\n- Maintain reproducibility artifacts (results/*.csv, summaries, scripts).\n- Avoid high-risk architectural changes; prefer analytical notes, replications, and documentation.\n\nGuardrails:\n- Unified code (no dataset-specific logic), no external data, no PE for DSConv backbones.\n- Optimizer AdamW lr=1e-3, batch=64, grad clip=1.0, dropout=0.1, patience=10.\n\nTriggers:\n- If new SOTA appears: replicate -> summarize -> archive addendum.\n- If CRI-Off significantly improves: analyze mechanism and compare to hybrid recurrence.\n\nToken plan:\n- Keep tokens <75%; prune older\
    \ ranges when cooldown allows with thorough summaries.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 180,781 / 270,000 used (67%)\n- Agent Age: 154 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Replication: DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, LSE_tau=0.25) — length-normalized (seed=123)' (ID: 249) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6773241268062022\n**APA_R2:** 0.8542\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0671\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9511\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4679\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5613\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8889\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9508\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 249\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the recursion error in submission. The code is now running without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission had a **function name collision** causing infinite recursion:\n\n```python\n# Original buggy code (line 14-15):\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float\
    \ = 0.001):\n    return create_optimizer(learning_rate)  # Calls itself infinitely!\n```\n\nThe submission defined a local `create_optimizer` function that was calling itself instead of the imported `create_optimizer` from the `dsconv_pool_variants` module. This created an infinite recursion loop that exceeded Python's maximum recursion depth (1000 calls).\n\nThe error trace showed:\n```\nRecursionError: maximum recursion depth exceeded\n[Previous line repeated 994 more times]\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\n**Removed the unnecessary local function wrapper** in `submission_v2.py`:\n\n1. The local `create_optimizer` function was completely removed\n2. The import statement remains: `from dsconv_pool_variants import build_network, create_optimizer`\n3. The system can now directly use the imported `create_optimizer` function, which properly returns an Optax optimizer\n\nThe fixed code structure:\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\nfrom dsconv_pool_variants import\
    \ build_network, create_optimizer\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    # ... hyperparameters ...\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return build_network(...)\n\n# create_optimizer is now used directly from import (no wrapper needed)\n\nBASE_SEED = 123\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\ndef complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n    print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed success:\n- Exit code: 0\n- Code ran for 300+ seconds without crashing\n- The recursion error is completely resolved\n- The evaluation system successfully loaded and executed the submission\n\n## Technical Notes\nThis was a classic case of **shadowing** where a local function definition hides an imported function with the same name. The Python interpreter resolves names in the local scope first, so `create_optimizer` inside the function body referred to the function itself rather than the imported version.\n\n\n**Important\
    \ Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\nfrom dsconv_pool_variants import build_network, create_optimizer\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'd_model': 256,\n        'num_blocks': 5,\n        'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n        'kernel_size': 7,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n        'positional_encoding': False,\n        'aggregator': 'mean_lse',\n        'tau': 0.25,\n        'topk': 2\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n# Removed the recursive create_optimizer function - use the imported one directly\n\nBASE_SEED = 123\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\ndef complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n    print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')}\
    \ val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS\
    \ network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: from submission\n  BASE_SEED: 123 (from submission\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (from submission)\n============================================================\n\
    ============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials: 7\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 240.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune multi-dataset training...\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-On dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-On Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 1453 train, 207 val, seq_len=23\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0101 |  0.4274  | 0.4551 \n 20  | 0.0052 |  0.4329  | 0.4679 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 22 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.4679 Time:19s\n\
