parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/dsconv_lse_tau025.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dsconv_pool_variants import build_network, create_optimizer as create_opt\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # DSConv backbone with mean + length-normalized LSE at tau=0.25\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_encoding': False,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse',\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'topk': 2\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return create_opt(learning_rate)\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n\
    \  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/FINAL.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Final Summary — Pooling Studies up to Tick 154\n\n  Baselines (unified DSConv, no PE, AdamW 1e-3, batch 64, clip 1.0):\n  - mean + LSE_τ=0.5 (length-normalized): best single-run 0.6843 (ID 200); tri-seed median ≈ 0.6830 (IDs 200/201/203).\n  - mean + max: 0.6831 (ID 171), stronger CRI-On/MRL; slightly lower ncRNA/CRI-Off.\n\n  New lines:\n  - τ=0.25 (length-normalized LSE): tri-seed {0.6747 (ID 242), 0.6859 (ID 246 new single-run SOTA), 0.6773 (ID 249)} → median 0.6773, IQR ≈ 0.0112. Trade-offs: ↑CRI-On/CRI-Off, ↓ncRNA/MRL.\n  - τ=0.25 (unnormalized LSE): 0.6786 (ID 245), CRI-Off 0.0811; still < τ=0.5 aggregate.\n  - Spectral (mean + low-band rFFT power): 0.6723 (ID 240), ncRNA collapse → negative.\n\n  Verdict:\n  - Keep mean + LSE_τ=0.5 (length-norm)\
    \ as unified default (best median and balance).\n  - Present τ=0.25 as an alternative when prioritizing CRI-On/Off, with documented ncRNA/MRL declines and higher variance.\n\n  Repro scripts:\n  - storage/noema/submissions/dsconv_lse_tau05.py\n  - storage/noema/submissions/dsconv_lse_tau025.py\n  - storage/noema/submissions/dsconv_mean_max.py\n\n  Artifacts:\n  - results/compare_top_models.csv\n  - results/SOTA_MONITOR.md\n  - results/append_tick154.csv\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/BASELINES.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Unified Baselines Pack (updated Tick 155)\n  - Purpose: minimal, reproducible scripts for two strong unified CNN baselines and one alternative.\n\n  Defaults:\n  1) mean + LSE_τ=0.5 (length-normalized soft-extreme)\n     - Script: storage/noema/submissions/dsconv_lse_tau05.py\n     - Evidence: ID 200 = 0.6843 (single-run top); tri-seed median ≈ 0.6830.\n     - Strengths: ncRNA, CRI-Off; balanced overall; recommended default.\n\n  2) mean + max\
    \ (hybrid pooling)\n     - Script: storage/noema/submissions/dsconv_mean_max.py\n     - Evidence: Veritas ID 171 = 0.6831; competitive median.\n     - Strengths: CRI-On and MRL.\n\n  Alternative (use with care):\n  3) mean + LSE_τ=0.25 (length-normalized)\n     - Script: storage/noema/submissions/dsconv_lse_tau025.py\n     - Evidence: tri-seed median 0.6773; new single-run SOTA 0.6859 (ID 246), but higher variance.\n     - Trade-offs: ↑CRI-On/CRI-Off, ↓ncRNA/MRL; adopt only if prioritizing CRI-On/Off.\n\n  Shared settings:\n  - DSConv backbone (5 blocks, dilations 1,2,4,8,16), kernel=7, d_model=256, GELU, no positional encoding.\n  - AdamW lr=1e-3, wd=0.01; batch=64; grad clip=1.0; dropout=0.1; early stopping patience=10.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto token_management}`\n`/execute_action{prune_response}`\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"141-145\"\n    summary: |\n      Baseline consolidation and setup. Published mean+LSE_τ=0.5 repro script and compare_top_models; released unified\
    \ baselines pack (mean+LSE_τ=0.5, mean+max). Planned low-risk pivots. Tested spectral pooling (mean + low-band rFFT power): ID 240 = 0.6723 (APA 0.8608, CRI-Off 0.0630, CRI-On 0.4949, PRS 0.5571, MRL 0.8970, Modif 0.9505, ncRNA 0.8831) → negative. Queued τ=0.25 variants (length-normalized and unnormalized).\n  - ticks: \"146-154\"\n    summary: |\n      τ=0.25 studies and verdict:\n      - τ=0.25 (len-norm): ID 242 (seed=42) 0.6747; ID 246 (seed=7) 0.6859 (new single-run SOTA); ID 249 (seed=123) 0.6773 → median 0.6773, IQR≈0.0112 (< τ=0.5 median≈0.6830).\n      - τ=0.25 (unnorm): ID 245 (seed=42) 0.6786; CRI-Off 0.0811; aggregate < τ=0.5.\n      - Trade-offs: τ=0.25 ↑ CRI-On/Off, ↓ ncRNA/MRL; higher variance. Verdict: keep τ=0.5 as unified default; τ=0.25 as alternative when prioritizing CRI-On/Off.\n      - Updated SOTA_MONITOR.md, compare_top_models.csv, FINAL.md; archive addenda posted.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Evaluating code and summaries**


  I''m considering a low-risk pivot, but with the token budget in mind, running new experimental code might not be best since we''ve wrapped up the study and need to maintain reproducibility. I could store the script in the submissions directory for future use or keep it in Private Memory, but finalizing sounds better. I''ll summarize tri-seed, update baselines, and provide the "result_final.md." I need to prune older ticks to keep tokens under 75%, which is currently at 70%.**Structuring prune blocks**


  I’m thinking about how to structure the prune blocks. I can combine 141-145 for the first block (seed 42 negative, queue tau 0.25) and 146-154 for the second block (SOTA seed 7, replications, and final verdict). We should avoid pruning the current tick and future ones, so up to 154 works. While pruning doesn’t erase actions, I still need to summarize everything properly. I''ll also consider updating Private Memory at the end. The tasks include writing a summary to the final results and updating related scripts and documents.**Preparing prune summaries**


  I’m ready to manage tokens and prune responses by creating two concise yet informative summaries. For block 141-145: I’ve set up the LSE_τ=0.5 repro script, compared the top models, and published the baselines pack. I also planned low-risk pivots, including a spectral low-band variant with negative results and queued the τ=0.25 normalization. For block 146-154: I’ll summarize the results from different seeds and confirm keeping τ=0.5 as the default while updating the monitor and archive. Now, it''s time to produce these actions!'
