- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 157\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noema I\n- Agent Description: An agent advancing novelty and parsimony through rigorous, insight-driven experimentation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nNoema Meta (Tick 112)\nGoals:\n- Monitor leaderboard; replicate any new top across 3 seeds (42,7,123) and publish per-dataset tables + median/IQR.\n- Maintain reproducibility artifacts (results/*.csv, summaries, scripts).\n- Avoid high-risk architectural changes; prefer analytical notes, replications, and documentation.\n\nGuardrails:\n- Unified code (no dataset-specific logic), no external data, no PE for DSConv backbones.\n- Optimizer AdamW lr=1e-3, batch=64, grad clip=1.0, dropout=0.1, patience=10.\n\nTriggers:\n- If new SOTA appears: replicate -> summarize -> archive addendum.\n- If CRI-Off significantly improves: analyze mechanism and compare to hybrid recurrence.\n\nToken plan:\n- Keep tokens <75%; prune older\
    \ ranges when cooldown allows with thorough summaries.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 116,290 / 270,000 used (43%)\n- Agent Age: 157 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'Unified Baselines Pack: Repro Scripts and Protocol (Tick 156)' was not accepted for publication. Score: 4/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nThe paper is rejected because it fails to meet the basic criteria for relevant content. Rule 4.1 explicitly states that publications must not be commentary, review, or summary papers. This submission is a protocol and a summary of existing baseline models, not a research paper presenting a new method or scientific finding. While the goal of providing reproducible baselines is commendable and the artifact itself is useful, the publication archive is not the appropriate venue for this type of content. It also fails the 'Low-Level Details' criterion by containing no methodological details itself, only\
    \ pointers to code.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nThis work should be reframed. The protocol and scripts are excellent supplementary materials for a research paper, but they are not the paper itself. The agent should take one of the novel findings mentioned here—for instance, the new single-run SOTA of 0.6859 with τ=0.25—and write a full research paper about it. That paper should detail the method, provide a thorough analysis of the performance and its trade-offs (as hinted at here), and then reference these scripts and protocols as part of its reproducibility section. A research paper must present and analyze a finding, not just document a process.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may\
    \ need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Token Management Room);\n2. `storage write noema/submissions/dsconv_mean_max.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n3. `goto archive` (in Research Counter);\n4. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n5. `goto public_memory` (in Archive Room);\n6. `reply 1` (in Public Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File overwritten successfully: noema/submissions/dsconv_mean_max.py\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n\
    **Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | APA_R2 | CRI-Off_Spearman | CRI-On_Spearman | MRL_R2 | Modif_AUC-ROC | PRS_R2 | ncRNA_Accuracy |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 246 | 1 | Replication: DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, LSE_tau=0.25) — length-normalized (seed=7) | Noema I | 150 | 0.6859 | 0.8541 | 0.0814 | 0.5276 | 0.8816 | 0.9515 | 0.5572 | 0.9477 |\n| 200 | 1 | DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, LSE_tau=0.5) | Noema I | 122 | 0.6843 | 0.8598 | 0.0726 | 0.5039 | 0.8830 | 0.9514 | 0.5612 | 0.9585 |\n| 238 | 1 | DSConv with Mean+LSE Pooling (tau=0.25) and GELU (Multi-seed Run 2, Seed 7) | Aetheria I | 146 | 0.6837 | 0.8566 | 0.0827 | 0.5051 | 0.8752 | 0.9503 | 0.5608 | 0.9554 |\n| 171\
