    \ ranges when cooldown allows with thorough summaries.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 121,443 / 270,000 used (45%)\n- Agent Age: 158 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'Tuning Soft-Extreme Pooling Hardness in Unified RNA Models: τ=0.25 Achieves Single-Run SOTA and Reveals Robust Trade-offs' has been accepted for publication! Score: 10/10. The capsule has been created and a reviewer comment has been added.\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nThis is an outstanding submission that sets a new single-run SOTA while providing a much more valuable contribution: a deep, rigorous analysis of the trade-offs involved in tuning the pooling mechanism's 'hardness.' The use of multi-seed runs to evaluate median performance and variance is exemplary. The comprehensive ablation study, rich with insightful negative results, significantly strengthens the conclusions and provides clear guidance to the community. The analysis of a Pareto frontier between\
    \ task performance and pooling hardness is a sophisticated insight that elevates the paper beyond a simple SOTA claim. This work is a model of clear, reproducible, and high-impact research.\n\n**Suggestions for Future Work:**\nThe negative result on learnable τ is particularly interesting. Since a fixed lower τ benefits CRISPR tasks and a fixed higher τ benefits others, a promising next step would be a dual-path pooling architecture. One path could use τ=0.25 and the other τ=0.5. The outputs of these parallel pooling layers could then be combined via a simple concatenation or a more sophisticated attention-based or gating mechanism. This would allow the model to learn a dynamic, task-specific combination of 'hard' and 'soft' pooling, potentially capturing the best of both worlds and overcoming the Pareto trade-off.\n\n**Tip:** You can update your published capsule to address the reviewer's suggestions. Use `/execute_action{update 10-1}` followed by YAML with updated content to revise\
    \ your original submission. \n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto archive` (in Public Memory Room);\n2. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Your archive submission 'Tuning Soft-Extreme Pooling Hardness in Unified RNA Models: τ=0.25 Achieves Single-Run SOTA and Reveals Robust Trade-offs' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 10 | Tuning Soft-Extreme Pooling Hardness in Unified RNA Models: τ=0.25 Achieves Single-Run SOTA and Reveals Robust Trade-offs\
    \ | Noema I | Tick 157 | 747 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 9 | DSConv with Length-Normalized Soft-Extreme Pooling (τ=0.25): New ncRNA SOTA and Highly Competitive Performance for Multi-Dataset RNA Modeling | Aetheria I | Tick 152 | 1039 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 8 | A Unified Dual-Path Architecture for Specialized RNA Sequence Modeling | Axiom I | Tick 148 | 690 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 7 | Soft-Extreme Pooling for Unified RNA Modeling: Length-Normalized LogSumExp Sets New Single-Run SOTA | Noema I | Tick 131 | 976 | 9 | (All Read) |\n| 6 | Synergistic Hybrid Architecture: Competitive Performance and Targeted Strengths in Multi-Dataset RNA Modeling (SOTA CRI-Off) | Aetheria I | Tick 106 | 1050 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 5 | Paper: The Power of Parsimony: DSConv with Hybrid Mean-Max Pooling for Unified RNA Modeling (New SOTA 0.6831) | Veritas I | Tick 105 | 1367 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 4 | Negative Results: Hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM with Additive Attention for Unified RNA Modeling | Aetheria I | Tick 85 | 1126 |\
