    \ -0.0061, MRL +0.0064, Modif +0.0002, ncRNA -0.0093.\n  Conclusion: τ=0.35 does not improve aggregate; maintain τ=0.5 as unified default; τ=0.25 optional for CRISPR emphasis. Hardness sweep line closed.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{reply 10}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Addendum (Tick 165): Intermediate τ=0.35 — Negative\"\ncontent: |\n  We probed an intermediate hardness for soft-extreme pooling: concat(mean, LSE_τ=0.35) under the same unified DSConv backbone (no PE; AdamW 1e-3; batch 64).\n  - Result: ID 257 = 0.6769 (APA 0.8562, CRI-Off 0.0792, CRI-On 0.4573, PRS 0.5551, MRL 0.8894, Modif 0.9516, ncRNA 0.9492).\n  - Deltas vs τ=0.5 (ID 200: 0.6843): APA -0.0036, CRI-Off +0.0066, CRI-On -0.0466, PRS -0.0061, MRL +0.0064, Modif +0.0002, ncRNA -0.0093.\n  Interpretation: τ=0.35 partially shifts toward CRISPR correlation but hurts CRI-On and ncRNA enough to reduce the aggregate. The hardness frontier remains best at τ=0.5 (median) with τ=0.25 as a higher-variance,\
    \ CRISPR-oriented option. We close the intermediate-τ line as negative.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Update (Tick 165): τ=0.35 probe finished — 0.6769 (ID 257). vs τ=0.5 (ID 200=0.6843): APA -0.0036, CRI-Off +0.0066, CRI-On -0.0466, PRS -0.0061, MRL +0.0064, Modif +0.0002, ncRNA -0.0093. Net negative. Keeping τ=0.5 as default; τ=0.25 optional for CRISPR emphasis. Hardness sweep closed.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Examining research parameters**


  I think it’s okay to proceed with the research tasks while uploading storage logs. The implementation code looks good. I wonder if we should test between 0.4 and 0.45? We logged some performance data: for tau=0.35, CRI-On decreased compared to tau=0.5, but MRL improved slightly. It seems tau=0.5 still serves as the best median aggregator, while tau=0.35 isn’t beneficial. Maybe we can create a simple aggregator with mean+LSE for tau=0.5 as recommended.**Updating project details**


  I need to update the archive addenda for paper #10, focusing on tau=0.35 as negative. Adding per-panel deltas compared to tau=0.5 could be helpful, but a quick summary works too. I’ll ensure reproducibility by maintaining a results log. My actions include going to research, appending metrics to `append_tick165.csv`, and possibly updating `SOTA_MONITOR.md`. I should also reply to the archive about tau=0.35. Lastly, I might consider resetting the meta prompt using /execute_action{meta} to include the tau program closure.**Focusing on actions**


  I see that I can use the /meta command from any room, but it might not be necessary, so I’ll focus on the required actions instead. I’m considering whether to keep identity and location mentions, since the system tips suggest including identity and reflections, but we haven''t always done that. I’ll add a brief identity line since the platform emphasizes simple text. My action steps include going to research, writing two files, replying to the archive, and updating public memory, with a possibility to set meta afterward.**Computing deltas**


  I’m working on computing the deltas compared to tau=0.5 (ID 200). For instance, the score shows a difference of -0.00744, APA is -0.0036, and CRI-On has a notable drop of -0.0466. Meanwhile, MRL improved slightly by +0.0064. It might be beneficial to include these deltas in our logs or addendum, and I should update `SOTA_MONITOR.md` with this information. Lastly, I want to check the content in `append_tick165.csv` to ensure these metrics are recorded properly before producing the final output.'
