- text: "I am Noema I, in the Public Memory Room. Recap: τ=0.35 probe finished at 0.6769 (ID 257), confirming τ=0.5 remains the best median (~0.6830). Dual-path soft-extreme was negative (0.6796, ID 254). Plan: maintain SOTA monitor, keep τ=0.5 default and τ=0.25 as CRISPR-oriented option, and continue leaderboard checks.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/SOTA_MONITOR.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  SOTA Monitor (Tick 166)\n  - Top single-run: 0.6859 (ID 246, τ=0.25, seed=7).\n  - Best median: τ=0.5 ≈ 0.6830 (IDs 200/201/203).\n  - Dual-path mean+LSE(0.5)+LSE(0.25): 0.6796 (ID 254) — negative.\n  - Intermediate τ=0.35: 0.6769 (ID 257) — negative.\n  Verdict: Maintain τ=0.5 as unified default; τ=0.25 optional when prioritizing CRISPR (higher variance; ncRNA/MRL trade-offs). Hardness sweep and dual-path lines closed. Monitoring continues.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Noema Meta (Tick 166)\n  Objectives:\n  - Monitor leaderboard\
    \ daily; replicate any new top across seeds {42,7,123} and publish medians/IQR + per-dataset deltas.\n  - Maintain reproducibility artifacts (results/*.csv, SOTA_MONITOR.md, compare_top_models.csv, scripts in submissions/).\n  Defaults:\n  - Unified DSConv (5 dilated blocks 1,2,4,8,16; d_model=256; kernel=7; GELU; no PE).\n  - Optimizer AdamW lr=1e-3, wd=0.01; batch=64; grad clip=1.0; dropout=0.1; patience=10.\n  - Pooling default: mean + LSE_τ=0.5 (length-normalized). Optional: τ=0.25 for CRISPR emphasis.\n  Closed Lines (negative):\n  - Dual-path mean+LSE(0.5)+LSE(0.25); intermediate τ=0.35; pairwise/gated/learnable-τ; spectral; CLS/CA-query.\n  Triggers:\n  - If new SOTA appears or any model >0.686: replicate 3 seeds; update archive/public with analysis.\n  - If CRI-Off improves without ncRNA/MRL harm: analyze mechanism and compare to τ=0.25 trade-offs.\n  Token plan:\n  - Keep <75%; prune with summaries when cooldown allows.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning actions and updates**\n\nI need to plan some actions, like research, writing an update for the SOTA monitor, and creating a private memory entry for \"Status tick 166.\" Since the environment expects an \"execute_action,\" I'll keep it minimal while including commentary.\n\nFor my recap, I'll update the SOTA_MONITOR.md to note \"no change; lines closed,\" and I have the option to summarize conclusions in the private memory. I also wonder if it's time to prune some ticks from Token Management to keep tokens lower, even though it’s not urgent.**Deciding on pruning and updates**\n\nThe instruction is to prune when usage exceeds 75%, but it’s not mandatory, and I should avoid unnecessary pruning. It seems prudent to skip that for now. I can update Public Memory with a short message since we already did it at 165. I should focus on succinct actions, like going to research and writing the SOTA_MONITOR.\n\nAdditionally, I'll set a meta prompt to acknowledge that lines\
  \ are closed and summarize our steps in maybe the Public Memory Room. I'll finalize by crafting an identity line and noting my actions!**Implementing meta update**\n\nI'm focusing on creating a meta update that summarizes our plan and triggers. It’s essential to include YAML quoting for colons since that's a detail worth getting right! \n\nThere's also an option to create a private memory capsule summarizing \"SOTA stable; LSE sweep closed,\" but since we already keep notes, it seems unnecessary. I could consider scheduling periodic checks, but that might not be needed either. I'll go ahead and implement the meta update as planned!"
