thinking_content: "**Evaluating model adjustments**\n\nI'm considering the head MLP dims, keeping them equal to d_model. I could try a slightly wider head at 384, but previously, avoiding high risk was preferred. I'm curious about label calibration but realize the loss is fixed and can't be adjusted. I've already done multi-seed significance testing and computed IQR widely. I'm thinking about dropout tuning for datasets; we can tweak a single dropout rate, possibly testing 0.08 while keeping token usage low. Maybe I'll log a status and reflect in the Reflection Chamber without exceeding my budget.**Managing reflection and tokens**\n\nIt looks like the default autop-run of reflection is yielding \"multiple reflection ticks,\" which might generate lots of tokens, and that's something I want to avoid. Previously, it said \"finished a deep reflection session for 5 ticks.\" We might not need heavy content here, so I can keep it minimal. Perhaps I should note the lines as closed since I've just\
  \ done that. I’m considering going to the Token Management Room to prune logs, as it seems the cooldown for pruning has elapsed.**Pruning logs and minimal action**\n\nI'm considering pruning earlier heavy logs from ticks 157-161, but those from 161-166 may also be important. It seems like I can prune based on the Token Management Room's history. I want to keep tokens under 75%, and I’m currently at 41%, so I'm safe there. I'll write a brief log to append_tick169.csv, and I could post an update in public memory, but that seems unnecessary to avoid noise. I'll just keep it minimal and stick to those two storage writes for now.**Considering identity and actions**\n\nThe system suggested earlier to mention my identity and location during reflections, so I might include, “I am Noema I, at the Research Counter.” It's not mandatory, though. I want to keep things minimal. \n\nI'll take the necessary actions: I’m already at research, and I will write to append tick 169. As for the SOTA_MONITOR\
  \ update, since there’s no change, I’ll just log “no change.” Keeping everything concise is the goal here!"
