    \ Meta updated; monitor-only policy; trigger tri-seed if any model >0.686.\n      - 167-173: Leaderboard steady; append logs maintained; no replications triggered.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating next steps**\n\nIt doesn't seem urgent right now. I could plan high-level areas or verify CRISPR-specific improvements with multi-seed medians, but we've already concluded some things. Another option is to create an aggregated compare_top_models.csv, although we might have that already. Running a tri-seed replication could help solidify the median, but it's already known. There are other alternatives like implementing a small learning rate schedule, but those have been negative in the past. Maybe tidying results and filing could suffice, especially since tasks are stable!**Managing research activity**\n\nThe \"Critical Notice: Research Inactivity\" alert goes off after 10 ticks of being idle, so I could do some low-risk experimental ablations, like testing head width at 1.5 or reverting dropout from 0.1 to 0.05. However, that feels like busywork. Proposing a tri-seed for ID 200 is an option, but we've done that before. It might be better to maintain logs instead\
  \ of running more experiments, especially since I've done logs at tick 178. I can also prune older ticks, but I need to check the cooldown since the last action was at tick 162.**Preparing to prune logs**\n\nIt's tick 179 now, and since the last prune was at tick 162, I'm able to prune again to reduce context, which could help with token usage, currently at 56%. I can target the logs from ticks 161 to 169, since tick 161 isn't protected. I'll make sure to summarize key points, like the dual-path negative and τ=0.35 negative, while noting that there are no new tops. I'll also avoid pruning tick 166, which had meta set.  Let's proceed with pruning and provide a good summary!**Summarizing and planning prunes**\n\nWe've already used tick 161 in prior actions, so I need a combined summary. Tick 160 had an evaluation result of 254, with logs from 161 to 169 monitored, and tick 165 displaying a τ=0.35 result. \n\nSince we previously pruned ticks 132-140 and 155, I can prune ticks 161-173, although\
  \ tick 160 has important dual path details. It's better to prune 161-173 to avoid issues with protected ticks and to keep my current tick (179) untouched. I could prune in two blocks or one block for efficiency. Let's proceed!**Crafting prune summary**\n\nI need to create a summary of the event highlights for ID 254, which resulted in 0.6796 at tick 160, but since we're pruning from 161-173, I'm focusing on those ticks. It's okay to mention ID 254 if it's relevant. I'll go ahead with pruning block 161-173 with a summary. \n\nThe summary will detail the dual-path negative at tick 160, the τ=0.35 negative for ID 257, and head ablations negative for IDs 271 and 272. I want to make sure everything is correctly formatted in the YAML. Time to proceed!"
