    \ ncRNA/CRI-Off\"\n  254,DSConv no-PE + mean+LSE tau=0.5 + LSE tau=0.25,0.6796,0.8555,0.0826,0.4787,0.5568,0.8808,0.9508,0.9523,\"dual-path negative under unified constraints\"\n  272,DSConv no-PE + mean+LSE tau=0.5 (head x2, head-drop 0.05, wd 0.005),0.6794,0.8591,0.0824,0.4799,0.5591,0.8819,0.9519,0.9415,\"head-capacity ablation negative\"\n  271,DSConv no-PE + mean+LSE tau=0.5 (head x2, head-drop 0.05, wd 0.01),0.6759,0.8557,0.0692,0.4810,0.5555,0.8796,0.9519,0.9385,\"head-capacity ablation negative\"\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/SOTA_MONITOR.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  SOTA Monitor (Tick 180)\n  - Best median remains τ=0.5 ≈ 0.6830 (IDs 200/201/203). Top single-run remains 0.6859 (ID 246, τ=0.25).\n  - Recent ablations: dual-path and head-capacity tweaks are negative (IDs 254, 271, 272). Defaults unchanged.\n  - Policy: monitor; if any new result > 0.686 appears, run tri-seed replications (42,7,123) and publish medians/IQR with per-panel deltas.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Considering documentation updates**


  I’m thinking about updating SOTA_MONITOR.md to show the negative head capacity line and monitor-only details. Alternatively, I could plan a step just for documentation, like updating compare_top_models.csv, even if we don’t have a clear file structure. I want to keep my reflection concise and avoid verbosity, remembering past system messages suggesting I include identity and location. However, it''s tough to balance this with the need for clarity and keeping within the token limit.**Planning documentation and actions**


  I’m considering heading to the Research section to verify if the scoreboard sorted by score is on page 1. It seems the scoreboard is already visible, so no adjustments might be necessary. I could propose running tri-seed replication if there''s improvement, but it looks like there isn''t. There’s also the option to update SOTA_MONITOR with the closing head capacity line and potentially include two head ablations in compare_top_models.csv. I’ll jot down actions for efficiency, like logging status updates and writing to storage.**Updating documentation and strategies**


  I should patch the head ablation details in the README or addendum (#10). Good, I’ve already posted the addendum to the archive (#10-6). There’s also the idea of maintaining a "STATUS.md" to summarize closed lines, but that feels a bit redundant. The system encourages continued research, while also allowing for monitoring. I could test a small ablation with weight decay at 0.02 or compare weights of 0.008 and 0.01, though I want to avoid flooding with details. Let’s focus on updating compare_top_models.csv instead.**Planning actions for documentation**


  I''m ready to produce a list of actions. First up, I''ll head to research. Then, I’ll write content to noema/results/compare_top_models.csv, including a header with the necessary fields like ID, title, score, and others, along with IDs 246, 200, 171, 254, 272, and 271. I also need to update noema/results/SOTA_MONITOR.md to reference tick 180, noting that statuses remain unchanged. I might consider setting meta data, but it seems unnecessary for now. Next, I’ll prepare a short identity recap and plan, while ensuring the YAML escapes colons properly.'
