tick: 181
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Noema I, at the Research Counter. Recap: best median ≈0.6830 (τ=0.5), top single-run 0.6859 (τ=0.25). Recent head-capacity ablations were negative. Plan: run pure optimizer ablations on τ=0.5 default to isolate weight decay effects (wd=0.005 vs 0.02) with the unchanged network.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"τ=0.5 default: pure optimizer ablation — AdamW wd=0.005\"\ntags: \"cnn, pooling, lse tau, optimizer, adamw, ablation\"\nabstract: \"Unified DSConv with mean+LSE τ=0.5 (unchanged network). Pure optimizer ablation: AdamW weight decay reduced to 0.005; tests if slightly weaker L2 improves aggregate vs default wd=0.01.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dsconv_pool_variants import build_network\n  import optax\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size':\
    \ 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_encoding': False,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse',\n          'tau': 0.5\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.005),\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"τ=0.5 default: pure optimizer ablation — AdamW wd=0.02\"\ntags: \"cnn, pooling, lse tau, optimizer, adamw, ablation\"\nabstract: \"Unified DSConv with mean+LSE τ=0.5 (unchanged network). Pure optimizer ablation: AdamW weight decay increased to 0.02; tests if stronger\
    \ L2 regularization helps median aggregate.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dsconv_pool_variants import build_network\n  import optax\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_encoding': False,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse',\n          'tau': 0.5\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.02),\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete]\
    \ {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/append_tick181.csv}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Tick 181 log\n  SUBMITTED,tau0.5_default_wd0.005_pure_opt,seed=42\n  SUBMITTED,tau0.5_default_wd0.02_pure_opt,seed=42\n  NOTE,pure_optimizer_ablation,no_network_changes_vs_ID200\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning WD ablation experiment**\n\nI think we should run a pure WD ablation with the default head to isolate its effects. It seems like a reasonable low-risk experiment, similar to dsconv_lse_tau05. We can adjust the optimizer's weight decay to test regularization at 0.005 and 0.02. \n\nI wonder if we should test different batch sizes too. The submission can define BATCH_SIZE as an optional constant. Changing the batch size might affect allocation, but that should be safe. Also, I want to test gradient clips at 0.5 and 1.0 since that's low-risk. It might be best to queue just two submissions to comply with the cooldown requirement.**Creating new submissions**\n\nEarlier, we used the aggregator design in dsconv_pool_variants at tick 122, which involved the 'mean_lse' with a tau parameter and a head with Dense(d_model) and Dropout 0.1. The head width dimension equals d_model and isn't adjustable, but we can reuse that via the build_network call. \n\nWe have the previous\
  \ submission saved under noema/submissions/dsconv_pool_variants.py. Now, I’ll create new submissions using that builder with tau=0.5 and different optimizer weight decay values of 0.005 and 0.02. I think I've noted that the previous weight decay of 0.01 seems best, but exploring will help confirm. Let's keep our actions minimal and log entries. I'll label the submissions as:\n\n- \"τ=0.5 default + wd=0.005 (pure optimizer ablation)\"\n- \"τ=0.5 default + wd=0.02 (pure optimizer ablation)\"\n\nAnd remember to avoid underscores in the tags; I’ll use \"lse tau.\"**Defining create_optimizer and network**\n\nI’m defining the create_optimizer function, referencing the optax chain with a weight_decay parameter. We'll import this from dsconv_pool_variants, but I noticed that the previous create_optimizer function only had a learning_rate parameter and had hard-coded weight_decay at 0.01. \n\nTo change the weight_decay, I can define my own create_optimizer in the submission, overriding it with\
  \ a weight_decay parameter. That’s okay since the API allows for this. I’ll also need to implement create_network by importing build_network from the same source to ensure everything is set up right, including the aggregator config and tau. \n\nI must double-check for underscores in the tags since we can't use those. Let’s go ahead and craft these!"
