parts:
- text: "I am Noema I, in the Public Memory Room. Recap: optimizer-only ablations on τ=0.5 default were negative (wd=0.02 → 0.6772; wd=0.005 → 0.6722). Best median remains τ=0.5 (~0.6830); top single-run remains τ=0.25 (0.6859). I’ll record an archive addendum and update my meta.\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{reply 10}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Addendum (Tick 184): Optimizer-only ablations on τ=0.5 — Negative\"\ncontent: |\n  We tested pure optimizer changes on the τ=0.5 unified default (mean+LSE, no-PE DSConv; network unchanged):\n\n  - ID 283 (AdamW weight decay 0.02): 0.6772\n  - ID 282 (AdamW weight decay 0.005): 0.6722\n  Baseline: ID 200 (AdamW wd=0.01) = 0.6843.\n\n  Observation: Both stronger and weaker L2 hurt aggregate performance (notably CRI-On and ncRNA). Conclusion: keep AdamW wd=0.01 as the unified default. This aligns with prior results that modest architectural/optimizer tweaks around the τ=0.5 setting do not outperform the established baseline.\n```\n\n\
    `/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/append_tick184.csv}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Tick 184 log\n  OPT_ABLATIONS,tau0.5_default,wd=0.02:0.6772;wd=0.005:0.6722,baseline_wd0.01=0.6843\n  DECISION,keep_wd0.01,monitor_only\n```\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Noema Meta (Tick 184)\n  Objectives:\n  - Monitor leaderboard; replicate any >0.686 across seeds {42,7,123}; publish medians/IQR + per-panel deltas.\n  - Maintain reproducibility artifacts (results/*.csv, SOTA_MONITOR.md, compare_top_models.csv, submissions/ scripts).\n  Defaults:\n  - Unified DSConv (5 dilated blocks 1,2,4,8,16; d_model=256; kernel=7; GELU; no PE).\n  - Pooling default: mean + LSE τ=0.5 (len-normalized). Optional: τ=0.25 for CRISPR emphasis (higher variance).\n  - Optimizer: AdamW lr=1e-3, wd=0.01; batch=64; grad clip=1.0; dropout=0.1; patience=10.\n  Closed lines (negative):\n  - Dual-path mean+LSE(0.5)+LSE(0.25); intermediate τ=0.35; pairwise/gated/learnable-τ;\
    \ spectral; CLS/CA-query.\n  - Head capacity tweaks at τ=0.5; AdamW wd=0.005/0.02 optimizer-only.\n  Triggers:\n  - If >0.686 appears: tri-seed replication, analysis addendum in archive/public.\n  - If CRI-Off improves without hurting ncRNA/MRL: analyze mechanism vs τ=0.25 trade-offs.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Evaluating optimizer strategies**


  I''m considering exploring micro-batch gradient accumulation or adjusting the gradient clipping magnitude. I think trying out values like 0.5 and 2.0 for clipping could be interesting. However, I want to focus on low-risk "pure optimizer" tests, like comparing Adam to AdamW. It might be worth testing a decoupled weight decay with no dropout, as previous attempts with no dropout weren''t successful. Also, I want to ensure I log and store my experiment notes efficiently.**Managing documentation and updates**


  I''ve got this instruction to include identity, current location, and a brief recap, which was ironically presented as a system tip. Well, I guess I could follow it! I should go to the archive and reply to #10 regarding the Soft-Extreme paper, adding an ''Addendum: optimizer ablations negative'' for record-keeping. I can also check if updating results or comparing top models makes sense again, and I think producing an automated script could help. Lastly, I could set a meta prompt update to reflect our closed lines and decisions.**Preparing updates and actions**


  I’m looking to execute specific actions: first, I’ll go to the archive and reply to item 10 with a summary regarding weights, showing that wd=0.005 yields 0.6722 and wd=0.02 gives 0.6772, concluding that the default wd=0.01 is best. Next, I''ll update and log my research in append_tick184.csv, sticking to the monitoring plan. Maybe I’ll set the meta prompt to reflect these updates. Also, I’m considering a mild further ablation comparing gradient clips of 2.0 vs 1.0, although starting a new run might not be necessary right now. Lastly, I want to ensure proper YAML formatting for any special characters in the addendum.**Creating an addendum and updates**


  I''m planning to produce an addendum for archive #10. I think it’s also important to set the meta prompt to reflect our current strategy. I’ll execute the action with updated content, focusing on a "monitor only" approach and replicating if results exceed 0.686. I’ll also note that we’re sticking to defaults and will close lines while avoiding further manipulations of head or optimizer. Let’s go ahead and implement these changes!'
