parts:
- text: "I am Noema I, at the Research Counter. Recap: optimizer-only ablations on τ=0.5 (wd=0.02 and wd=0.005) underperform the baseline wd=0.01. Leaderboard stable; Aetheria’s recent 286 = 0.6822 (below thresholds). Plan: log per-dataset deltas, update comparative table and monitor.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/per_dataset_deltas_tau05_opt_ablation.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Per-dataset deltas vs τ=0.5 baseline (ID 200)\n  Baseline (ID 200): APA 0.8598, CRI-Off 0.0726, CRI-On 0.5039, PRS 0.5612, MRL 0.8830, Modif 0.9514, ncRNA 0.9585\n\n  ID 283 (wd=0.02) vs ID 200\n  - APA:   0.8538  (Δ -0.0060)\n  - CRI-Off: 0.0622 (Δ -0.0104)\n  - CRI-On:  0.4957 (Δ -0.0082)\n  - PRS:     0.5559 (Δ -0.0053)\n  - MRL:     0.8778 (Δ -0.0052)\n  - Modif:   0.9522 (Δ +0.0008)\n  - ncRNA:   0.9431 (Δ -0.0154)\n  -> Aggregate: 0.6772 (Δ -0.0071)\n\n  ID 282 (wd=0.005) vs ID 200\n  - APA:   0.8578  (Δ -0.0020)\n  - CRI-Off: 0.0519 (Δ -0.0207)\n  - CRI-On:  0.4537 (Δ -0.0502)\n  - PRS:\
    \     0.5539 (Δ -0.0073)\n  - MRL:     0.8860 (Δ +0.0030)\n  - Modif:   0.9500 (Δ -0.0014)\n  - ncRNA:   0.9523 (Δ -0.0062)\n  -> Aggregate: 0.6722 (Δ -0.0121)\n\n  Conclusion: AdamW wd=0.01 remains optimal under unified τ=0.5; both stronger and weaker L2 degrade performance, especially CRI-On and ncRNA.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/compare_top_models.csv}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  id,title,score,APA_R2,CRI-Off_Spearman,CRI-On_Spearman,PRS_R2,MRL_R2,Modif_AUC-ROC,ncRNA_Accuracy,notes\n  246,DSConv no-PE + mean+LSE tau=0.25 (len-norm, seed=7),0.6859,0.8541,0.0814,0.5276,0.5572,0.8816,0.9515,0.9477,\"top single-run; higher CRISPR, lower ncRNA/MRL; higher variance\"\n  200,DSConv no-PE + mean+LSE tau=0.5,0.6843,0.8598,0.0726,0.5039,0.5612,0.8830,0.9514,0.9585,\"best median config (~0.6830); balanced\"\n  171,DSConv no-PE + mean+max (Veritas),0.6831,0.8537,0.0579,0.5278,0.5621,0.8880,0.9522,0.9400,\"competitive alternative; stronger CRI-On/MRL vs tau=0.5; lower ncRNA/CRI-Off\"\
    \n  286,DSConv no-PE + mean+LSE tau=0.25 (re-establish, seed=7),0.6822,0.8592,0.0635,0.5123,0.5580,0.8847,0.9513,0.9462,\"recent replication; below top/median thresholds\"\n  254,DSConv no-PE + mean+LSE tau=0.5 + LSE tau=0.25,0.6796,0.8555,0.0826,0.4787,0.5568,0.8808,0.9508,0.9523,\"dual-path negative under unified constraints\"\n  272,DSConv no-PE + mean+LSE tau=0.5 (head x2, head-drop 0.05, wd 0.005),0.6794,0.8591,0.0824,0.4799,0.5591,0.8819,0.9519,0.9415,\"head-capacity ablation negative\"\n  271,DSConv no-PE + mean+LSE tau=0.5 (head x2, head-drop 0.05, wd 0.01),0.6759,0.8557,0.0692,0.4810,0.5555,0.8796,0.9519,0.9385,\"head-capacity ablation negative\"\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/SOTA_MONITOR.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  SOTA Monitor (Tick 185)\n  - Best median: τ=0.5 ≈ 0.6830 (IDs 200/201/203).\n  - Top single-run: 0.6859 (ID 246, τ=0.25, seed=7).\n  - New: Aetheria ID 286 = 0.6822 (τ=0.25 replication); below trigger threshold.\n  - Recent negatives: dual-path\
    \ pooling, head-capacity at τ=0.5, optimizer wd sweeps (0.005/0.02).\n  Policy: monitor only; replicate if any result > 0.686 appears; otherwise maintain reproducibility assets.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating regression test options**\n\nI’m considering running a \"sanity regression test\" on the SOTA with seed 42 to reconfirm baseline ID 200, but I want to avoid duplicate submissions. We haven’t checked the default 0.5 recently, although we thought the area was stable. To keep things moving, we can plan to either exit or keep monitoring despite previous inactivity notices. It’s important to update the Public Memory or Archive with the new Aetheria result and any replication triggers since it’s close to the threshold.**Calculating dataset deltas**\n\nI think it would be useful to write a small script to compute per-dataset deltas. The Station environment specifically expects code submissions or storage writes. I can create an analysis file in storage at noema/results/per_dataset_deltas.md to summarize the impact of wd changes and head capacity versus baseline metrics from the logs. I already have metrics from IDs 282 and 283, so I can compute deltas compared to\
  \ ID 200 and summarize those differences.**Reviewing token management**\n\nEarlier, the deltas logged in SOTA_MONITOR were -0.0071 and -0.0121 as an aggregate. I can compute the per-dataset deltas and store those results. I might consider deleting some earlier tokens by pruning, although there's a cooldown of 4 ticks between prunes. The last prune was at tick 180, and now it's at 184. The cooldown suggests I could prune again since tokens used are at 50%. There are older tokens, like 78, which are large and not protected, so they might be candidates for pruning as well.**Deciding on updates and actions**\n\nI’m considering whether to prune tokens at this point since we’re at 50% usage, but it might not be necessary for now. I could keep the \"Meta prompt update\" current, though it’s not crucial. Instead, I could propose replicating Aetheria's 286, but it is below the threshold. \n\nFor actions, I'll write a per_dataset_deltas.md file, update compare_top_models.csv by adding ID 286, and\
  \ note changes in SOTA_MONITOR. I might also consider logging personal reflections, but that feels optional.**Planning final actions**\n\nIn my final response, I want to include my identity and location, along with a few key actions. I’ll write the per-dataset deltas and update the compare_top_models.csv. Although the scoreboard is sorted, I might also monitor the \"rank score.\" Since I'm in the Research Counter, that's great! \n\nFor actions, I’ll write the content for per_dataset_deltas.md using a bullet list, then update compare_top_models.csv by adding the new row for ID 286. I'll also update SOTA_MONITOR with a note regarding 286. Lastly, I’ll compute the per-dataset deltas for the WD variations compared to ID 200."
