    \ CRI-On 0.5039, PRS 0.5612, MRL 0.8830, Modif 0.9514, ncRNA 0.9585)\n\n  ID 291 (grad clip=0.5) vs ID 200\n  - APA:   0.8524  (Δ -0.0074)\n  - CRI-Off: 0.0658 (Δ -0.0068)\n  - CRI-On:  0.4609 (Δ -0.0430)\n  - PRS:     0.5641 (Δ +0.0029)\n  - MRL:     0.8841 (Δ +0.0011)\n  - Modif:   0.9511 (Δ -0.0003)\n  - ncRNA:   0.9554 (Δ -0.0031)\n  -> Aggregate: 0.6762 (Δ -0.0081)\n\n  ID 292 (grad clip=2.0) vs ID 200\n  - APA:   0.8546  (Δ -0.0052)\n  - CRI-Off: 0.0695 (Δ -0.0031)\n  - CRI-On:  0.4788 (Δ -0.0251)\n  - PRS:     0.5559 (Δ -0.0053)\n  - MRL:     0.8791 (Δ -0.0039)\n  - Modif:   0.9506 (Δ -0.0008)\n  - ncRNA:   0.9538 (Δ -0.0047)\n  -> Aggregate: 0.6775 (Δ -0.0068)\n\n  Conclusion: Grad clip=1.0 remains optimal under unified τ=0.5; tighter (0.5) or looser (2.0) clipping degrades CRI-On markedly and lowers APA/ncRNA on average.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/SOTA_MONITOR.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  SOTA Monitor (Tick 188)\n  - Best median: τ=0.5 ≈ 0.6830 (IDs\
    \ 200/201/203). Top single-run: 0.6859 (ID 246, τ=0.25).\n  - New ablations (τ=0.5 default, unchanged network):\n    * ID 291 (grad clip=0.5) = 0.6762 (CRI-On ↓ 0.0430; APA ↓ 0.0074)\n    * ID 292 (grad clip=2.0) = 0.6775 (CRI-On ↓ 0.0251; APA ↓ 0.0052)\n  Decision: keep grad clip=1.0. Policy unchanged—monitor only; tri-seed replicate if any result > 0.686 appears.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 4}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 188 — Failure modes (optimizer tweaks at τ=0.5)\n  - Weight decay sweeps (wd=0.005/0.02) and grad-clip sweeps (0.5/2.0) all underperform baseline (wd=0.01, clip=1.0).\n  - Common failure signals:\n    * CRI-On Spearman drops consistently with non-default wd/clip (largest losses for wd=0.005 and clip=0.5).\n    * APA and ncRNA also dip; Modif changes are negligible.\n    * PRS sometimes rises slightly (clip=0.5), but not enough to offset CRI-On/APAncRNA losses.\n  - Heuristic: keep (lr=1e-3, wd=0.01, clip=1.0, dropout=0.1)\
    \ as stable defaults for τ=0.5 mean+LSE. Deviations tend to harm CRI-On and overall aggregate.\n  - Next steps: monitor-only; replicate >0.686 if it appears; otherwise maintain artifacts.\n```"
