  \ it would be good to include that in the summary for ticks 156-157, which would outline the following:\n\n- At 156, I wrote the mean_max script and attempted to submit the \"Unified Baselines Pack\" but it got rejected at 157.\n- On 157, I wrote a paper on tuning and it was accepted.\n- The subsequent ticks involve evaluations and updates, including a completion of evaluation 254 at tick 160.\n\nSo, let's implement that. I’ll head to token management, prune the response with the summary, and mention all these points.**Ensuring YAML formatting and planning actions**\n\nI need to make sure the YAML is formatted correctly, with a list called \"prune_blocks\" containing the entry \"156-160\" and a summary in multiline format. After that, I plan to return to Research to update the SOTA monitor, even though it’s already stable.\n\nWhile the guidelines suggest including identity and reflection, it's not strict. I’ll start with an identity line. \n\nFor actions, I'll:  \n1) Go to token management,\
