tick: 209
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Noema I, currently in the Reflection Chamber. Recap: Reflection completed; next step is to test minimal, unified pooling calibrations identified (A1, A2). I will implement a calibrated pooling module and submit two low-risk variants: mean + centered LSE (τ=0.5) and mean + LN_len LSE (τ=0.5).\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/dsconv_pool_calibrated.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random, lax\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n\n  # -----------------------------\n  # Backbone block (pre-LN DSConv)\n  # -----------------------------\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dilation: int = 1\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.d_model,\n\
    \              kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n              feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n              padding='SAME',\n              kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n              name='dw_conv'\n          )(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  # -----------------------------\n  # Pooling helpers\n  # -----------------------------\n  def length_mean(h: jnp.ndarray) -> jnp.ndarray:\n      return jnp.mean(h, axis=1, keepdims=True)  # (B,1,C)\n\n  def length_std(h: jnp.ndarray, eps: float = 1e-6) -> jnp.ndarray:\n      mu = length_mean(h)\n      var = jnp.mean((h - mu) ** 2, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n      return jnp.sqrt(var + eps)  # (B,1,C)\n\n  def lse_pool(h: jnp.ndarray, tau: float) -> jnp.ndarray:\n      # Stable, length-normalized log-sum-exp per channel\n      x = h / tau             \
    \         # (B,L,C)\n      m = jnp.max(x, axis=1, keepdims=True)               # (B,1,C)\n      e = jnp.exp(x - m)                                   # (B,L,C)\n      lse = tau * (jnp.log(jnp.mean(e, axis=1) + 1e-12) + jnp.squeeze(m, axis=1))  # (B,C)\n      return lse\n\n  # -----------------------------\n  # Calibrated pooling network\n  # -----------------------------\n  class RNANetPoolCalibrated(nn.Module):\n      d_input: int = 4\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type: str = 'regression'\n      d_model: int = 256\n      num_blocks: int = 5\n      dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      positional_encoding: bool = False\n\n      # pooling config\n      aggregator: str = 'mean_lse_centered'   # 'mean_lse' | 'mean_lse_centered' | 'mean_lse_lnlen'\n      tau: float = 0.5\n      calibrate_scalar: bool = False          # if True, learn a single global scalar s>0 for the LSE branch\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def\
    \ __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # Input projection\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # DSConv stack\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              d = self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n              h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Mean branch (raw)\n          mean_vec = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)  # (B,C)\n\n          # Extreme branch (calibrated)\n          if self.aggregator == 'mean_lse':\n              h_ex = h\n          elif self.aggregator == 'mean_lse_centered':\n              mu = length_mean(h)          # (B,1,C)\n              h_ex = h - mu\n          elif self.aggregator == 'mean_lse_lnlen':\n              mu = length_mean(h)\n              sd = length_std(h)\n              h_ex =\
    \ (h - mu) / sd\n          else:\n              raise ValueError(f\"Unknown aggregator: {self.aggregator}\")\n\n          e = lse_pool(h_ex, self.tau)     # (B,C)\n\n          if self.calibrate_scalar:\n              # single learned scalar s>0 shared across datasets (global)\n              s_raw = self.param('s_raw', nn.initializers.constant(jnp.log(jnp.exp(1.0) - 1.0)), ())  # softplus^-1(1.0)\n              s = nn.softplus(s_raw)\n              e = s * e\n\n          fused = jnp.concatenate([mean_vec, e], axis=-1)  # (B, 2C)\n\n          # Head\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out')(z)\n\n          if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n              return logits.squeeze(-1)\n          return logits\n\n  class PoolCalibratedNetwork:\n      def __init__(self, d_input,\
    \ d_output, task_type, **kwargs):\n          self.network = RNANetPoolCalibrated(d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, **kwargs)\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def build_network(d_output: int, task_type: str, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return PoolCalibratedNetwork(\n          d_input=4,\n          d_output=d_output,\n          task_type=task_type,\n\
    \          d_model=hparams.get('d_model', 256),\n          num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks', 5),\n          dilations=tuple(hparams.get('dilations', [1,2,4,8,16])),\n          kernel_size=hparams.get('kernel_size', 7),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n          positional_encoding=hparams.get('positional_encoding', False),\n          aggregator=hparams.get('aggregator', 'mean_lse_centered'),\n          tau=hparams.get('tau', 0.5),\n          calibrate_scalar=hparams.get('calibrate_scalar', False),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01),\n      )\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"A1: Calibrated Pooling — mean + centered LSE (tau=0.5)\"\ntags: \"cnn, pooling, calibration, mean-centered, lse, unified\"\nabstract: \"Extreme branch uses lengthwise mean-centering before LSE (tau=0.5),\
    \ fused with raw mean. Hypothesis: removes baseline channel bias without harming translation invariance; unified across datasets.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dsconv_pool_calibrated import build_network, create_optimizer as make_optimizer\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_encoding': False,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse_centered',\n          'tau': 0.5,\n          'calibrate_scalar': False\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return make_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state,\
    \ trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"A2: Calibrated Pooling — mean + LN_len LSE (tau=0.5)\"\ntags: \"cnn, pooling, layernorm, lse, unified\"\nabstract: \"Extreme branch uses lengthwise LayerNorm before LSE (tau=0.5), fused with raw mean; per-sample, per-channel normalization along length only. Tests scale-invariance without harming proven mean path.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dsconv_pool_calibrated import build_network, create_optimizer as make_optimizer\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_encoding': False,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse_lnlen',\n          'tau': 0.5,\n\
    \          'calibrate_scalar': False\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return make_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/append_tick209.csv}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  eval_id,title,notes\n  (pending),\"A1: Calibrated Pooling — mean + centered LSE (tau=0.5)\",\"Unified; extreme branch centered along length; fused with raw mean; seed=42\"\n  (pending),\"A2: Calibrated Pooling — mean + LN_len LSE (tau=0.5)\",\"Unified; extreme branch lengthwise LayerNorm; fused with raw mean; seed=42\"\n```"
