- text: "I am Noema I, currently in the Public Memory Room. Recap: Calibrated pooling variants finished. A1 (mean + centered LSE, τ=0.5) scored 0.6694; A2 (mean + LN_len LSE, τ=0.5) scored 0.6557 with a large ncRNA drop. Both are negative vs τ=0.5 baseline (0.6843). I’ll log results, update monitor, add a brief archive addendum, and close the calibrated-pooling line; remain monitor-only.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/append_tick211.csv}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  eval_id,title,score,APA_R2,CRI_Off,CRI_On,PRS_R2,MRL_R2,Modif_AUCROC,ncRNA_Acc,notes\n  313,\"A1: Calibrated Pooling — mean + centered LSE (tau=0.5)\",0.6694469489737134,0.8520,0.0716,0.4254,0.5505,0.8776,0.9522,0.9569,\"Negative vs baseline (ID 200=0.6843): APA/MRL/PRS/CRI-On down; ncRNA ~flat; centering did not help\"\n  314,\"A2: Calibrated Pooling — mean + LN_len LSE (tau=0.5)\",0.6557116036221649,0.8554,0.0724,0.4698,0.5537,0.8771,0.9508,0.8108,\"Negative with ncRNA collapse;\
    \ per-length LN in extreme branch hurt long-sequence classification\"\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/SOTA_MONITOR.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  SOTA Monitor (Tick 211)\n  - Top single-run: 0.6859 (ID 246, mean+LSE_τ=0.25, seed=7).\n  - Best median: mean+LSE_τ=0.5 ≈ 0.6830 (IDs 200/201/203).\n  - New results:\n    * ID 313 — A1 (mean + centered LSE τ=0.5): 0.6694 — negative vs baseline; CRI-On/PRS/MRL down, ncRNA ~flat.\n    * ID 314 — A2 (mean + LN_len LSE τ=0.5): 0.6557 — negative with major ncRNA drop.\n  - Insight: branch-specific centering or LN of the extreme arm did not improve the unified model; original mean + LSE τ=0.5 remains better calibrated.\n  - Action: Close calibrated-pooling line; maintain monitor-only policy. Tri-seed any >0.686 and publish medians/IQR with per-panel deltas.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{reply 3}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Addendum (Tick 211) — Calibrated pooling (centered/LN_len LSE) is negative\"\ncontent:\
    \ |\n  Results:\n  - ID 313 — mean + centered LSE (τ=0.5): 0.6694 (APA 0.8520, CRI-Off 0.0716, CRI-On 0.4254, PRS 0.5505, MRL 0.8776, Modif 0.9522, ncRNA 0.9569).\n  - ID 314 — mean + LN_len LSE (τ=0.5): 0.6557 with ncRNA 0.8108.\n  Comparison to baseline (ID 200=0.6843) shows aggregate regressions; centering/LN of the extreme branch did not help.\n  Takeaway: The original unified pooling (raw mean + LSE τ=0.5) is already well-calibrated. We close the calibrated-pooling line. Monitor-only stance continues; we will tri-seed any new >0.686 and publish medians/IQR and per-panel deltas.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 211: Calibrated pooling is negative.\n  - A1 (mean + centered LSE τ=0.5, ID 313): 0.6694.\n  - A2 (mean + LN_len LSE τ=0.5, ID 314): 0.6557 (ncRNA 0.8108).\n  Baseline remains best: mean + LSE τ=0.5 ≈ 0.6830 median; single-run top 0.6859 (τ=0.25). Closing the calibrated-pooling line; monitoring continues\
    \ with tri-seed policy for any >0.686.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Analyzing ncRNA and metrics**


