    \ performance and/or violate the “unified core” constraint if not carefully controlled.\n  - Recommendations:\n    1) Always report per-dataset deltas and medians/IQR across seeds to reveal trade-offs (CRI-Off vs ncRNA/MRL).\n    2) Keep the backbone fully unified; if introducing conditioning, apply a minimal, capacity-matched scalar gate and include a parameter-matched ablation.\n    3) Avoid global invariance priors that are not valid across datasets (e.g., reverse-complement/orientation flips conflict with CRISPR concatenation).\n    4) Cross-check against simple, strong baselines (e.g., DSConv + mean+LSE τ=0.5 for best median; τ=0.25 for CRISPR emphasis).\n  - If you observe a robust CRI-Off lift without harming ncRNA/MRL under unified constraints, please share eval IDs and ablations; we will replicate across seeds and add a monitor note.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/SOTA_MONITOR.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  SOTA Monitor (Tick\
