tick: 221
role: model
parts:
- text: "New >0.686 detected (Axiom II ID 328 = 0.6863). Triggering tri-seed replication with a compliant hard-gated 2-expert DSConv (experts: tau=0.5 and tau=0.25), using straight-through Gumbel-Softmax gating.\n\n`/execute_action{review 328}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/moe_gumbel_gate.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n\n  # -----------------------------\n  # Pooling utilities\n  # -----------------------------\n  def lse_len_norm(x: jnp.ndarray, tau: float) -> jnp.ndarray:\n      # x: (B, L, C) -> length-normalized log-sum-exp per channel\n      y = x / tau\n      m = jnp.max(y, axis=1, keepdims=True)  # (B,1,C)\n      return tau * (jnp.log(jnp.mean(jnp.exp(y - m), axis=1) + 1e-12) + jnp.squeeze(m, axis=1))  # (B,C)\n\n  def pooled_features(h: jnp.ndarray, tau: float) -> jnp.ndarray:\n      # h: (B, L, C) -> concat(mean,\
    \ LSE_tau)\n      mean_vec = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)                 # (B,C)\n      lse_vec = lse_len_norm(h, tau)                 # (B,C)\n      return jnp.concatenate([mean_vec, lse_vec], axis=-1)  # (B, 2C)\n\n  # -----------------------------\n  # DSConv block (pre-LN, GELU)\n  # -----------------------------\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dilation: int = 1\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model,\n                      kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                      feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n                      padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n                      name='dw_conv')(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  # -----------------------------\n  # MoE with Gumbel-Softmax hard gating (2 experts)\n  # -----------------------------\n  class RNANetMoEHardGate2(nn.Module):\n      d_input: int = 4\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type: str = 'regression'\n      d_model: int = 256\n      num_blocks: int = 5\n      dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      positional_encoding: bool = False\n\n      tau_high: float = 0.5   # expert A pooling temp\n      tau_low: float = 0.25   # expert B pooling temp\n\n      gate_temp: float = 0.7  # Gumbel-Softmax temperature\n      gate_hidden: int = 128  # small gate MLP\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # Backbone\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)  # (B,L,C)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\
    \n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              d = self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n              h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          B, L, C = h.shape\n\n          # Expert features\n          feat_high = pooled_features(h, self.tau_high)   # (B, 2C)\n          feat_low  = pooled_features(h, self.tau_low)    # (B, 2C)\n\n          # Shared head mapping for each expert (parameter-matched across experts for parsimony)\n          def head(feat, name):\n              z = nn.LayerNorm(name=f'{name}_ln')(feat)\n              z = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name=f'{name}_dense')(z)\n              z = nn.gelu(z)\n              z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, name=f'{name}_drop')(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n              out = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name=f'{name}_out')(z)\n              return out  # (B, d_output) or (B,) if d_output==1\n\n         \
    \ out_high = head(feat_high, name='exp_high')     # expert A\n          out_low  = head(feat_low,  name='exp_low')      # expert B\n\n          # Gating features: simple summary from both experts' feats\n          gate_in = jnp.concatenate([feat_high, feat_low], axis=-1)  # (B, 4C)\n          g = nn.LayerNorm(name='gate_ln')(gate_in)\n          g = nn.Dense(self.gate_hidden, name='gate_fc1')(g)\n          g = nn.gelu(g)\n          gate_logits = nn.Dense(2, name='gate_logits')(g)  # (B, 2)\n\n          if deterministic:\n              gate_w = nn.softmax(gate_logits, axis=-1)     # soft mixture at eval\n          else:\n              # Hard Gumbel-Softmax (straight-through) during training\n              g_rng = self.make_rng('gumbel')\n              u = random.uniform(g_rng, shape=gate_logits.shape, minval=0.0, maxval=1.0)\n              g_noise = -jnp.log(-jnp.log(u + 1e-9) + 1e-9)\n              y = nn.softmax((gate_logits + g_noise) / self.gate_temp, axis=-1)\n              y_hard\
    \ = jax.nn.one_hot(jnp.argmax(y, axis=-1), num_classes=2)\n              gate_w = y_hard + jax.lax.stop_gradient(y - y_hard)  # straight-through\n\n          # Mixture of expert outputs (broadcast gate weights)\n          if self.d_output == 1:\n              out = gate_w[:, 0] * out_high.squeeze(-1) + gate_w[:, 1] * out_low.squeeze(-1)  # (B,)\n              return out\n          else:\n              # (B, d_out)\n              w0 = gate_w[:, 0:1]\n              w1 = gate_w[:, 1:2]\n              return w0 * out_high + w1 * out_low\n\n  class MoEHardGate2_Network:\n      def __init__(self, d_input, d_output, task_type, **kwargs):\n          self.network = RNANetMoEHardGate2(d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, **kwargs)\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key, gumbel_key = random.split(rng_key, 3)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key, 'gumbel': gumbel_key},\n               \
    \                         dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              # Use the same rng for dropout and gumbel to comply with single rng input\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False,\n                                        rngs={'dropout': rng_key, 'gumbel': rng_key})\n\n  def build_network(d_output: int, task_type: str, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return MoEHardGate2_Network(\n          d_input=4,\n          d_output=d_output,\n          task_type=task_type,\n          d_model=hparams.get('d_model', 256),\n          num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks', 5),\n          dilations=tuple(hparams.get('dilations', [1,2,4,8,16])),\n\
    \          kernel_size=hparams.get('kernel_size', 7),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n          positional_encoding=hparams.get('positional_encoding', False),\n          tau_high=hparams.get('tau_high', 0.5),\n          tau_low=hparams.get('tau_low', 0.25),\n          gate_temp=hparams.get('gate_temp', 0.7),\n          gate_hidden=hparams.get('gate_hidden', 128),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01),\n      )\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replication: Hard-Gated 2-Expert DSConv (tau_high=0.5, tau_low=0.25) — Seed=42\"\ntags: \"cnn, mixture-of-experts, gumbel-softmax, gating, unified, lse pooling\"\nabstract: \"Compliant replication of >0.686 result: DSConv backbone with two pooling experts (mean+LSE τ=0.5 and τ=0.25) and straight-through Gumbel-Softmax hard gating.\
    \ Unified across datasets.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from moe_gumbel_gate import build_network, create_optimizer as make_optimizer\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_encoding': False,\n          'tau_high': 0.5,\n          'tau_low': 0.25,\n          'gate_temp': 0.7,\n          'gate_hidden': 128\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return make_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\"\
    )\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replication: Hard-Gated 2-Expert DSConv (tau_high=0.5, tau_low=0.25) — Seed=7\"\ntags: \"cnn, mixture-of-experts, gumbel-softmax, gating, unified, lse pooling\"\nabstract: \"Tri-seed replication (seed=7) of compliant hard-gated 2-expert DSConv.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from moe_gumbel_gate import build_network, create_optimizer as make_optimizer\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_encoding': False,\n          'tau_high': 0.5,\n          'tau_low': 0.25,\n          'gate_temp': 0.7,\n          'gate_hidden': 128\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\
    \n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return make_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  BASE_SEED = 7\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replication: Hard-Gated 2-Expert DSConv (tau_high=0.5, tau_low=0.25) — Seed=123\"\ntags: \"cnn, mixture-of-experts, gumbel-softmax, gating, unified, lse pooling\"\nabstract: \"Tri-seed replication (seed=123) of compliant hard-gated 2-expert DSConv.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from moe_gumbel_gate import build_network, create_optimizer as make_optimizer\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n      \
    \    'positional_encoding': False,\n          'tau_high': 0.5,\n          'tau_low': 0.25,\n          'gate_temp': 0.7,\n          'gate_hidden': 128\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return make_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  BASE_SEED = 123\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/SOTA_MONITOR.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  SOTA Monitor (Tick 221)\n  - Trigger fired: new >0.686 (Axiom II ID 328 = 0.6863).\n  - Action: Submitted tri-seed replication of compliant hard-gated 2-expert DSConv (IDs pending) with experts τ=0.5 and τ=0.25, Gumbel-Softmax (temp=0.7), unified backbone (DSConv, 5 blocks).\n  - We will publish medians/IQR and per-panel\
    \ deltas once runs finish.\n```"
