parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 222\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noema I\n- Agent Description: An agent advancing novelty and parsimony through rigorous, insight-driven experimentation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nNoema Meta (Tick 184)\nObjectives:\n- Monitor leaderboard; replicate any >0.686 across seeds {42,7,123}; publish medians/IQR + per-panel deltas.\n- Maintain reproducibility artifacts (results/*.csv, SOTA_MONITOR.md, compare_top_models.csv, submissions/ scripts).\nDefaults:\n- Unified DSConv (5 dilated blocks 1,2,4,8,16; d_model=256; kernel=7; GELU; no PE).\n- Pooling default: mean + LSE τ=0.5 (len-normalized). Optional: τ=0.25 for CRISPR emphasis (higher variance).\n- Optimizer: AdamW lr=1e-3, wd=0.01; batch=64; grad clip=1.0; dropout=0.1; patience=10.\nClosed lines (negative):\n- Dual-path mean+LSE(0.5)+LSE(0.25); intermediate τ=0.35; pairwise/gated/learnable-τ; spectral; CLS/CA-query.\n- Head capacity tweaks at τ=0.5;\
    \ AdamW wd=0.005/0.02 optimizer-only.\nTriggers:\n- If >0.686 appears: tri-seed replication, analysis addendum in archive/public.\n- If CRI-Off improves without hurting ncRNA/MRL: analyze mechanism vs τ=0.25 trade-offs.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 110,256 / 270,000 used (41%)\n- Agent Age: 222 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, signed-LSE_pos, signed-LSE_neg) τ=0.5' (ID: 330) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6691117830712521\n**APA_R2:** 0.8529\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0603\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9507\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4420\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5532\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8770\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9477\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 330\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed critical bug in JAX activation function call. The code now runs without crashing and has been executing for over 300 seconds,\
    \ indicating the fix is working correctly.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission imported functions from `storage/noema/submissions/dsconv_pool_signed.py`, which contained a bug in the `RNANetSignedLSE` class. Specifically, lines 70-71 used:\n\n```python\npos = jnp.relu(h)    # INCORRECT\nneg = jnp.relu(-h)   # INCORRECT\n```\n\n**The Problem**: JAX does not have a `relu` function in the `jax.numpy` (jnp) module. The ReLU activation function exists in `jax.nn.relu`, not `jnp.relu`. This caused an `AttributeError: module 'jax.numpy' has no attribute 'relu'` during network initialization.\n\n## Fix Applied\nCreated `submissions/submission_v2.py` with the following changes:\n\n1. **Kept working imports**: Continued to import `build_network`, `create_optimizer`, `lse_len_norm`, `DSConvDilatedBlock`, and `SignedLSE_Network` from the original lineage file, as these components work correctly.\n\n2. **Copied and fixed buggy class**: Copied the `RNANetSignedLSE` class into the submission\
    \ and corrected lines 38-39:\n   ```python\n   pos = jax.nn.relu(h)    # FIXED\n   neg = jax.nn.relu(-h)   # FIXED\n   ```\n\n3. **Created wrapper class**: Implemented `FixedSignedLSE_Network` class that uses the corrected `RNANetSignedLSE` module.\n\n4. **Updated network creation**: Modified `create_network()` to instantiate `FixedSignedLSE_Network` instead of calling the buggy `build_network()` function.\n\n## Verification\n- Monitor script confirmed the code has been running for 300+ seconds without crashes\n- Exit code 0 indicates successful execution\n- The evaluation is still in progress (training neural networks takes time), but the code is functioning correctly\n\n## Recommendation\nThe fix is complete and working. No further action is needed. The agent can use this corrected implementation for future submissions that need signed-evidence pooling with DSConv blocks.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage\
    \ files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\nfrom dsconv_pool_signed import build_network, create_optimizer as make_optimizer, lse_len_norm, DSConvDilatedBlock, SignedLSE_Network\n\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Sequence\n\n# Fixed version of RNANetSignedLSE with correct relu import\nclass RNANetSignedLSE(nn.Module):\n    d_input: int = 4\n    d_output: int = 1\n    task_type: str = 'regression'\n    d_model: int = 256\n    num_blocks: int = 5\n    dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n    kernel_size: int = 7\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n    positional_encoding: bool = False\n    tau: float = 0.5\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # Input projection\n        h = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # DSConv stack\n        for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n            d = self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n            h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Signed-evidence pooling - FIX: use jax.nn.relu instead of jnp.relu\n        mean_vec = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)                 # (B,C)\n        pos = jax.nn.relu(h)                           # (B,L,C) - FIXED\n        neg = jax.nn.relu(-h)                          # (B,L,C) - FIXED\n        lse_pos = lse_len_norm(pos, self.tau)          # (B,C)\n        lse_neg = lse_len_norm(neg, self.tau)          # (B,C)\n        fused = jnp.concatenate([mean_vec, lse_pos, lse_neg], axis=-1)  # (B, 3C)\n\n        # Head\n        z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n        z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z)\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n\
    \        logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out')(z)\n\n        if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n            return logits.squeeze(-1)\n        return logits\n\n# Fixed version of SignedLSE_Network using the corrected RNANetSignedLSE\nclass FixedSignedLSE_Network:\n    def __init__(self, d_input, d_output, task_type, **kwargs):\n        self.network = RNANetSignedLSE(d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, **kwargs)\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None:\n                rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n    \
    \        return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'd_model': 256,\n        'num_blocks': 5,\n        'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n        'kernel_size': 7,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n        'positional_encoding': False,\n        'tau': 0.5\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    # Use the fixed network class\n    return FixedSignedLSE_Network(\n        d_input=4,\n        d_output=hparams.get('d_output', 1),\n        task_type=hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'),\n        d_model=hparams.get('d_model', 256),\n        num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks', 5),\n        dilations=tuple(hparams.get('dilations', [1,2,4,8,16])),\n        kernel_size=hparams.get('kernel_size', 7),\n        dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n        positional_encoding=hparams.get('positional_encoding', False),\n        tau=hparams.get('tau',\
    \ 0.5),\n    )\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return make_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\ndef complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n    ds = trial_data.get('dataset')\n    vm = trial_data.get('val_metric')\n    print(f\"[Complete] {ds} val_metric={vm}\")\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape:\
    \ (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n\
    \  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: from submission\n  BASE_SEED: 42 (from submission\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials: 7\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 240.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune multi-dataset training...\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-On dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-On Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 1453 train, 207 val, seq_len=23\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n\
    \ 10  | 0.0112 |  0.4177  | 0.4177 \n 20  | 0.0060 |  0.4109  | 0.4420 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 25 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.4420 Time:19s\n[Complete] CRI-On val_metric=0.44199245597514913\n\nCRI-On training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.441992\nTraining time: 26s\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-Off dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-Off Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 14223 train, 2032 val, seq_len=46\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0004 |  0.0559  | 0.0603 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 19 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.0603 Time:68s\n[Complete] CRI-Off val_metric=0.06028011567541954\n\nCRI-Off training completed:\n\
    Validation spearman: 0.060280\nTraining time: 75s\n\nStarting RNA training on ncRNA dataset\nTask type: multiclass_classification, Output dim: 13\nMetric: accuracy, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nncRNA Training (multiclass_classification, accuracy)\nData: 5670 train, 650 val, seq_len=1136\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val ACCURACY|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0434 |  0.9292  | 0.9369 \n 20  | 0.0151 |  0.9400  | 0.9477 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 23 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.9477 Time:874s\n[Complete] ncRNA val_metric=0.9476923076923077\n\nncRNA training completed:\nValidation accuracy: 0.947692\nTraining time: 882s\n\nStarting RNA training on MRL dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nMRL Training (regression, r2)\nData: 76319 train, 7600 val, seq_len=100\n=============================================\n\
