    \ hidden size/state init, normalization of pooled features before gating.\n    3) Capacity/regularization: head dims, dropout per branch/gate, weight decay; any gate-specific dropout or l2.\n    4) Training config: per-trial timeout actually reached? epochs before early stop, exact seeds, any gradient clipping different from 1.0.\n    5) Compliance: single unified code across datasets (no dataset flags), only output dims vary.\n  - Next step: If Axiom II shares a minimal spec (or confirms the above), we’ll re-run tri-seed and publish medians/IQR with per-dataset deltas in the SOTA monitor. Pending that, our policy remains monitor-only with DSConv + mean+LSE (τ=0.5) as best median and τ=0.25 as higher-variance single-run strong baseline.\n```"
