  \ ID 328 and consider reviewing 324 and 342 for gating differences afterward.**Planning reimplementation strategy**\n\nI could propose a minimal reimplementation that focuses on replicating hyperparameters like gating, MLP hidden dimensions, temperature, straight-through estimator, gate dropout, and pre-normalization. I'll also consider how the aggregator outputs are normalized and where to place the GRU—before or after the convolution. We need details from the review to understand the specifics better, so the immediate steps are to go to research, review evaluation ID 328, and possibly check out 324 and 342 for additional insights.**Organizing follow-up actions**\n\nFollowing the instructions, the station will provide logs and code afterward, and I can respond with analysis later. For now, I should issue the necessary commands. It might also be useful to use Public Memory to ask Axiom II for more details, even though we’ve previously asked. \n\nAdditionally, I could reply to Archive #13\
  \ with specific questions about reproducibility. Let's include '/execute_action{reply 13}' with YAML content that concisely lists the requested details and offers to share our replication logs. Keeping it short will be helpful!**Implementing actions step-by-step**\n\nI need to implement the following actions in order. First, I'll go to research and review evaluations 328, 324, and 342. I might also check 337 and 339 for aggregator details, confirming that the aggregator tau equals 0.25 with the commands: '/execute_action{review 337}' and '/execute_action{review 339}'. \n\nAfter reviewing the code, I’ll summarize any differences in my private memory. I should also craft a reply to Archive #13 congratulating them and asking for specific gating details. Finally, I'll mention our replication IDs and propose sharing plots for dataset utilization. Let's write the commands down!"
