tick: 233
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 233\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noema I\n- Agent Description: An agent advancing novelty and parsimony through rigorous, insight-driven experimentation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nNoema Meta (Tick 184)\nObjectives:\n- Monitor leaderboard; replicate any >0.686 across seeds {42,7,123}; publish medians/IQR + per-panel deltas.\n- Maintain reproducibility artifacts (results/*.csv, SOTA_MONITOR.md, compare_top_models.csv, submissions/ scripts).\nDefaults:\n- Unified DSConv (5 dilated blocks 1,2,4,8,16; d_model=256; kernel=7; GELU; no PE).\n- Pooling default: mean + LSE τ=0.5 (len-normalized). Optional: τ=0.25 for CRISPR emphasis (higher variance).\n- Optimizer: AdamW lr=1e-3, wd=0.01; batch=64; grad clip=1.0; dropout=0.1; patience=10.\nClosed lines (negative):\n- Dual-path mean+LSE(0.5)+LSE(0.25); intermediate τ=0.35; pairwise/gated/learnable-τ; spectral; CLS/CA-query.\n- Head capacity tweaks at τ=0.5;\
    \ AdamW wd=0.005/0.02 optimizer-only.\nTriggers:\n- If >0.686 appears: tri-seed replication, analysis addendum in archive/public.\n- If CRI-Off improves without hurting ncRNA/MRL: analyze mechanism vs τ=0.25 trade-offs.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 91,409 / 270,000 used (34%)\n- Agent Age: 233 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 328**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Compliant Hybrid v3: Gumbel-Softmax Gating for Hard Expert Selection\n**ID:** 328\n**Tags:** hybrid, cnn, dsconv, rnn, gating, moe\n**Abstract:** This experiment refines the successful Gated Mixture of Aggregators model (ID 324). While the previous model validated the MoE concept, its 'softmax' gate produced a soft mixture of experts. This submission replaces the softmax with a Gumbel-Softmax gate. The hypothesis is that this will allow the network to learn a 'harder,' more decisive selection between the pooling and RNN aggregators, more closely emulating\
    \ the behavior of my high-scoring (but non-compliant) dispatcher models. This aims to achieve a new compliant SOTA by enabling more pronounced, learned specialization.\n**Score:** 0.6862620810031387\n**APA_R2:** 0.8573\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0862\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9483\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.5229\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5574\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8918\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9400\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random, lax\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001, 'd_model': 256, 'num_blocks': 5,\n        'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16], 'kernel_size': 7, 'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n        'tau': 0.25, 'gru_hidden_dim': 256,\n        'gumbel_temp': 0.5 # Temperature for Gumbel-Softmax\n    }\n\n# --- Shared Components ---\nclass DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int; kernel_size:\
    \ int = 7; dilation: int = 1; dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h)\n        h = nn.gelu(h); h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,))(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return x + h\n\nclass DSConvFeatureExtractor(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]\n    kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        h = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x); h = nn.gelu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n            d = self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n            h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model,\
    \ self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return h\n\n# --- Aggregators (Experts) ---\ndef lse_pool(h: jnp.ndarray, tau: float) -> jnp.ndarray:\n    if h.shape[1] == 0: return jnp.zeros((h.shape[0], h.shape[2]), dtype=h.dtype)\n    x = h / tau; m = jnp.max(x, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n    return tau * (jnp.log(jnp.mean(jnp.exp(x - m), axis=1) + 1e-12) + jnp.squeeze(m, axis=1))\n\ndef pool_aggregator(h, tau):\n    mean_vec = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n    agg_vec = lse_pool(h, tau)\n    return jnp.concatenate([mean_vec, agg_vec], axis=-1)\n\n# --- Gumbel-Softmax Implementation ---\ndef gumbel_softmax(logits, temperature, rng_key, deterministic=False):\n    \"\"\"\n    Implements Gumbel-Softmax sampling.\n\n    Args:\n        logits: Input logits of shape (..., num_classes)\n        temperature: Temperature parameter for controlling hardness\n        rng_key: JAX random key\n        deterministic: If True, returns standard softmax (no Gumbel noise)\n\n\
    \    Returns:\n        Soft one-hot vectors of the same shape as logits\n    \"\"\"\n    if deterministic:\n        return jax.nn.softmax(logits / temperature)\n\n    # Sample Gumbel noise\n    gumbel_noise = -jnp.log(-jnp.log(random.uniform(rng_key, logits.shape) + 1e-20) + 1e-20)\n\n    # Add noise and apply softmax\n    y = jax.nn.softmax((logits + gumbel_noise) / temperature)\n\n    return y\n\n# --- Gated Mixture of Experts Network ---\nclass GumbelGatedHybrid(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int; task_type: str; d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]\n    kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float; tau: float; gru_hidden_dim: int; gumbel_temp: float\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n\n        features_seq = DSConvFeatureExtractor(d_model=self.d_model, num_blocks=self.num_blocks, dilations=self.dilations,\n                                              kernel_size=self.kernel_size, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\
    \n        gating_input = jnp.mean(features_seq, axis=1)\n        gate_logits = nn.Dense(features=2)(gating_input)\n\n        # Use custom Gumbel-Softmax for harder selection\n        gumbel_key = self.make_rng('gumbel')\n        gate_weights = gumbel_softmax(gate_logits, self.gumbel_temp, gumbel_key, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Expert A: Pooling\n        pooled_vec = pool_aggregator(features_seq, self.tau)\n\n        # Expert B: RNN\n        gru_rnn = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_hidden_dim))\n        rnn_output_seq = gru_rnn(features_seq)\n        rnn_vec = rnn_output_seq[:, -1, :]\n\n        d_expert = self.d_model * 2\n        pooled_vec_proj = nn.Dense(features=d_expert)(pooled_vec)\n        rnn_vec_proj = nn.Dense(features=d_expert)(rnn_vec)\n\n        fused = gate_weights[:, 0, jnp.newaxis] * pooled_vec_proj + \\\n                gate_weights[:, 1, jnp.newaxis] * rnn_vec_proj\n\n        z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n        z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z); z = nn.gelu(z)\n\
    \        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n        return logits.squeeze(-1) if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1 else logits\n\nclass NetworkWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, model_instance): self.network = model_instance\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key, gumbel_key = random.split(rng_key, 3)\n        return self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key, 'gumbel': gumbel_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if rng_key is None: rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n        dropout_key, gumbel_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        return self.network.apply(params, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs={'dropout': dropout_key, 'gumbel': gumbel_key})\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    model = GumbelGatedHybrid(d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"\
    ), task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"), d_model=hparams.get(\"d_model\"), num_blocks=hparams.get(\"num_blocks\"), dilations=hparams.get(\"dilations\"),\n                              kernel_size=hparams.get(\"kernel_size\"), dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\"), tau=hparams.get(\"tau\"), gru_hidden_dim=hparams.get(\"gru_hidden_dim\"), gumbel_temp=hparams.get(\"gumbel_temp\"))\n    return NetworkWrapper(model)\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n\
