    \ Compliant Hybrid v2: Gated Mixture of Aggregators\n**ID:** 324\n**Tags:** hybrid, cnn, dsconv, rnn, pooling, gating\n**Abstract:** This submission implements a 'Mixture of Experts' architecture, directly inspired by reviewer feedback (Archive #8) and the results of my first compliant hybrid (ID 321). Instead of naive concatenation, this model introduces a learned gating mechanism. For each input, it computes a DSConv feature sequence. From this sequence, a small gating network predicts a set of weights. These weights are then used to create a weighted sum of the outputs from two parallel 'expert' aggregators: a pooling aggregator and an RNN aggregator. This allows the model to learn a dynamic, task-specific fusion of aggregation strategies in a fully compliant manner.\n**Score:** 0.6783199781794546\n**APA_R2:** 0.8441\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0789\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9502\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4863\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5565\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8800\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9523\n**Evaluation\
    \ Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random, lax\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001, 'd_model': 256, 'num_blocks': 5,\n        'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16], 'kernel_size': 7, 'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n        'tau': 0.25, 'gru_hidden_dim': 256\n    }\n\n# --- Shared Components ---\nclass DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int; kernel_size: int = 7; dilation: int = 1; dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h)\n        h = nn.gelu(h); h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,))(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic)\n        return x + h\n\nclass DSConvFeatureExtractor(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]\n    kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        h = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x); h = nn.gelu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n            d = self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n            h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return h\n\n# --- Aggregators (Experts) ---\ndef lse_pool(h: jnp.ndarray, tau: float) -> jnp.ndarray:\n    if h.shape[1] == 0: return jnp.zeros((h.shape[0], h.shape[2]), dtype=h.dtype)\n    x = h / tau; m = jnp.max(x, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n    return tau * (jnp.log(jnp.mean(jnp.exp(x - m), axis=1) + 1e-12) + jnp.squeeze(m, axis=1))\n\n\
    def pool_aggregator(h, tau):\n    mean_vec = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n    agg_vec = lse_pool(h, tau)\n    return jnp.concatenate([mean_vec, agg_vec], axis=-1)\n\n# --- Gated Mixture of Experts Network ---\nclass GatedHybrid(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int; task_type: str; d_model: int; num_blocks: int; dilations: Sequence[int]\n    kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float; tau: float; gru_hidden_dim: int\n    \n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        \n        # 1. Unified Feature Extraction\n        feature_extractor = DSConvFeatureExtractor(d_model=self.d_model, num_blocks=self.num_blocks, dilations=self.dilations,\n                                                   kernel_size=self.kernel_size, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)\n        features_seq = feature_extractor(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # 2. Gating Network\n        gating_input = jnp.mean(features_seq, axis=1) # Simple global average for gate\n        gate_logits = nn.Dense(features=2)(gating_input)\n\
    \        gate_weights = nn.softmax(gate_logits, axis=-1)\n\n        # 3. Parallel Experts\n        # Expert A: Pooling Aggregator\n        pooled_vec = pool_aggregator(features_seq, self.tau)\n\n        # Expert B: RNN Aggregator\n        gru_rnn = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_hidden_dim))\n        rnn_output_seq = gru_rnn(features_seq)\n        rnn_vec = rnn_output_seq[:, -1, :]\n        \n        # Resize experts to same dimension for weighted sum\n        d_expert = self.d_model * 2\n        pooled_vec_proj = nn.Dense(features=d_expert)(pooled_vec)\n        rnn_vec_proj = nn.Dense(features=d_expert)(rnn_vec)\n\n        # 4. Gated Fusion (Mixture of Experts)\n        fused = gate_weights[:, 0, jnp.newaxis] * pooled_vec_proj + \\\n                gate_weights[:, 1, jnp.newaxis] * rnn_vec_proj\n        \n        # 5. Final MLP Head\n        z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n        z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z); z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n\
    \        logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n        return logits.squeeze(-1) if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1 else logits\n\nclass NetworkWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, model_instance): self.network = model_instance\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        return self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if rng_key is None: rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n        return self.network.apply(params, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    model = GatedHybrid(d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"), task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"), d_model=hparams.get(\"d_model\"), num_blocks=hparams.get(\"num_blocks\"), dilations=hparams.get(\"dilations\"),\n                        kernel_size=hparams.get(\"kernel_size\"\
    ), dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\"), tau=hparams.get(\"tau\"), gru_hidden_dim=hparams.get(\"gru_hidden_dim\"))\n    return NetworkWrapper(model)\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n\
