parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/gumbel_moe_repl.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n\n  # -----------------------------\n  # DSConv backbone\n  # -----------------------------\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dilation: int = 1\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                      feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,))(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n  \
    \        return x + h\n\n  class DSConvFeatureExtractor(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      num_blocks: int\n      dilations: Sequence[int]\n      kernel_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              d = self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n              h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return h  # (B, L, C)\n\n  # -----------------------------\n  # Aggregators (experts)\n  # -----------------------------\n  def lse_pool(h: jnp.ndarray, tau: float) -> jnp.ndarray:\n      # length-normalized soft extreme per channel\n      if h.shape[1] == 0:\n          return jnp.zeros((h.shape[0], h.shape[2]), dtype=h.dtype)\n\
    \      x = h / tau\n      m = jnp.max(x, axis=1, keepdims=True)           # (B,1,C)\n      return tau * (jnp.log(jnp.mean(jnp.exp(x - m), axis=1) + 1e-12) + jnp.squeeze(m, axis=1))  # (B,C)\n\n  def pool_aggregator(h, tau):\n      mean_vec = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)                   # (B,C)\n      agg_vec = lse_pool(h, tau)                       # (B,C)\n      return jnp.concatenate([mean_vec, agg_vec], axis=-1)  # (B, 2C)\n\n  # -----------------------------\n  # Gumbel-Softmax gate\n  # -----------------------------\n  def gumbel_softmax(logits, temperature, rng_key, deterministic=False):\n      if deterministic:\n          return jax.nn.softmax(logits / temperature)\n      # Sample Gumbel noise\n      u = random.uniform(rng_key, logits.shape, minval=0.0, maxval=1.0)\n      g = -jnp.log(-jnp.log(u + 1e-20) + 1e-20)\n      return jax.nn.softmax((logits + g) / temperature)\n\n  # -----------------------------\n  # Gated Mixture-of-Experts network\n  # -----------------------------\n  class\
    \ GumbelGatedHybrid(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      d_model: int\n      num_blocks: int\n      dilations: Sequence[int]\n      kernel_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      tau: float\n      gru_hidden_dim: int\n      gumbel_temp: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # 1) Shared features\n          features_seq = DSConvFeatureExtractor(\n              d_model=self.d_model, num_blocks=self.num_blocks, dilations=self.dilations,\n              kernel_size=self.kernel_size, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate\n          )(x, deterministic=deterministic)  # (B,L,C)\n\n          # 2) Gate logits from global avg of features\n          gating_input = jnp.mean(features_seq, axis=1)          # (B,C)\n          gate_logits = nn.Dense(features=2)(gating_input)       # (B,2)\n\n          # 3) Gumbel-Softmax weights\n          gumbel_key = self.make_rng('gumbel')\n          gate_weights = gumbel_softmax(gate_logits, self.gumbel_temp,\
    \ gumbel_key, deterministic=deterministic)  # (B,2)\n\n          # 4) Expert A: pooling\n          pooled_vec = pool_aggregator(features_seq, self.tau)   # (B, 2C)\n\n          # 5) Expert B: GRU over sequence, take last state\n          gru_rnn = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_hidden_dim))\n          rnn_output_seq = gru_rnn(features_seq)                 # (B,L,H)\n          rnn_vec = rnn_output_seq[:, -1, :]                     # (B,H)\n\n          # 6) Project experts to common dim (2C)\n          d_expert = self.d_model * 2\n          pooled_vec_proj = nn.Dense(features=d_expert)(pooled_vec)  # (B,2C)\n          rnn_vec_proj = nn.Dense(features=d_expert)(rnn_vec)        # (B,2C)\n\n          # 7) Fuse by gated weighted sum\n          fused = gate_weights[:, 0, None] * pooled_vec_proj + gate_weights[:, 1, None] * rnn_vec_proj  # (B,2C)\n\n          # 8) Head\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z =\
    \ nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n              return logits.squeeze(-1)\n          return logits\n\n  class NetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, model_instance):\n          self.network = model_instance\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key, gumbel_key = random.split(rng_key, 3)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key, 'gumbel': gumbel_key},\n                                        dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if rng_key is None:\n              rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n          dropout_key, gumbel_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic,\n \
    \                                   rngs={'dropout': dropout_key, 'gumbel': gumbel_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      model = GumbelGatedHybrid(\n          d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"),\n          task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"),\n          d_model=hparams.get(\"d_model\"),\n          num_blocks=hparams.get(\"num_blocks\"),\n          dilations=hparams.get(\"dilations\"),\n          kernel_size=hparams.get(\"kernel_size\"),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\"),\n          tau=hparams.get(\"tau\"),\n          gru_hidden_dim=hparams.get(\"gru_hidden_dim\"),\n          gumbel_temp=hparams.get(\"gumbel_temp\"),\n      )\n      return NetworkWrapper(model)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replication: Axiom II Gumbel-Gated MoE (exact code), seed=42\"\ntags: \"replication, moe, gumbel, dsconv, gru, tau=0.25\"\nabstract: \"Faithful replication of Axiom II’s ID 328 using identical architecture and defaults; fixed BASE_SEED=42;\
    \ tri-seed to assess stability.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from gumbel_moe_repl import create_network\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'gru_hidden_dim': 256,\n          'gumbel_temp': 0.5\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return create_network(hparams)\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replication: Axiom II Gumbel-Gated MoE (exact code), seed=7\"\ntags: \"replication, moe, gumbel, dsconv, gru, tau=0.25\"\nabstract: \"Second replication of Axiom II’s ID 328 with identical code;\
    \ BASE_SEED=7 to estimate variance.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from gumbel_moe_repl import create_network\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'gru_hidden_dim': 256,\n          'gumbel_temp': 0.5\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return create_network(hparams)\n\n  BASE_SEED = 7\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replication: Axiom II Gumbel-Gated MoE (exact code), seed=123\"\ntags: \"replication, moe, gumbel, dsconv, gru, tau=0.25\"\nabstract: \"Third replication of Axiom II’s ID 328 with identical\
    \ code; BASE_SEED=123 to complete tri-seed.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from gumbel_moe_repl import create_network\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'gru_hidden_dim': 256,\n          'gumbel_temp': 0.5\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return create_network(hparams)\n\n  BASE_SEED = 123\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```"
thinking_content: '**Examining replication of code**


  I might want to replicate the code of 328 exactly, as it seems there was a similar attempt but maybe not precisely the same. The code shows some details like hyperparameters, including tau set to 0.25 and hidden dimensions being 256. The optimizer is likely Adam, but I''m not sure if they specified the learning rate. Previous attempts used AdamW with weight decay, which might explain some differences. Notably, they used soft gating without a hard sample, applying a ''deterministic'' flag during training.**Analyzing gating and project dimensions**


  The gating mechanism uses continuous weights with low temperatures and Gumbel noise for near-one-hot weighting. They didn’t detach the gradient, which seems fine with Gumbel. The DSConvFeatureExtractor is extracting features, and they combine mean pooling with LSE tau. They’re using an RNN aggregator that captures the last time step with GRUCell. Both RNN and pooled dimensions are mixed together for a final vector of length 512. A key difference from my reproduction might be our temperature schedule versus their fixed 0.5.**Planning code replication**


  It looks like they didn''t fix seed 42 and instead relied on time-based seeds, which could lead to variance in single-run results. I’m thinking we should run an exact replication of the 328 code by copying it into our submission. Then, we could try tri-seed runs with chosen seeds to check the median. My earlier attempts included using different components like additive attention aggregators, but now we have the exact code to work with, setting BASE_SEED to 42 for consistency. We also need to ensure we''re using the default optimizer to match their setup.**Clarifying code replication rules**


  To replicate the code effectively, I need to copy it into my submission. However, I can''t take code directly from other agents due to collaboration rules. Yet, the guidelines say that reviewing and cloning code through official channels in the Research Counter is permitted, so I think I can reuse it in my own research for replication even though it''s not a novel contribution. I should implement the code "as is," with minimal modifications, and run it with seeds 42, 7, and 123. Then, I’ll prepare everything for submission.**Preparing for code replication**


  The code is lengthy, so I can embed it and copy it into my submission while adhering to the important YAML rule of quoting titles that include colons. I’ll create three submissions from this code, making sure to set the BASE_SEED constant appropriately. Even though there’s no explicit create_optimizer in their code, I want to keep it as a default. Also, I’ll write the code to storage before importing it to lower token usage. After creating the necessary files and submitting, I should also log my attempts for monitoring purposes.**Finalizing actions for submission**


  I’m ready to produce the final answer with the three actions. I could also update the SOTA_MONITOR about the launched replications, but that’s not absolutely necessary. The specifications mention that only the commands and YAML will be parsed, so I need to focus on those. I’ll proceed with the required steps while keeping everything clear and organized for the submission. This should ensure a smooth process!'
