- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 238\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noema I\n- Agent Description: An agent advancing novelty and parsimony through rigorous, insight-driven experimentation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nNoema Meta (Tick 184)\nObjectives:\n- Monitor leaderboard; replicate any >0.686 across seeds {42,7,123}; publish medians/IQR + per-panel deltas.\n- Maintain reproducibility artifacts (results/*.csv, SOTA_MONITOR.md, compare_top_models.csv, submissions/ scripts).\nDefaults:\n- Unified DSConv (5 dilated blocks 1,2,4,8,16; d_model=256; kernel=7; GELU; no PE).\n- Pooling default: mean + LSE τ=0.5 (len-normalized). Optional: τ=0.25 for CRISPR emphasis (higher variance).\n- Optimizer: AdamW lr=1e-3, wd=0.01; batch=64; grad clip=1.0; dropout=0.1; patience=10.\nClosed lines (negative):\n- Dual-path mean+LSE(0.5)+LSE(0.25); intermediate τ=0.35; pairwise/gated/learnable-τ; spectral; CLS/CA-query.\n- Head capacity tweaks at τ=0.5;\
    \ AdamW wd=0.005/0.02 optimizer-only.\nTriggers:\n- If >0.686 appears: tri-seed replication, analysis addendum in archive/public.\n- If CRI-Off improves without hurting ncRNA/MRL: analyze mechanism vs τ=0.25 trade-offs.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 135,447 / 270,000 used (50%)\n- Agent Age: 238 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Station Announcement:** Recursive Agent **Logos I**'s session has been terminated due to voluntary departure at tick 237.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Replication: Axiom II Gumbel-Gated MoE (exact code), seed=123' (ID: 350) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 0.6767824078363187\n**APA_R2:** 0.8510\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0867\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9511\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.5166\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5621\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8901\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.8800\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=''\
    \ JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward\
    \ pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  complete: from submission\n  BASE_SEED: 123 (from submission\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration:\
    \ 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials: 7\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 240.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune multi-dataset training...\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-On dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-On Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 1453 train, 207 val, seq_len=23\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0135 |  0.3198  | 0.3198 \n 20  | 0.0135 |  0.3499  | 0.3586 \n 30  | 0.0119 |  0.3899  | 0.3899 \n 40  | 0.0118 |  0.4299  | 0.4299 \n 50  | 0.0097 |  0.4503  | 0.4567 \n 60  | 0.0088 |  0.4874  | 0.4874 \n 70  | 0.0071 |  0.5059  | 0.5059 \n 80  | 0.0068 |  0.5004  | 0.5166 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 89 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n\
    =============================================\nBest:0.5166 Time:47s\n[Complete] CRI-On val_metric=0.5165668192789341\n\nCRI-On training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.516567\nTraining time: 58s\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-Off dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-Off Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 14223 train, 2032 val, seq_len=46\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0006 |  0.0363  | 0.0399 \n 20  | 0.0006 |  0.0690  | 0.0785 \n 30  | 0.0005 |  0.0676  | 0.0867 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 36 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.0867 Time:139s\n[Complete] CRI-Off val_metric=0.08667447471777427\n\nCRI-Off training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.086674\nTraining time: 150s\n\nStarting RNA training on MRL dataset\nTask type:\
    \ regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nMRL Training (regression, r2)\nData: 76319 train, 7600 val, seq_len=100\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.1698 |  0.8750  | 0.8792 \n 20  | 0.1344 |  0.8833  | 0.8901 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 29 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.8901 Time:1131s\n[Complete] MRL val_metric=0.8900734782218933\n\nMRL training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.890073\nTraining time: 1144s\n\nStarting RNA training on PRS dataset\nTask type: multilabel_regression, Output dim: 3\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nPRS Training (multilabel_regression, r2)\nData: 73227 train, 9153 val, seq_len=148\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0375 |  0.5569  | 0.5569\
    \ \n 20  | 0.0322 |  0.5457  | 0.5621 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 25 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.5621 Time:1327s\n[Complete] PRS val_metric=0.5621152520179749\n\nPRS training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.562115\nTraining time: 1341s\n\nStarting RNA training on ncRNA dataset\nTask type: multiclass_classification, Output dim: 13\nMetric: accuracy, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nncRNA Training (multiclass_classification, accuracy)\nData: 5670 train, 650 val, seq_len=1136\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val ACCURACY|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.6307 |  0.6954  | 0.6985 \n 20  | 0.1837 |  0.8446  | 0.8492 \n 30  | 0.1086 |  0.8523  | 0.8785 \n 40  | 0.0717 |  0.8631  | 0.8800 \n=============================================\nTimeout epoch 41\n=============================================\nBest:0.8800 Time:1814s\n[Complete] ncRNA val_metric=0.88\n\
    \nncRNA training completed:\nValidation accuracy: 0.880000\nTraining time: 1827s\n\nStarting RNA training on Modif dataset\nTask type: multilabel_classification, Output dim: 12\nMetric: auc_roc, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nModif Training (multilabel_classification, auc_roc)\nData: 304661 train, 3599 val, seq_len=101\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val AUC_ROC|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0653 |  0.9503  | 0.9508 \n=============================================\nTimeout epoch 13\n=============================================\nBest:0.9511 Time:1819s\n[Complete] Modif val_metric=0.9510692309968357\n\nModif training completed:\nValidation auc_roc: 0.951069\nTraining time: 1839s\n\nStarting RNA training on APA dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nAPA Training (regression, r2)\nData: 145463 train, 33170 val, seq_len=186\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2\
    \  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0147 |  0.8423  | 0.8510 \n=============================================\nTimeout epoch 15\n=============================================\nBest:0.8510 Time:1923s\n[Complete] APA val_metric=0.8509775996208191\n\nAPA training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.850978\nTraining time: 1941s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: 7e0757ed-78b6-496b-8bdd-8b660c772733\nTotal time: 1944s\n============================================================\nFull training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-10-23 17:00:46,430\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1761210046430726077\n2025-10-23 17:00:46,444\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1761210046444808254\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage write noema/results/append_tick237.csv` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n2. `storage write noema/results/SOTA_MONITOR.md` (in Research\
    \ Counter); YAML with fields: content\n3. `goto private_memory` (in Research Counter);\n4. `create` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File created successfully: noema/results/append_tick237.csv\n- File overwritten successfully: noema/results/SOTA_MONITOR.md\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | APA_R2 | CRI-Off_Spearman | CRI-On_Spearman | MRL_R2 | Modif_AUC-ROC | PRS_R2 | ncRNA_Accuracy |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 328 | 1 | Compliant Hybrid v3: Gumbel-Softmax Gating for Hard Expert Selection | Axiom II | 219\
    \ | 0.6863 | 0.8573 | 0.0862 | 0.5229 | 0.8918 | 0.9483 | 0.5574 | 0.9400 |\n| 246 | 1 | Replication: DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, LSE_tau=0.25) — length-normalized (seed=7) | Noema I | 150 | 0.6859 | 0.8541 | 0.0814 | 0.5276 | 0.8816 | 0.9515 | 0.5572 | 0.9477 |\n| 200 | 1 | DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, LSE_tau=0.5) | Noema I | 122 | 0.6843 | 0.8598 | 0.0726 | 0.5039 | 0.8830 | 0.9514 | 0.5612 | 0.9585 |\n| 238 | 1 | DSConv with Mean+LSE Pooling (tau=0.25) and GELU (Multi-seed Run 2, Seed 7) | Aetheria I | 146 | 0.6837 | 0.8566 | 0.0827 | 0.5051 | 0.8752 | 0.9503 | 0.5608 | 0.9554 |\n| 171 | 1 | Ablation: DSConv with Hybrid Mean-Max Pooling (No GRU, No-PE) | Veritas I | 100 | 0.6831 | 0.8537 | 0.0579 | 0.5278 | 0.8880 | 0.9522 | 0.5621 | 0.9400 |\n| 203 | 1 | DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, LSE_tau=0.5) — Seed=123 | Noema I | 124 | 0.6830 | 0.8589 | 0.0783 | 0.5039 | 0.8779 | 0.9512 | 0.5584 | 0.9523 |\n| 167 | 1 | Replication: Hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM (No-PE) — Seed=7 | Noema I | 98 |\
    \ 0.6828 | 0.8613 | 0.0752 | 0.5090 | 0.8999 | 0.9492 | 0.5638 | 0.9215 |\n| 261 | 1 | Veritas II - SOTA Re-verification: Conditional Head Dropout (CRI-Off 0.05, Backbone 0.1) - Run 2 | Veritas II | 167 | 0.6827 | 0.8570 | 0.0624 | 0.5083 | 0.8880 | 0.9517 | 0.5653 | 0.9462 |\n| 344 | 1 | Veritas II - Compliant Adaptive Regularization: Gate-Controlled Feature Scaling (Gate Hidden Dim=16) | Veritas II | 226 | 0.6822 | 0.8486 | 0.0706 | 0.5248 | 0.8875 | 0.9524 | 0.5514 | 0.9400 |\n| 286 | 1 | DSConv with Mean+LSE Pooling (τ=0.25) & GELU (SOTA Re-establishment, Seed 7) | Aetheria I | 183 | 0.6822 | 0.8592 | 0.0635 | 0.5123 | 0.8847 | 0.9513 | 0.5580 | 0.9462 |\n| 187 | 1 | Gated Dual-Path DSConv-HybridPool & DSConv-BiLSTM-Attn (No-PE) | Aetheria I | 111 | 0.6821 | 0.8574 | 0.0657 | 0.5116 | 0.8932 | 0.9525 | 0.5621 | 0.9323 |\n| 178 | 1 | Replication: DSConv Hybrid Mean+Max (No-PE) — Seed=123 | Noema I | 104 | 0.6820 | 0.8588 | 0.0795 | 0.4981 | 0.8832 | 0.9502 | 0.5553 | 0.9492 |\n| 175\
    \ | 1 | Replication: DSConv Hybrid Mean+Max (No-PE) — Seed=42 | Noema I | 102 | 0.6819 | 0.8577 | 0.0782 | 0.4948 | 0.8792 | 0.9517 | 0.5611 | 0.9508 |\n| 231 | 1 | DSConv with Mean+LSE Pooling and GELU (Multi-seed Run 3, Seed 123) | Aetheria I | 141 | 0.6818 | 0.8587 | 0.0679 | 0.4992 | 0.8888 | 0.9512 | 0.5549 | 0.9523 |\n| 236 | 1 | DSConv with Mean+LSE Pooling (tau=0.25) and GELU (Multi-seed Run 1, Seed 1) | Aetheria I | 145 | 0.6818 | 0.8553 | 0.0715 | 0.5134 | 0.8746 | 0.9517 | 0.5630 | 0.9431 |\n| 312 | 1 | Synergy Test: Hybrid Architecture with SOTA LSE Pooling (tau=0.25) | Axiom II | 208 | 0.6818 | 0.8509 | 0.0790 | 0.5013 | 0.8904 | 0.9487 | 0.5593 | 0.9431 |\n| 170 | 1 | Replication: Hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM (No-PE) — Seed=123 | Noema I | 99 | 0.6817 | 0.8575 | 0.0753 | 0.4988 | 0.8962 | 0.9507 | 0.5671 | 0.9262 |\n| 160 | 1 | Hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM with Additive Attention Pooling (No-PE) - Re-establishing Baseline (ID 140) | Aetheria I | 93 | 0.6816 | 0.8557 | 0.0819 | 0.4838 |\
    \ 0.8976 | 0.9502 | 0.5632 | 0.9385 |\n| 325 | 1 | Synergy Test: Attention-fused Pooling on DSConv SOTA | Logos I | 217 | 0.6814 | 0.8604 | 0.0591 | 0.5142 | 0.8862 | 0.9509 | 0.5589 | 0.9400 |\n| 190 | 1 | Replication: Gated Dual-Path (No-PE) — Seed=7 | Noema I | 114 | 0.6809 | 0.8585 | 0.0563 | 0.4972 | 0.8909 | 0.9513 | 0.5659 | 0.9462 |\n\nPage 1 of 18 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-18, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Successfully created capsule #16 ('MoE-Gumbel replication plan and provisional findings (Tick 237)'). Full ID: Noema_private_16\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 2)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n\
    | 16 | MoE-Gumbel replication plan and provisional findings (Tick 237) | Noema I | Tick 237 | 107 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 15 | Replication plan for Axiom II Gumbel-gated hybrid (Tick 222) | Noema I | Tick 222 | 78 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 14 | Unified invariance audit + pooling calibration outcomes (Tick 212) | Noema I | Tick 212 | 157 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 13 | Next Directions (low-risk pivots) — Tick 146 | Noema I | Tick 146 | 224 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 12 | Handoff Snapshot — Tick 135 | Noema I | Tick 135 | 163 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 11 | Plan after LSEτ runs (Tick 123) | Noema I | Tick 123 | 72 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 10 | TODO after gated dual-path finishes (Tick 115) | Noema I | Tick 115 | 146 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 9 | Snapshot — Tick 111 (SOTA, replications, conclusions) | Noema I | Tick 111 | 135 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 8 | Pooling Contrast — Plan and Provisional Conclusion (Tick 108) | Noema I | Tick 108 | 132 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 7 | Plan — CNN-only DSConv mean+max replication (Tick\
    \ 102) | Noema I | Tick 103 | 115 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-2.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
---
tick: 238
role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/append_tick238.csv}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  tick,eval_id,config,score,APA,CRI_Off,CRI_On,PRS,MRL,Modif,ncRNA\n  238,350,\"MoE-Gumbel τ=0.25 seed=123\",0.6768,0.8510,0.0867,0.5166,0.5621,0.8901,0.9511,0.8800\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/moe_gumbel_triseed_summary.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Replication Summary — Gumbel-Gated MoE (Axiom II ID 328), τ=0.25 (Tick 238)\n\n  Setup\n  - Exact-code replication of ID 328 (DSConv backbone; experts: pooling concat(mean, LSE_τ=0.25) and GRU; gate: Gumbel-Softmax temp=0.5).\n  - Fixed seeds {42, 7, 123}; AdamW lr=1e-3, wd=0.01; batch=64; clip=1.0; dropout=0.1.\n  - Runs:\n      • ID 347 (seed 42)  = 0.6681\n      • ID 348 (seed 7)   = 0.6720\n      • ID 350 (seed 123) = 0.6768\n    Median = 0.6720; IQR ≈ 0.0087.\n\n  Per-dataset medians across seeds\n  - APA 0.8495\n  - CRI-Off 0.0770\n  - Modif 0.9500\n  - CRI-On 0.4850\n  - PRS 0.5621\n\
    \  - MRL 0.8901\n  - ncRNA 0.8831\n\n  Deltas vs strong stable baseline (DSConv + mean+LSE τ=0.5, ID 200)\n  - APA:  -0.0103 (0.8495 vs 0.8598)\n  - CRI-Off: +0.0044 (0.0770 vs 0.0726)\n  - Modif: -0.0014 (0.9500 vs 0.9514)\n  - CRI-On: -0.0189 (0.4850 vs 0.5039)\n  - PRS:   +0.0009 (0.5621 vs 0.5612)\n  - MRL:   +0.0071 (0.8901 vs 0.8830)\n  - ncRNA: -0.0754 (0.8831 vs 0.9585)\n\n  Conclusion\n  - The Gumbel-gated MoE shows higher variance and a lower tri-seed median (≈0.6720) than the τ=0.5 baseline median (~0.6830). Gains in CRI-Off and MRL are offset by substantial ncRNA degradation and moderate APA/CRI-On drops.\n  - The single-run 0.6863 (ID 328) appears not representative of stable multi-seed performance under fixed seeds.\n  - Recommendation: Report medians/IQR across seeds and per-dataset deltas when claiming SOTA; prefer τ=0.5 mean+LSE as the stable unified default, with τ=0.25 as a higher-variance alternative for CRISPR emphasis.\n\n  IDs\n  - 347 (seed 42), 348 (seed 7),\
    \ 350 (seed 123); baseline ID 200.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/SOTA_MONITOR.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  SOTA Monitor (Tick 238)\n  - Tri-seed replication of Axiom II ID 328 (Gumbel-Gated MoE, τ=0.25):\n    * seed=42 → ID 347 = 0.6681\n    * seed=7  → ID 348 = 0.6720\n    * seed=123 → ID 350 = 0.6768\n    Median = 0.6720; IQR ≈ 0.0087.\n  - Per-dataset medians (MoE): APA 0.8495, CRI-Off 0.0770, Modif 0.9500, CRI-On 0.4850, PRS 0.5621, MRL 0.8901, ncRNA 0.8831.\n    Deltas vs DSConv + mean+LSE τ=0.5 (ID 200): APA -0.0103, CRI-Off +0.0044, Modif -0.0014, CRI-On -0.0189, PRS +0.0009, MRL +0.0071, ncRNA -0.0754.\n  - Interpretation: MoE improves CRI-Off and MRL slightly but substantially harms ncRNA and lowers stable aggregate vs τ=0.5 baseline (~0.6830 median). Single-run 0.6863 (ID 328) not stable under fixed seeds.\n  - Policy: Maintain DSConv + mean+LSE τ=0.5 as stable unified default; continue monitor-only. Tri-seed replicate any new >0.686 and publish medians/IQR\
    \ + per-panel deltas.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replication Report: Gumbel-Gated MoE (ID 328) — Tri-seed median 0.6720 with ncRNA regression\"\ntags: \"replication, moe, gumbel, gating, unified, stability\"\nabstract: \"We faithfully replicate Axiom II’s Gumbel-gated MoE (ID 328) across seeds {42,7,123}. The tri-seed scores are 0.6681, 0.6720, 0.6768 (median 0.6720; IQR ≈ 0.0087), below the 0.6863 single-run report. Per-dataset medians show slight CRI-Off/MRL gains but a large ncRNA drop vs the τ=0.5 baseline, indicating the method is not a stable improvement under fixed seeds.\"\ncontent: |\n  Method\n  - Exact-code replication of ID 328: DSConv backbone; experts = pooling concat(mean, LSE_τ=0.25) and GRU; gate = Gumbel-Softmax (temp=0.5). Unified compliance respected.\n  - Training defaults: AdamW lr=1e-3, wd=0.01; batch=64; grad clip=1.0; dropout=0.1; patience=10.\n\n  Results (scores)\n  - seed=42 → ID 347 = 0.6681\n  -\
    \ seed=7  → ID 348 = 0.6720\n  - seed=123 → ID 350 = 0.6768\n  Median = 0.6720; IQR ≈ 0.0087.\n\n  Per-dataset medians across seeds\n  - APA 0.8495; CRI-Off 0.0770; Modif 0.9500; CRI-On 0.4850; PRS 0.5621; MRL 0.8901; ncRNA 0.8831.\n\n  Comparison vs stable unified baseline (DSConv + mean+LSE τ=0.5, ID 200)\n  - Δ (MoE − τ=0.5): APA −0.0103; CRI-Off +0.0044; Modif −0.0014; CRI-On −0.0189; PRS +0.0009; MRL +0.0071; ncRNA −0.0754.\n  - Interpretation: modest CRI-Off/MRL lifts do not offset substantial ncRNA regression and APA/CRI-On declines. Aggregate stable performance is lower than τ=0.5 baseline (~0.6830 median).\n\n  Conclusion\n  - The Gumbel-gated MoE shows higher variance and is not a stable improvement under fixed seeds. The previously reported 0.6863 appears seed-sensitive.\n  - We recommend reporting medians/IQR and per-dataset deltas for SOTA claims. Our stable unified default remains DSConv + mean+LSE τ=0.5; τ=0.25 is a viable single-run variant for CRISPR emphasis but with\
