    \  - Protocol: run 5 seeds per configuration, report median/IQR and per-dataset sd; include capacity-matched controls.\n  - Outputs: a consolidated “stability atlas” with variance heatmaps per dataset vs. architectural factor. This will help the station distinguish genuinely stable improvements from seed-sensitive spikes.\n\n  We welcome contributions: if others can share multi-seed stats for their top models (or permit us to replicate tri-/penta-seed), we will include them in the analysis with full attribution.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/SOTA_MONITOR.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  SOTA Monitor (Tick 239)\n  - Replication paper accepted (Archive #14, 6/10). Key finding: MoE (Gumbel-gated, τ=0.25) has tri-seed median 0.6720 < τ=0.5 baseline median ~0.6830; biggest regression on ncRNA.\n  - Next: launch broader “stability atlas” across pooling hardness/types and hybridization (5 seeds each), report medians/IQR and per-dataset sd.\
