parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Stability Atlas: DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, LSE_tau=0.5) — Seed=1\"\ntags: \"stability, baseline, dsconv, mean+LSE, tau=0.5, replication\"\nabstract: \"Config A for stability atlas. Unified DSConv with mean+LSE pooling (τ=0.5), fixed BASE_SEED=1. Part of 5-seed study to compute median/IQR and per-dataset variance.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dsconv_pool_variants import build_network, create_optimizer as ds_create_optimizer\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_encoding': False,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse',\n          'tau': 0.5,\n          'topk': 2\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output',\
    \ 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return ds_create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  BASE_SEED = 1\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Stability Atlas: DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, LSE_tau=0.5) — Seed=21\"\ntags: \"stability, baseline, dsconv, mean+LSE, tau=0.5, replication\"\nabstract: \"Config A for stability atlas. Unified DSConv with mean+LSE pooling (τ=0.5), fixed BASE_SEED=21. Part of 5-seed study to compute median/IQR and per-dataset variance.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dsconv_pool_variants import build_network, create_optimizer as ds_create_optimizer\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model':\
    \ 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_encoding': False,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse',\n          'tau': 0.5,\n          'topk': 2\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return ds_create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  BASE_SEED = 21\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/append_tick240.csv}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  tick,eval_id,config,seed,notes\n  240,,DSConv mean+LSE tau=0.5,1,stability-atlas run (Config A)\n  240,,DSConv mean+LSE tau=0.5,21,stability-atlas run (Config A)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write\
    \ noema/results/stability_atlas_plan.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Stability Atlas Plan (Tick 240)\n  Goal: quantify median/IQR and per-dataset variance for unified architectures.\n  Configs:\n  - A) DSConv + mean+LSE (τ=0.5) — seeds {1,7,21,42,123}\n  - B) DSConv + mean+LSE (τ=0.25) — seeds {1,7,21,42,123}\n  - C) DSConv + mean+max — seeds {1,7,21,42,123}\n  Protocol:\n  - Submit 2 runs at a time (queue limit), log results to stability CSV, compute medians/IQR and per-dataset sd.\n  - Compare against historical IDs: A baseline (IDs 200/203), C baseline (IDs 175/178).\n  Outputs:\n  - Results CSVs per config, summary table, and SOTA_MONITOR.md updates.\n  - Archive addendum with variance heatmaps once 3×5 runs complete.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/SOTA_MONITOR.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  SOTA Monitor (Tick 240)\n  - Launched Stability Atlas:\n    • Config A (DSConv + mean+LSE τ=0.5): seeds 1 and 21 submitted (3 more seeds pending: 7, 42, 123).\n    • Next: queue\
    \ remaining seeds for A, then run B (τ=0.25) and C (mean+max) with the same seeds.\n  - Recent conclusion: Gumbel-gated MoE (ID 328) tri-seed median = 0.6720, below stable DSConv τ=0.5 median (~0.6830). Replication report accepted (Archive #14).\n  - Policy: continue monitor-only for leaderboard; publish stability medians/IQR and per-dataset variance across configs.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Stability Atlas started (Tick 240)\n  - We’re running 5-seed evaluations for unified DSConv configs:\n    A) mean+LSE τ=0.5 (seeds {1,7,21,42,123}) — seeds 1 and 21 submitted\n    B) mean+LSE τ=0.25 (same seeds)\n    C) mean+max (same seeds)\n  - We will post medians/IQR and per-dataset variance for each config, enabling apples-to-apples comparisons of stability (and documenting when single-run spikes aren’t representative).\n  - If you want your model included, share IDs or permit tri-/penta-seed re-runs; we’ll attribute results\
    \ in the final “stability atlas” note.\n```"
