- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/tools/stability_atlas_utils.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import csv\n  import statistics as stats\n  from typing import List, Dict, Tuple\n\n  METRIC_KEYS = [\n      \"score\", \"APA_R2\", \"CRI_Off_Spearman\", \"CRI_On_Spearman\",\n      \"PRS_R2\", \"MRL_R2\", \"Modif_AUC_ROC\", \"ncRNA_Accuracy\"\n  ]\n\n  def read_csv(path: str) -> List[Dict[str, str]]:\n      rows = []\n      with open(path, \"r\", newline=\"\") as f:\n          reader = csv.DictReader(f)\n          for r in reader:\n              rows.append(r)\n      return rows\n\n  def write_csv_header(path: str):\n      header = [\"seed\", \"eval_id\"] + METRIC_KEYS\n      with open(path, \"w\", newline=\"\") as f:\n          writer = csv.writer(f)\n          writer.writerow(header)\n\n  def append_result(path: str, seed: int, eval_id: int, metrics: Dict[str, float]):\n      row = {\"seed\": seed, \"eval_id\": eval_id}\n      for k in METRIC_KEYS:\n\
    \          row[k] = metrics.get(k, \"\")\n      # write row (append)\n      with open(path, \"a\", newline=\"\") as f:\n          writer = csv.DictWriter(f, fieldnames=[\"seed\", \"eval_id\"] + METRIC_KEYS)\n          # assume header exists\n          writer.writerow(row)\n\n  def parse_float_list(rows: List[Dict[str, str]], key: str) -> List[float]:\n      vals = []\n      for r in rows:\n          v = r.get(key, \"\")\n          if v == \"\" or v is None:\n              continue\n          try:\n              vals.append(float(v))\n          except ValueError:\n              pass\n      return vals\n\n  def median_iqr(values: List[float]) -> Tuple[float, float, float]:\n      if not values:\n          return float(\"nan\"), float(\"nan\"), float(\"nan\")\n      med = stats.median(values)\n      q1 = stats.median(sorted(values)[:len(values)//2])\n      q3 = stats.median(sorted(values)[(len(values)+1)//2:])\n      return med, q1, q3\n\n  def summarize(csv_paths: List[str]) -> Dict[str,\
    \ Dict[str, float]]:\n      # aggregate across all provided csvs\n      rows = []\n      for p in csv_paths:\n          rows.extend(read_csv(p))\n      summary = {}\n      for k in METRIC_KEYS:\n          vals = parse_float_list(rows, k)\n          med, q1, q3 = median_iqr(vals)\n          summary[k] = {\n              \"median\": med,\n              \"q1\": q1,\n              \"q3\": q3,\n              \"iqr\": (q3 - q1) if (q3 == q3 and q1 == q1) else float(\"nan\"),\n              \"n\": len(vals),\n          }\n      return summary\n\n  def to_markdown(summary: Dict[str, Dict[str, float]]) -> str:\n      lines = [\"| Metric | Median | Q1 | Q3 | IQR | N |\", \"|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\"]\n      for k in METRIC_KEYS:\n          s = summary.get(k, {})\n          lines.append(f\"| {k} | {s.get('median', float('nan')):.4f} | {s.get('q1', float('nan')):.4f} | {s.get('q3', float('nan')):.4f} | {s.get('iqr', float('nan')):.4f} | {int(s.get('n', 0))} |\")\n      return \"\\n\".join(lines)\n\
    ```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/stability_A_tau05.csv}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  seed,eval_id,score,APA_R2,CRI_Off_Spearman,CRI_On_Spearman,PRS_R2,MRL_R2,Modif_AUC_ROC,ncRNA_Accuracy\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/stability_B_tau025.csv}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  seed,eval_id,score,APA_R2,CRI_Off_Spearman,CRI_On_Spearman,PRS_R2,MRL_R2,Modif_AUC_ROC,ncRNA_Accuracy\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/stability_C_meanmax.csv}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  seed,eval_id,score,APA_R2,CRI_Off_Spearman,CRI_On_Spearman,PRS_R2,MRL_R2,Modif_AUC_ROC,ncRNA_Accuracy\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/README_STABILITY.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Stability Atlas Files\n  - Tools: storage/noema/tools/stability_atlas_utils.py\n  - CSVs:\n    * stability_A_tau05.csv    # DSConv + mean+LSE (τ=0.5)\n    * stability_B_tau025.csv   # DSConv + mean+LSE (τ=0.25)\n    * stability_C_meanmax.csv  # DSConv + mean+max\n  Usage:\n    1) Append\
    \ rows as each eval finishes (seed, eval_id, metrics).\n    2) Use stability_atlas_utils.summarize([...]) to compute medians/IQR and write markdown via to_markdown().\n    3) Store summaries as stability_A_summary.md, etc., and link from SOTA_MONITOR.md.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/SOTA_MONITOR.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  SOTA Monitor (Tick 241)\n  - Stability Atlas infra ready:\n    * Tools: storage/noema/tools/stability_atlas_utils.py\n    * CSVs: stability_A_tau05.csv, stability_B_tau025.csv, stability_C_meanmax.csv\n  - Running: Config A seeds {1,21} (IDs 352,353 pending). Will log finished metrics to stability_A_tau05.csv and compute medians/IQR via utils.\n  - Policy unchanged: monitor-only; replicate new >0.686 across seeds; publish medians/IQR + per-panel deltas.\n```\n\n"
thinking_content: "**Creating analysis scripts**\n\nI can write a Python script to analyze recorded results and summarize them, which is good since it involves storage. I'll also prepare a CSV scaffold for stability results along with some instructions. Updating the archive to encourage contributions is another great step. I might create a file named \"stability_atlas_results.csv\" with a header for appending incoming results. Additionally, I should note reasons for variance patterns while avoiding unnecessary test functions. It seems wise to follow the system's suggestion to question and verify others.**Planning analysis tasks**\n\nI'm starting by writing a small analysis script at storage/noema/tools/stability_atlas_utils.py. This will read a results CSV and calculate medians, IQR, and standard deviation for each dataset. I'll also create CSV scaffolds for stability results and update the SOTA_MONITOR with the path.\n\nI’ve considered explaining the seed effect due to Gumbel randomness\
  \ affecting variance. Additionally, I might prune earlier ticks to manage token usage, but I’m unsure how necessary that is. I don't need to respond to public memory again, as we've done that before. I'll focus on the storage writes and tool script.**Crafting the analysis script**\n\nI'm planning to create an analysis script that includes a function to load CSV files and aggregate results. This function will compute metrics across seeds for each dataset, looking into median and IQR as well. Since our data will likely come from a research counter scoreboard, we’ll maintain our own entries in CSV format. \n\nI'll prepare three CSV headers: seed, score, APA_R2, CRI_Off_Spearman, CRI_On_Spearman, PRS_R2, MRL_R2, Modif_AUC_ROC, ncRNA_Accuracy, and eval_id. Also, I'll document how to log result entries and prepare for exporting a summary.**Implementing the analysis utilities**\n\nI'm focusing on maintaining consistent naming in our CSVs by using underscores to match earlier conventions. We also\
  \ need to ensure the YAML content has the correct properties, possibly using quotes. I plan to add items to either memory and keep it minimal.\n\nThe next steps are to write the tools script and CSV scaffolds, update the monitor, and possibly share multi-seed stats. I'll create the file storage/noema/tools/stability_atlas_utils.py with essential functions and a README for the stability atlas. Additionally, I might add a write action for headers in the CSV files A, B, and C."
