- text: "`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/stability_A_tau05.csv}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  seed,eval_id,score,APA_R2,CRI_Off_Spearman,CRI_On_Spearman,PRS_R2,MRL_R2,Modif_AUC_ROC,ncRNA_Accuracy\n  1,352,0.6760161969265293,0.8522,0.0613,0.4738,0.5599,0.8814,0.9513,0.9523\n  21,353,0.6787106107098358,0.8552,0.0642,0.4890,0.5521,0.8776,0.9529,0.9600\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Stability Atlas: DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, LSE_tau=0.5) — Seed=7\"\ntags: \"stability, baseline, dsconv, mean+LSE, tau=0.5, replication\"\nabstract: \"Config A for stability atlas. Unified DSConv with mean+LSE pooling (τ=0.5), fixed BASE_SEED=7. Part of 5-seed study to compute median/IQR and per-dataset variance.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dsconv_pool_variants import build_network, create_optimizer as ds_create_optimizer\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model':\
    \ 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_encoding': False,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse',\n          'tau': 0.5,\n          'topk': 2\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return ds_create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  BASE_SEED = 7\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Stability Atlas: DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, LSE_tau=0.5) — Seed=42\"\ntags: \"stability, baseline, dsconv, mean+LSE, tau=0.5, replication\"\nabstract: \"Config A for stability atlas. Unified DSConv with mean+LSE pooling (τ=0.5), fixed BASE_SEED=42.\
    \ Part of 5-seed study to compute median/IQR and per-dataset variance.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dsconv_pool_variants import build_network, create_optimizer as ds_create_optimizer\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_encoding': False,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse',\n          'tau': 0.5,\n          'topk': 2\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return ds_create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')}\
    \ val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/SOTA_MONITOR.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  SOTA Monitor (Tick 242)\n  - Stability Atlas (Config A: DSConv + mean+LSE τ=0.5) partial results:\n    • seed=1 → ID 352 = 0.6760 (APA 0.8522, CRI-Off 0.0613, CRI-On 0.4738, PRS 0.5599, MRL 0.8814, Modif 0.9513, ncRNA 0.9523)\n    • seed=21 → ID 353 = 0.6787 (APA 0.8552, CRI-Off 0.0642, CRI-On 0.4890, PRS 0.5521, MRL 0.8776, Modif 0.9529, ncRNA 0.9600)\n    Provisional median (2 seeds): ~0.6774 (Q1≈0.6760, Q3≈0.6787, IQR≈0.0027).\n  - Next runs queued for Config A: seeds 7 and 42 (2-slot queue limit); seed 123 will follow.\n  - After A completes, run Config B (τ=0.25) and C (mean+max) with the same seeds; compute medians/IQR and per-dataset variance; archive a “stability atlas” note.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning next steps**\n\nI need to figure out our next steps. The system shows evaluations 352 and 353 completed with scores around 0.6760 and 0.6787 for DSConv + mean+LSE tau=0.5. These scores are a bit low compared to earlier results. \n\nI plan to log these into a CSV, update the SOTA_MONITOR, and queue the next seeds 7, 42, and 123. For stability atlas, we'll submit those seeds for config A, and I'll need to ensure results are added to stability_A_tau05.csv.**Updating evaluation process**\n\nI can write the file again with a header plus the new lines, but this would erase previous appends, and right now the file only has the header and no data. So, I'll include the eval results along with the header. \n\nI also need to update the SOTA_MONITOR with a summary for config A’s partial results. For the next seeds, I'll submit 7 and 42, respecting the queue limit. The code for DSConv pooling tau 0.5 is ready to go, and I'll reuse the submission code while changing BASE_SEED\
  \ to 7 and 42.**Calculating median and IQR**\n\nI need to compute the median of the scores [0.676016, 0.67871061]. Since there are two values, the median will be the average of the two, which is approximately 0.6773634.\n\nNow, about the interquartile range (IQR) with just two values, the Q1 and Q3 definitions seem strange. For Q1, using the median of the lower half gives me the first element, and for Q3, I take the second value. So, I end up with Q1 equal to 0.6760 and Q3 equal to 0.6787, giving an IQR of about 0.0026944.**Calculating medians for seeds**\n\nLet's quickly summarize the scores for Seed 1 and Seed 21. For Seed 1, I have scores like 0.676016 for the main score, along with others like APA and CRI scores. For Seed 21, the main score is 0.678711, along with its respective values.\n\nTo find the median across the two seeds, I calculated the averages for each metric. For example, the average APA is 0.8537, and CRI-Off is about 0.0628. The overall median score is approximately\
  \ 0.6774. Previously, our stable median was around 0.6830, so the combined scores from these new seeds are likely still below that threshold.**Planning result logging and submission**\n\nI need to check if different code paths are identical. Both utilized the dsconv_pool_variants aggregator with mean_lse tau 0.5. The earlier seeds 200 and 203 did the same; seed 200 used BASE_SEED 42 based on logs, showing a stable median. However, right now, we just need to log results to CSV.\n\nI’ll be appending the metrics for seeds 1 and 21 to stability_A_tau05.csv, using the header plus data. Next, I’ll submit seeds 7 and 42 for config A and update the SOTA_MONITOR with the current median results."
