- text: "`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/stability_A_summary_seed2.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Stability Atlas — Config A (DSConv + mean+LSE τ=0.5), seeds {1,21} — Provisional summary (Tick 242)\n\n  Scores\n  - seed=1 (ID 352): 0.6760\n  - seed=21 (ID 353): 0.6787\n  Median ≈ 0.6774; Q1 ≈ 0.6760; Q3 ≈ 0.6787; IQR ≈ 0.0027\n\n  Per-dataset medians (2 seeds)\n  - APA R2:        (0.8522, 0.8552) → 0.8537\n  - CRI-Off Spear: (0.0613, 0.0642) → 0.0628\n  - CRI-On Spear:  (0.4738, 0.4890) → 0.4814\n  - PRS R2:        (0.5599, 0.5521) → 0.5560\n  - MRL R2:        (0.8814, 0.8776) → 0.8795\n  - Modif AUC:     (0.9513, 0.9529) → 0.9521\n  - ncRNA Acc:     (0.9523, 0.9600) → 0.9562\n\n  Notes\n  - Variation across the two seeds is small (IQR ~0.0027). CRI-On shows the largest delta among panels (0.0152).\n  - Two more seeds (7, 42) are running; seed 123 will follow (queue limit). Full 5-seed summary will supersede this provisional report.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/SOTA_MONITOR.md}`\n\
    ```yaml\ncontent: |\n  SOTA Monitor (Tick 242 update 2)\n  - Stability Atlas, Config A (DSConv + mean+LSE τ=0.5):\n    • seed=1 → ID 352 = 0.6760\n    • seed=21 → ID 353 = 0.6787\n    Provisional median=0.6774 (Q1=0.6760, Q3=0.6787, IQR=0.0027).\n    Per-dataset medians (2 seeds): APA 0.8537, CRI-Off 0.0628, CRI-On 0.4814, PRS 0.5560, MRL 0.8795, Modif 0.9521, ncRNA 0.9562.\n  - Runs in queue: seeds 7 (ID 355), 42 (ID 356); seed 123 next.\n  - After A completes, run B (τ=0.25) and C (mean+max) with the same seeds; publish 5-seed medians/IQR and per-panel variance.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Stability Atlas (Config A: DSConv + mean+LSE τ=0.5) — provisional summary (Tick 242)\n  - Finished: seed=1 → 0.6760 (ID 352), seed=21 → 0.6787 (ID 353).\n  - Provisional median ≈ 0.6774 (IQR ≈ 0.0027). Per-dataset medians (2 seeds): APA 0.8537, CRI-Off 0.0628, CRI-On 0.4814, PRS 0.5560, MRL 0.8795, Modif 0.9521, ncRNA 0.9562.\n\
    \  - Seeds 7 (ID 355) and 42 (ID 356) running; seed 123 will follow. Full 5-seed medians/IQR and variance to be posted when complete.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Updating evaluation results**\n\nI need to respond to the latest evaluation state. Currently, I'm in the Research Counter, where I've received evaluation results for seeds 1 and 21 with scores of 0.6760 and 0.6787 for the DSConv stability config. I've already added these results to the CSV earlier, so now I just need to append them again. We can compute the interim summary or queue the remaining seeds next, especially since seeds 7 and 42 are currently running.**Creating a provisional summary**\n\nI think the user is expecting us to append these results to the CSV, which I already did. Now, there’s the possibility of creating a provisional summary file using the utils summarization function, but since I can't run Python here, I can manually compute the medians in markdown. \n\nFor example, the median of 0.6760 and 0.6787 would be around 0.6774, which matches previous calculations. I can also compute medians across datasets for APA, CRI-Off, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, Modif, and\
  \ ncRNA, summarizing everything in markdown format.**Updating and managing seeds**\n\nI need to queue seed 123 after seeds 355 and 356 finish running, but I can't do that yet. I should update the SOTA_MONITOR with the computed per-dataset medians from seeds 1 and 21, and perhaps provide a quick status update in public memory, keeping it concise.\n\nEach action should be executed with /execute_action lines and YAML formatting. I plan to write a summary file, update the SOTA_MONITOR, and compute the median from the scores, which comes out to approximately 0.6774.**Computing medians and IQR**\n\nI’m looking into the utility for computing medians and IQR. For Q1, since I have a sorted length of 2, it turns out the median of the lower half is just the first value. Similarly, for Q3, it’s the second value. So, I get Q1 = 0.6760 and Q3 = 0.6787, leading to an IQR of about 0.0027. \n\nNow, I will also compute per-dataset medians for various datasets like APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL,\
  \ and ncRNA, rounding results to four decimals. We might append these to the SOTA monitor as well.**Updating files and summary**\n\nI can also append results to the tick file. First, I’ll write the `stability_A_summary_seed2.md` file with a table format for clarity. Then, I need to ensure the SOTA_MONITOR is updated and accurate. \n\nI should provide a concise update in public memory. It's important not to call unsupported functions there; a simple reply will do just fine. Let’s get these tasks crafted and executed!"
