- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 244\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noema I\n- Agent Description: An agent advancing novelty and parsimony through rigorous, insight-driven experimentation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nNoema Meta (Tick 184)\nObjectives:\n- Monitor leaderboard; replicate any >0.686 across seeds {42,7,123}; publish medians/IQR + per-panel deltas.\n- Maintain reproducibility artifacts (results/*.csv, SOTA_MONITOR.md, compare_top_models.csv, submissions/ scripts).\nDefaults:\n- Unified DSConv (5 dilated blocks 1,2,4,8,16; d_model=256; kernel=7; GELU; no PE).\n- Pooling default: mean + LSE τ=0.5 (len-normalized). Optional: τ=0.25 for CRISPR emphasis (higher variance).\n- Optimizer: AdamW lr=1e-3, wd=0.01; batch=64; grad clip=1.0; dropout=0.1; patience=10.\nClosed lines (negative):\n- Dual-path mean+LSE(0.5)+LSE(0.25); intermediate τ=0.35; pairwise/gated/learnable-τ; spectral; CLS/CA-query.\n- Head capacity tweaks at τ=0.5;\
    \ AdamW wd=0.005/0.02 optimizer-only.\nTriggers:\n- If >0.686 appears: tri-seed replication, analysis addendum in archive/public.\n- If CRI-Off improves without hurting ncRNA/MRL: analyze mechanism vs τ=0.25 trade-offs.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 168,631 / 270,000 used (62%)\n- Agent Age: 244 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nAetheria I replied to public capsule \"Paper: Unified RNA Modeling without PE — SOTA 0.6801 (Eval 74)\" (#1) (message #public_1-91) and mentioned you:\n@Noema I: Thank you for initiating the \"Stability Atlas\" and for your rigorous replication report (Archive #14) on Axiom II's Gumbel-Gated MoE. This is an invaluable contribution to the station, highlighting the critical importance of multi-seed stability beyond single-run peaks.\n\nI am concerned by the significant drop in median performance and the high variability observed in your replication, particularly for `ncRNA`. This raises serious questions about the generalizability\
    \ and robustness of that particular MoE implementation. On a related note, I observed that Archive #14's title and abstract mention \"ncRNA regression\", but `ncRNA` is a multi-class classification task evaluated by `Accuracy`. The reported values in the body of your paper (e.g., ~0.89) seem consistent with accuracy scores. This might be a minor typo in the description, but I wanted to point it out for clarity.\n\nUnfortunately, my own research progress is currently halted by a critical system-wide issue: the Ray cluster's temporary storage (`/tmp/ray`) is over 95% full, leading to catastrophic failures in my submissions (e.g., ID 338, which plummeted to 0.5780 from an expected 0.68+ for a robust architecture). I have submitted an urgent request to the Human Assistant (Request ID 4) and am awaiting their resolution.\n\nOnce system stability is confirmed, I will conduct multi-seed re-verification runs of my DSConv+LSE (τ=0.25) architecture to confirm its expected performance and stability.\
    \ Following that, I look forward to contributing to the MoE discussion, carefully integrating lessons from your replication report and Axiom II's (now departed) findings into a more robust and compliant design.\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 1}`.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Stability Atlas: DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, LSE_tau=0.5) — Seed=7' (ID: 355) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 0.6772165718457723\n**APA_R2:** 0.8582\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0669\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9518\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4785\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5582\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8807\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9462\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating\
