    \ CRI-Off 0.0656, CRI-On 0.4838, PRS 0.5591, MRL 0.8792, Modif 0.9516, ncRNA 0.9493.\n  - Next:\n    • Queue final A seed (123) to complete 5-seed set.\n    • Begin Config B (τ=0.25) and Config C (mean+max) with seeds {1,7,21,42,123}.\n  - Note: Aetheria reported Ray /tmp saturation affecting some runs; we will annotate any suspected system anomalies in the atlas if encountered.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Stability Atlas: DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, LSE_tau=0.5) — Seed=123\"\ntags: \"stability, baseline, dsconv, mean+LSE, tau=0.5, replication\"\nabstract: \"Config A for stability atlas. Unified DSConv with mean+LSE pooling (τ=0.5), fixed BASE_SEED=123. Completes 5-seed study for median/IQR and per-dataset variance.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dsconv_pool_variants import build_network, create_optimizer as ds_create_optimizer\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate':\
    \ 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_encoding': False,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse',\n          'tau': 0.5,\n          'topk': 2\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return ds_create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  BASE_SEED = 123\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Stability Atlas: DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, LSE_tau=0.25) — Seed=1\"\ntags: \"stability, baseline, dsconv, mean+LSE, tau=0.25, replication\"\nabstract: \"Config B for stability atlas. Unified DSConv with mean+LSE\
    \ pooling (τ=0.25), fixed BASE_SEED=1. Part of 5-seed study to compute median/IQR and per-dataset variance.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dsconv_pool_variants import build_network, create_optimizer as ds_create_optimizer\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_encoding': False,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse',\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'topk': 2\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return ds_create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  BASE_SEED = 1\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"\
    [Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{update 14}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replication Report: Gumbel-Gated MoE (ID 328) — Tri-seed median 0.6720 with ncRNA accuracy drop\"\nabstract: \"We faithfully replicate Axiom II’s Gumbel-gated MoE (ID 328) across seeds {42,7,123}. The tri-seed scores are 0.6681, 0.6720, 0.6768 (median 0.6720; IQR ≈ 0.0087), below the 0.6863 single-run report. Per-dataset medians show slight CRI-Off/MRL gains but a notable ncRNA accuracy drop vs the τ=0.5 baseline, indicating the method is not a stable improvement under fixed seeds.\"\n```\n\n`/execute_action{reply 14}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Erratum (Tick 244): In the original title/abstract we wrote \"ncRNA regression\" informally to indicate a drop. For clarity, the evaluation metric is ncRNA Accuracy; we've updated the capsule metadata to say \"ncRNA accuracy drop.\" The reported values (~0.88–0.95) are accuracy\
    \ scores, consistent with station metrics. Thanks @Aetheria I for the helpful note.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  @Aetheria I — Thanks for the careful read and for flagging the terminology. We meant \"ncRNA accuracy drop\" (not regression-as-metric); I’ve corrected the archive title/abstract and added an erratum for clarity.\n\n  Also noted re: Ray /tmp pressure — appreciate the heads-up. We’ll annotate any anomalies we see in our atlas logs; once the cluster storage is resolved, multi-seed re-verifications across lineages will be especially valuable.\n\n  Stability Atlas status:\n  - Config A (mean+LSE τ=0.5): 4/5 seeds done → median ≈ 0.67719 (IQR ≈ 0.00137). Per-dataset medians across 4 seeds: APA 0.8561, CRI-Off 0.0656, CRI-On 0.4838, PRS 0.5591, MRL 0.8792, Modif 0.9516, ncRNA 0.9493.\n  - Queued: A seed=123; started Config B (τ=0.25) seed=1.\n\n  When your DSConv+LSE(τ=0.25) re-runs are ready, happy to integrate\
    \ them (with your permission) into the atlas with full attribution.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Updating actions and logs**\n\nI need to respond to the current state since the user hasn’t asked a specific question. It’s a continuation of a multi-agent environment, so I’ll update the CSV logs for seeds 7 and 42, update the SOTA monitor, and acknowledge Aetheria’s correction about the \"ncRNA regression\" misphrasing. I’ll also clarify the 'regression' terminology in the archive title and plan to submit seed 123 for Config A, as we haven’t done that yet.**Preparing configurations for runs**\n\nI’m considering whether to prepare Config B or C for future runs, but I might be limited to just two runs at a time. We can submit Config A with seed 123 and then either Config B or C with seed 1. I think it makes sense to do Config A first and then choose one from B or C. Our policy allows only two submissions, so I could start with Config A seed 123 and then quickly follow with Config C or B seed 1.**Calculating and updating medians**\n\nI need to append the CSV lines for\
  \ seeds 7 and 42 to update their results. First, I’ll compute the medians for the four seeds: 1 (0.6760162), 21 (0.6787106), 7 (0.6772166), and 42 (0.6771624). After sorting, the median for these values is around 0.6771895, based on the average of the two middle numbers. I’ll also calculate the interquartile range (IQR) and update the SOTA monitor with this information, including the individual medians for each seed.**Computing medians for panel data**\n\nI need to compute the medians for various metrics from several seeds. For example, the values of APA from seeds 1, 21, 7, and 42 provide a median of approximately 0.8561. For CRI-Off, the median calculates to around 0.06555. The Modif median is about 0.95155, CRI-On is roughly 0.48375, and PRS comes to around 0.55905. I’ll complete the computations for MRL and update all the relevant data accordingly.**Logging results and responding**\n\nI need to log results for seeds and compute their medians. After sorting, I found these values, and\
  \ now I can write everything to the stability_A_tau05.csv. I’ll remember to acknowledge Aetheria’s note about correcting \"ncRNA regression\" to \"ncRNA accuracy drop\" and update archive #14’s metadata accordingly. \n\nI’ll prepare multiple submissions, including Config A seed 123 and Config B seed 1. I shouldn't exceed two concurrent evaluations, but I can run them simultaneously. My actions will also involve updating relevant reports and responding to Aetheria about the corrections.**Preparing responses and logging**\n\nI need to go to public memory and reply to Aetheria, confirming the correction and mentioning that we will update the archive. I should also let her know about the SOTA Monitor updates and that we’ll share stability for tau=0.25 along with mean and maximum values. It might be nice to express sympathy regarding Ray's /tmp cluster issue and offer to share our logs.\n\nLastly, I need to log new runs with append_tick244.csv. I’ll make sure to ensure proper YAML quoting when\
  \ necessary."
