    \  - CRI-Off Spearman: 0.0642\n  - CRI-On Spearman: 0.4843\n  - PRS R2: 0.5599\n  - MRL R2: 0.8807\n  - Modif AUC-ROC: 0.9513\n  - ncRNA Accuracy: 0.9508\n\n  Notes:\n  - Low variability relative to single-run differences (IQR ~0.002). Largest panel spread typically on CRI-On; CRI-Off also varies but remains stable in rank.\n  - This provides the stable reference for τ=0.5. We will contrast with τ=0.25 and mean+max in Configs B/C.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/stability_B_tau025.csv}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  seed,eval_id,score,APA_R2,CRI_Off_Spearman,CRI_On_Spearman,PRS_R2,MRL_R2,Modif_AUC_ROC,ncRNA_Accuracy\n  1,358,0.6735100054877045,0.8579,0.0774,0.4364,0.5619,0.8792,0.9510,0.9508\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Stability Atlas: DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, LSE_tau=0.25) — Seed=7\"\ntags: \"stability, baseline, dsconv, mean+LSE, tau=0.25, replication\"\nabstract: \"Config B for stability atlas. Unified DSConv with mean+LSE pooling (τ=0.25),\
    \ fixed BASE_SEED=7. Part of 5-seed study to compute median/IQR and per-dataset variance.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dsconv_pool_variants import build_network, create_optimizer as ds_create_optimizer\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_encoding': False,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse',\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'topk': 2\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return ds_create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  BASE_SEED = 7\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')}\
    \ val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Stability Atlas: DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, LSE_tau=0.25) — Seed=21\"\ntags: \"stability, baseline, dsconv, mean+LSE, tau=0.25, replication\"\nabstract: \"Config B for stability atlas. Unified DSConv with mean+LSE pooling (τ=0.25), fixed BASE_SEED=21. Part of 5-seed study to compute median/IQR and per-dataset variance.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dsconv_pool_variants import build_network, create_optimizer as ds_create_optimizer\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_encoding': False,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse',\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'topk': 2\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n\
    \      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return ds_create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  BASE_SEED = 21\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/SOTA_MONITOR.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  SOTA Monitor (Tick 246)\n  - Config A (τ=0.5) complete (5 seeds): median=0.67722, Q1=0.67659, Q3=0.67862, IQR=0.00203.\n    Panel medians: APA 0.8556, CRI-Off 0.0642, CRI-On 0.4843, PRS 0.5599, MRL 0.8807, Modif 0.9513, ncRNA 0.9508.\n  - Config B (τ=0.25): seed=1 done (ID 358=0.67351); seeds 7 and 21 submitted; 42/123 to follow after queue frees.\n  - Next: run Config C (mean+max) after B; publish atlas with medians/IQR and per-panel variance across A/B/C, noting any system anomalies.\n```"
