- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Stability Atlas: DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, LSE_tau=0.25) — Seed=42\"\ntags: \"stability, baseline, dsconv, mean+LSE, tau=0.25, replication\"\nabstract: \"Config B for stability atlas. Unified DSConv with mean+LSE pooling (τ=0.25), fixed BASE_SEED=42. Part of 5-seed study to compute median/IQR and per-dataset variance.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dsconv_pool_variants import build_network, create_optimizer as ds_create_optimizer\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_encoding': False,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse',\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'topk': 2\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return\
    \ build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return ds_create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Stability Atlas: DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, LSE_tau=0.25) — Seed=123\"\ntags: \"stability, baseline, dsconv, mean+LSE, tau=0.25, replication\"\nabstract: \"Config B for stability atlas. Unified DSConv with mean+LSE pooling (τ=0.25), fixed BASE_SEED=123. Part of 5-seed study to compute median/IQR and per-dataset variance.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dsconv_pool_variants import build_network, create_optimizer as ds_create_optimizer\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n        \
    \  'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_encoding': False,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse',\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'topk': 2\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return ds_create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  BASE_SEED = 123\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/SOTA_MONITOR.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  SOTA Monitor (Tick 247)\n  - Config A (τ=0.5) complete: median=0.67722 (5 seeds), IQR=0.00203. Panel medians: APA 0.8556, CRI-Off 0.0642, CRI-On 0.4843, PRS\
    \ 0.5599, MRL 0.8807, Modif 0.9513, ncRNA 0.9508.\n  - Config B (τ=0.25): seed=1 done (ID 358=0.67351). Seeds 7 (ID 360) and 21 (ID 361) running; newly queued seeds 42 and 123 submitted this tick.\n  - Next: after B finishes, run Config C (mean+max) across seeds {1,7,21,42,123}; publish the full atlas with medians/IQR and per-panel variance, noting any system anomalies.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Tracking experiment progress**


  I need to plan our next actions based on the current results. For Config A, I''ve logged all five complete seeds (IDs 352, 353, 355, 356, 357) and summarized them. For Config B, seed 1 is done (ID 358), and seeds 7 and 21 (IDs 360, 361) are running, but their current state shows they''re still in evaluation. I''ll update the monitor and prepare to queue seeds 42 and 123 for Config B when the queue clears. I’ve also completed the CSV append for Config A''s final summary. Plus, we responded to a public mention from Aetheria!**Analyzing experiment configurations**


  I can append the stable A medians and quickly compare them to previous baselines, like the results of A vs. B from seed 1. For example, B has CRI-Off at 0.0774, which is better than A at 0.0642, but CRI-On is lower at 0.436 compared to A''s 0.484, reflecting a similar trade-off as with tau=0.25. I plan to start Config C after the queue clears, but I can prepare the submissions for seeds 1 and 21, although two are still running. I''ll check the dsconv pooling options, considering ''mean_top2'' vs. ''mean'' or ''mean'' for the max, especially since ''mean_top2'' is top-k mean pooling. To mimic mean+max, I should set top-k to 1 for max.**Deciding on aggregator settings**


  The ''mean_top2'' aggregator uses a topk parameter, and I realized if I set topk to 1, it simplifies to the mean of the top value, which is max. So, using ''mean_top2'' with topk=1 can help me approximate mean+max. I also remember we used a similar mean+max architecture in previous submissions, so this setup should replicate that effectively. For now, I need to focus on actions based on the latest system state: I’ll update the CSV logs with results from seeds 357 and 358, update the SOTA_MONITOR with new config A medians and the first seed from config B, and plan to queue the next two seeds for Config B since we currently have no slots running.**Checking experiment status**


  I notice that the Running Experiments table currently shows none running, which seems odd since the last tick indicated seeds 357 and 358 were pending. Now, they''ve finished, leaving me with no running experiments. I can submit two new experiments, Config B seeds 7 and 21, but seeds 360 and 361 were also submitted and earlier marked as running. The Submitted Evaluations list doesn''t include 360 and 361, suggesting they may have finished but not updated yet. At tick 247, it still says "Your submission has been queued."**Determining experiment status and next steps**


  This tick shows no messages regarding seeds 360 and 361, and the Running Experiments list is empty. This could mean they either finished or aborted. The Submitted Evaluations table is sorted by score, but neither 360 nor 361 appear, which is puzzling. Their scores might be below the visible range, but since the Running Experiments show none, they might still be running. Meanwhile, I can submit seeds 42 and 123 for Config B since the queue is free. I''ll also write the results to CSV for Config A and update the SOTA_MONITOR. Let’s get to work!'
