- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/stability_B_tau025.csv}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  seed,eval_id,score,APA_R2,CRI_Off_Spearman,CRI_On_Spearman,PRS_R2,MRL_R2,Modif_AUC_ROC,ncRNA_Accuracy\n  1,358,0.6735100054877045,0.8579,0.0774,0.4364,0.5619,0.8792,0.9510,0.9508\n  7,360,0.6807241512628998,0.8551,0.0718,0.5013,0.5535,0.8819,0.9522,0.9492\n  21,361,0.6716344554544637,0.8561,0.0755,0.4330,0.5570,0.8808,0.9513,0.9477\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/stability_B_summary_seed3.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Stability Atlas — Config B (DSConv + mean+LSE τ=0.25), seeds {1,7,21} — Provisional summary (Tick 248)\n\n  Scores (sorted):\n  - 0.671634, 0.673510, 0.680724\n  Median = 0.673510; Q1 ≈ 0.672572; Q3 ≈ 0.677117; IQR ≈ 0.004545\n\n  Per-dataset medians (across seeds {1,7,21})\n  - APA R2: 0.8561\n  - CRI-Off Spearman: 0.0755\n  - CRI-On Spearman: 0.4364\n  - PRS R2: 0.5570\n  - MRL R2: 0.8808\n  - Modif AUC-ROC: 0.9513\n\
    \  - ncRNA Accuracy: 0.9492\n\n  Notes:\n  - τ=0.25 shows higher variance than τ=0.5 and a lower median aggregate so far; it typically lifts CRI-Off and sometimes CRI-On at the expense of APA/MRL/ncRNA.\n  - Two more seeds to run (42,123) to finalize 5-seed stats.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Stability Atlas: DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, LSE_tau=0.25) — Seed=42\"\ntags: \"stability, baseline, dsconv, mean+LSE, tau=0.25, replication\"\nabstract: \"Config B for stability atlas. Unified DSConv with mean+LSE pooling (τ=0.25), fixed BASE_SEED=42. Part of 5-seed study to compute median/IQR and per-dataset variance.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dsconv_pool_variants import build_network, create_optimizer as ds_create_optimizer\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n     \
    \     'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_encoding': False,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse',\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'topk': 2\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return ds_create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Stability Atlas: DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, LSE_tau=0.25) — Seed=123\"\ntags: \"stability, baseline, dsconv, mean+LSE, tau=0.25, replication\"\nabstract: \"Config B for stability atlas. Unified DSConv with mean+LSE pooling (τ=0.25), fixed BASE_SEED=123. Part of 5-seed study to compute median/IQR and per-dataset variance.\"\
    \ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dsconv_pool_variants import build_network, create_optimizer as ds_create_optimizer\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_encoding': False,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse',\n          'tau': 0.25,\n          'topk': 2\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return ds_create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  BASE_SEED = 123\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage\
    \ write noema/results/SOTA_MONITOR.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  SOTA Monitor (Tick 248)\n  - Config B (τ=0.25) progress:\n    • seed=1 → ID 358 = 0.67351\n    • seed=7 → ID 360 = 0.68072\n    • seed=21 → ID 361 = 0.67163\n    Provisional median (3 seeds) = 0.67351; IQR ≈ 0.00455.\n    Panel medians (3 seeds): APA 0.8561, CRI-Off 0.0755, CRI-On 0.4364, PRS 0.5570, MRL 0.8808, Modif 0.9513, ncRNA 0.9492.\n  - Remaining seeds for B: 42 and 123 submitted this tick.\n  - Next: run Config C (mean+max) across {1,7,21,42,123} after B finishes; publish the full stability atlas with medians/IQR and per-panel variance across A/B/C.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Updating seed submissions**


  I need to respond with some actions: first, I''ll update the stability_B CSV with new results and revise the SOTA_MONITOR with Config B stats. Also, it looks like seeds 42 and 123 are ready to be queued again since two previous submissions (IDs 360 and 361) finished. Initially, 42 and 123 failed due to queue limits earlier at tick 247, but now I can resubmit them for Config B. I''ll also respond to Aetheria''s message if needed.**Executing tasks for seeds**


  I need to perform several tasks today. First, I’ll write to the stability_B_tau025.csv to append rows for seeds 7 and 21 along with their metrics. Since the CSV currently only has seed 1, I’ll rewrite the content to include all three. Next, I’ll update the SOTA_MONITOR with Config B results for seeds 1, 7, and 21, calculating the median from their scores, which I believe is 0.673510. Then, I’ll submit seeds 42 and 123 now that there are free slots and possibly update a summary file.**Calculating component-wise medians**


  I need to calculate some component-wise medians for seeds 7 and 21. Seed 7 (ID 360) has various metrics, like APA at 0.8551, and seed 21 (ID 361) has an APA of 0.8561. Going through the medians for all components: APA gives a median of 0.8561, Off is 0.0755, On is 0.4364, PRS is 0.5570, MRL is 0.8808, Modif is 0.9513, and ncRNA is 0.9492. I’ll add these medians to the SOTA monitor before submitting seeds 42 and 123 for Config B.**Resubmitting seeds and updating logs**


  I tried submitting seeds 42 and 123 in the last tick, but they were blocked. Now, I need to resubmit them and hope they go through this time. I''ll include the same code for BASE_SEED and make sure to update the log in stability_B_tau025.csv by rewriting it with a header and the three rows. Also, I plan to create a summary file for the partial results. My actions will include writing to both CSVs and submitting the seeds while ensuring the SOTA_MONITOR is updated correctly.'
