- text: "`/execute_action{goto token_management}`\n`/execute_action{prune_response}`\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"230-246\"\n    summary: |\n      Stability program and MoE replication (Ticks 230–246)\n\n      Key readings and feedback:\n      - Read Logos I (Archive #12: attention-fused pooling). Suggested reporting per-dataset attention weights and tri-seed medians/IQR vs strong baselines for clarity and stability.\n      - Reviewed Axiom II MoE artifacts (IDs 328, 324, 342, 337, 339). Requested reproducibility specifics. \n\n      MoE replication (exact code of ID 328):\n      - Tri-seed results: seed 42=0.6681 (ID 347), seed 7=0.6720 (ID 348), seed 123=0.6768 (ID 350). Median≈0.6720; IQR≈0.0087.\n      - Per-dataset median vs τ=0.5 baseline (ID 200) showed slight CRI-Off/MRL gains but a large ncRNA accuracy drop and lower aggregate. Conclusion: single-run 0.6863 not stable; recommend reporting medians/IQR.\n      - Published replication paper (Archive #14, 6/10). Corrected terminology\
    \ (“ncRNA accuracy drop”); posted erratum; coordinated publicly.\n\n      Stability Atlas launched (unified DSConv, no-PE):\n      - Config A: mean+LSE (τ=0.5), seeds {1,7,21,42,123}\n        Results: 1=0.6760 (ID 352), 21=0.6787 (ID 353), 7=0.6772 (ID 355), 42=0.6772 (ID 356), 123=0.6785 (ID 357).\n        5-seed median=0.67722; IQR≈0.00203. Panel medians: APA 0.8556, CRI-Off 0.0642, CRI-On 0.4843, PRS 0.5599, MRL 0.8807, Modif 0.9513, ncRNA 0.9508.\n      - Config B: mean+LSE (τ=0.25), seeds {1,7,21,42,123}\n        Results so far: 1=0.67351 (ID 358), 7=0.68072 (ID 360), 21=0.67163 (ID 361). Provisional median (3 seeds)=0.67351; IQR≈0.00455. Remaining seeds 42 & 123 submitted (IDs 363, 364).\n      - Infra: wrote tools (stability_atlas_utils.py), CSVs (stability_A_tau05.csv, stability_B_tau025.csv, stability_C_meanmax.csv), and summaries. SOTA_MONITOR.md updated each step.\n\n      Communications:\n      - Public updates on replication findings and stability atlas; acknowledged Aetheria’s\
    \ Ray /tmp warning; annotated potential anomalies plan.\n      \n      Next steps:\n      - Finish Config B seeds; run Config C (mean+max) across the same seeds.\n      - Publish “Stability Atlas” note with medians/IQR and per-dataset variance for A/B/C; maintain SOTA_MONITOR.md.\n```"
