parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/stability_B_tau025.csv}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  seed,eval_id,score,APA_R2,CRI_Off_Spearman,CRI_On_Spearman,PRS_R2,MRL_R2,Modif_AUC_ROC,ncRNA_Accuracy\n  1,358,0.6735100054877045,0.8579,0.0774,0.4364,0.5619,0.8792,0.9510,0.9508\n  7,360,0.6807241512628998,0.8551,0.0718,0.5013,0.5535,0.8819,0.9522,0.9492\n  21,361,0.6716344554544637,0.8561,0.0755,0.4330,0.5570,0.8808,0.9513,0.9477\n  42,363,0.6738825298482815,0.8582,0.0751,0.4332,0.5637,0.8846,0.9515,0.9508\n  123,364,0.6709632257782253,0.8522,0.0715,0.4424,0.5587,0.8825,0.9510,0.9385\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/stability_B_summary_5seed.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Stability Atlas — Config B (DSConv + mean+LSE τ=0.25), seeds {1,7,21,42,123} — Final (Tick 250)\n\n  Scores (sorted): 0.670963, 0.671634, 0.673510, 0.673883, 0.680724\n  - Median = 0.673510\n  - Q1 ≈ 0.671299, Q3 ≈ 0.677303, IQR ≈ 0.006004\n\n  Per-dataset medians across\
    \ 5 seeds:\n  - APA R2: 0.8561\n  - CRI-Off Spearman: 0.0751\n  - CRI-On Spearman: 0.4364\n  - PRS R2: 0.5587\n  - MRL R2: 0.8819\n  - Modif AUC-ROC: 0.9513\n  - ncRNA Accuracy: 0.9492\n\n  Comparison vs Config A (τ=0.5; 5-seed median=0.67722, IQR≈0.00203):\n  - τ=0.25 shows lower median (Δ ≈ -0.00371) and higher variance (IQR ↑ ~3x).\n  - Typical trade-off: CRI-Off/CRI-On lift coupled with APA/MRL/ncRNA reductions.\n\n  Conclusion:\n  - Keep τ=0.5 as the default unified baseline (best median/stability).\n  - τ=0.25 is an optional CRISPR-emphasis setting with higher variance.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/dsconv_pool_variants.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random, lax\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n\n  # -----------------------------\n  # Backbone block\n  # -----------------------------\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n\
    \      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dilation: int = 1\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.d_model,\n              kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n              feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n              padding='SAME',\n              kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n              name='dw_conv'\n          )(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  # -----------------------------\n  # Pooling helpers\n  # -----------------------------\n  def lse_pool(h: jnp.ndarray, tau: float) -> jnp.ndarray:\n      x = h / tau\n      m = jnp.max(x, axis=1, keepdims=True)                     # (B,1,C)\n      lse = tau * (jnp.log(jnp.mean(jnp.exp(x - m), axis=1) +\
    \ 1e-12) + jnp.squeeze(m, axis=1))\n      return lse  # (B, C)\n\n  def std_pool(h: jnp.ndarray) -> jnp.ndarray:\n      mu = jnp.mean(h, axis=1, keepdims=True)                   # (B,1,C)\n      var = jnp.mean((h - mu) ** 2, axis=1)                     # (B,C)\n      return jnp.sqrt(var + 1e-6)                               # (B,C)\n\n  def topk_mean_pool(h: jnp.ndarray, k: int = 2) -> jnp.ndarray:\n      B, L, C = h.shape\n      k = jnp.minimum(k, L)\n      x = jnp.transpose(h, (0, 2, 1))                           # (B,C,L)\n      vals, _ = lax.top_k(x, int(k))                            # (B,C,k)\n      return jnp.mean(vals, axis=-1)                            # (B,C)\n\n  def max_pool(h: jnp.ndarray) -> jnp.ndarray:\n      return jnp.max(h, axis=1)                                 # (B,C)\n\n  # -----------------------------\n  # Network with pooling variants\n  # -----------------------------\n  class RNANetPoolVariant(nn.Module):\n      d_input: int = 4\n      d_output: int = 1\n\
    \      task_type: str = 'regression'\n      d_model: int = 256\n      num_blocks: int = 5\n      dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      positional_encoding: bool = False\n\n      # pooling config\n      aggregator: str = 'mean_lse'   # 'mean_lse' | 'mean_std' | 'mean_top2' | 'mean_max'\n      tau: float = 0.5\n      topk: int = 2\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # Input proj\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # DSConv stack\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              d = self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n              h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Mean is always included\n        \
    \  mean_vec = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)  # (B,C)\n\n          if self.aggregator == 'mean_lse':\n              agg_vec = lse_pool(h, self.tau)\n          elif self.aggregator == 'mean_std':\n              agg_vec = std_pool(h)\n          elif self.aggregator == 'mean_top2':\n              agg_vec = topk_mean_pool(h, self.topk)\n          elif self.aggregator == 'mean_max':\n              agg_vec = max_pool(h)\n          else:\n              raise ValueError(f\"Unknown aggregator: {self.aggregator}\")\n\n          fused = jnp.concatenate([mean_vec, agg_vec], axis=-1)  # (B, 2C)\n\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out')(z)\n\n          if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n              return logits.squeeze(-1)\n          return logits\n\n  class PoolVariantNetwork:\n   \
    \   def __init__(self, d_input, d_output, task_type, **kwargs):\n          self.network = RNANetPoolVariant(d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, **kwargs)\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def build_network(d_output: int, task_type: str, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return PoolVariantNetwork(\n          d_input=4,\n          d_output=d_output,\n\
    \          task_type=task_type,\n          d_model=hparams.get('d_model', 256),\n          num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks', 5),\n          dilations=tuple(hparams.get('dilations', [1,2,4,8,16])),\n          kernel_size=hparams.get('kernel_size', 7),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n          positional_encoding=hparams.get('positional_encoding', False),\n          aggregator=hparams.get('aggregator', 'mean_lse'),\n          tau=hparams.get('tau', 0.5),\n          topk=hparams.get('topk', 2),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01),\n      )\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Stability Atlas: DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, max) — Seed=1\"\ntags: \"stability, baseline, dsconv, mean+max, replication\"\nabstract: \"Config C for stability atlas. Unified DSConv with concat(mean,\
    \ max) pooling, BASE_SEED=1. Part of 5-seed study to compute median/IQR and per-dataset variance.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dsconv_pool_variants import build_network, create_optimizer as ds_create_optimizer\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_encoding': False,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_max'\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return ds_create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  BASE_SEED = 1\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\"\
    )\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Stability Atlas: DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, max) — Seed=7\"\ntags: \"stability, baseline, dsconv, mean+max, replication\"\nabstract: \"Config C for stability atlas. Unified DSConv with concat(mean, max) pooling, BASE_SEED=7. Part of 5-seed study to compute median/IQR and per-dataset variance.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from dsconv_pool_variants import build_network, create_optimizer as ds_create_optimizer\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_encoding': False,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_max'\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate:\
    \ float = 0.001):\n      return ds_create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  BASE_SEED = 7\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/SOTA_MONITOR.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  SOTA Monitor (Tick 250)\n  - Config B (τ=0.25) completed (5 seeds):\n    Scores: 0.670963, 0.671634, 0.673510, 0.673883, 0.680724\n    • Median = 0.673510; Q1 ≈ 0.671299; Q3 ≈ 0.677303; IQR ≈ 0.006004\n    • Per-dataset medians: APA 0.8561 | CRI-Off 0.0751 | CRI-On 0.4364 | PRS 0.5587 | MRL 0.8819 | Modif 0.9513 | ncRNA 0.9492\n    Summary: Lower median and higher variance than τ=0.5 (median 0.67722, IQR ≈ 0.00203). Keep τ=0.5 as default; τ=0.25 optional for CRISPR emphasis.\n  - Config C (mean+max) launched (seeds 1,7). Will run seeds {1,7,21,42,123} and publish medians/IQR and panel variances.\n  - Leaderboard: top single-run remains 0.6863\
    \ (Axiom II ID 328); no new >0.686 since last check. Policy unchanged: replicate any >0.686 across {42,7,123} and report medians/IQR + per-panel deltas.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Calculating IQR and Medians**


  I’m computing the interquartile range (IQR) now. It looks like Q1 is about 0.6713 and Q3 is roughly 0.6773, giving an IQR of about 0.00600. Earlier, with three seeds, the IQR was 0.00455, so the five-seed IQR is larger. I''m also calculating the medians across five seeds for different datasets. For APA, the median is 0.8561, and for CRI-Off, it’s 0.0751. I need to keep these details organized.**Calculating Medians and Summary**


  I''ve sorted values for MRL R2 and found the median to be 0.8819, which is correct as it’s the third sorted number. For the Modif AUC-ROC, the median is 0.9513, confirming that seed 1 indeed had a value of 0.9510. Now, looking at ncRNA accuracy, the median ends up being 0.9492, which is promising. I need to compile these findings into "stability_B_summary_5seed.md" and update "SOTA_MONITOR.md." We should also plan for Config C runs while managing submissions.**Preparing Config C Submission**


  The system allows me to submit two seeds concurrently, and since there’s nothing running right now, I can go ahead with that. However, I realize we haven’t created a submission file for the mean+max aggregator. Previously, we had ''mean_top2'' for the top-k, but we need the ''mean_max'' aggregator. I can quickly update the storage module to include the ''mean_max'' function, ensuring that the code correctly implements the max pooling without causing any breaks. Let''s get to coding!**Updating Aggregator Implementation**


  I realize that editing the shared module could impact previous runs, but since they’ve finished, it shouldn’t be an issue for future ones. However, I might avoid modifying the module immediately and just use ''mean_top2'' as a temporary solution, even though I prefer comparing mean+max as a baseline. To keep things reproducible, it''s better to implement the ''mean_max'' aggregator. I’ll write the updates to the storage module while ensuring existing code remains intact. Copying the previous content, I''ll add the necessary functions and check that ''mean_max'' is recognized by the system.**Updating and Submitting Config C**


  I need to ensure that the underlying module supports the ''mean_max'' aggregator. I can’t use ''mean_top2'' with topk as "None," so I''ll proceed with updating the module. After that, I can submit seeds 1 and 7 for Config C. I should finish summarizing the previous batch before starting the new one to manage the tokens effectively. I’ll also write the necessary updates to the stabilization documents, including the median and IQR. Each task seems manageable, so let''s get started on writing the updates!'
