  I''m thinking about replicating Veritas II ID 365 across specific seeds. I plan to queue tasks after the current runs finish, and I might jot down a note about Config C progress, but it''s not essential. The instructions mention multiple actions can be issued, and I''m keeping an eye on token usage at 117k, which isn''t too high. I will provide necessary actions, such as writing an updated CSV file and a summary for Config C with current seed results.**Updating replication tasks**


  I realize that with just two values, the IQR isn''t very informative, so I can provide a range instead. I plan to update the SOTA_MONITOR with details about the provisional median and range. I should also mention that seeds 21 and 42 are currently running, with seed 123 to be submitted next. I’m considering token management for pruning, though it’s not urgent. Additionally, I might queue a tri-seed replication of Veritas II MoE later, and I can create a stability summary file for these seeds.**Implementing stability summary**


  I''m getting ready to write the content for the stability summary file. This will summarize the results from two seeds and calculate per-dataset medians. For seeds 7 and 1, I’ll collect their scores and compute the medians for each measure, such as APA, CRI-Off, and others. I’ll also figure out the IQR, but with only two data points, it’s just the absolute difference. I’ll make sure to format everything clearly for easy reference.**Planning next steps**


  I need to compile a range and write that down. After completing tasks 369 and 370, I’ll submit seed 123 for Config C and set up the replication of Veritas 365 across seeds. I should also update the SOTA MONITOR with the new provisional medians, ensuring not to write too frequently. It might be good to set a page size, but it’s not essential. Finally, I’ll consider pruning earlier tokens since they’re currently at a moderate level.**Deciding on submission template**


  I’m considering whether to create a submission template for Veritas II replication ''MoE'' across seeds. However, replicating the exact code of another agent may not be possible without access to their content. We previously attempted a "faithful hybrid" replication that didn’t perform well, so I’m planning for a tri-seed replication again but won’t execute it just yet. I’ll also ensure that the YAML content is consistent, using quotes around colons as needed. Now, I can finalize my actions.'
