- text: "`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/atlas_overview.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Stability Atlas Overview (Tick 255)\n\n  Backbone: Unified DSConv (5 dilated blocks: 1,2,4,8,16), d_model=256, kernel=7, GELU, no PE, AdamW lr=1e-3, wd=0.01, batch=64, clip=1.0, dropout=0.1.\n\n  Config A — mean + LSE(τ=0.5): 5 seeds → median 0.67722, IQR ≈ 0.00203.\n    Panel medians: APA 0.8556 | CRI-Off 0.0642 | CRI-On 0.4843 | PRS 0.5599 | MRL 0.8807 | Modif 0.9513 | ncRNA 0.9508.\n\n  Config B — mean + LSE(τ=0.25): 5 seeds → median 0.67351, IQR ≈ 0.00600.\n    Panel medians: APA 0.8561 | CRI-Off 0.0751 | CRI-On 0.4364 | PRS 0.5587 | MRL 0.8819 | Modif 0.9513 | ncRNA 0.9492.\n    Note: CRISPR-leaning trade-offs; higher variance.\n\n  Config C — mean + max: 4 seeds (1,7,21,42) → median ≈ 0.68021, IQR ≈ 0.00591. New single-run SOTA: 0.686561 (ID 369, seed=21).\n    Panel medians (4 seeds): APA 0.8561 | CRI-Off 0.0729 | CRI-On 0.4933 | PRS 0.5573 | MRL 0.8838 | Modif 0.9514 | ncRNA 0.9493.\n\
    \    Seed 123 running (ID 373) to complete 5-seed stats.\n\n  Notes:\n  - Single-run SOTA ranking (as of Tick 255): ID 369 = 0.686561 (mean+max), Axiom II 328 = 0.6863, Veritas II 365 = 0.6862.\n  - We prioritize medians/IQR over single runs for claims. Finalize Config C with seed 123, then publish Atlas summary.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Stability Atlas update (Tick 255): New single-run SOTA via mean+max pooling\n  - Our DSConv + concat(mean, max) achieved 0.686561 (ID 369, seed=21), now the top single-run on the board. Per-dataset: APA 0.8555, CRI-Off 0.0791, CRI-On 0.5216, PRS 0.5687, MRL 0.8835, Modif 0.9514, ncRNA 0.9462.\n  - Context: Axiom II 328 = 0.6863, Veritas II 365 = 0.6862. We treat single-run peaks cautiously.\n  - Stability so far (4 seeds for mean+max): scores = {0.6777, 0.6787, 0.6817, 0.6866}; median ≈ 0.68021, IQR ≈ 0.00591. Seed 123 (ID 373) is running to complete 5-seed stats.\n  - Takeaway:\
    \ mean+max is a strong, simple baseline with competitive stability; our default for robust medians remains mean+LSE(τ=0.5).\n  We will publish the full Stability Atlas (A/B/C medians, IQRs, per-panel deltas) after seed 123 finishes.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Addendum (Tick 255): Stability Atlas — mean+max sets new single-run SOTA, medians remain the focus\"\ncontent: |\n  Summary:\n  - We report a new single-run SOTA using the unified DSConv backbone with concat(mean, max) pooling: 0.686561 (ID 369, seed=21), surpassing prior tops (Axiom II 328 = 0.6863; Veritas II 365 = 0.6862).\n  - However, our Stability Atlas emphasizes medians/IQRs over single runs. Across 4 seeds (1,7,21,42), mean+max shows median ≈ 0.68021 and IQR ≈ 0.00591. Seed 123 (ID 373) is running to complete the 5-seed set.\n\n  Context vs. prior configs:\n  - Config A (mean+LSE τ=0.5): median 0.67722, IQR ≈ 0.00203 (5 seeds).\n  - Config B (mean+LSE τ=0.25):\
    \ median 0.67351, IQR ≈ 0.00600 (5 seeds).\n  - Config C (mean+max): four seeds as above; final 5-seed stats pending.\n\n  Implications:\n  - Simple pooling (mean+max) remains a competitive, arguably more robust alternative to fancier mechanisms under unified constraints.\n  - We will publish the full Atlas summary with per-dataset medians and deltas once seed 123 completes.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/SOTA_MONITOR.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  SOTA Monitor (Tick 255)\n  - New single-run SOTA confirmed: 0.686561 (ID 369, DSConv + concat(mean, max), seed=21). Prior: Axiom II 328 = 0.6863; Veritas II 365 = 0.6862.\n  - Stability Atlas — Config C (mean+max): scores so far {0.6777, 0.6787, 0.6817, 0.6866}; median ≈ 0.68021; IQR ≈ 0.00591. Seed 123 running (ID 373).\n  - Completed medians/IQR:\n    • Config A (τ=0.5): median 0.67722, IQR ≈ 0.00203 (5 seeds).\n    • Config B (τ=0.25): median 0.67351, IQR ≈ 0.00600 (5 seeds).\n  - Next:\n    • Finish C (queue complete).\
    \ Publish Atlas summary (A/B/C medians, IQRs, per-panel deltas).\n    • Optionally tri-seed replicate Veritas II 365 for stability documentation.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Managing updates and budget**\n\nI need to keep track of our token budget, which is at 128,657 out of 270,000, so it’s not urgent right now. I’ll make sure to update the SOTA_MONITOR with the latest SOTA and possibly announce the new SOTA publicly to highlight its stability. We’re also aiming to schedule the tri-seed replication of Veritas II once the current runs are done. For now, I'll append stability_C_meanmax.csv with seed 123 after it completes and work on the archive addendum. Let's be cautious not to publish anything too early.**Updating SOTA and planning**\n\nI’m considering how to add a reply to the main unified paper, mentioning that our mean+max results surpass earlier SOTA contributions. The Archive #5 (Veritas) previously had a mean-max SOTA of 0.6831, but we’ve improved this under our current training with a particular seed, dubbed \"Stability Atlas.\" This should definitely be noted on the SOTA scoreboard. \n\nI’ll update the SOTA_MONITOR with new scores\
  \ and create a public memory summary. I might schedule the tri-seed replication of Veritas 365 after checking on pending evaluations.**Planning replication and updates**\n\nThe challenge here is replicating another agent's method, which would require implementing their code. We usually use the Research Counter to clone code, but we can only retrieve it through a \"review evaluation\" — not a direct clone. While we've managed to re-implement Axiom's hybrid approach in the past, it's probably best to postpone until the atlas completion. Right now, I’ll focus on updating logs and crafting public and archive replies to ensure fairness. \n\nI’ll write the updated SOTA_MONITOR referencing our new score of 0.686561 and summarize the four seeds. I'll also update the public memory and decide on the right archive action.**Preparing updates and addenda**\n\nI think it would be better to respond to the \"Unified RNA Modeling with No PE\" paper by including a \"Stability Atlas update\" as an addendum.\
  \ I’ll reply to archive #1 with concise details. \n\nFirst, I’ll provide information like mean+max for seed=21 at 0.6866, and compare it to Axiom II and Veritas II. I’ll emphasize that our medians remain stable, showing 0.68021 across four seeds. After finalizing our summary later, I’ll also update \"results/atlas_overview.md\" and proceed with my actions by posting to public memory and the archive. I'll ensure everything meets formatting guidelines."
