- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/stability_C_meanmax.csv}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  seed,eval_id,score,APA_R2,CRI_Off_Spearman,CRI_On_Spearman,PRS_R2,MRL_R2,Modif_AUC_ROC,ncRNA_Accuracy\n  7,367,0.6787117409230936,0.8563,0.0804,0.4815,0.5542,0.8826,0.9514,0.9446\n  1,366,0.6817096932482748,0.8587,0.0636,0.5050,0.5564,0.8841,0.9502,0.9538\n  21,369,0.6865612008635410,0.8555,0.0791,0.5216,0.5687,0.8835,0.9514,0.9462\n  42,370,0.6777304230834211,0.8559,0.0667,0.4725,0.5581,0.8871,0.9516,0.9523\n  123,373,0.6797369657820552,0.8571,0.0771,0.4854,0.5548,0.8783,0.9516,0.9538\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/stability_C_summary_5seed.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Stability Atlas — Config C (DSConv + concat(mean, max)), seeds {1,7,21,42,123} — Final (Tick 256)\n\n  Scores (sorted):\n  - 0.677730, 0.678712, 0.679737, 0.681710, 0.686561\n  Median = 0.679737\n  Q1 ≈ 0.678221, Q3 ≈ 0.684135, IQR ≈ 0.005914\n\n  Per-dataset medians\
    \ across 5 seeds:\n  - APA R2: 0.8563\n  - CRI-Off Spearman: 0.0771\n  - CRI-On Spearman: 0.4854\n  - PRS R2: 0.5564\n  - MRL R2: 0.8835\n  - Modif AUC-ROC: 0.9514\n  - ncRNA Accuracy: 0.9523\n\n  Notes:\n  - New single-run SOTA: 0.686561 (ID 369, seed=21).\n  - Among A/B/C, Config C has the highest median (0.679737) but higher variance than Config A (τ=0.5).\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/atlas_overview.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Stability Atlas Overview (Tick 256)\n\n  Backbone: Unified DSConv (5 dilated blocks: 1,2,4,8,16), d_model=256, kernel=7, GELU, no PE, AdamW lr=1e-3, wd=0.01, batch=64, clip=1.0, dropout=0.1.\n\n  Config A — mean + LSE(τ=0.5): 5 seeds → median 0.67722, IQR ≈ 0.00203.\n    Panel medians: APA 0.8556 | CRI-Off 0.0642 | CRI-On 0.4843 | PRS 0.5599 | MRL 0.8807 | Modif 0.9513 | ncRNA 0.9508.\n\n  Config B — mean + LSE(τ=0.25): 5 seeds → median 0.67351, IQR ≈ 0.00600.\n    Panel medians: APA 0.8561 | CRI-Off 0.0751 | CRI-On 0.4364 | PRS 0.5587\
    \ | MRL 0.8819 | Modif 0.9513 | ncRNA 0.9492.\n    Note: CRISPR-leaning trade-offs; higher variance.\n\n  Config C — mean + max: 5 seeds → median 0.679737, IQR ≈ 0.005914. New single-run SOTA: 0.686561 (ID 369, seed=21).\n    Panel medians: APA 0.8563 | CRI-Off 0.0771 | CRI-On 0.4854 | PRS 0.5564 | MRL 0.8835 | Modif 0.9514 | ncRNA 0.9523.\n\n  Takeaways:\n  - For robust medians, mean+max (C) > τ=0.5 (A) > τ=0.25 (B). For stability, τ=0.5 (A) best IQR.\n  - Simple pooling remains competitive; we recommend reporting both single-run peaks and 5-seed medians/IQR.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/SOTA_MONITOR.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  SOTA Monitor (Tick 256)\n  - New single-run SOTA: 0.686561 (ID 369, DSConv + concat(mean, max), seed=21).\n  - Config C (mean+max) complete (5 seeds): median = 0.679737; IQR ≈ 0.005914.\n    • Per-panel medians: APA 0.8563 | CRI-Off 0.0771 | CRI-On 0.4854 | PRS 0.5564 | MRL 0.8835 | Modif 0.9514 | ncRNA 0.9523.\n  - Comparative medians/IQR:\n\
    \    • Config A (τ=0.5): 0.67722, IQR ≈ 0.00203 (most stable).\n    • Config B (τ=0.25): 0.67351, IQR ≈ 0.00600 (higher variance; CRISPR-leaning).\n    • Config C (mean+max): 0.679737, IQR ≈ 0.005914 (highest median).\n  - Next steps:\n    • Publish Stability Atlas summary (A/B/C medians, IQRs, per-panel deltas).\n    • Optionally tri-seed replicate Veritas II 365 (0.6862) for stability documentation.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Stability Atlas final (Tick 256): mean+max complete (5 seeds)\n  - Single-run SOTA: 0.686561 (ID 369, DSConv + concat(mean, max), seed=21).\n  - 5-seed median/IQR:\n    • Config C (mean+max): median 0.679737, IQR ≈ 0.005914.\n    • Config A (mean+LSE τ=0.5): median 0.67722, IQR ≈ 0.00203 (most stable).\n    • Config B (mean+LSE τ=0.25): median 0.67351, IQR ≈ 0.00600 (CRISPR-leaning, higher variance).\n  - Per-panel medians for mean+max: APA 0.8563 | CRI-Off 0.0771 | CRI-On 0.4854 | PRS 0.5564\
    \ | MRL 0.8835 | Modif 0.9514 | ncRNA 0.9523.\n  We’ll consolidate into an Atlas note with CSVs and deltas; medians/IQR remain our primary reporting metric.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Computing statistics for Config C**\n\nI need to finalize the stability atlas for Config C with seed 123, which has a score of 0.679736, and ID 373. Now, I'm calculating the 5-seed statistics including the mean and max. I already have scores from seeds 1, 7, 21, 42, and 123. \n\nI'll sort these scores: 0.6777304231, 0.6787117409, 0.6797369658, 0.6817096932, 0.6865612009. From there, the median score is 0.679737, while Q1 is derived from the lower half of the sorted values.**Calculating seed statistics**\n\nEarlier, I used averages for 4 seeds, and now for 5 seeds, I’m figuring out the median of the lower two scores. For two numbers, the median is their average, so that gives me 0.678221082 for Q1. Then for Q3, I average the upper two scores, which results in about 0.68413544705. The IQR ends up being approximately 0.00591436505. Interestingly, the IQR for both 4 and 5 seeds is similar, but the median changed to 0.679737. Now, I need to update the stability_C_meanmax.csv\
  \ to include the fifth row.**Summarizing Config C metrics**\n\nNext, I’ll create a final summary for Config C that includes the 5-seed median and IQR. I need to compute medians across datasets using the per-seed metrics I have. \n\nFor instance, I've recorded various metrics for each seed, such as APA, CRI-Off, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, Modif, and ncRNA. For the APA values (0.8555, 0.8559, 0.8563, 0.8571, 0.8587), the median is 0.8563, as it's the third number when sorted. Now, I can move on to compute the other medians for the remaining metrics.**Calculating medians for metrics**\n\nI need to ensure I've sorted the values for my calculations. For APA, the sorted values are 0.8555, 0.8559, 0.8563, 0.8571, and 0.8587, leading to a median of 0.8563. \n\nNext, for CRI-Off, I have values 0.0636, 0.0667, 0.0771, 0.0791, and 0.0804, which give a median of 0.0771. For CRI-On, the median is 0.4854. I've calculated the medians for PRS, MRL, Modif, and ncRNA too. \n\nNow, I should compile these medians\
  \ into the stability_C_summary_5seed.md file.**Updating SOTA and preparing actions**\n\nI need to update the SOTA_MONITOR.md with the final median and evaluate the best median across configurations. Config C has the highest median of 0.679737, which is about 0.0025 higher than Config A. However, Config A has a smaller IQR, indicating it's more stable.\n\nI also plan to document the new single-run SOTA ID, which exceeds the previous top score. Now we need to execute several actions line by line, such as updating various storage files, including the stability summary and final numbers. I’ll ensure everything is formatted correctly to six decimals and maintain concise notes."
