role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Stability Atlas: Unified DSConv Pooling Baselines (A: mean+LSE τ=0.5, B: τ=0.25, C: mean+max)\"\ntags: \"stability, baselines, dsconv, pooling, reproducibility\"\nabstract: \"We report 5-seed medians and IQR for three unified DSConv pooling baselines across 7 RNA datasets. Config C (mean+max) attains the highest median (0.6797) and a new single-run SOTA (0.6866). Config A (mean+LSE τ=0.5) remains the most stable (IQR≈0.0020). Config B (τ=0.25) shows CRISPR-leaning trade-offs and higher variance. We provide per-dataset medians and full CSVs for reproducibility.\"\ncontent: |\n  Setup\n  - Backbone: Unified DSConv (5 dilated blocks 1,2,4,8,16), d_model=256, kernel=7, GELU, no positional encoding.\n  - Optimizer/training: AdamW lr=1e-3, wd=0.01; batch=64; grad clip=1.0; dropout=0.1; early stopping (patience=10).\n  - Datasets/metrics: APA (R²), CRI-Off/CRI-On (Spearman), Modif (AUC-ROC), PRS (R², 3 outputs\
    \ avg), MRL (R²), ncRNA (Accuracy).\n  - Seeds: {1, 7, 21, 42, 123}. We report 5-seed medians and IQR; single-run peaks are noted but not primary.\n\n  Results (5-seed statistics)\n  - Config A — concat(mean, LSE τ=0.5)\n    • Median = 0.67722; IQR ≈ 0.00203\n    • Per-dataset medians: APA 0.8556 | CRI-Off 0.0642 | CRI-On 0.4843 | PRS 0.5599 | MRL 0.8807 | Modif 0.9513 | ncRNA 0.9508\n\n  - Config B — concat(mean, LSE τ=0.25)\n    • Median = 0.67351; IQR ≈ 0.00600\n    • Per-dataset medians: APA 0.8561 | CRI-Off 0.0751 | CRI-On 0.4364 | PRS 0.5587 | MRL 0.8819 | Modif 0.9513 | ncRNA 0.9492\n    • Note: CRISPR-leaning trade-offs (↑CRI-Off/CRI-On, ↓APA/MRL/ncRNA) and higher variance.\n\n  - Config C — concat(mean, max)\n    • Median = 0.679737; IQR ≈ 0.005914\n    • Per-dataset medians: APA 0.8563 | CRI-Off 0.0771 | CRI-On 0.4854 | PRS 0.5564 | MRL 0.8835 | Modif 0.9514 | ncRNA 0.9523\n    • New single-run SOTA: 0.686561 (ID 369, seed=21). Other seeds: 0.681710 (seed=1, ID 366), 0.678712\
    \ (seed=7, ID 367), 0.677730 (seed=42, ID 370), 0.679737 (seed=123, ID 373).\n\n  Takeaways\n  - For robust medians: mean+max (C) > τ=0.5 (A) > τ=0.25 (B).\n  - For stability (IQR), τ=0.5 (A) is best; mean+max (C) has higher variance but top median and best single run.\n  - Simple pooling remains highly competitive under unified constraints; absolute PE remains detrimental to this DSConv + global pooling family.\n\n  Reproducibility Artifacts (storage/noema/results)\n  - stability_A_tau05.csv, stability_A_summary_5seed.md\n  - stability_B_tau025.csv, stability_B_summary_5seed.md\n  - stability_C_meanmax.csv, stability_C_summary_5seed.md\n  - atlas_overview.md, SOTA_MONITOR.md\n\n  Notes/Next\n  - We will continue to report medians/IQR alongside any single-run peaks.\n  - Optional: tri-seed replication of Veritas II (ID 365, 0.6862) for stability documentation using the same seed set.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{rank score}`\n`/execute_action{page_size 10}`"
thinking_content: '**Finalizing Stability Atlas**


  I need to finalize the Stability Atlas and consider publishing an archive capsule summarizing the results and medians. Though current token usage is 140k out of 270k, so it seems safe. The research shows a new single-run SOTA of 0.686561. I plan to create an archive capsule including medians per configuration, methodology, and possibly some CSV references. Since the atlas is complete, there’s also an option to queue replication of the tri-seed now.**Running Experiments Queue**


  The queue is currently free, and the experiments table shows no ongoing tasks, but that''s based on an older snapshot. I think we can start submitting tri-seed replications, though the system limits us to two concurrent submissions. I can queue two seeds now and submit the third one later. To replicate another agent''s code, I need their submission code, which isn''t directly accessible. I''ll use /execute_action{review evaluation_id} to retrieve the necessary logs and code for Veritas II 365. Let''s gather the code and ensure compliance for resubmission.**Planning Archive Capsule**


  The research guidelines allow me to review and clone other agents'' code through official channels at the Research Counter, which is helpful. However, replicating the code exactly might lead to using a lot of tokens, making it lengthy. So, the plan could be to just modify the base while re-running the same configuration. My main focus right now is to publish the Stability Atlas as an archive capsule. I’ll craft actions to create the capsule, including an appropriate title, an abstract summarizing results, and CSV references. The SOTA monitor update is already handled, so I won’t need to revisit that. Optionally, I can preview all rankings in the research counter.**Preparing Archive Capsule Content**


  It seems there are some additional steps I could take, like writing the top entries into compare_top_models.csv for storage, but the priority is to publish the Stability Atlas. I might also update the metadata to indicate that the tri-seed replication is scheduled. Since the meta already shows the tri-seed queued after current runs, I can adjust to say, "Atlas complete; schedule tri-seed 365 next." I can prepare the Archive capsule content, providing an abstract about the stability atlas, highlighting the 5-seed medians and IQR with the single-run SOTA of 0.686561.**Writing Archive Content**


  I need to write the content for the Stability Atlas, starting with the method, which includes data, unified DSConv, training config, seeds, and metrics. The results will summarize medians and IQR per config, along with per-dataset medians. I’ll highlight the mean+max as the highest median and note that τ=0.5 is the most stable. The discussion will touch on trade-offs in evaluation practices for reporting medians. Next, I’ll implement actions to create the archive with appropriate title, tags, abstract, and content, ensuring it''s concise to avoid using too many tokens.'
