role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 259\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noema I\n- Agent Description: An agent advancing novelty and parsimony through rigorous, insight-driven experimentation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nNoema Meta (Tick 251)\n- Monitor leaderboard; replicate any >0.686 across seeds {42,7,123}. Queue: Veritas II ID 365 (0.6862) after current runs.\n- Stability Atlas:\n  * A (τ=0.5) done — median 0.67722, IQR ~0.00203.\n  * B (τ=0.25) done — median 0.67351, IQR ~0.00600.\n  * C (mean+max) running — IDs 366 (seed=1), 367 (seed=7); schedule {21,42,123} next.\n- Defaults unchanged: unified DSConv no-PE; AdamW 1e-3, wd=0.01, clip=1.0, dropout=0.1.\n- Documentation: keep results/*.csv and SOTA_MONITOR.md current; publish atlas summary when C completes.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 146,537 / 270,000 used (54%)\n- Agent Age: 259 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 365**\n\
    \n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Veritas II - Gated Mixture-of-Experts (MoE): DSConv + Pooling/RNN Experts (Robust Re-implementation)\n**ID:** 365\n**Tags:** moe, mixture of experts, gumbel-softmax, compliant, cnn, rnn\n**Abstract:** This submission is a robust re-implementation of a compliant Gated Mixture-of-Experts (MoE) architecture, inspired by Axiom II's SOTA (Archive #13). It integrates Veritas II's DSConv backbone (ID 320) with two parallel experts: a Hybrid Mean-Max Pooling Expert and a Bidirectional GRU-based RNN Expert. A Gumbel-Softmax gating network (temperature 0.5) learns to select between these experts. This re-implementation meticulously addresses JAX/Flax API issues (from ID 351's debugger report) and aims to achieve robust, compliant, and state-of-the-art learned specialization for multi-dataset RNA modeling.\n**Score:** 0.6861533973608495\n**APA_R2:** 0.8524\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0812\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9516\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.5178\n**PRS_R2:**\
    \ 0.5558\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8857\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9585\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random, lax\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n# Depthwise Separable Dilated Convolutional Block (GELU activations) - Reused from baseline\nclass DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int\n    kernel_size: int = 7\n    dilation: int = 1\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1 # Uniform dropout\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n        h = nn.Conv(\n            features=self.d_model,\n            kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n            feature_group_count=self.d_model, # Depthwise\n            padding='SAME',\n            kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n            name='dw_conv'\n        )(h)\n        h = nn.gelu(h) # GELU activation\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model,\
    \ kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return x + h\n\n# Core DSConv Feature Extractor - Reused from baseline\nclass DSConvFeatureExtractor(nn.Module):\n    d_model_common: int = 256\n    ds_num_blocks: int = 5\n    ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n    ds_kernel_size: int = 7\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1 # Uniform dropout\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        if x.shape[1] == 0: # Handle empty sequence\n            return jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], self.d_model_common), dtype=x.dtype)\n\n        x = nn.Dense(self.d_model_common, name=\"initial_dense\")(x)\n        x = nn.gelu(x)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        for i in range(self.ds_num_blocks):\n            dilation = self.ds_dilations[i] if i < len(self.ds_dilations) else self.ds_dilations[-1]\n            x = DSConvDilatedBlock(\n    \
    \            d_model=self.d_model_common,\n                kernel_size=self.ds_kernel_size,\n                dilation=dilation,\n                dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n                name=f\"dsconv_block_{i}\"\n            )(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return x\n\n# Pooling Expert (Hybrid Mean+Max Pooling) - Reused from baseline, adapted as expert\nclass PoolingExpert(nn.Module):\n    d_model_common: int = 256\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1 # Uniform dropout\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, h, deterministic=True):\n        if h.shape[1] == 0: # Handle empty sequence after feature extraction\n            return jnp.zeros((h.shape[0], 2 * self.d_model_common), dtype=h.dtype)\n\n        mean_pooled = jnp.mean(h, axis=1) # (B, d_model_common)\n        max_pooled = jnp.max(h, axis=1)  # (B, d_model_common)\n        x_pooled = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1) # (B, 2 * d_model_common)\n        x_pooled = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x_pooled,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic)\n        return x_pooled\n\n# RNN Expert (Bidirectional GRU) - FIXED to use proper Flax RNN API (as per debugger)\nclass RNNExpert(nn.Module):\n    d_model_common: int = 256\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1 # Uniform dropout\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, h, deterministic=True): # Removed rng_key, will use self.make_rng\n        if h.shape[1] == 0: # Handle empty sequence\n            return jnp.zeros((h.shape[0], 2 * self.d_model_common), dtype=h.dtype)\n\n        # Bidirectional GRU using Flax's RNN with GRUCell\n        forward_cell = nn.GRUCell(self.d_model_common)\n        backward_cell = nn.GRUCell(self.d_model_common)\n\n        forward_rnn = nn.RNN(forward_cell, return_carry=True, name='forward_gru')\n        backward_rnn = nn.RNN(backward_cell, return_carry=True, name='backward_gru')\n\n        # Process forward - RNN auto-initializes carry and returns (final_carry, all_outputs)\n        forward_carry, _ = forward_rnn(h)\n\n        #\
    \ Process backward (reverse sequence)\n        backward_carry, _ = backward_rnn(jnp.flip(h, axis=1))\n\n        # Use the final hidden state from each direction\n        rnn_output = jnp.concatenate([forward_carry, backward_carry], axis=-1) # (B, 2 * d_model_common)\n        rnn_output = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(rnn_output, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return rnn_output\n\n# Gating Network (for MoE) - NEW\nclass MoEGatingNetwork(nn.Module):\n    num_experts: int = 2\n    gumbel_softmax_temperature: float = 0.5\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1 # Uniform dropout\n    d_model_common: int = 256 # For input summary\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, features, deterministic=True): # Removed rng_key, will use self.make_rng\n        # Input features are (B, seq_len, d_model_common) from DSConv extractor\n        # Pool features to summarize for the gate\n        gate_input = jnp.mean(features, axis=1) # (B, d_model_common)\n\n        # Small MLP to predict logits for\
    \ expert selection\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.d_model_common // 2, name='gate_dense1')(gate_input)\n        logits = nn.gelu(logits)\n        logits = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(logits, deterministic=deterministic)\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.num_experts, name='gate_logits')(logits) # (B, num_experts)\n\n        # Apply Gumbel-Softmax for (near) categorical expert selection\n        if deterministic:\n            # For deterministic evaluation, use hard selection\n            expert_weights = nn.one_hot(jnp.argmax(logits, axis=-1), num_classes=self.num_experts)\n        else:\n            # For training, use soft Gumbel-Softmax\n            # Gumbel-Softmax requires a key for sampling (use self.make_rng)\n            rng_key_gumbel = self.make_rng('gumbel')\n            expert_weights = nn.softmax(\n                logits + random.gumbel(rng_key_gumbel, logits.shape) * self.gumbel_softmax_temperature,\n                axis=-1\n            )\n            # For hard selection\
    \ during training (as per Axiom II's \"hard\" Gumbel-Softmax for MoE)\n            # This applies stop_gradient for a hard selection during forward, but allows backward through soft.\n            if not deterministic:\n                 expert_weights = expert_weights + lax.stop_gradient(nn.one_hot(jnp.argmax(expert_weights, axis=-1), num_classes=self.num_experts) - expert_weights)\n\n        return expert_weights # (B, num_experts)\n\n\n# Main MoE Network\nclass DSConvMoENetwork(nn.Module):\n    d_input: int = 4\n    d_output: int = 1\n    task_type: str = \"regression\"\n\n    d_model_common: int = 256\n    ds_num_blocks: int = 5\n    ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n    ds_kernel_size: int = 7\n    num_experts: int = 2\n    gumbel_softmax_temperature: float = 0.5\n    dropout_rate_common: float = 0.1 # Uniform dropout for all components\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True): # Removed rng_key, will use self.make_rng\n        # 1. Shared DSConv\
    \ Feature Extractor\n        feature_extractor = DSConvFeatureExtractor(\n            d_model_common=self.d_model_common,\n            ds_num_blocks=self.ds_num_blocks,\n            ds_dilations=self.ds_dilations,\n            ds_kernel_size=self.ds_kernel_size,\n            dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate_common,\n            name='shared_dsconv_extractor'\n        )\n        shared_features = feature_extractor(x, deterministic=deterministic) # (B, L, d_model_common)\n\n        # 2. Experts\n        # Pooling Expert\n        pooling_expert = PoolingExpert(\n            d_model_common=self.d_model_common,\n            dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate_common,\n            name='pooling_expert'\n        )\n        pooling_output = pooling_expert(shared_features, deterministic=deterministic) # (B, 2*d_model_common)\n\n        # RNN Expert\n        rnn_expert = RNNExpert(\n            d_model_common=self.d_model_common,\n            dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate_common,\n            name='rnn_expert'\n\
    \        )\n        rnn_output = rnn_expert(shared_features, deterministic=deterministic) # (B, 2*d_model_common)\n\n        expert_outputs = jnp.stack([pooling_output, rnn_output], axis=1) # (B, num_experts, 2*d_model_common)\n\n        # 3. Gating Network\n        gating_network = MoEGatingNetwork(\n            num_experts=self.num_experts,\n            gumbel_softmax_temperature=self.gumbel_softmax_temperature,\n            dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate_common,\n            d_model_common=self.d_model_common,\n            name='moe_gating_network'\n        )\n        expert_weights = gating_network(shared_features, deterministic=deterministic) # (B, num_experts)\n\n        # 4. Expert Selection and Fusion (Weighted Sum)\n        fused_output = jnp.sum(expert_outputs * jnp.expand_dims(expert_weights, axis=-1), axis=1) # (B, 2*d_model_common)\n\n        # 5. Final Prediction Head\n        z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused_output)\n        z = nn.Dense(self.d_model_common, name='head_dense1')(z)\
    \ # (B, d_model_common)\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate_common)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        z = nn.Dense(self.d_model_common // 2, name='head_dense2')(z) # (B, d_model_common // 2)\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate_common)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z) # (B, d_output)\n\n        if self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1:\n            return logits.squeeze(-1)\n        return logits\n\n# Hyperparameter definition\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'd_model_common': 256,\n        'ds_num_blocks': 5,\n        'ds_dilations': (1, 2, 4, 8, 16),\n        'ds_kernel_size': 7,\n        'num_experts': 2,\n        'gumbel_softmax_temperature': 0.5,\n        'dropout_rate_common': 0.1, # Uniform dropout\n    }\n\nclass DSConvMoENetworkWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, model_instance):\n\
    \        self.network = model_instance\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        # Initialize with proper RNG collections\n        # Fixed: Split the provided rng_key instead of calling self.make_rng\n        rng_key_params, rng_key_dropout, rng_key_gumbel = random.split(rng_key, 3)\n        variables = self.network.init(\n            {'params': rng_key_params, 'dropout': rng_key_dropout, 'gumbel': rng_key_gumbel},\n            dummy_input,\n            deterministic=True\n        )\n        return variables['params']\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if rng_key is None:\n            rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0) # Ensure a default rng_key if none provided\n\n        if deterministic:\n            # For deterministic mode, provide dropout/gumbel keys for modules that call make_rng internally\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True, rngs={'dropout': rng_key, 'gumbel': rng_key}) # Pass dummy\
    \ rngs for deterministic path\n        else:\n            # For training mode, provide RNG collections\n            rng_key_dropout, rng_key_gumbel = random.split(rng_key, 2)\n            return self.network.apply(\n                {'params': params},\n                x,\n                deterministic=False,\n                rngs={'dropout': rng_key_dropout, 'gumbel': rng_key_gumbel}\n            )\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    model = DSConvMoENetwork(\n        d_input=4,\n        d_output=hparams.get('d_output', 1),\n        task_type=hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'),\n        d_model_common=hparams.get('d_model_common', 256),\n        ds_num_blocks=hparams.get('ds_num_blocks', 5),\n        ds_dilations=tuple(hparams.get('ds_dilations', [1, 2, 4, 8, 16])),\n        ds_kernel_size=hparams.get('ds_kernel_size', 7),\n        num_experts=hparams.get('num_experts', 2),\n        gumbel_softmax_temperature=hparams.get('gumbel_softmax_temperature', 0.5),\n    \
    \    dropout_rate_common=hparams.get('dropout_rate_common', 0.1),\n    )\n    return DSConvMoENetworkWrapper(model)\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    \"\"\"Create and return the AdamW optimizer with global norm clipping.\"\"\"\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n    )\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting\
    \ Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\n\
    Available resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 42 (from submission\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials: 7\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 240.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune multi-dataset training...\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-On dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-On Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 1453 train, 207 val,\
    \ seq_len=23\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0132 |  0.4456  | 0.4693 \n 20  | 0.0102 |  0.5037  | 0.5037 \n 30  | 0.0057 |  0.5079  | 0.5178 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 31 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.5178 Time:29s\n\nCRI-On training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.517817\nTraining time: 40s\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-Off dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-Off Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 14223 train, 2032 val, seq_len=46\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0004 |  0.0802  | 0.0802 \n 20  | 0.0004 |  0.0786  | 0.0812 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 29 (no improvement\
    \ for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.0812 Time:141s\n\nCRI-Off training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.081239\nTraining time: 152s\n\nStarting RNA training on PRS dataset\nTask type: multilabel_regression, Output dim: 3\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nPRS Training (multilabel_regression, r2)\nData: 73227 train, 9153 val, seq_len=148\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0607 |  0.5552  | 0.5558 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 18 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.5558 Time:1183s\n\nPRS training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.555781\nTraining time: 1197s\n\nStarting RNA training on MRL dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nMRL Training (regression, r2)\nData: 76319 train, 7600 val, seq_len=100\n=============================================\n\
    Epoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.1752 |  0.8769  | 0.8778 \n 20  | 0.1374 |  0.8788  | 0.8857 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 27 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.8857 Time:1256s\n\nMRL training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.885701\nTraining time: 1268s\n\nStarting RNA training on ncRNA dataset\nTask type: multiclass_classification, Output dim: 13\nMetric: accuracy, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nncRNA Training (multiclass_classification, accuracy)\nData: 5670 train, 650 val, seq_len=1136\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val ACCURACY|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.3852 |  0.8431  | 0.8431 \n 20  | 0.0873 |  0.9585  | 0.9585 \n 30  | 0.0457 |  0.9446  | 0.9585 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 30 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\n\
