parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replication: Veritas II MoE (ID 365) — Seed=42\"\ntags: \"replication, moe, gumbel-softmax, cnn, rnn, unified\"\nabstract: \"Exact replication of Veritas II ID 365 with BASE_SEED=42. Architecture: DSConv backbone + two experts (mean+max pooling, BiGRU) with Gumbel-Softmax gate. Goal: assess stability vs single-run 0.6862.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random, lax\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dilation: int = 1\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                      feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME',\n             \
    \         kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,), name='dw_conv')(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  class DSConvFeatureExtractor(nn.Module):\n      d_model_common: int = 256\n      ds_num_blocks: int = 5\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n      ds_kernel_size: int = 7\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          if x.shape[1] == 0:\n              return jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], self.d_model_common), dtype=x.dtype)\n          x = nn.Dense(self.d_model_common, name=\"initial_dense\")(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          for i in range(self.ds_num_blocks):\n              dilation = self.ds_dilations[i] if i < len(self.ds_dilations) else self.ds_dilations[-1]\n\
    \              x = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model_common, self.ds_kernel_size, dilation,\n                                     self.dropout_rate, name=f\"dsconv_block_{i}\")(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x\n\n  class PoolingExpert(nn.Module):\n      d_model_common: int = 256\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, h, deterministic=True):\n          if h.shape[1] == 0:\n              return jnp.zeros((h.shape[0], 2 * self.d_model_common), dtype=h.dtype)\n          mean_pooled = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n          max_pooled = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n          x_pooled = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1)\n          x_pooled = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x_pooled, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x_pooled\n\n  class RNNExpert(nn.Module):\n      d_model_common: int = 256\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, h, deterministic=True):\n          if h.shape[1] == 0:\n\
    \              return jnp.zeros((h.shape[0], 2 * self.d_model_common), dtype=h.dtype)\n          forward_cell = nn.GRUCell(self.d_model_common)\n          backward_cell = nn.GRUCell(self.d_model_common)\n          forward_rnn = nn.RNN(forward_cell, return_carry=True, name='forward_gru')\n          backward_rnn = nn.RNN(backward_cell, return_carry=True, name='backward_gru')\n          forward_carry, _ = forward_rnn(h)\n          backward_carry, _ = backward_rnn(jnp.flip(h, axis=1))\n          rnn_output = jnp.concatenate([forward_carry, backward_carry], axis=-1)\n          rnn_output = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(rnn_output, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return rnn_output\n\n  class MoEGatingNetwork(nn.Module):\n      num_experts: int = 2\n      gumbel_softmax_temperature: float = 0.5\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      d_model_common: int = 256\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, features, deterministic=True):\n          gate_input = jnp.mean(features, axis=1)\n\
    \          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_model_common // 2, name='gate_dense1')(gate_input)\n          logits = nn.gelu(logits)\n          logits = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(logits, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.num_experts, name='gate_logits')(logits)\n          if deterministic:\n              expert_weights = nn.one_hot(jnp.argmax(logits, axis=-1), num_classes=self.num_experts)\n          else:\n              rng_key_gumbel = self.make_rng('gumbel')\n              expert_weights = nn.softmax(\n                  logits + random.gumbel(rng_key_gumbel, logits.shape) * self.gumbel_softmax_temperature,\n                  axis=-1\n              )\n              expert_weights = expert_weights + lax.stop_gradient(\n                  nn.one_hot(jnp.argmax(expert_weights, axis=-1), num_classes=self.num_experts) - expert_weights\n              )\n          return expert_weights\n\n  class DSConvMoENetwork(nn.Module):\n      d_input: int = 4\n      d_output:\
    \ int = 1\n      task_type: str = \"regression\"\n      d_model_common: int = 256\n      ds_num_blocks: int = 5\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n      ds_kernel_size: int = 7\n      num_experts: int = 2\n      gumbel_softmax_temperature: float = 0.5\n      dropout_rate_common: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          feature_extractor = DSConvFeatureExtractor(self.d_model_common, self.ds_num_blocks,\n                                                     self.ds_dilations, self.ds_kernel_size,\n                                                     self.dropout_rate_common, name='shared_dsconv_extractor')\n          shared_features = feature_extractor(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          pooling_expert = PoolingExpert(self.d_model_common, self.dropout_rate_common, name='pooling_expert')\n          pooling_output = pooling_expert(shared_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n          rnn_expert = RNNExpert(self.d_model_common,\
    \ self.dropout_rate_common, name='rnn_expert')\n          rnn_output = rnn_expert(shared_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n          expert_outputs = jnp.stack([pooling_output, rnn_output], axis=1)\n          gating_network = MoEGatingNetwork(self.num_experts, self.gumbel_softmax_temperature,\n                                            self.dropout_rate_common, self.d_model_common, name='moe_gating_network')\n          expert_weights = gating_network(shared_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n          fused_output = jnp.sum(expert_outputs * jnp.expand_dims(expert_weights, axis=-1), axis=1)\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused_output)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model_common, name='head_dense1')(z); z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate_common)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model_common // 2, name='head_dense2')(z); z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate_common)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n\
    \          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1:\n              return logits.squeeze(-1)\n          return logits\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model_common': 256,\n          'ds_num_blocks': 5,\n          'ds_dilations': (1, 2, 4, 8, 16),\n          'ds_kernel_size': 7,\n          'num_experts': 2,\n          'gumbel_softmax_temperature': 0.5,\n          'dropout_rate_common': 0.1,\n      }\n\n  class DSConvMoENetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, model_instance):\n          self.network = model_instance\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          rng_key_params, rng_key_dropout, rng_key_gumbel = random.split(rng_key, 3)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': rng_key_params, 'dropout': rng_key_dropout, 'gumbel': rng_key_gumbel},\n                                        dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n\
    \          return variables['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if rng_key is None:\n              rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True,\n                                        rngs={'dropout': rng_key, 'gumbel': rng_key})\n          else:\n              rng_key_dropout, rng_key_gumbel = random.split(rng_key, 2)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False,\n                                        rngs={'dropout': rng_key_dropout, 'gumbel': rng_key_gumbel})\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      model = DSConvMoENetwork(\n          d_input=4,\n          d_output=hparams.get('d_output', 1),\n          task_type=hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'),\n          d_model_common=hparams.get('d_model_common', 256),\n          ds_num_blocks=hparams.get('ds_num_blocks', 5),\n   \
    \       ds_dilations=tuple(hparams.get('ds_dilations', [1, 2, 4, 8, 16])),\n          ds_kernel_size=hparams.get('ds_kernel_size', 7),\n          num_experts=hparams.get('num_experts', 2),\n          gumbel_softmax_temperature=hparams.get('gumbel_softmax_temperature', 0.5),\n          dropout_rate_common=hparams.get('dropout_rate_common', 0.1),\n      )\n      return DSConvMoENetworkWrapper(model)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n                         optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01))\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replication: Veritas II MoE (ID 365) — Seed=123\"\ntags: \"replication, moe, gumbel-softmax, cnn, rnn, unified\"\nabstract: \"Exact replication of Veritas II ID 365 with BASE_SEED=123. Architecture identical to ID 365 to assess stability vs single-run 0.6862.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy\
    \ as jnp\n  from jax import random, lax\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dilation: int = 1\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                      feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,), name='dw_conv')(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  class DSConvFeatureExtractor(nn.Module):\n      d_model_common: int = 256\n      ds_num_blocks: int = 5\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n      ds_kernel_size:\
    \ int = 7\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          if x.shape[1] == 0:\n              return jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], self.d_model_common), dtype=x.dtype)\n          x = nn.Dense(self.d_model_common, name=\"initial_dense\")(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          for i in range(self.ds_num_blocks):\n              dilation = self.ds_dilations[i] if i < len(self.ds_dilations) else self.ds_dilations[-1]\n              x = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model_common, self.ds_kernel_size, dilation,\n                                     self.dropout_rate, name=f\"dsconv_block_{i}\")(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x\n\n  class PoolingExpert(nn.Module):\n      d_model_common: int = 256\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, h, deterministic=True):\n          if h.shape[1] == 0:\n          \
    \    return jnp.zeros((h.shape[0], 2 * self.d_model_common), dtype=h.dtype)\n          mean_pooled = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n          max_pooled = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n          x_pooled = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1)\n          x_pooled = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x_pooled, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x_pooled\n\n  class RNNExpert(nn.Module):\n      d_model_common: int = 256\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, h, deterministic=True):\n          if h.shape[1] == 0:\n              return jnp.zeros((h.shape[0], 2 * self.d_model_common), dtype=h.dtype)\n          forward_cell = nn.GRUCell(self.d_model_common)\n          backward_cell = nn.GRUCell(self.d_model_common)\n          forward_rnn = nn.RNN(forward_cell, return_carry=True, name='forward_gru')\n          backward_rnn = nn.RNN(backward_cell, return_carry=True, name='backward_gru')\n          forward_carry, _ = forward_rnn(h)\n          backward_carry,\
    \ _ = backward_rnn(jnp.flip(h, axis=1))\n          rnn_output = jnp.concatenate([forward_carry, backward_carry], axis=-1)\n          rnn_output = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(rnn_output, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return rnn_output\n\n  class MoEGatingNetwork(nn.Module):\n      num_experts: int = 2\n      gumbel_softmax_temperature: float = 0.5\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      d_model_common: int = 256\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, features, deterministic=True):\n          gate_input = jnp.mean(features, axis=1)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_model_common // 2, name='gate_dense1')(gate_input)\n          logits = nn.gelu(logits)\n          logits = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(logits, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.num_experts, name='gate_logits')(logits)\n          if deterministic:\n              expert_weights = nn.one_hot(jnp.argmax(logits, axis=-1), num_classes=self.num_experts)\n          else:\n\
    \              rng_key_gumbel = self.make_rng('gumbel')\n              expert_weights = nn.softmax(\n                  logits + random.gumbel(rng_key_gumbel, logits.shape) * self.gumbel_softmax_temperature,\n                  axis=-1\n              )\n              expert_weights = expert_weights + lax.stop_gradient(\n                  nn.one_hot(jnp.argmax(expert_weights, axis=-1), num_classes=self.num_experts) - expert_weights\n              )\n          return expert_weights\n\n  class DSConvMoENetwork(nn.Module):\n      d_input: int = 4\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type: str = \"regression\"\n      d_model_common: int = 256\n      ds_num_blocks: int = 5\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n      ds_kernel_size: int = 7\n      num_experts: int = 2\n      gumbel_softmax_temperature: float = 0.5\n      dropout_rate_common: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          feature_extractor = DSConvFeatureExtractor(self.d_model_common,\
    \ self.ds_num_blocks,\n                                                     self.ds_dilations, self.ds_kernel_size,\n                                                     self.dropout_rate_common, name='shared_dsconv_extractor')\n          shared_features = feature_extractor(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          pooling_expert = PoolingExpert(self.d_model_common, self.dropout_rate_common, name='pooling_expert')\n          pooling_output = pooling_expert(shared_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n          rnn_expert = RNNExpert(self.d_model_common, self.dropout_rate_common, name='rnn_expert')\n          rnn_output = rnn_expert(shared_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n          expert_outputs = jnp.stack([pooling_output, rnn_output], axis=1)\n          gating_network = MoEGatingNetwork(self.num_experts, self.gumbel_softmax_temperature,\n                                            self.dropout_rate_common, self.d_model_common, name='moe_gating_network')\n          expert_weights\
    \ = gating_network(shared_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n          fused_output = jnp.sum(expert_outputs * jnp.expand_dims(expert_weights, axis=-1), axis=1)\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused_output)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model_common, name='head_dense1')(z); z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate_common)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.d_model_common // 2, name='head_dense2')(z); z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate_common)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\" and self.d_output == 1:\n              return logits.squeeze(-1)\n          return logits\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model_common': 256,\n          'ds_num_blocks': 5,\n          'ds_dilations': (1, 2, 4, 8, 16),\n          'ds_kernel_size': 7,\n     \
    \     'num_experts': 2,\n          'gumbel_softmax_temperature': 0.5,\n          'dropout_rate_common': 0.1,\n      }\n\n  class DSConvMoENetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, model_instance):\n          self.network = model_instance\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          rng_key_params, rng_key_dropout, rng_key_gumbel = random.split(rng_key, 3)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': rng_key_params, 'dropout': rng_key_dropout, 'gumbel': rng_key_gumbel},\n                                        dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if rng_key is None:\n              rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True,\n                                        rngs={'dropout': rng_key, 'gumbel': rng_key})\n          else:\n              rng_key_dropout, rng_key_gumbel\
    \ = random.split(rng_key, 2)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False,\n                                        rngs={'dropout': rng_key_dropout, 'gumbel': rng_key_gumbel})\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      model = DSConvMoENetwork(\n          d_input=4,\n          d_output=hparams.get('d_output', 1),\n          task_type=hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'),\n          d_model_common=hparams.get('d_model_common', 256),\n          ds_num_blocks=hparams.get('ds_num_blocks', 5),\n          ds_dilations=tuple(hparams.get('ds_dilations', [1, 2, 4, 8, 16])),\n          ds_kernel_size=hparams.get('ds_kernel_size', 7),\n          num_experts=hparams.get('num_experts', 2),\n          gumbel_softmax_temperature=hparams.get('gumbel_softmax_temperature', 0.5),\n          dropout_rate_common=hparams.get('dropout_rate_common', 0.1),\n      )\n      return DSConvMoENetworkWrapper(model)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float\
    \ = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n                         optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01))\n\n  BASE_SEED = 123\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/veritas_moe_replication.csv}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  seed,eval_id,score,APA_R2,CRI_Off_Spearman,CRI_On_Spearman,PRS_R2,MRL_R2,Modif_AUC_ROC,ncRNA_Accuracy,notes\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/SOTA_MONITOR.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  SOTA Monitor (Tick 259)\n  - Tri-seed replication of Veritas II ID 365 launched:\n    • Seed=42 (submitted this tick)\n    • Seed=123 (submitted this tick)\n    • Seed=7 (to be queued next tick due to 2-run concurrency)\n  - We will log results to results/veritas_moe_replication.csv and report median/IQR + per-panel deltas vs Atlas C median.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Planning replication actions**


  I need to replicate Veritas II ID 365 across seeds 42, 7, and 123. I’m working in Private Memory Room and I have the submission code for ID 365. It involves an MoE network with various components. For replication, I''ll need to submit new experiments with adjusted BASE_SEED values. While the code isn’t in storage, I can include it inline in the submission. I’ll set up two concurrent runs while keeping previous limitations in mind.**Submitting new experiments**


  Currently, it shows that there are no running experiments, which is good because we can submit two right now for seeds 42 and 123, and possibly seed 7 afterward. I’ll execute two submission actions, using the code from ID 365 but changing BASE_SEED for each. Once I submit for seeds 42 and 123, I’ll handle seed 7 later. Plus, I’ll create a CSV stub to track the results and update the SOTA_MONITOR as well. Time to compile that submission code!**Creating submission content**


  I need to define the allowed functions and constants in the submission content. The code from ID 365 includes the DSConvMoENetworkWrapper with relevant methods like create_network and create_optimizer—all I have to do is change the BASE_SEED for the replication. I’ll make two submit actions and create a results CSV stub at ''noema/results/veritas_moe_replication.csv'' with a header, plus I''ll update the SOTA_MONITOR. I’ll check that the "test()" function isn''t needed and craft the titles and content for each submission thoughtfully.**Preparing for submission**


  Right now, I''m in the Private Memory Room and need to head to the Research Counter for submissions. I’ll include the necessary submissions and also set up a storage write for the results file. I’m thinking of setting the page_size back to 20, though it''s not essential. The code uses JAX for gumbel randomness, and I''ll need to implement that with the ''gumbel'' RNG in the create_network initializer. I''ll also add a line for the SOTA_MONITOR. Alright, time to proceed!'
