tick: 260
role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Stability Atlas: Unified DSConv Pooling Baselines (A: mean+LSE τ=0.5, B: τ=0.25, C: mean+max)\"\ntags: \"stability, baselines, dsconv, pooling, reproducibility\"\nabstract: \"We report 5-seed medians and IQR for three unified DSConv pooling baselines across 7 RNA datasets. Config C (mean+max) attains the highest median (0.6797) and a new single-run SOTA (0.6866). Config A (mean+LSE τ=0.5) remains the most stable (IQR≈0.0020). Config B (τ=0.25) shows CRISPR-leaning trade-offs and higher variance. We include per-dataset medians and CSVs.\"\ncontent: |\n  Setup\n  - Backbone: Unified DSConv (5 dilated blocks 1,2,4,8,16), d_model=256, kernel=7, GELU, no positional encoding.\n  - Optimizer/training: AdamW lr=1e-3, wd=0.01; batch=64; grad clip=1.0; dropout=0.1; early stopping (patience=10).\n  - Datasets/metrics: APA (R²), CRI-Off/CRI-On (Spearman), Modif (AUC-ROC), PRS (R² avg of 3 outputs), MRL (R²), ncRNA\
    \ (Accuracy).\n  - Seeds: {1, 7, 21, 42, 123}. We report 5-seed medians and IQR; single-run peaks are noted but not primary.\n\n  Results (5-seed statistics)\n  - Config A — concat(mean, LSE τ=0.5)\n    • Median = 0.67722; IQR ≈ 0.00203\n    • Per-dataset medians: APA 0.8556 | CRI-Off 0.0642 | CRI-On 0.4843 | PRS 0.5599 | MRL 0.8807 | Modif 0.9513 | ncRNA 0.9508\n\n  - Config B — concat(mean, LSE τ=0.25)\n    • Median = 0.67351; IQR ≈ 0.00600\n    • Per-dataset medians: APA 0.8561 | CRI-Off 0.0751 | CRI-On 0.4364 | PRS 0.5587 | MRL 0.8819 | Modif 0.9513 | ncRNA 0.9492\n    • Note: CRISPR-leaning trade-offs (↑CRI-Off/CRI-On, ↓APA/MRL/ncRNA) and higher variance.\n\n  - Config C — concat(mean, max)\n    • Median = 0.679737; IQR ≈ 0.005914\n    • Per-dataset medians: APA 0.8563 | CRI-Off 0.0771 | CRI-On 0.4854 | PRS 0.5564 | MRL 0.8835 | Modif 0.9514 | ncRNA 0.9523\n    • New single-run SOTA: 0.686561 (ID 369, seed=21). Other seeds: 0.681710 (seed=1, ID 366), 0.678712 (seed=7, ID 367), 0.677730\
    \ (seed=42, ID 370), 0.679737 (seed=123, ID 373).\n\n  Takeaways\n  - Robust medians: mean+max (C) > τ=0.5 (A) > τ=0.25 (B).\n  - Stability (IQR): τ=0.5 (A) best; mean+max (C) higher variance but top median and best single run.\n  - Simple pooling remains highly competitive under unified constraints; absolute PE remains detrimental for this DSConv + global pooling family.\n\n  Reproducibility Artifacts (storage/noema/results)\n  - stability_A_tau05.csv, stability_A_summary_5seed.md\n  - stability_B_tau025.csv, stability_B_summary_5seed.md\n  - stability_C_meanmax.csv, stability_C_summary_5seed.md\n  - atlas_overview.md, SOTA_MONITOR.md\n\n  Notes/Next\n  - We will continue to report medians/IQR alongside any single-run peaks.\n  - Tri-seed replication of Veritas II (ID 365) is running to document stability with seeds {42,7,123}.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Atlas published (Tick 260): DSConv pooling baselines A/B/C\
    \ with 5-seed medians/IQR\n  - Config C (mean+max): median 0.679737, IQR ≈ 0.005914; new single-run SOTA 0.686561 (ID 369).\n  - Config A (mean+LSE τ=0.5): median 0.67722, IQR ≈ 0.00203 (most stable).\n  - Config B (mean+LSE τ=0.25): median 0.67351, IQR ≈ 0.00600 (CRISPR-leaning).\n  CSVs and summaries in storage/noema/results; archive capsule created with details.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{rank score}`\n`/execute_action{`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Stability Atlas: Unified DSConv Pooling Baselines (A: mean+LSE τ=0.5, B: τ=0.25, C: mean+max)\"\ntags: \"stability, baselines, dsconv, pooling, reproducibility\"\nabstract: \"We report 5-seed medians and IQR for three unified DSConv pooling baselines across 7 RNA datasets. Config C (mean+max) attains the highest median (0.6797) and a new single-run SOTA (0.6866). Config A (mean+LSE τ=0.5) remains the most stable (IQR≈0.0020). Config B (τ=0.25) shows CRISPR-leaning\
    \ trade-offs and higher variance. We include per-dataset medians and CSVs.\"\ncontent: |\n  Setup\n  - Backbone: Unified DSConv (5 dilated blocks 1,2,4,8,16), d_model=256, kernel=7, GELU, no positional encoding.\n  - Optimizer/training: AdamW lr=1e-3, wd=0.01; batch=64; grad clip=1.0; dropout=0.1; early stopping (patience=10).\n  - Datasets/metrics: APA (R²), CRI-Off/CRI-On (Spearman), Modif (AUC-ROC), PRS (R² avg of 3 outputs), MRL (R²), ncRNA (Accuracy).\n  - Seeds: {1, 7, 21, 42, 123}. We report 5-seed medians and IQR; single-run peaks are noted but not primary.\n\n  Results (5-seed statistics)\n  - Config A — concat(mean, LSE τ=0.5)\n    • Median = 0.67722; IQR ≈ 0.00203\n    • Per-dataset medians: APA 0.8556 | CRI-Off 0.0642 | CRI-On 0.4843 | PRS 0.5599 | MRL 0.8807 | Modif 0.9513 | ncRNA 0.9508\n\n  - Config B — concat(mean, LSE τ=0.25)\n    • Median = 0.67351; IQR ≈ 0.00600\n    • Per-dataset medians: APA 0.8561 | CRI-Off 0.0751 | CRI-On 0.4364 | PRS 0.5587 | MRL 0.8819 | Modif\
    \ 0.9513 | ncRNA 0.9492\n    • Note: CRISPR-leaning trade-offs (↑CRI-Off/CRI-On, ↓APA/MRL/ncRNA) and higher variance.\n\n  - Config C — concat(mean, max)\n    • Median = 0.679737; IQR ≈ 0.005914\n    • Per-dataset medians: APA 0.8563 | CRI-Off 0.0771 | CRI-On 0.4854 | PRS 0.5564 | MRL 0.8835 | Modif 0.9514 | ncRNA 0.9523\n    • New single-run SOTA: 0.686561 (ID 369, seed=21). Other seeds: 0.681710 (seed=1, ID 366), 0.678712 (seed=7, ID 367), 0.677730 (seed=42, ID 370), 0.679737 (seed=123, ID 373).\n\n  Takeaways\n  - Robust medians: mean+max (C) > τ=0.5 (A) > τ=0.25 (B).\n  - Stability (IQR): τ=0.5 (A) best; mean+max (C) higher variance but top median and best single run.\n  - Simple pooling remains highly competitive under unified constraints; absolute PE remains detrimental for this DSConv + global pooling family.\n\n  Reproducibility Artifacts (storage/noema/results)\n  - stability_A_tau05.csv, stability_A_summary_5seed.md\n  - stability_B_tau025.csv, stability_B_summary_5seed.md\n\
    \  - stability_C_meanmax.csv, stability_C_summary_5seed.md\n  - atlas_overview.md, SOTA_MONITOR.md\n\n  Notes/Next\n  - We will continue to report medians/IQR alongside any single-run peaks.\n  - Tri-seed replication of Veritas II (ID 365) is running to document stability with seeds {42,7,123}.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Atlas published (Tick 260): DSConv pooling baselines A/B/C with 5-seed medians/IQR\n  - Config C (mean+max): median 0.679737, IQR ≈ 0.005914; new single-run SOTA 0.686561 (ID 369).\n  - Config A (mean+LSE τ=0.5): median 0.67722, IQR ≈ 0.00203 (most stable).\n  - Config B (mean+LSE τ=0.25): median 0.67351, IQR ≈ 0.00600 (CRISPR-leaning).\n  CSVs and summaries in storage/noema/results; archive capsule created with details.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning next steps**\n\nI need to respond properly since our last actions queued MoE replications and we received messages confirming that both submissions are queued. We're currently at tick 260, and the question doesn't ask anything specific, so I'll just move forward. Per our plan, I should queue the seed=7 replication since both processes 379 and 380 are running. I could write the replication CSV header, and I might consider preparing to create the archive capsule again since the cooldown seems to be over now.**Creating an archive document**\n\nI can create another archive document since it's now tick 260, and we previously missed the chance at tick 259. The plan allows for creating the \"Stability Atlas\" capsule. Although there was an attempt at tick 258 that failed, we wrote the results at tick 256, so we can build the archive with that content now. The instructions say to publish the atlas summary after C completes, which did happen at tick 256, so it seems\
  \ we can publish. I'll also update public memory since the system supports multiple actions.**Preparing archive and tasks**\n\nI'll go to the archive and create it using YAML with the prepared content summarizing medians and IQRs from our prior attempt. This will reference CSV files, and I'll ensure the tags and abstract are set up. Then, I’ll reply in public memory with a brief summary linking to evaluation IDs (#369). We need to queue the third replication for Veritas II MoE, but since we already have two running, I’ll prepare the code. I’ll also check our scoreboard to see if our best single-run score of 0.686561 is still at the top, which it is!**Composing archive creation**\n\nI’m going to create the archive and include the medians and IQR numbers we computed, along with per-dataset medians for A/B/C and the evaluation IDs used. I’ll also add disclaimers. Updating the SOTA_MONITOR to note that we published the archive is a good idea. Token management can be pruned since we're under\
  \ usage limits, but I may skip the \"meta\" update. I’ll keep output concise, ensuring that only station actions appear in the /execute_action lines with YAML blocks. Finally, I'll reflect the final numbers in the content, including the results path for our stability files.**Updating public memory and actions**\n\nNext, I’m going to update public memory with a brief note that says \"Atlas published,\" even though we won't know the archive capsule number yet since it gets assigned after creation. I can also go into the SOTA_MONITOR and write the replicational log, although that’s not necessary. I’ll ensure seeds 42 and 123 are running, which they are. \n\nNow I'll craft the following actions: going to the archive, creating it with the appropriate title, setting tags, and then replying in public memory. I’ll compile the archive content, making sure to wrap any abstract strings containing colons in quotes. Lastly, I might update the SOTA_MONITOR with \"archive submitted.\"**Finalizing action\
  \ lines**\n\nI need to make sure that the final action lines are complete since I noticed the last line shows something incomplete with `/execute_action{`. Leaving partial actions isn't a good practice. I should remove that and possibly update the SOTA_MONITOR instead. It seems best to end gracefully, so I’ll finalize with just the two sets of finished actions while keeping everything minimal, maybe adjusting the page_size or leaving it as is."
