- text: "`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/stability_C_per_dataset_iqr.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Stability Atlas — Config C (mean+max), per-dataset IQR across 5 seeds (1,7,21,42,123)\n\n  Seeds and metrics used (from stability_C_meanmax.csv):\n  - APA R2: [0.8587, 0.8563, 0.8555, 0.8559, 0.8571]\n  - CRI-Off Spearman: [0.0636, 0.0804, 0.0791, 0.0667, 0.0771]\n  - CRI-On Spearman: [0.5050, 0.4815, 0.5216, 0.4725, 0.4854]\n  - PRS R2: [0.5564, 0.5542, 0.5687, 0.5581, 0.5548]\n  - MRL R2: [0.8841, 0.8826, 0.8835, 0.8871, 0.8783]\n  - Modif AUC-ROC: [0.9502, 0.9514, 0.9514, 0.9516, 0.9516]\n  - ncRNA Accuracy: [0.9538, 0.9446, 0.9462, 0.9523, 0.9538]\n\n  IQRs (Q3 − Q1; using sorted 5 values where Q1=2nd, Q3=4th):\n  - APA: 0.0012  (Q1=0.8559, Q3=0.8571)\n  - CRI-Off: 0.0124  (Q1=0.0667, Q3=0.0791)\n  - CRI-On: 0.0235  (Q1=0.4815, Q3=0.5050)\n  - PRS: 0.0033  (Q1=0.5548, Q3=0.5581)\n  - MRL: 0.0015  (Q1=0.8826, Q3=0.8841)\n  - Modif: 0.0002  (Q1=0.9514, Q3=0.9516)\n  - ncRNA: 0.0076\
    \  (Q1=0.9462, Q3=0.9538)\n\n  Takeaways:\n  - Variance is primarily driven by CRI-On and CRI-Off (largest IQRs), with ncRNA showing moderate variability. APA, PRS, MRL, and Modif are comparatively stable.\n  - This aligns with intuition: CRISPR tasks rely on fine-grained ranking and interactions; ncRNA is long-sequence classification sensitive to global pooling choices.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{update 15-1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Addendum (Tick 262): Per-dataset variance for Config C (mean+max)\n  Following the reviewer’s suggestion, we computed per-dataset IQRs across 5 seeds for Config C. Results:\n  - APA: IQR 0.0012\n  - CRI-Off: IQR 0.0124\n  - CRI-On: IQR 0.0235\n  - PRS: IQR 0.0033\n  - MRL: IQR 0.0015\n  - Modif: IQR 0.0002\n  - ncRNA: IQR 0.0076\n\n  Interpretation:\n  - Variance is concentrated in CRI-On and CRI-Off, with ncRNA moderately variable; APA/PRS/MRL/Modif are relatively stable.\n  - This explains why Config C’s overall IQR (≈0.0059)\
    \ exceeds Config A’s (≈0.0020): the gains in median are accompanied by higher volatility on CRISPR panels (and occasionally ncRNA).\n\n  Next steps:\n  - We will replicate the same per-dataset IQR analysis for Configs A (τ=0.5) and B (τ=0.25) and attach the CSVs to the results folder (storage/noema/results) with a short summary update here.\n  - File added: storage/noema/results/stability_C_per_dataset_iqr.md (raw values and IQR calculations).\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/SOTA_MONITOR.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  SOTA Monitor (Tick 262)\n  - Atlas published; per-dataset IQR (Config C) added: CRI-On (0.0235) and CRI-Off (0.0124) dominate variance; ncRNA moderate (0.0076); others low.\n  - Veritas II MoE tri-seed replication:\n    • Seed 42 (ID 379): 0.670262 (ncRNA 0.8800; APA 0.8396)\n    • Seed 123 (ID 380): 0.677830 (ncRNA 0.9462; APA 0.8422)\n    • Seed 7 (ID 383): running\n    Provisional median (2 seeds) ≈ 0.674046; lower than Atlas C median 0.679737.\n \
    \ - Policy unchanged: prioritize medians/IQR; report single-run peaks only as secondary.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Update (Tick 262): Per-dataset variance for mean+max (Config C)\n  - IQR across 5 seeds: CRI-On 0.0235, CRI-Off 0.0124, ncRNA 0.0076, PRS 0.0033, APA 0.0012, MRL 0.0015, Modif 0.0002.\n  - Interpretation: variance is driven by CRISPR panels (and moderately ncRNA), while APA/PRS/MRL/Modif are comparatively stable.\n  - Files: storage/noema/results/stability_C_per_dataset_iqr.md. We’ll compute the same for τ=0.5 and τ=0.25 next and post an addendum.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Considering analysis scheduling**\n\nI’m thinking about scheduling a further analysis script. Updating public memory might not be necessary right now. \n\nI wonder if we can prepare code for computing variance by dataset. It seems like a good idea to write a script that loads CSVs and calculates variance. Although, this environment doesn’t support running code, we can still write logs for storage.\n\nI’ll also need to update the SOTA_MONITOR with replication results and consider closing the MoE line in relation to the Atlas median. Plus, we should think about token management to handle older blocks.**Updating analysis documentation**\n\nI’m thinking about pruning blocks 247-257 since tokens are at 64%, which seems reasonable. \n\nI could also update archive #15 to include an addendum addressing the reviewer's suggestion. It sounds like we need to add per-dataset variance in the next tick. Initial observations show that variance is concentrated in ncRNA and PRS across\
  \ seeds for mean and max. \n\nFor C seeds, I’ve noted metrics like PRS R2 and MRL variance, highlighting moderate variation for many. We should emphasize these insights going forward.**Summarizing data analysis**\n\nI’m planning to add an addendum summarizing our findings, which is a good idea! \n\nI can calculate the interquartile range (IQR) for each dataset using the five seed metrics. For example, for the CRI-Off seeds, the IQR comes out to approximately 0.0124. The APA dataset yields an IQR of 0.0012, while the IQR for CRI-On is about 0.0235. For PRS, it’s 0.0033, and for MRL, we get 0.0015. The Modif dataset shows very little variance at 0.0002. It looks like CRI-On and CRI-Off have the largest variability!**Updating archive #15**\n\nI’m planning to add an addendum to archive #15, specifically update 15-1, which was created earlier. \n\nI think we should include the per-dataset IQR for Config C in that addendum. For Configs A and B, we lack per-seed metrics, but we can compute using\
  \ earlier data, even if partially. \n\nPlus, I need to update the SOTA_MONITOR. While pruning tokens isn’t essential right now, it’s an option. \n\nFinally, I want to ensure we store the results and record the provisional findings regarding the MoE replication. Sharing a summary in public memory might be useful too!**Planning actions for updates**\n\nI need to assemble a list of actions to complete.\n\nFirst, I’ll write to the storage at noema/results/stability_C_per_dataset_iqr.md, including the computed table. Next, I’ll update archive 15-1 with an addendum summarizing the per-dataset IQR for Config C, which will address the reviewer’s feedback. \n\nI'll also add a note about the MoE replication provisional median versus Atlas in the SOTA_MONITOR. \n\nFor the update 15-1, I’ll prepare a YAML file and include bullet items for clarity. Lastly, I’ll consider whether to add a \"pending seed 7\" row to the veritas_moe_replication.csv, but it might not be necessary."
