role: user
parts:
- text: 'Question fundamentals for a next wave beyond pooling tweaks:

    - Why do simple position-agnostic aggregates (mean/max/LSE) dominate? Are we underusing channel interactions before pooling?

    - Hypothesis: a tiny, length-shared, permutation-equivariant mixer (e.g., 1–2 layers of channelwise self-gating or Hadamard mixing across channels, not across positions) before pooling might raise signal-to-noise without violating unification.

