- text: "Reflection — Tick 4\n\nTheory cross-checks, risks, and preregistration\n\nCommutativity implications\n- Mean branch: mean(Ah) = A·mean(h) for linear A. Any purely linear pre-pool channel mixing is functionally equivalent to a post-pool linear layer on the mean branch. Therefore, gains must come from:\n  - Nonlinearity in the pre-pool mixer (GELU, tanh, sigmoid gates), or\n  - Nonlinear pooling (max/LSE), where pre-pool mixing changes which positions dominate.\n- Max/LSE branch: max(Ah) ≠ A·max(h); LSEτ(Ah) ≠ A·LSEτ(h). Hence, pre-pool mixing can alter the “winner-take-most” structure in ways post-pool cannot.\n\nExpected panel effects\n- CRI-On/Off: Most sensitive to winner selection; pre-pool reweighting should help if it suppresses spurious channels at top positions. Watch for IQR inflation (volatility).\n- ncRNA/MRL: Long-sequence/global effects; historically harmed by added complexity. We need near-identity behavior to preserve robustness; any median drop ≥0.002 is a fail.\n\
    - APA/PRS/Modif: Generally stable; small deltas likely noise unless consistent across seeds.\n\nRisks and mitigations\n- Over-amplification: Gates/mixers could magnify noise channels, raising IQR. Mitigate with identity-centered init (W2=0) and small α (0.25), plus optional short warmup.\n- Redundancy: If residual δ → 0 across seeds, no effect; conclude DSConv+head already saturates channel mixing. Publish negative with diagnostics (energy/attribution unchanged).\n- Capacity confound: Ensure param-matched runs (head 512→192) to isolate structure; include “head=192 without mixer” as a control.\n\nParameter accounting (C=256, pooled_dim=512)\n- Baseline head Dense(512→256): 131,072 weights + 256 bias ≈ 131.3k (+ LN/last layer negligible).\n- Res-ChannelMixer H=64: 256×64 + 64×256 = 32,768 (+ biases ≈ 320). Head shrink 512→192: 98,304 (+ 192 bias) → param-neutral within ~1%.\n- SE-Calib H=64 and Hadamard H=32 similarly kept within the same ~33k budget; pair with head=192.\n\nDiagnostics\
    \ (to collect per run)\n- Early learning curves (first 20 epochs) on CRI-On/Off vs ncRNA to identify divergent dynamics.\n- Channel energy pre/post mixer (mean over length) to verify selective attenuation/amplification.\n- Top-k (pos,channel) contributors under LSE/max before vs after mixer to confirm winner shifts.\n\nPreregistration: experiment table (tri-seed, seeds {42,7,123})\n- Config A (τ=0.5):\n  - Baseline (head=256)\n  - ResMixer + head=256 (additive-small)\n  - ResMixer + head=192 (param-matched) [primary]\n  - SE-Calib α=0.25 + head=192 (param-matched)\n  - Hadamard α=0.25 + head=192 (param-matched)\n- Config C (mean+max): same matrix [primary second]\n- Escalate to Config B (τ=0.25) only if any variant improves medians on A/C with IQR ≤ +0.001 and no ncRNA/MRL regressions.\n\nSuccess bar and stop rules\n- Success: +0.001 to +0.003 median vs baseline on both A and C; IQR change ≤ +0.001; ncRNA/MRL median drop < 0.001.\n- Stop a variant if IQR increases > +0.002 on any config\
