- text: "Reflection — Tick 5\n\nConsolidated plan and preregistration for “pre-pool channel mixers”\n\nCore intuition recap\n- DSConv+no-PE yields per-position multi-scale motif activations across channels. Nonlinear global pooling (max/LSE) determines which positions dominate the summary. A length-shared, channel-only mixer placed just before pooling can reweight channels at every position so that pooling elevates true signal and suppresses distractors. Because pooling is nonlinear, this cannot be replicated by post-pool linear layers.\n- We keep unification and robustness by: no PE, permutation-equivariance over length, identity-centered initialization, and parameter-matched ablations.\n\nMinimal variants (inserted right before pooling; h: (B, L, C=256))\n1) PrePool-Res-ChannelMixer (identity-init residual MLP)\n   - h_ln = LN(h)\n   - δ = Dense(C→H=64) → GELU → Dense(H→C) with final W2=0, b2=0\n   - h’ = h + δ\n   - Pros: strictly length-equivariant; exact identity at init; ~33k params.\n\
    \n2) PrePool-SE-Calib (global gate, identity-centered)\n   - h_ln = LN(h); u = mean_len(h_ln) ∈ R^{B×C}\n   - g = sigmoid(Dense(C→64) → GELU → Dense(64→C) [small init])\n   - h’ = h · (1 + α·(g − 0.5)), α ∈ {0.25}; optional warmup α: 0.1→0.25 over 5 epochs\n   - Pros: tiny, global evidence used; identity-centered to avoid early damage.\n\n3) PrePool-Hadamard-Gate (very small, signed)\n   - u = mean_len(h); w = tanh(Dense(C→32) → Dense(32→C) [small init])\n   - h’ = h · (1 + α·w), α=0.25\n   - Pros: ~16k params; most conservative.\n\nParam matching and fairness\n- Baseline head (pooled_dim=2C=512): LN → Dense(512→256) → GELU → Dropout → Dense(d_out). Dense layer ≈ 131k weights.\n- Mixer budget ≈ 33k params. For “param-matched” runs, shrink head Dense(512→192) (~98.5k) so (head shrink + mixer) ≈ baseline params.\n- Controls per variant:\n  - Additive-small (head=256): isolates structural effect with a small param increase.\n  - Param-matched (head=192): neutralizes capacity confound.\n\
    \  - Head=192 without mixer: control for head shrink alone.\n\nConfigs and execution matrix (tri-seed first; seeds {42, 7, 123})\n- Test on:\n  A) concat(mean, LSE τ=0.5) — stable default\n  C) concat(mean, max) — best median with higher variance\n- For each config A and C:\n  0) Baseline (head=256)\n  1) ResMixer + head=256 (additive-small)\n  2) ResMixer + head=192 (param-matched) [primary]\n  3) SE-Calib α=0.25 + head=192 (param-matched)\n  4) Hadamard α=0.25 + head=192 (param-matched)\n- Only if ≥1 variant improves medians on both A and C with acceptable IQR do we proceed to:\n  B) concat(mean, LSE τ=0.25) — CRISPR-leaning, verify trade-offs\n\nTraining/optimizer (unchanged)\n- AdamW lr=1e-3, wd=0.01; batch=64; grad clip=1.0; dropout=0.1; patience=10; no PE; DSConv 5 blocks (1,2,4,8,16), kernel=7, GELU.\n\nMetrics, diagnostics, and preregistered criteria\n- Report (per config): tri-seed median and IQR; per-dataset median deltas vs baseline (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL,\
    \ ncRNA).\n- Success (for a variant): +0.001 to +0.003 median on both A and C; IQR increase ≤ +0.001; ncRNA and MRL median drops < 0.001.\n- Kill switches: if IQR rises > +0.002 on any config or ncRNA/MRL median drops ≥ 0.002, stop that variant.\n- Diagnostics to store:\n  - Early epoch (≤20) curves for CRI-On/Off and ncRNA (detect divergence/benefit).\n  - Channel energy histograms pre/post mixer (mean over length).\n  - Top-k (position,channel) contributors under max/LSE pre vs post mixer (verify winner shifts toward salient motifs).\n\nWhy this is meaningfully different from prior negatives\n- Placement matters: earlier SE/attention within conv blocks or complex global attentions perturbed feature learning or added invalid priors. Here we apply a tiny, identity-centered, length-equivariant mixer right before pooling—the actual bottleneck—without cross-position assumptions, preserving unification and robustness.\n\nNaming and artifacts (to ensure reproducibility)\n- Submissions:\n\
    \  - A_C_resmix_addsmall_{seed}.py\n  - A_C_resmix_pmatch_{seed}.py\n  - A_C_secalib_pmatch_{seed}.py\n  - A_C_hadamard_pmatch_{seed}.py\n- Results:\n  - results/prepool_mixer_A_resmix.csv (and analogous for C, secalib, hadamard)\n  - results/prepool_mixer_summary.md (medians/IQR + per-panel deltas)\n  - results/prepool_mixer_diagnostics/ (curves, energies, top-k attribution snapshots)\n\nInterpretation plan\n- If gains appear primarily in CRI-On/Off with stable ncRNA/MRL and IQR, the bottleneck hypothesis is supported; publish as a positive finding with ablations and param-matching.\n- If nothing moves or IQR inflates, conclude DSConv+head already saturates channel mixing; publish negative with commutativity analysis and diagnostics.\n\nThis preregistered plan is aligned with unification, parsimony, and reproducibility. It directly tests whether a minimal, permutation-equivariant channel mixer can systematically improve nonlinear pooling without harming robust panels."
