role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/prepool_mixer_net.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Sequence, Dict, Any\n\n  # -----------------------------\n  # Backbone: DSConv dilated block\n  # -----------------------------\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dilation: int = 1\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          # Depthwise conv (groups = channels), SAME padding with dilation\n          h = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.d_model,\n              kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n              feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n              padding='SAME',\n              kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n              name='dw_conv'\n          )(h)\n\
    \          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  # -----------------------------\n  # Pre-pool channel mixers (length-equivariant)\n  # -----------------------------\n  class ResChannelMixer(nn.Module):\n      hidden: int = 64\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x: (B, L, C)\n          c = x.shape[-1]\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden)(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          # Zero-init final projection for exact identity at init\n          h = nn.Dense(c, kernel_init=nn.initializers.zeros, bias_init=nn.initializers.zeros)(h)\n          return x + h\n\n  class SECalibMixer(nn.Module):\n      hidden: int = 64\n      alpha: float = 0.25\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x: (B, L, C)\n      \
    \    c = x.shape[-1]\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          u = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)            # (B, C)\n          g = nn.Dense(self.hidden)(u)\n          g = nn.gelu(g)\n          g = nn.Dense(c, kernel_init=nn.initializers.normal(0.02))(g)\n          g = nn.sigmoid(g)                  # (B, C)\n          scale = 1.0 + self.alpha * (g - 0.5)\n          return x * scale[:, None, :]\n\n  class HadamardGateMixer(nn.Module):\n      hidden: int = 32\n      alpha: float = 0.25\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # x: (B, L, C)\n          c = x.shape[-1]\n          u = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)            # (B, C)\n          w = nn.Dense(self.hidden)(u)\n          w = nn.tanh(w)\n          w = nn.Dense(c, kernel_init=nn.initializers.normal(0.02))(w)\n          w = nn.tanh(w)                     # (B, C), centered\n          scale = 1.0 + self.alpha * w\n          return x * scale[:, None, :]\n\n  # -----------------------------\n  # Pooling helpers\n\
    \  # -----------------------------\n  def lse_pool(h: jnp.ndarray, tau: float) -> jnp.ndarray:\n      # h: (B, L, C), per-channel LSE: tau * log(mean(exp(h/tau)))\n      x = h / tau\n      m = jnp.max(x, axis=1, keepdims=True)           # (B,1,C)\n      lse = tau * (jnp.log(jnp.mean(jnp.exp(x - m), axis=1) + 1e-12) + jnp.squeeze(m, axis=1))\n      return lse                                       # (B, C)\n\n  # -----------------------------\n  # Full network with optional pre-pool mixer\n  # -----------------------------\n  class RNANetPrePool(nn.Module):\n      d_input: int = 4\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type: str = 'regression'\n      d_model: int = 256\n      num_blocks: int = 5\n      dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      positional_encoding: bool = False\n\n      # Mixer config\n      use_mixer: bool = False\n      mixer_type: str = 'res_mlp'        # 'res_mlp' | 'se_calib' | 'hadamard'\n      mixer_hidden:\
    \ int = 64\n      mixer_alpha: float = 0.25\n\n      # Pooling config\n      aggregator: str = 'mean_lse'       # 'mean_lse' | 'mean_max'\n      tau: float = 0.5\n\n      # Head config\n      head_hidden: int = 256\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # Input projection\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # DSConv stack\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              d = self.dilations[i] if i < len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n              h = DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Optional pre-pool mixer (length-equivariant, channel-only)\n          if self.use_mixer:\n              if self.mixer_type == 'res_mlp':\n                  h = ResChannelMixer(hidden=self.mixer_hidden)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\
    \              elif self.mixer_type == 'se_calib':\n                  h = SECalibMixer(hidden=self.mixer_hidden, alpha=self.mixer_alpha)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n              elif self.mixer_type == 'hadamard':\n                  h = HadamardGateMixer(hidden=max(1, self.mixer_hidden // 2), alpha=self.mixer_alpha)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n              else:\n                  raise ValueError(f'Unknown mixer_type: {self.mixer_type}')\n\n          # Pooling\n          mean_vec = jnp.mean(h, axis=1)\n          if self.aggregator == 'mean_lse':\n              agg_vec = lse_pool(h, self.tau)\n          elif self.aggregator == 'mean_max':\n              agg_vec = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n          else:\n              raise ValueError(f'Unknown aggregator: {self.aggregator}')\n\n          fused = jnp.concatenate([mean_vec, agg_vec], axis=-1)  # (B, 2C)\n\n          # Head\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden)(z)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n\
    \          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n          if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n              return logits.squeeze(-1)\n          return logits\n\n  class PrePoolMixerNetwork:\n      def __init__(self, d_input, d_output, task_type, **kwargs):\n          self.network = RNANetPrePool(d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, **kwargs)\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key =\
    \ random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def build_network(d_output: int, task_type: str, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return PrePoolMixerNetwork(\n          d_input=4,\n          d_output=d_output,\n          task_type=task_type,\n          d_model=hparams.get('d_model', 256),\n          num_blocks=hparams.get('num_blocks', 5),\n          dilations=tuple(hparams.get('dilations', [1,2,4,8,16])),\n          kernel_size=hparams.get('kernel_size', 7),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n          positional_encoding=hparams.get('positional_encoding', False),\n          use_mixer=hparams.get('use_mixer', False),\n          mixer_type=hparams.get('mixer_type', 'res_mlp'),\n          mixer_hidden=hparams.get('mixer_hidden', 64),\n          mixer_alpha=hparams.get('mixer_alpha', 0.25),\n          aggregator=hparams.get('aggregator', 'mean_lse'),\n          tau=hparams.get('tau',\
    \ 0.5),\n          head_hidden=hparams.get('head_hidden', 256),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01),\n      )\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"PrePool Res-ChannelMixer (param-matched) — Config A (mean+LSE τ=0.5) — seed=42\"\ntags: \"cnn, pre-pool mixer, channel-only, permutation-equivariant, mean+LSE, param-matched\"\nabstract: \"Insert a tiny, length-equivariant channel mixer before pooling (identity-init residual MLP) to reweight motif channels per position. Param-matched by shrinking head to 192. Config A: concat(mean, LSE τ=0.5).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from prepool_mixer_net import build_network, create_optimizer\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n        \
    \  'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_encoding': False,\n          'use_mixer': True,\n          'mixer_type': 'res_mlp',\n          'mixer_hidden': 64,\n          'mixer_alpha': 0.25,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse',\n          'tau': 0.5,\n          'head_hidden': 192   # param-matched vs baseline head=256\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"PrePool Res-ChannelMixer (param-matched) — Config A (mean+LSE τ=0.5) — seed=7\"\ntags: \"cnn, pre-pool mixer, channel-only, permutation-equivariant, mean+LSE, param-matched, replication\"\nabstract: \"Replication of the pre-pool residual\
    \ channel mixer on Config A with seed=7 to assess median/IQR across seeds.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from prepool_mixer_net import build_network, create_optimizer\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_encoding': False,\n          'use_mixer': True,\n          'mixer_type': 'res_mlp',\n          'mixer_hidden': 64,\n          'mixer_alpha': 0.25,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse',\n          'tau': 0.5,\n          'head_hidden': 192\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  BASE_SEED = 7\n  BATCH_SIZE\
    \ = 64\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"PrePool Res-ChannelMixer (param-matched) — Config A (mean+LSE τ=0.5) — seed=123\"\ntags: \"cnn, pre-pool mixer, channel-only, permutation-equivariant, mean+LSE, param-matched, replication\"\nabstract: \"Third seed for tri-seed evaluation of the pre-pool residual channel mixer on Config A (concat mean + LSE τ=0.5).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from prepool_mixer_net import build_network, create_optimizer\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_encoding': False,\n          'use_mixer': True,\n          'mixer_type': 'res_mlp',\n          'mixer_hidden': 64,\n          'mixer_alpha': 0.25,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse',\n          'tau': 0.5,\n      \
    \    'head_hidden': 192\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  BASE_SEED = 123\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Control (param-matched head=192, no mixer) — Config A (mean+LSE τ=0.5) — seed=42\"\ntags: \"control, param-matched, head-shrink, mean+LSE, unified\"\nabstract: \"Param-matched control for pre-pool mixer experiments: shrink head to 192 without any mixer. Config A (mean+LSE τ=0.5), seed=42.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from prepool_mixer_net import build_network, create_optimizer\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size':\
    \ 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_encoding': False,\n          'use_mixer': False,            # control: no mixer\n          'mixer_type': 'res_mlp',\n          'mixer_hidden': 64,\n          'mixer_alpha': 0.25,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse',\n          'tau': 0.5,\n          'head_hidden': 192            # param-matched head only\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n```"
thinking_content: '**Considering experiment setup**


  I''m looking at the prereg plan, which calls for using three seeds, but I wonder if the station has any limits on concurrency. I want to submit 4-6 jobs but the inactivity notice suggests I should resume experiments promptly. To balance things, I can start with three runs and one control. Initially, I''ll write the module and make three submit commands, each with different seeds. If needed, I can run the control seed in later sessions. It''s all about managing submissions effectively while keeping compliant!**Crafting code for depthwise convolution**


  I need to ensure I''m using optax.adamw with the clip_by_global_norm chain effectively. Variable dropout should be deterministic, too. I''m crafting some code for a Depthwise Conv Dilated Block, considering the kernel_dilation and feature_group_count. Typically, I use depthwise conv with groups equal to the number of channels, but if d_model is 256, the depthwise conv features would equal self.d_model. I''ll set group_count based on the number of input channels to make sure everything aligns correctly. This is vital for getting the expected output!**Structuring code details**


  I’m working on the PrePoolResChannelMixer, where I’ll set W2 for kernel_init to zeros, and have biases as zeros, while keeping W1 at default. For the aggregators, I''ll compute the lse_pool using logarithmic functions. In the network''s __call__, I''ll check if the prepool mixer should be applied after the DSConv layer. The output heads will line up for logits in classification tasks and return squeezed output for regression tasks. I need to ensure consistent shapes for different outputs, along with clear function definitions.**Developing prepool mixer module**


  I''m going to write the module file named ''prepool_mixer_net.py'' in the storage directory and include the DSConv and builder functions like build_network with parameters for d_output, task_type, and hparams. For each submission, I''ll import this function. The content will set the aggregator to ''mean_lse'' with tau at 0.5, enabling the prepool mixer. I''ll implement different mixer types and factors for configurations while maintaining a batch size of 64. Then I can submit everything, including variations to ensure fair comparisons!**Preparing submissions and class implementation**


  I''m planning to perform four submissions now: three with variant seeds and one control seed set to 42; the rest will follow in the next steps. I’ll include a multi-action response with code writing and structure the submissions in YAML format. Each command needs to be on a new line, and I''ll take care with quoting in the YAML content. Additionally, I''ll implement the PrePoolMixer class and its branches, ensuring I import the required JAX initializers. Once everything is in place, I''ll keep an eye on edge cases and follow YAML rules for consistency!'
