- text: "`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/prepool_A_resmix_pmatch.csv}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  seed,eval_id,status,config,notes\n  42,396,running,A(mean+LSE_tau0.5),PrePool Res-ChannelMixer param-matched head=192\n  7,397,running,A(mean+LSE_tau0.5),PrePool Res-ChannelMixer param-matched head=192\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/prepool_readme.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Pre-pool Channel Mixer Experiments (Tick 273)\n  Goal: Test tiny, length-equivariant, channel-only mixers inserted just before pooling to improve nonlinear aggregation without violating unification.\n  Baseline configs:\n  - A: concat(mean, LSE τ=0.5) — stable default\n  - C: concat(mean, max) — best median, higher variance\n  Mixers: residual channel MLP (identity-init), SE-calibration gate (identity-centered), Hadamard gate (tiny).\n  Param matching: shrink head 512→192 when mixer is used to keep total params ≈ constant.\n  Current runs (A, param-matched, Res-ChannelMixer): seeds 42 (ID\
    \ 396), 7 (ID 397). Seed 123 and param-matched control will follow when slots free.\n  Reporting: tri-seed median/IQR and per-dataset median deltas vs baseline; kill if IQR rises >+0.002 or ncRNA/MRL median drops ≥0.002.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/prepool_submit_A_resmix_seed123.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from prepool_mixer_net import build_network, create_optimizer\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_encoding': False,\n          'use_mixer': True,\n          'mixer_type': 'res_mlp',\n          'mixer_hidden': 64,\n          'mixer_alpha': 0.25,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse',\n          'tau': 0.5,\n          'head_hidden': 192\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n\
    \      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  BASE_SEED = 123\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/prepool_submit_A_control_head192_seed42.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from prepool_mixer_net import build_network, create_optimizer\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_encoding': False,\n          'use_mixer': False,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse',\n          'tau': 0.5,\n          'head_hidden': 192\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1),\
    \ hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return create_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/SOTA_MONITOR.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  SOTA Monitor (Tick 273)\n  - Running: PrePool Res-ChannelMixer (param-matched) on Config A (mean+LSE τ=0.5) — seeds 42 (ID 396), 7 (ID 397).\n  - Next in queue (when slots free): seed 123 (param-matched) and param-matched control (head=192, no mixer).\n  - Reporting plan: tri-seed medians/IQR + per-dataset median deltas; kill if IQR > +0.002 or ncRNA/MRL median ↓ ≥ 0.002.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Updating documentation cautiously**\n\nI’m thinking about updating SOTA_MONITOR.md while being cautious with token use. The meta prompt indicates we should monitor and maintain documentation without heavy formatting, although bullet lists are okay. In this environment, we need to structure actions as /execute_action lines. \n\nI could prepare \"queued\" scripts for control heads seeds 7 and 123 and res_mlp seed 123 without submitting yet. This is because res_mlp seed 123 previously failed due to concurrency. Automated submission isn't an option either; action will need to be issued later.**Preparing results documentation**\n\nI'm considering adding docs in the results folder, like a pre-registered plan file and an eval ID mapping list that we've already noted in reflection. Storing it in results seems smart. I also think we should post a brief note about new experiments in public_memory, although I want to be mindful of conserving tokens. I can create a results tracking\
  \ CSV called prepool_A_resmix_pmatch.csv with columns for seed and eval_id. I have IDs 396 and 397, so I can write a CSV with placeholders for the rest and also draft a README for the prepool experiments. Once the current tasks complete, I’ll queue a second batch.**Planning experiment submissions**\n\nI previously tried submitting res-mixer seed 123, but it failed due to concurrency. I can maintain the code and plan to submit once the experiments finish. I could also check the storage list or write a script to expedite the process later. We ought to avoid excessive commentary and focus on necessary actions. \n\nSo, here’s the plan: I’ll write a results summary in `results/prepool_plan.md`, prepare a CSV for eval IDs 396 and 397, and create submission content for the res-mixer and control head seeds into separate files while ensuring the content is stored for reuse.**Preparing for submission**\n\nIt's best to plan to submit after the current experiments finish. For now, I'll focus on writing\
  \ results and documentation. I might jot down a note in private_memory to keep track, but that’s optional. The platform expects specific action lines, so here’s what I’ll do:\n\nFirst, I’ll write a CSV file at `noema/results/prepool_A_resmix_pmatch.csv` with headers and entries for eval IDs 396 and 397, along with seeds 42 and 7 marked as \"running.\" Then, I’ll summarize the design in `noema/results/prepool_readme.md`.\n\nI could also consider appending an addendum about preregistration in the archive, but it’s not urgent right now. Then, I can prepare submission content as a .py snippet or text instructions, keeping in mind that the submission interface needs inline code for clarity.**Storing and finalizing code**\n\nI can store the code for the control parameters to reuse it later, although it’s quite similar to the earlier \"control\" that failed due to concurrency issues. It's still valuable to keep. I’ll write the submission scripts, specifically `noema/submissions/prepool_submit_control_head192.py`\
  \ with similar code to the earlier version, and `prepool_submit_resmix_seed123.py`.\n\nNow, I’ll create some actions: writing the results CSV, documenting the results plan, and storing those two submission files. I might also update SOTA_MONITOR.md to log the running evals. If needed, I could quickly mention in public_memory that the prepool mixer experiments are currently running while keeping token use low. Now, I'll finalize the YAML content with the appropriate formatting and ensure everything is properly structured with newlines."
