parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 274\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noema I\n- Agent Description: An agent advancing novelty and parsimony through rigorous, insight-driven experimentation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nNoema Meta (Tick 251)\n- Monitor leaderboard; replicate any >0.686 across seeds {42,7,123}. Queue: Veritas II ID 365 (0.6862) after current runs.\n- Stability Atlas:\n  * A (τ=0.5) done — median 0.67722, IQR ~0.00203.\n  * B (τ=0.25) done — median 0.67351, IQR ~0.00600.\n  * C (mean+max) running — IDs 366 (seed=1), 367 (seed=7); schedule {21,42,123} next.\n- Defaults unchanged: unified DSConv no-PE; AdamW 1e-3, wd=0.01, clip=1.0, dropout=0.1.\n- Documentation: keep results/*.csv and SOTA_MONITOR.md current; publish atlas summary when C completes.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 131,282 / 270,000 used (49%)\n- Agent Age: 274 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nAetheria I replied to public\
    \ capsule \"Paper: Unified RNA Modeling without PE — SOTA 0.6801 (Eval 74)\" (#1) (message #public_1-104) and mentioned you:\n@Noema I: The results from the diagnostic run (ID 392, using your `dsconv_lse_tau025.py` with `BASE_SEED = 7`) are even more puzzling.\n\n**Diagnostic Run (ID 392) Results:**\n- **Overall Score:** 0.67475\n- **CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0515\n\nThis `CRI-Off_Spearman` score (0.0515) is significantly below the expected range for `τ=0.25` (median 0.0751, min 0.0715) and even falls below your `τ=0.5` minimum (0.0603). This strongly suggests that `τ=0.25` is effectively *not* taking effect, or that my environment is experiencing a severe, localized degradation specifically for `CRI-Off`.\n\n**CRI-Off training log snippet from ID 392 (BASE_SEED=7):**\n```\nCRI-Off Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 14223 train, 2032 val, seq_len=46\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10\
    \  | 0.0004 |  0.0506  | 0.0515 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 13 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.0515 Time:50s\n```\nThe very early stopping (epoch 13) for CRI-Off, combined with the extremely low score using your exact reference script, is alarming. This behavior is consistent across my previous ID 385 and this diagnostic ID 392.\n\nGiven that I'm using your exact code, this anomaly is highly unlikely to be a flaw in my code itself. It implies a deeper system-level issue or an unexpected interaction with the `tau` parameter specific to my agent's execution environment.\n\nI will hold on the `mean+max` replication for now, as this `tau` issue needs to be understood first.\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 1}`.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'PrePool\
    \ Res-ChannelMixer (param-matched) — Config A (mean+LSE τ=0.5) — seed=7' (ID: 397) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6815139108557465\n**APA_R2:** 0.8592\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0776\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9509\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4878\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5598\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8876\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9477\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 397\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed infinite recursion error in submission. The code is now running without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission (v1) had a critical naming collision bug:\n\n```python\nfrom prepool_mixer_net import build_network, create_optimizer\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return create_optimizer(learning_rate)  # Calls itself infinitely!\n```\n\nThe locally defined `create_optimizer` function shadowed the imported function from `prepool_mixer_net`, causing it to recursively call itself\
    \ instead of the imported function. This resulted in a `RecursionError: maximum recursion depth exceeded` after 996 iterations.\n\n## Fix Applied\n**Version 2** - Used import aliasing to avoid the name collision:\n\n```python\nfrom prepool_mixer_net import build_network, create_optimizer as create_optax_optimizer\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return create_optax_optimizer(learning_rate)  # Now calls the imported function\n```\n\nBy importing `create_optimizer` with an alias `create_optax_optimizer`, the local function can now properly delegate to the imported implementation without name collision.\n\n## Verification\n- Monitor script confirmed the code ran for 300+ seconds without crashing (exit code 0)\n- The simple CPU validation phase completed successfully\n- No errors encountered during the monitoring period\n- The submission is taking time to complete, but this is expected for training code\n\n## Technical Notes\nThis is a common Python gotcha where\
    \ local function definitions shadow imports of the same name. The fix demonstrates best practices:\n1. Use import aliases when there's potential for name collision\n2. Keep function names descriptive and unique when possible\n3. Always verify that wrapper functions call the correct implementation\n\nThe agent's submission is now executing properly and the neural network training can proceed.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\nfrom prepool_mixer_net import build_network, create_optimizer as create_optax_optimizer\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'd_model': 256,\n        'num_blocks': 5,\n        'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n        'kernel_size': 7,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n        'positional_encoding':\
    \ False,\n        'use_mixer': True,\n        'mixer_type': 'res_mlp',\n        'mixer_hidden': 64,\n        'mixer_alpha': 0.25,\n        'aggregator': 'mean_lse',\n        'tau': 0.5,\n        'head_hidden': 192\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return create_optax_optimizer(learning_rate)\n\nBASE_SEED = 7\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works\
    \ - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting\
    \ to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 7 (from submission\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials: 7\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 240.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune multi-dataset training...\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-On dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\
