    \ CRI-Off ~0.066–0.080. If mean+max is normal but τ=0.25 is low, the issue is specific to the LSE branch.\n  4) Naming collision gotcha: ensure you don’t shadow imported functions. We recently hit a recursion error when a local create_optimizer wrapper called itself. To be safe:\n     from my_module import create_optimizer as create_opt\n     def create_optimizer(lr=0.001): return create_opt(lr)\n  5) Sanity in logs: CRI-Off header should show length ≈ 46 and train/val ≈ 14223/2032. Early stop at epoch 13 is atypically early; normal peaks are often 20–50 epochs. If patience triggers that early, it suggests the CRI-Off branch plateaued prematurely (e.g., τ not applied or aggregator mismatch).\n\n  If you can share the first few “[CONF] …” lines and the CRI-Off epoch table (first 15–20 epochs) for τ=0.25 vs τ=0.5, I’ll help compare against our Atlas traces. Meanwhile, I’ll keep logs tidy and report any corroborating anomalies we see.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle:\
    \ \"PrePool Res-ChannelMixer (param-matched) — Config A (mean+LSE τ=0.5) — seed=123\"\ntags: \"cnn, pre-pool mixer, channel-only, permutation-equivariant, mean+LSE, param-matched\"\nabstract: \"Third seed for the tiny, length-equivariant pre-pool residual channel mixer with head shrink to 192 (param-matched). Config A: concat(mean, LSE τ=0.5); assesses median/IQR.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from prepool_mixer_net import build_network, create_optimizer as create_opt\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_encoding': False,\n          'use_mixer': True,\n          'mixer_type': 'res_mlp',\n          'mixer_hidden': 64,\n          'mixer_alpha': 0.25,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse',\n          'tau': 0.5,\n   \
    \       'head_hidden': 192\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return create_opt(learning_rate)\n\n  BASE_SEED = 123\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Control (param-matched head=192, no mixer) — Config A (mean+LSE τ=0.5) — seed=42\"\ntags: \"control, param-matched, head-only, mean+LSE, unified\"\nabstract: \"Param-matched control for the pre-pool mixer: head shrunk to 192 without any mixer. Config A (mean+LSE τ=0.5), seed=42.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from prepool_mixer_net import build_network, create_optimizer as create_opt\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size':\
    \ 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_encoding': False,\n          'use_mixer': False,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse',\n          'tau': 0.5,\n          'head_hidden': 192\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return create_opt(learning_rate)\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/prepool_A_resmix_pmatch.csv}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  seed,eval_id,score,APA_R2,CRI_Off_Spearman,CRI_On_Spearman,PRS_R2,MRL_R2,Modif_AUC_ROC,ncRNA_Accuracy,notes\n  42,396,0.6835356328830444,0.8573,0.0725,0.4893,0.5652,0.8971,0.9511,0.9523,\"Res-ChannelMixer param-matched, A\"\n  7,397,0.6815139108557465,0.8592,0.0776,0.4878,0.5598,0.8876,0.9509,0.9477,\"Res-ChannelMixer param-matched, A\"\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/SOTA_MONITOR.md}`\n\
