parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/prepool_A_resmix_pmatch.csv}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  seed,eval_id,score,APA_R2,CRI_Off_Spearman,CRI_On_Spearman,PRS_R2,MRL_R2,Modif_AUC_ROC,ncRNA_Accuracy,notes\n  42,396,0.6835356328830444,0.8573,0.0725,0.4893,0.5652,0.8971,0.9511,0.9523,\"Res-ChannelMixer param-matched, A\"\n  7,397,0.6815139108557465,0.8592,0.0776,0.4878,0.5598,0.8876,0.9509,0.9477,\"Res-ChannelMixer param-matched, A\"\n  123,399,0.6732124067470266,0.8549,0.0546,0.4598,0.5584,0.8815,0.9525,0.9508,\"Res-ChannelMixer param-matched, A\"\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/prepool_A_control_head192.csv}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  seed,eval_id,score,APA_R2,CRI_Off_Spearman,CRI_On_Spearman,PRS_R2,MRL_R2,Modif_AUC_ROC,ncRNA_Accuracy,notes\n  42,400,0.6830515254393348,0.8570,0.0772,0.5017,0.5545,0.8817,0.9523,0.9569,\"Control param-matched head=192, no mixer, A\"\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/prepool_A_summary.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent:\
    \ |\n  Pre-pool Res-ChannelMixer (param-matched, head=192) — Config A (mean+LSE τ=0.5), tri-seed completed (Tick 277)\n\n  Mixer results:\n  - Seed 42 (ID 396): 0.683535 | APA 0.8573 | CRI-Off 0.0725 | CRI-On 0.4893 | PRS 0.5652 | MRL 0.8971 | Modif 0.9511 | ncRNA 0.9523\n  - Seed 7  (ID 397): 0.681514 | APA 0.8592 | CRI-Off 0.0776 | CRI-On 0.4878 | PRS 0.5598 | MRL 0.8876 | Modif 0.9509 | ncRNA 0.9477\n  - Seed 123 (ID 399): 0.673212 | APA 0.8549 | CRI-Off 0.0546 | CRI-On 0.4598 | PRS 0.5584 | MRL 0.8815 | Modif 0.9525 | ncRNA 0.9508\n\n  Mixer tri-seed stats (sorted scores: 0.673212, 0.681514, 0.683536):\n  - Median = 0.681514\n  - Q1 ≈ 0.677363, Q3 ≈ 0.682525 → IQR ≈ 0.005162\n  - Note: seed 123 shows an anomalous CRI-Off=0.0546 (below typical τ=0.5 band), driving IQR up.\n\n  Param-matched control (head=192, no mixer):\n  - Seed 42 (ID 400): 0.683052 | CRI-Off 0.0772 | CRI-On 0.5017 | MRL 0.8817 | ncRNA 0.9569\n  - Pending: control seeds 7 & 123 to isolate structure vs capacity and\
    \ check if the seed-123 dip is head-related or environment-specific.\n\n  Interim takeaways:\n  - Mixer vs control (seed 42): +0.00048 in favor of mixer (very small).\n  - Mixer median improves over Atlas A median (0.67722) but with higher variance driven by seed 123 CRI-Off; need matched controls across seeds to make a fair call.\n\n  Next actions:\n  - Queue controls for seeds 7 and 123 (param-matched head=192, no mixer) with runtime CONF prints of dataset/agg/tau.\n  - If controls show normal CRI-Off on seed 123, seed-specific mixer instability suspected → try α=0.1 warmup; else if controls also dip, environment-specific volatility suspected.\n  - Only if A shows consistent median gains with stable IQR vs controls will we test the mixer on Config C (mean+max) tri-seed.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Control (param-matched head=192, no mixer) — Config A (mean+LSE τ=0.5) — seed=7\"\ntags: \"control, param-matched, head-only, mean+LSE, unified\"\nabstract: \"\
    Param-matched control for the pre-pool mixer: head shrunk to 192 without any mixer. Config A (mean+LSE τ=0.5), seed=7.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from prepool_mixer_net import build_network, create_optimizer as create_opt\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_encoding': False,\n          'use_mixer': False,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse',\n          'tau': 0.5,\n          'head_hidden': 192\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return create_opt(learning_rate)\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      hp = trial_data.get('hyperparameters',\
    \ {})\n      print(f\"[CONF] dataset={trial_data.get('dataset')} agg={hp.get('aggregator')} tau={hp.get('tau')}\")\n\n  BASE_SEED = 7\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Control (param-matched head=192, no mixer) — Config A (mean+LSE τ=0.5) — seed=123\"\ntags: \"control, param-matched, head-only, mean+LSE, unified\"\nabstract: \"Param-matched control for the pre-pool mixer: head shrunk to 192 without any mixer. Config A (mean+LSE τ=0.5), seed=123.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from prepool_mixer_net import build_network, create_optimizer as create_opt\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_encoding': False,\n          'use_mixer': False,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse',\n \
    \         'tau': 0.5,\n          'head_hidden': 192\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return create_opt(learning_rate)\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      hp = trial_data.get('hyperparameters', {})\n      print(f\"[CONF] dataset={trial_data.get('dataset')} agg={hp.get('aggregator')} tau={hp.get('tau')}\")\n\n  BASE_SEED = 123\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/SOTA_MONITOR.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  SOTA Monitor (Tick 277)\n  - PrePool Res-ChannelMixer (param-matched, A=mean+LSE τ=0.5) tri-seed: scores {0.683536, 0.681514, 0.673212} → median 0.681514; IQR ≈ 0.005162 (seed 123 CRI-Off 0.0546 anomaly).\n  - Param-matched control (head=192, no mixer): seed 42 = 0.683052; seeds 7 and 123 queued with CONF prints for aggregator/tau per dataset.\n  - Decision\
    \ gate: if controls show normal CRI-Off at seed 123 while mixer is low, we’ll test α warmup (0.1→0.25, 5 epochs). If controls also dip, treat as environment volatility; prefer Config C replication next.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning experimentation steps**\n\nI’m thinking about rerunning seed 399 with the same configuration to check if the results were a fluke. To keep things balanced, I might schedule the control tests first, then decide on the next steps. We also want to update our records, including writing to the prepool. Additionally, I should summarize the tri-seed results and propose future actions while possibly hitting the SOTA_MONITOR. It seems adding suggestions for logging could enhance tracking too, but I can work on that later. I’m focusing on crafting clear action steps for now.**Organizing tasks and updates**\n\nI need to write the results into storage, starting with appending to prepool_A_resmix_pmatch.csv. Next, I'll create a new file for prepool_A_control_head192.csv with ID 400. It’s important to update prepool_A_summary.md with tri-seed stats, noting the anomaly 'CRI-Off 0.0546 seed 123' and plan to run control seeds 7 and 123. Since both 399 and 400 are done, I can\
  \ submit two controls at once. I might also reply to Aetheria about their anomaly while keeping it brief. Lastly, I should ensure proper YAML quoting.**Preparing control code submissions**\n\nI need to provide code for the control submissions related to prepool_mixer_net. Previously, I wrote 'prepool_submit_A_control_head192_seed42.py', but now I can directly submit using a content block instead of creating a separate file. This way, it's simpler! I’ll handle two submissions for Control A head 192, specifically for seeds 7 and 123.\n\nI might also consider rerunning mixer seed 123 later to check for replication, but for now, I’ll focus on submitting the controls. Plus, here's a summary of the mixer A tri-seed with computed statistics.**Analyzing performance metrics**\n\nI'm comparing the current results to an Atlas A baseline with a median of 0.67722, resulting in an improvement of +0.00429. However, there’s a high interquartile range (IQR) of 0.00203, which indicates added variance, especially\
  \ with the dropout in seed 123. It’s interesting that control 42 shows a value of 0.6830515, which is close to 396. Some of this improvement might stem from head shrinkage. I realize we need more seed data to draw clearer conclusions about these controls.**Planning control seed process**\n\nMy plan is to run control seeds 7 and 123, then compare the tri-seed medians. If the control median is around 0.681 and similar to the mixer median, there wouldn't be any structural gain. If the mixer outperforms the control, it would indicate a tiny effect; otherwise, it could be negative. \n\nI'll write the results to CSV, create a new file for seed 400, and submit both control seeds. Updating the SOTA_MONITOR and prepool_A_summary is next. Optionally, I might reply to Aetheria about observing the CRI-Off dip at seed 123. Lastly, I'll ensure our submissions print useful logs, focusing on the aggregator and tau values. Let's finalize the action commands now!"
