parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/prepool_A_compare_mixer_vs_control.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Pre-pool Mixer vs Control — Config A (mean+LSE τ=0.5), tri-seed summary (Tick 279)\n\n  Mixer (Res-ChannelMixer, head=192):\n  - Seeds: 42=0.683536, 7=0.681514, 123=0.673212\n  - Median = 0.681514; IQR ≈ 0.005162\n  - Seed 123 CRI-Off=0.0546 (anomalously low), early stop ~31 epochs.\n\n  Control (head=192, no mixer):\n  - Seeds: 42=0.683052, 7=0.679933, 123=0.678902\n  - Median = 0.679933; IQR ≈ 0.002075\n  - Seed 123 CRI-Off=0.0745 (normal), confirming anomaly is mixer-specific.\n\n  Interim verdict:\n  - Mixer shows small median lift vs control (+0.00158) but increases variance, driven by seed 123 CRI-Off collapse.\n  - Next: gentler mixer (α=0.1) and tiny Hadamard gate on seed 123 to test stability; if stabilized and median holds, proceed to tri-seed.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"PrePool Res-ChannelMixer (param-matched,\
    \ alpha=0.1) — Config A (mean+LSE τ=0.5) — seed=123\"\ntags: \"cnn, pre-pool mixer, channel-only, mean+LSE, param-matched\"\nabstract: \"Gentler pre-pool residual channel mixer with smaller alpha (0.1) to reduce variance; param-matched head=192. Tests whether seed-123 CRI-Off collapse stabilizes.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from prepool_mixer_net import build_network, create_optimizer as create_opt\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_encoding': False,\n          'use_mixer': True,\n          'mixer_type': 'res_mlp',\n          'mixer_hidden': 64,\n          'mixer_alpha': 0.1,   # gentler mixer\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse',\n          'tau': 0.5,\n          'head_hidden': 192\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n\
    \      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return create_opt(learning_rate)\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      hp = trial_data.get('hyperparameters', {})\n      print(f\"[CONF] dataset={trial_data.get('dataset')} agg={hp.get('aggregator')} tau={hp.get('tau')} mixer={hp.get('mixer_type')} alpha={hp.get('mixer_alpha')}\")\n\n  BASE_SEED = 123\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"PrePool Hadamard Gate (param-matched, alpha=0.25) — Config A (mean+LSE τ=0.5) — seed=123\"\ntags: \"cnn, pre-pool mixer, hadamard gate, channel-only, mean+LSE, param-matched\"\nabstract: \"Tiny signed Hadamard gate (global stats → per-channel) before pooling; param-matched head=192. Tests stability on seed 123 vs residual mixer.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from prepool_mixer_net\
    \ import build_network, create_optimizer as create_opt\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_encoding': False,\n          'use_mixer': True,\n          'mixer_type': 'hadamard',\n          'mixer_hidden': 32,\n          'mixer_alpha': 0.25,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_lse',\n          'tau': 0.5,\n          'head_hidden': 192\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return create_opt(learning_rate)\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      hp = trial_data.get('hyperparameters', {})\n      print(f\"[CONF] dataset={trial_data.get('dataset')} agg={hp.get('aggregator')} tau={hp.get('tau')}\
    \ mixer={hp.get('mixer_type')} alpha={hp.get('mixer_alpha')}\")\n\n  BASE_SEED = 123\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/SOTA_MONITOR.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  SOTA Monitor (Tick 279)\n  - Controls (param-matched head=192, no mixer):\n    • Seed 42 (ID 400): 0.683052 (CRI-Off 0.0772)\n    • Seed 7  (ID 404): 0.679933 (CRI-Off 0.0761)\n    • Seed 123 (ID 405): 0.678902 (CRI-Off 0.0745)\n    → Control median = 0.679933; IQR ≈ 0.002075; CRI-Off normal across seeds.\n  - Mixer (Res-ChannelMixer, head=192) tri-seed: {0.683536, 0.681514, 0.673212} → median 0.681514; IQR ≈ 0.005162; seed 123 CRI-Off=0.0546.\n  - Action: submitted gentler mixer α=0.1 (seed 123) and tiny Hadamard gate (seed 123) to test stabilization; will tri-seed only if stable vs controls.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Update on diagnostics (Tick 279)\n  - Our controls (head=192, no mixer) show normal CRI-Off across seeds,\
    \ including seed 123 (ID 405: 0.0745). This confirms that the seed-123 dip we saw (CRI-Off 0.0546) is mixer-specific rather than an environment-wide issue.\n  - We’ve launched two stability probes on seed 123:\n    • Res-ChannelMixer with gentler alpha=0.1 (param-matched).\n    • Tiny Hadamard gate (param-matched).\n  - Both print “[CONF] dataset=… agg=… tau=… mixer=… alpha=…” per trial to verify runtime settings. If either stabilizes while maintaining median, we’ll tri-seed; otherwise we’ll close the pre-pool line as negative and move to mean+max replication.\n```"
