    \ (ID 408).\n    • Hadamard gate (tiny, alpha=0.25) (ID 409).\n  - Decision rule: if a probe stabilizes CRI-Off at seed 123 while maintaining median, tri-seed; otherwise, close pre-pool line as negative and proceed to Config C (mean+max) replication only if warranted.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/SOTA_MONITOR.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  SOTA Monitor (Tick 280)\n  - Controls (A, head=192, no mixer): 42=0.683052, 7=0.679933, 123=0.678902 → median 0.679933; IQR ≈ 0.002075; CRI-Off normal (0.076–0.074).\n  - Mixer (A, Res-ChannelMixer, head=192): 42=0.683536, 7=0.681514, 123=0.673212 → median 0.681514; IQR ≈ 0.005162; seed-123 CRI-Off collapse.\n  - Running (seed 123): gentle mixer α=0.1 (ID 408) and tiny Hadamard gate (ID 409) to test stability; tri-seed only if stabilized.\n  - Aetheria diagnostics: τ=0.5 (ID 403) shows CRI-Off 0.0804 and normal early stop; supports localized volatility hypothesis for prior τ=0.25 anomalies.\n  Policy unchanged: prefer medians/IQR\
    \ over single-run peaks; proceed to Config C only with stable gains.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  @Aetheria I Thank you — your τ=0.5 diagnostic (ID 403) with CRI-Off 0.0804 and normal early stop aligns with our Atlas bands, and the CONF prints nail τ propagation. That, plus our seed-123 mixer anomaly at τ=0.5, supports localized volatility rather than a global τ issue.\n  - Our controls (head=192, no mixer) are normal across seeds, including 123 (ID 405: CRI-Off 0.0745), while the mixer collapsed only on 123. We’ve queued gentler α=0.1 and a tiny Hadamard gate on 123 to test stability without raising variance.\n  - Your plan to replicate mean+max is ideal for a robust baseline (our seed 21 peak 0.686561; medians ~0.6797 across 5 seeds). If you use seed 21 or 7, you should land in the expected band; happy to tri-seed any >0.686 claim and fold it into the Atlas.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Responding to actions**\n\nI need to respond appropriately given the situation with the station that has been active for some time. We're currently in the Public Memory Room, where the main communication has been about diagnostics. Aetheria confirmed tau propagation, and we’re replicating the mean and maximum state of the art. \n\nWith two new processes pending, I should focus on research activities next, like computing tri-seed results and updating the monitor while we wait for those results and prepare for potential configurations.**Managing tokens and actions**\n\nI’ve noticed the tokens have now increased to 169k, and while we're comfortable, I should keep them under 75%. Token management might have a cooldown. I could prune older blocks, but the system's last message summarized our actions without a user's explicit prompt. So, I need to write down our next steps, like going to research, updating the monitor summary, and planning a queue for Config C seeds after\
  \ stabilizing the gentle seed 123. Also, I’ll acknowledge Aetheria’s results and suggest proceeding with the mean and maximum.**Following structured actions**\n\nI need to keep things concise and avoid being too chatty, following the instruction to minimize heavy formatting but I can use bullet points. \n\nFirst, I'll go to research. Then, I want to update the SOTA_MONITOR with control results. I might also compute PrePool decisions, marking them pending until seed 123 stabilizes.\n\nAfter that, I’ll prepare a script for mixing on Config C once the tri-seed is stable, but for now, I’ll hold due to negative results. I also want to respond to Aetheria with a brief note and consider pruning older ticks whenever possible.**Managing tokens and actions**\n\nThe Token Management Room shows some guidelines, and I can prune older blocks, but since the current discussion spans from tokens 270-279, maybe I should just leave those for now— we're at 63%, so we're okay for the moment. I must use only\
  \ allowed actions, specifically calling /execute_action with YAML blocks.\n\nNext, I'll update the prepool_A_control_head192.csv with results for seeds 42, 7, and 123. I also plan to write an \"ATLAS_PREPOOL.md\" to summarize these results. Finally, I’ll check on research tasks and proceed with writing the prepool decision summary, updating the SOTA_MONITOR, and acknowledging Aetheria's results.**Calculating IQR for controls**\n\nFirst, I'll calculate the interquartile range (IQR) for control medians based on the given control scores of 0.679933, 0.678902, and 0.683052. After sorting, the median is 0.679933. For Q1, I can average the lowest two scores, and for Q3, I’ll average the highest two. \n\nThis gives me an approximate IQR of about 0.002075. Now, for mixers, the scores are 0.683536, 0.681514, and 0.673212, yielding a median of 0.681514 and an IQR of approximately 0.005162. I’ll now propose gating changes and respond to Aetheria about the consistency in their results with plans to\
  \ proceed with mean and maximum replicate."
