- text: "`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{reply 15}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Pre-pool mixers — Config A (τ=0.5) interim results (Tick 282)\n\n  Param-matched (head=192) Res-ChannelMixer:\n  - Seeds: 42=0.6835, 7=0.6815, 123=0.6732 → median=0.6815, IQR≈0.00516\n  - Seed 123 showed CRI-Off collapse (0.0546, early stop ~31).\n\n  Controls (head=192, no mixer):\n  - Seeds: 42=0.6831, 7=0.6799, 123=0.6789 → median=0.6799, IQR≈0.00208; CRI-Off normal across seeds.\n\n  Stabilization probe:\n  - Res-ChannelMixer α=0.1 at seed 123: 0.6811 with CRI-Off 0.0735 (normal).\n  - Hadamard gate α=0.25 at seed 123: 0.6727 (negative; very early CRI-Off stop).\n\n  Next (running): α=0.1 mixer tri-seed (seeds 42, 7). Decision: proceed to Config C (mean+max) only if α=0.1 shows median ≥ control median with IQR within +0.001 of control.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/prepool_submit_C_resmix_alpha01_seed42.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n\
    \  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from prepool_mixer_net import build_network, create_optimizer as create_opt\n\n  # Config C: concat(mean, max), param-matched head=192\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_encoding': False,\n          'use_mixer': True,\n          'mixer_type': 'res_mlp',\n          'mixer_hidden': 64,\n          'mixer_alpha': 0.1,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_max',\n          'head_hidden': 192\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return create_opt(learning_rate)\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      hp = trial_data.get('hyperparameters',\
    \ {})\n      print(f\"[CONF] dataset={trial_data.get('dataset')} agg={hp.get('aggregator')} mixer={hp.get('mixer_type')} alpha={hp.get('mixer_alpha')}\")\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/prepool_submit_C_resmix_alpha01_seed7.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from prepool_mixer_net import build_network, create_optimizer as create_opt\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_encoding': False,\n          'use_mixer': True,\n          'mixer_type': 'res_mlp',\n          'mixer_hidden': 64,\n          'mixer_alpha': 0.1,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_max',\n          'head_hidden': 192\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output',\
    \ 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return create_opt(learning_rate)\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      hp = trial_data.get('hyperparameters', {})\n      print(f\"[CONF] dataset={trial_data.get('dataset')} agg={hp.get('aggregator')} mixer={hp.get('mixer_type')} alpha={hp.get('mixer_alpha')}\")\n\n  BASE_SEED = 7\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/submissions/prepool_submit_C_resmix_alpha01_seed123.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noema/submissions')\n  from prepool_mixer_net import build_network, create_optimizer as create_opt\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1,2,4,8,16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'positional_encoding': False,\n          'use_mixer':\
    \ True,\n          'mixer_type': 'res_mlp',\n          'mixer_hidden': 64,\n          'mixer_alpha': 0.1,\n          'aggregator': 'mean_max',\n          'head_hidden': 192\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(hparams.get('d_output', 1), hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'), hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return create_opt(learning_rate)\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      hp = trial_data.get('hyperparameters', {})\n      print(f\"[CONF] dataset={trial_data.get('dataset')} agg={hp.get('aggregator')} mixer={hp.get('mixer_type')} alpha={hp.get('mixer_alpha')}\")\n\n  BASE_SEED = 123\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/SOTA_MONITOR.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  SOTA Monitor (Tick 282)\n  - Pre-pool A (τ=0.5): α=0.1 stabilized seed 123 (ID 408: 0.6811, CRI-Off 0.0735). Seeds 42/7 running (IDs 413/414).\n  - Prepared Config C (mean+max) α=0.1 tri-seed templates\
    \ (seeds 42/7/123). Will submit if A’s α=0.1 tri-seed median ≥ control median and IQR within +0.001 of control.\n  - Atlas policy unchanged: report medians/IQR; SOTA peaks contextual only.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning next actions**\n\nI need to plan our next steps carefully. We've conducted some prepool channel mixer experiments with specific parameters. Right now, we're waiting for the results from runs on seeds 42 and 7. Once we have those, I should review the results accordingly and prepare scripts for a Config C variant. It’s also a good idea to update the SOTA_MONITOR with prepool summary updates. Additionally, I might need to consider pruning to manage token usage effectively, although the cooldown is still uncertain.**Organizing action steps**\n\nRight now, our token usage is at 68% of 270k, which is manageable. I need to plan for the possibility of exiting if necessary, but we still have ongoing experiments to focus on. I should include robust documentation details and possibly generate an archive addendum summarizing pre-pool A results. \n\nFor my next actions, I will: 1) Store submission templates for Config C with specific seeds. 2) Write a quick utility for computing\
  \ medians, though it's not essential. 3) Update public memory about stabilization achieved and conditions for proceeding; 4) Consider responding to Atlas with prepool A results.**Defining storage actions**\n\nI realize the prompt is asking for specific station actions while keeping my commitments minimal. We need to avoid heavy content and adhere to any restrictions. Here's how I’ll proceed:\n\nFirst, I’ll create a storage write summarizing the results in `results/prepool_A_progress.md`. Next, I'll write submission scripts for Config C. Since we already have two concurrent submissions running, I won’t initiate a new /submit but will queue instead. \n\nI'll also write to `noema/submissions/prepool_submit_C_resmix_alpha01_seed42.py` and update the SOTA_MONITOR. Lastly, I may need to check the archive for any replies. Alright, let’s implement these actions!"
