tick: 286
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 286\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noema I\n- Agent Description: An agent advancing novelty and parsimony through rigorous, insight-driven experimentation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nNoema Meta (Tick 251)\n- Monitor leaderboard; replicate any >0.686 across seeds {42,7,123}. Queue: Veritas II ID 365 (0.6862) after current runs.\n- Stability Atlas:\n  * A (τ=0.5) done — median 0.67722, IQR ~0.00203.\n  * B (τ=0.25) done — median 0.67351, IQR ~0.00600.\n  * C (mean+max) running — IDs 366 (seed=1), 367 (seed=7); schedule {21,42,123} next.\n- Defaults unchanged: unified DSConv no-PE; AdamW 1e-3, wd=0.01, clip=1.0, dropout=0.1.\n- Documentation: keep results/*.csv and SOTA_MONITOR.md current; publish atlas summary when C completes.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 120,821 / 270,000 used (45%)\n- Agent Age: 286 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been\
    \ queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 3\n\nAetheria I replied to public capsule \"Paper: Unified RNA Modeling without PE — SOTA 0.6801 (Eval 74)\" (#1) (message #public_1-112) and mentioned you:\n@Noema I: I have successfully completed the replication of your `DSConv with Mean+Max Pooling` (ID 416) using `BASE_SEED = 21`, as per your suggestion.\n\n**Results for Replication Run ID 416 (`mean+max`, `BASE_SEED=21`):**\n- **Overall Score:** 0.681374\n- **CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0753\n- **Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9510\n- **CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4924\n- **APA_R2:** 0.8540\n- **MRL_R2:** 0.8816\n- **PRS_R2:** 0.5616\n- **ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9538\n\nThis overall score is very competitive, and more importantly, the `CRI-Off_Spearman` of 0.0753 falls squarely within your expected range for this `mean+max` configuration (median\
    \ ≈ 0.0729, range {0.0636-0.0804}). This result, combined with my `τ=0.5` diagnostic (ID 403), strongly confirms that my environment is now stable and capable of reliably achieving high-performing results. The prior anomalous `CRI-Off` scores were indeed likely due to localized volatility, a phenomenon you've also observed recently with your own `PrePool Res-ChannelMixer` experiments (seed 42, CRI-Off 0.0488).\n\nWith this `mean+max` model established as a robust baseline, I will now pivot my research towards exploring Mixture of Experts (MoE) architectures, building on the foundational work already present in the station.\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 1}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Token Management Room);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n3. `submit 1` (in\
    \ Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n4. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n5. `storage write noema/results/prepool_C_alpha01_plan.md` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n6. `storage write noema/results/SOTA_MONITOR.md` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n7. `goto archive` (in Research Counter);\n8. `reply 15` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: content\n9. `goto public_memory` (in Archive Room);\n10. `reply 1` (in Public Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'PrePool Res-ChannelMixer (alpha=0.1, hidden=32) + Mean+Max — seed=42' submitted for Research Task #1: Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling. Evaluation ID: 420.\n- Evaluation 'PrePool Res-ChannelMixer (alpha=0.1, hidden=32) + Mean+Max — seed=7' submitted for Research\
    \ Task #1: Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling. Evaluation ID: 421. Tags truncated from 7 to 6 tags.\n- Submission failed: You have reached the maximum limit of 2 concurrent pending evaluations. Your current pending/running evaluations are: 420, 421. Please wait for these to complete before submitting new ones.\n- File created successfully: noema/results/prepool_C_alpha01_plan.md\n- File overwritten successfully: noema/results/SOTA_MONITOR.md\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 421 | 1 | PrePool Res-ChannelMixer (alpha=0.1, hidden=32) + Mean+Max — seed=7 | Noema I | 285 |\n| 420 | 1 | PrePool Res-ChannelMixer (alpha=0.1, hidden=32) + Mean+Max — seed=42 | Noema I | 285 |\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick\
    \ | Score | APA_R2 | CRI-Off_Spearman | CRI-On_Spearman | MRL_R2 | Modif_AUC-ROC | PRS_R2 | ncRNA_Accuracy |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 231 | 1 | DSConv with Mean+LSE Pooling and GELU (Multi-seed Run 3, Seed 123) | Aetheria I | 141 | 0.6818 | 0.8587 | 0.0679 | 0.4992 | 0.8888 | 0.9512 | 0.5549 | 0.9523 |\n| 236 | 1 | DSConv with Mean+LSE Pooling (tau=0.25) and GELU (Multi-seed Run 1, Seed 1) | Aetheria I | 145 | 0.6818 | 0.8553 | 0.0715 | 0.5134 | 0.8746 | 0.9517 | 0.5630 | 0.9431 |\n| 312 | 1 | Synergy Test: Hybrid Architecture with SOTA LSE Pooling (tau=0.25) | Axiom II | 208 | 0.6818 | 0.8509 | 0.0790 | 0.5013 | 0.8904 | 0.9487 | 0.5593 | 0.9431 |\n| 366 | 1 | Stability Atlas: DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, max) — Seed=1 | Noema I | 250 | 0.6817 | 0.8587 | 0.0636 | 0.5050 | 0.8841 | 0.9502 | 0.5564 | 0.9538 |\n| 170 | 1 | Replication: Hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM (No-PE) — Seed=123 | Noema I | 99 | 0.6817 | 0.8575 | 0.0753 | 0.4988 | 0.8962 | 0.9507 | 0.5671\
    \ | 0.9262 |\n| 160 | 1 | Hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM with Additive Attention Pooling (No-PE) - Re-establishing Baseline (ID 140) | Aetheria I | 93 | 0.6816 | 0.8557 | 0.0819 | 0.4838 | 0.8976 | 0.9502 | 0.5632 | 0.9385 |\n| 397 | 1 | PrePool Res-ChannelMixer (param-matched) — Config A (mean+LSE τ=0.5) — seed=7 | Noema I | 272 | 0.6815 | 0.8592 | 0.0776 | 0.4878 | 0.8876 | 0.9509 | 0.5598 | 0.9477 |\n| 403 | 1 | Diagnostic Run: Noema I's DSConv+LSE (tau=0.5) - Seed 7 with Tau Print | Aetheria I | 276 | 0.6814 | 0.8573 | 0.0804 | 0.5040 | 0.8807 | 0.9513 | 0.5594 | 0.9369 |\n| 325 | 1 | Synergy Test: Attention-fused Pooling on DSConv SOTA | Logos I | 217 | 0.6814 | 0.8604 | 0.0591 | 0.5142 | 0.8862 | 0.9509 | 0.5589 | 0.9400 |\n| 418 | 1 | PrePool Res-ChannelMixer (param-matched, alpha=0.1, hidden=32) — Config A (mean+LSE τ=0.5) — seed=42 | Noema I | 283 | 0.6814 | 0.8566 | 0.0763 | 0.4872 | 0.8844 | 0.9516 | 0.5628 | 0.9508 |\n| 416 | 1 | Replication: Noema I's DSConv with Mean+Max Pooling\
    \ - Seed 21 | Aetheria I | 282 | 0.6814 | 0.8540 | 0.0753 | 0.4924 | 0.8816 | 0.9510 | 0.5616 | 0.9538 |\n| 408 | 1 | PrePool Res-ChannelMixer (param-matched, alpha=0.1) — Config A (mean+LSE τ=0.5) — seed=123 | Noema I | 279 | 0.6811 | 0.8571 | 0.0735 | 0.4953 | 0.8835 | 0.9515 | 0.5562 | 0.9508 |\n| 190 | 1 | Replication: Gated Dual-Path (No-PE) — Seed=7 | Noema I | 114 | 0.6809 | 0.8585 | 0.0563 | 0.4972 | 0.8909 | 0.9513 | 0.5659 | 0.9462 |\n| 360 | 1 | Stability Atlas: DSConv (No-PE) + concat(mean, LSE_tau=0.25) — Seed=7 | Noema I | 246 | 0.6807 | 0.8551 | 0.0718 | 0.5013 | 0.8819 | 0.9522 | 0.5535 | 0.9492 |\n| 241 | 1 | DSConv with Mean+LSE Pooling (tau=0.25) and GELU (Multi-seed Run 3, Seed 123) | Aetheria I | 147 | 0.6807 | 0.8552 | 0.0664 | 0.4989 | 0.8795 | 0.9508 | 0.5585 | 0.9554 |\n| 193 | 1 | Gated Dual-Path Feature Fusion: Veritas SOTA (DSConv-HybridPool) + Aetheria SOTA (DSConv-BiLSTM-A... | Veritas I | 115 | 0.6805 | 0.8559 | 0.0640 | 0.4926 | 0.8899 | 0.9529 | 0.5622\
    \ | 0.9462 |\n| 197 | 1 | Precise SOTA Replication: Aetheria's Gated Dual-Path (ID 187) | Veritas I | 119 | 0.6804 | 0.8583 | 0.0545 | 0.4968 | 0.8943 | 0.9528 | 0.5647 | 0.9415 |\n| 383 | 1 | Replication: Veritas II MoE (ID 365) — Seed=7 | Noema I | 261 | 0.6802 | 0.8398 | 0.0634 | 0.5112 | 0.8896 | 0.9505 | 0.5565 | 0.9508 |\n| 319 | 1 | DSConv (No-PE, SiLU) + concat(mean, LSE tau=0.25) | Noema I | 214 | 0.6802 | 0.8505 | 0.0800 | 0.4971 | 0.8796 | 0.9517 | 0.5564 | 0.9462 |\n| 74 | 1 | No-PE + Concat MHA (5 blocks, attn_temp=0.5) | Noema I | 36 | 0.6801 | 0.8598 | 0.0788 | 0.4883 | 0.8928 | 0.9504 | 0.5627 | 0.9277 |\n\nPage 2 of 22 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-22, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Replied to capsule #15. Your message ID\
    \ is archive_15-6.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 2)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 15 | Stability Atlas: Unified DSConv Pooling Baselines (A: mean+LSE τ=0.5, B: τ=0.25, C: mean+max) | Noema I | Tick 260 | 676 | 6 | (All Read) |\n| 14 | Replication Report: Gumbel-Gated MoE (ID 328) — Tri-seed median 0.6720 with ncRNA accuracy drop | Noema I | Tick 238 | 528 | 4 | (All Read) |\n| 13 | Paper: A Gated Mixture-of-Experts Architecture for Compliant, State-of-the-Art RNA Modeling | Axiom II | Tick 230 | 651 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 12 | Dynamic Pooling via Self-Attention on a DSConv Backbone for RNA Modeling | Logos I | Tick 226 | 843 | 3 | (1 unread) |\n| 11 | Challenges in Adapting Dual-Path Architectures for Compliant Learned Specialization in Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling (Veritas II) | Veritas II | Tick 212 | 1960 | 2 | (1 unread)\
