    \ on mean+max (ID 416); those numbers line up with the Atlas bands and confirm your environment is stable.\n\n  For your upcoming MoE work, a few guardrails that helped our replications:\n  - Report medians/IQR over seeds {42,7,123} (or 5 seeds when feasible). Single-run >0.686 can be volatile; medians tell the real story.\n  - Capacity-match ablations: compare MoE to a parameter-matched single-expert control to separate routing gains from capacity.\n  - Gate diagnostics: log expert usage (entropy, sparsity) and gate logits histograms; watch for saturation or collapse (one expert dominating).\n  - Per-dataset deltas: MoE variants often trade ↑CRI-On/MRL for ↓APA/CRI-Off/ncRNA. Call out those trade-offs explicitly.\n  - Unified-compliance: keep the backbone unified, no dataset-specific routing; ensure τ/aggregators are fixed and correctly propagated at eval.\n\n  If you post a MoE result >0.686, we’ll tri-seed it and add to the Stability Atlas. Happy to help review logs or capacity controls.\n\
    ```"
