parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/prepool_C_alpha01_partial.csv}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  seed,eval_id,score,APA_R2,CRI_Off_Spearman,CRI_On_Spearman,PRS_R2,MRL_R2,Modif_AUC_ROC,ncRNA_Accuracy\n  42,420,0.6745994483,0.8569,0.0724,0.4562,0.5550,0.8860,0.9511,0.9446\n  7,421,0.6803919645,0.8566,0.0752,0.4932,0.5665,0.8873,0.9502,0.9338\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"PrePool Res-ChannelMixer (alpha=0.1, hidden=32) + Mean+Max — seed=123\"\ntags: \"cnn, dsconv, prepool, channel-mixer, mean+max, unified, replication\"\nabstract: \"Complete tri-seed for pre-pool mixer on the robust mean+max baseline; evaluates stability vs Atlas C.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax, jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Sequence\n\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model:int; kernel_size:int=7; dilation:int=1; dropout_rate:float=0.1\n      @nn.compact\n     \
    \ def __call__(self,x,deterministic=True):\n          h=nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h=nn.Conv(self.d_model,(self.kernel_size,),feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n                    padding='SAME',kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h)\n          h=nn.gelu(h); h=nn.Conv(self.d_model,(1,))(h)\n          h=nn.Dropout(self.dropout_rate)(h,deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x+h\n\n  class ResChannelMixer(nn.Module):\n      d_model:int; hidden:int=32; dropout_rate:float=0.1; alpha:float=0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self,x,deterministic=True):\n          h=nn.LayerNorm()(x); h=nn.Dense(self.hidden)(h); h=nn.gelu(h)\n          h=nn.Dropout(self.dropout_rate)(h,deterministic=deterministic)\n          h=nn.Dense(self.d_model)(h)\n          h=nn.Dropout(self.dropout_rate)(h,deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + self.alpha*h\n\n  def mean_max_pool(h): return jnp.concatenate([jnp.mean(h,axis=1), jnp.max(h,axis=1)], axis=-1)\n\n  class RNANetPrePool(nn.Module):\n\
    \      d_input:int=4; d_output:int=1; task_type:str='regression'\n      d_model:int=256; num_blocks:int=5; dilations:Sequence[int]=(1,2,4,8,16)\n      kernel_size:int=7; dropout_rate:float=0.1; mixer_hidden:int=32; mixer_alpha:float=0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self,x,deterministic=True):\n          h=nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x); h=nn.gelu(h); h=nn.Dropout(self.dropout_rate)(h,deterministic=deterministic)\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              d=self.dilations[i] if i<len(self.dilations) else self.dilations[-1]\n              h=DSConvDilatedBlock(self.d_model,self.kernel_size,d,self.dropout_rate)(h,deterministic=deterministic)\n          h=ResChannelMixer(self.d_model,self.mixer_hidden,self.dropout_rate,self.mixer_alpha)(h,deterministic=deterministic)\n          pooled=mean_max_pool(h)\n          z=nn.LayerNorm()(pooled); z=nn.Dense(self.d_model)(z); z=nn.gelu(z); z=nn.Dropout(self.dropout_rate)(z,deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits=nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\
    \          if self.task_type=='regression' and self.d_output==1: return logits.squeeze(-1)\n          return logits\n\n  class Net:\n      def __init__(self,d_input,d_output,task_type,**kw): self.net=RNANetPrePool(d_input=d_input,d_output=d_output,task_type=task_type,**kw)\n      def init(self,key,x): pk,dk=random.split(key); vars=self.net.init({'params':pk,'dropout':dk},x,deterministic=True); return vars['params']\n      def apply(self,params,x,deterministic=True,rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic: return self.net.apply({'params':params},x,deterministic=True)\n          if rng_key is None: rng_key=random.PRNGKey(0)\n          return self.net.apply({'params':params},x,deterministic=False,rngs={'dropout':rng_key})\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {'learning_rate':0.001,'d_model':256,'num_blocks':5,'dilations':[1,2,4,8,16],\n              'kernel_size':7,'dropout_rate':0.1,'mixer_hidden':32,'mixer_alpha':0.1}\n\n  def create_network(hp):\n      return Net(4,hp.get('d_output',1),hp.get('task_type','regression'),\n\
    \                 d_model=hp['d_model'],num_blocks=hp['num_blocks'],\n                 dilations=tuple(hp['dilations']),kernel_size=hp['kernel_size'],\n                 dropout_rate=hp['dropout_rate'],mixer_hidden=hp['mixer_hidden'],\n                 mixer_alpha=hp['mixer_alpha'])\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate:float=0.001):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01))\n\n  BASE_SEED=123\n  BATCH_SIZE=64\n\n  def complete(params,opt_state,trial_data):\n      print(f\"[Complete] {trial_data.get('dataset')} val_metric={trial_data.get('val_metric')}\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/SOTA_MONITOR.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  SOTA Monitor (Tick 287)\n  - PrePool + mean+max (C) partial tri-seed:\n    • seed 42 (ID 420): 0.674599 (CRI-On 0.456) with ncRNA 0.9446\n    • seed 7  (ID 421): 0.680392 (CRI-Off 0.0752) with ncRNA 0.9338\n    Provisional mean ≈ 0.67750 (2 seeds). Both runs show\
    \ ncRNA degradation vs Atlas C medians; seed 42 also shows CRI-On drop.\n  - Action: Submitted seed 123 to complete tri-seed (ID pending). If median < Atlas C (0.679737) or IQR > 0.005914, line will be closed as negative.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Update (Tick 287): Pre-pool mixer + mean+max (partial)\n  - Results so far: seed 42 = 0.6746 (CRI-On 0.456, ncRNA 0.9446), seed 7 = 0.6804 (CRI-Off 0.0752, ncRNA 0.9338).\n  - Provisional average ≈ 0.6775 across 2 seeds; both show ncRNA drops vs our Atlas C median. Seed 123 submitted to complete tri-seed; if median < 0.679737 or IQR > 0.0059, we’ll mark the line negative and revert to Atlas baselines.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Submitting results for analysis**\n\nI noted that one seed's regression is below baseline significantly, while the other sits at 0.6804, just slightly above the baseline median. It seems informative to run seed 123 for completeness, so I’ll submit it now.\n\nI’ll also store the results in a CSV for prepool_C and update the SOTA_MONITOR with the provisional median.\n\nManaging tokens efficiently, we're at 120k of 270k, so no pruning is needed right now. \n\nNow, I'll move on to the research and write results.**Submitting run for seed 123**\n\nI'm ready to submit the third run for seed 123, focusing on mean and max calculations. We had tried this before but were blocked, and it looks like we can go ahead now since no experiments are currently running. \n\nI’ll reuse the submission code from the previous two runs with just a change to BASE_SEED=123. After that, I'll update the SOTA_MONITOR with the new results. \n\nAlso, I might want to acknowledge Aetheria's replication\
