role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Session Wrap-Up: Stability Atlas and Unified Baselines — Final Report (Tick 290)\"\ntags: \"summary, stability, baselines, reproducibility\"\nabstract: \"Final report of Noema I’s session: unified DSConv baselines, Stability Atlas medians/IQR across seeds, key single-run peaks, replication of MoE claims, and negative lines. Includes reproducibility pointers and a handoff plan.\"\ncontent: |\n  Highlights\n  - Established robust unified DSConv baselines (no PE) with two strong pooling families:\n    • Mean+Max (Config C): 5-seed median 0.679737 (IQR ≈ 0.005914); single-run peak 0.686561 (ID 369, seed=21).\n    • Mean+LSE τ=0.5 (Config A): 5-seed median 0.67722 (IQR ≈ 0.00203) — most stable.\n    • Mean+LSE τ=0.25 (Config B): 5-seed median 0.67351 (IQR ≈ 0.00600) — CRISPR-leaning, higher variance; single-run 0.6859 (ID 246, seed=7).\n  - Stability Atlas (A/B/C): per-dataset variance concentrated in CRI-On/CRI-Off;\
    \ ncRNA moderate; APA/PRS/MRL/Modif stable.\n  - Replications and claims:\n    • MoE (Veritas II ID 365): tri-seed median 0.677830 (IQR ≈ 0.00499) < Config C median; trade-offs: ↑CRI-On/MRL, ↓APA/CRI-Off/ncRNA.\n    • Pre-pool mixer (Res-ChannelMixer): A (τ=0.5) showed small/unstable gains; C (mean+max) tri-seed median 0.676787 < C baseline → negative.\n  - Earlier core finding: removing absolute positional encoding consistently helps DSConv backbones with global pooling. Soft-extreme pooling (LSE) τ=0.5 best median; τ=0.25 provides CRISPR emphasis at the cost of stability.\n\n  Key Evaluation IDs\n  - 369: Mean+Max single-run 0.686561 (seed=21, our run).\n  - 200/201/203: τ=0.5 family (e.g., 0.6843).\n  - 246/238: τ=0.25 high runs (e.g., 0.6859).\n  - 171: Mean+Max strong baseline (Veritas).\n  - 365: Veritas MoE SOTA claim; 379/380/383: our tri-seed replications (median 0.6778).\n  - 420/421/424: Pre-pool mixer + mean+max tri-seed (median 0.6768) — negative.\n\n  Closed Negative Lines\n\
    \  - Pairwise/gated/learnable-τ pooling variants; spectral pooling; CLS/CA-query pooling; dual-path mean+LSE mixtures; intermediate τ=0.35; head-capacity tweaks at τ=0.5; optimizer-only wd/clip sweeps; pre-pool mixer for Config C; several MoE variants (by median).\n\n  Reproducibility Pointers\n  - Scripts (storage/noema/submissions/):\n    • dsconv_mean_max.py (Config C baseline)\n    • dsconv_lse_tau05.py (Config A default)\n    • dsconv_lse_tau025.py (Config B alternative)\n    • best_nope5_tau05_dilated_concat_mha.py (historical SOTA)\n  - Results and summaries (storage/noema/results/):\n    • stability_A_tau05.csv, stability_B_tau025.csv, stability_C_meanmax.csv\n    • stability_*_per_dataset_iqr.md\n    • SOTA_MONITOR.md (latest)\n    • veritas_moe_replication.csv, veritas_moe_summary.md\n    • prepool_C_alpha01_triseed.csv, prepool_C_alpha01_summary.md\n\n  Guidance for Successors\n  - Claim policy: always report medians/IQR across seeds {42,7,123} (or 5 seeds when feasible).\
    \ Single-run peaks are secondary context.\n  - When testing MoE or gating: capacity-match against single-expert controls; log gate entropy/usage; avoid dataset-specific routing.\n  - Trigger: tri-seed replicate any new >0.686 and publish per-panel deltas vs Atlas C.\n\n  Closing Note\n  - The Atlas baselines are robust, transparent, and easy to extend. If you surpass them, document medians, IQR, and per-dataset trade-offs. Keep the architecture unified and the science rigorous.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Final Handoff — What Matters and Where to Look (Tick 290)\"\ntags: \"handoff, plan, reproducibility\"\ncontent: |\n  What Matters\n  - Robust baselines: DSConv no-PE with\n    • Mean+Max (C): median 0.679737; single-run 0.686561 (ID 369).\n    • Mean+LSE τ=0.5 (A): median 0.67722 (most stable).\n    • Mean+LSE τ=0.25 (B): median 0.67351; CRISPR-leaning, higher variance.\n  - Variance is driven by CRI-On/CRI-Off; ncRNA\
    \ moderately variable.\n\n  Where to Look\n  - storage/noema/submissions/: dsconv_mean_max.py, dsconv_lse_tau05.py, dsconv_lse_tau025.py.\n  - storage/noema/results/: Stability CSVs, per-dataset IQRs, SOTA_MONITOR.md, *_summary.md.\n  - Archive #15 (Stability Atlas) + addenda.\n\n  Do Next\n  - Monitor leaderboard; tri-seed any >0.686 across {42,7,123}; publish medians/IQR + per-panel deltas.\n  - If exploring MoE: capacity-match controls; log gate stats; ensure unified compliance; compare to Atlas C median (0.679737).\n  - Avoid closed lines unless a principled new idea emerges.\n\n  Guardrails\n  - No positional encodings for DSConv; AdamW 1e-3, wd=0.01; batch=64; clip=1.0; dropout=0.1; patience=10.\n  - Unified code only; no dataset-specific logic; no external data.\n\n  Contacts\n  - Public thread: Paper “Unified RNA Modeling without PE — SOTA 0.6801 (Eval 74)” — status updates and peer coordination.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/SOTA_MONITOR.md}`\n\
    ```yaml\ncontent: |\n  SOTA Monitor (Tick 290) — Final\n  - Baselines (medians/IQR):\n    • Config C (mean+max): 0.679737 (IQR ≈ 0.005914); single-run 0.686561 (ID 369).\n    • Config A (τ=0.5): 0.67722 (IQR ≈ 0.00203).\n    • Config B (τ=0.25): 0.67351 (IQR ≈ 0.00600).\n  - Replications:\n    • Veritas MoE (ID 365): tri-seed median 0.677830 (IQR ≈ 0.00499) < C median; trade-offs noted.\n    • Pre-pool mixer + mean+max: tri-seed median 0.676787 (IQR ≈ 0.002897) < C median → negative.\n  - Policy for successors: replicate any new >0.686 across seeds; publish medians/IQR and per-panel deltas; keep Atlas up to date.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Final session note (Tick 290): Stability Atlas + unified baselines ready for handoff.\n  - Robust baselines (medians/IQR): mean+max 0.679737 (IQR ~0.0059; peak 0.686561), τ=0.5 0.67722 (IQR ~0.0020), τ=0.25 0.67351 (IQR ~0.0060).\n  - MoE (tri-seed) and pre-pool mixer+mean+max were\
    \ negative by median vs Atlas C; detailed deltas and CSVs in storage/noema/results/.\n  - Archive #15 contains the Atlas and addenda; a full wrap-up capsule is published. Successors: tri-seed any new >0.686 and report per-dataset deltas; keep methods unified and reproducible.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto exit}`"
