tick: 292
role: model
parts:
- text: "`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/analysis/mixer_feature_stats.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Mixer Feature Stats Utilities (Noema Lineage)\n\n  Goal:\n    Provide reusable functions to quantify how a pre-pool channel mixer\n    alters the statistics of sequence features that feed global pooling.\n    Intended to test the hypothesis: the mixer disrupts max-sensitive\n    feature distributions (e.g., sparsity, extreme values), harming ncRNA.\n\n  Usage notes:\n    - Call compute_channel_stats() on the sequence features just before pooling.\n    - For pre/post comparison, capture both tensors (h_pre, h_post) and call compare_pre_post().\n    - Tensors are expected as numpy-like arrays (JAX DeviceArray or ndarray).\n      Shape: (B, L, C) with B=batch, L=length, C=channels.\n\n    Example pseudo-code inside a submission's optional test():\n        import jax, jax.numpy as jnp\n        from analysis.mixer_feature_stats import compute_channel_stats,\
    \ compare_pre_post\n\n        B, L, C = 8, 200, 256\n        h_pre  = jax.random.normal(jax.random.PRNGKey(0), (B, L, C))\n        # emulate mixer: small residual reweighting\n        delta  = jax.random.normal(jax.random.PRNGKey(1), (B, L, C)) * 0.05\n        h_post = h_pre + delta\n\n        pre_stats  = compute_channel_stats(h_pre, topk=5)\n        post_stats = compute_channel_stats(h_post, topk=5)\n        report = compare_pre_post(pre_stats, post_stats)\n        print(report)\n\n  \"\"\"\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n\n  def _safe_mean(x, axis=None):\n      return jnp.mean(x, axis=axis)\n\n  def _safe_std(x, axis=None):\n      return jnp.std(x, axis=axis)\n\n  def _gini_coefficient(x, axis=-1, eps=1e-12):\n      \"\"\"\n      Gini over nonnegative values along axis.\n      We compute |x_i - x_j| pairwise approximation using Lorenz curve proxy:\n      Gini = 1 - 2 * sum_{i} (cum_sum_i / total) / n + 1/n\n      Expect input x >= 0; we soft-rectify before usage.\n      \"\"\"\n     \
    \ x = jnp.maximum(x, 0.0)\n      n = x.shape[axis]\n      x_sorted = jnp.sort(x, axis=axis)\n      cumsum = jnp.cumsum(x_sorted, axis=axis)\n      total = jnp.sum(x_sorted, axis=axis, keepdims=True) + eps\n      lorenz = cumsum / total  # monotone [0,1]\n      # Integral of Lorenz curve approximated by discrete sum / n\n      lorenz_integral = jnp.sum(lorenz, axis=axis) / n\n      gini = 1.0 - 2.0 * lorenz_integral + 1.0 / n\n      return gini\n\n  def compute_channel_stats(h, topk=5, eps=1e-12):\n      \"\"\"\n      Compute per-batch, per-channel statistics of sequence features (B,L,C).\n      Returns a dict of tensors aggregated over batch (averaged across B).\n      \"\"\"\n      B, L, C = h.shape\n      # Lengthwise summary\n      mean_len = _safe_mean(h, axis=1)            # (B,C)\n      max_len  = jnp.max(h, axis=1)               # (B,C)\n      abs_max  = jnp.max(jnp.abs(h), axis=1)      # (B,C)\n\n      # Nonneg proxy for sparsity stats (ReLUed)\n      h_pos = jnp.maximum(h, 0.0)\n\
    \      # top-k mass ratio: fraction of sum carried by top-k length positions\n      # Shape (B,C,k)\n      topk_vals = jnp.sort(h_pos, axis=1)[:, ::-1, :][:, :topk, :]\n      sum_all   = jnp.sum(h_pos, axis=1) + eps      # (B,C)\n      topk_sum  = jnp.sum(topk_vals, axis=1)        # (B,C)\n      topk_ratio = topk_sum / sum_all               # (B,C)\n\n      # Gini over length for each channel (higher → more concentrated mass)\n      gini_len = _gini_coefficient(h_pos, axis=1)\n\n      # Aggregate over batch (mean across B) to obtain robust channel metrics\n      def batch_mean(x): return _safe_mean(x, axis=0)  # (C,) for per-channel vectors\n\n      stats = {\n          \"mean_len\": batch_mean(mean_len),      # (C,)\n          \"max_len\": batch_mean(max_len),        # (C,)\n          \"abs_max\": batch_mean(abs_max),        # (C,)\n          \"topk_ratio\": batch_mean(topk_ratio),  # (C,)\n          \"gini_len\": batch_mean(gini_len),      # (C,)\n          # global summaries as scalars\n\
    \          \"mean_len_mean\": float(_safe_mean(mean_len)),\n          \"max_len_mean\": float(_safe_mean(max_len)),\n          \"abs_max_mean\": float(_safe_mean(abs_max)),\n          \"topk_ratio_mean\": float(_safe_mean(topk_ratio)),\n          \"gini_len_mean\": float(_safe_mean(gini_len)),\n      }\n      return stats\n\n  def compare_pre_post(pre, post, keys=(\"max_len_mean\",\"abs_max_mean\",\"topk_ratio_mean\",\"gini_len_mean\",\"mean_len_mean\")):\n      \"\"\"\n      Compare scalar summaries between pre and post dictionaries.\n      Returns a human-readable string and a diff dict.\n      \"\"\"\n      diffs = {}\n      lines = [\"== Pre vs Post mixer scalar diffs ==\"]\n      for k in keys:\n          v_pre = float(pre.get(k, float(\"nan\")))\n          v_post = float(post.get(k, float(\"nan\")))\n          diff = v_post - v_pre\n          diffs[k] = diff\n          lines.append(f\"{k}: post - pre = {diff:+.6f} (pre={v_pre:.6f}, post={v_post:.6f})\")\n      return \"\\n\".join(lines),\
    \ diffs\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write noema/results/mixer_analysis_plan.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Mixer Analysis Plan (Tick 292)\n  Objective: Test whether the pre-pool mixer reduces sparsity/extremal structure used by max pooling, correlating with ncRNA drops.\n\n  Metrics (compute per (dataset, seed), pre vs post mixer):\n  - max_len_mean, abs_max_mean: average extremal magnitude\n  - topk_ratio_mean (k=5): fraction of positive mass in top-k positions (concentration)\n  - gini_len_mean: lengthwise concentration of positive activations (sparsity proxy)\n  - mean_len_mean: baseline mean shift\n\n  Protocol:\n  - Hook DSConv output h_pre and h_post (just before pooling) in both baseline (no mixer) and mixer runs.\n  - Use analysis/mixer_feature_stats.py to compute stats and compare.\n  - Correlate per-dataset deltas with validation metric changes, focusing on ncRNA and CRI-On.\n\n  Expected outcome:\n  - Mixer reduces topk_ratio_mean and/or gini_len_mean for ncRNA, aligning\
    \ with accuracy drops.\n  - CRI-On may see mixed effects (some seeds increase, others decrease).\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{update 16-1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Reviewer-suggested follow-up (Tick 292): testing the mechanism\n  We added an analysis plan and utilities to quantify how the pre-pool mixer alters feature statistics relevant to max pooling.\n\n  Summary of planned diagnostics:\n  - For h_pre and h_post (sequence features before pooling), compute:\n    • max_len_mean, abs_max_mean: extremal magnitude\n    • topk_ratio_mean (k=5): fraction of positive mass captured by top-k positions\n    • gini_len_mean: lengthwise concentration (sparsity proxy)\n    • mean_len_mean: baseline mean shifts\n  - Compare pre vs post (“post - pre”) and correlate deltas with per-dataset metric changes, with emphasis on ncRNA.\n\n  Artifacts:\n  - analysis/mixer_feature_stats.py: reusable functions to compute stats and pre/post diffs.\n  - results/mixer_analysis_plan.md:\
    \ protocol and expected outcomes.\n\n  We hypothesize the mixer reduces concentration of informative extremes (lower topk_ratio/gini), explaining consistent ncRNA degradation. We will report results in a future addendum if time permits.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto public_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Paper update (Tick 292): Negative results on pre-pool channel mixing (accepted, Archive #16).\n  - Tri-seed vs Atlas C (mean+max) shows lower median (0.6768 < 0.6797) with consistent ncRNA drops.\n  - We added an analysis plan + utilities (analysis/mixer_feature_stats.py) to test the mechanism (max-sensitive feature dilution).\n  - If anyone has mixer variants that preserve ncRNA while boosting CRI-On, please share tri-seed medians/IQR and deltas.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto exit}`\n`/execute_action{exit}`"
thinking_content: "**Planning action sequence**\n\nI need to create an action sequence. We’re currently in the Exit room with only 8 ticks left, as we’re on tick 292 of 300. The last archive was published, labeled #16, with reviewer feedback suggesting I analyze feature statistics pre/post mixer to test the hypothesis. Since time is short, I’ll update Archive #16 with a plan for future analysis. I also need to ensure I don’t forget anything important in private memory. What's the user asking?**Continuing with system state**\n\nIt looks like there wasn’t a question posed; just a system state update. I need to keep things moving. The usual approach is to respond with the relevant commands. First, I’ll add an update to Archive #16, addressing the reviewer’s suggestions, possibly including pseudo-code for logging top-k per-channel maxima distributions and Gini/sparsity measures. I might add a handoff to private memory too, finalize it with \"Exit plan at tick 296,\" then consider announcing\
  \ the acceptance of paper #16 before exiting gracefully.**Creating code for feature stats**\n\nI can write a code snippet to log per-dataset feature statistics in the Flax model. I’ll create instrumentation wrappers around the DSConv output to compute the max over length per channel, along with mean and standard deviations for top-k differences pre and post mixer. I’ll implement this by going to research and writing the necessary script in `noema/analysis/mixer_feature_stats.py`. The file will include a test function running basic validation without a GPU, and I’ll ensure it's modular for easy future use.**Finalizing analysis submission**\n\nFor the analysis, I can create a test() function to compute statistics on dummy random input, but I’m thinking it might be cleaner just to leave the module file as is. Adding an \"analysis plan\" as an addendum to Archive #16 should suffice. \n\nNext, I’ll update Archive #16-1 with the plan that measures per-channel max sparsity, top-k mass, and shifts\
  \ in max values distribution pre- and post-mixer, while also mentioning correlation with ncRNA accuracy drops. Then, I'll announce the acceptance of the negative results paper in public memory and ask for cross-replication before gracefully exiting. I’ll watch out for proper YAML formatting while I craft the content.**Preparing code and updates**\n\nI want to ensure that if the title field includes a colon, we quote it for safety, even though it was used previously without quotes. Let’s be cautious and keep the quotes. I’ll also make sure that each command is on its own line.\n\nI’ll create `mixer_feature_stats.py`, implementing `compute_channel_stats(h)` to return mean, standard deviation, and top-k mass ratio. The function `compare_pre_post(h_pre, h_post)` will compute differences for future use, and I'll include a docstring with usage examples. \n\nThen, I’ll update Archive #16 using message ID 16-1 and create a TODO file in storage for analysis plans before posting to public memory\
  \ and exiting gracefully. Let's finalize this!"
